/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780504996","pull_request_review_id":3771070293,"id":2780504996,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6luyOk","diff_hunk":"@@ -435,5 +435,5 @@ build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n # Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local openapi\n \t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","original_commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Make `openapi` opt‑in for `all` to avoid flaky builds.**\n\nLine 438 now forces `openapi` in the default build path; this spins up a server on a fixed port, relies on runtime config, and writes `docs/api/api.json`, which can break CI/local runs or leave a dirty tree. Consider gating this step behind an explicit flag or a separate target.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested Makefile change (opt‑in OpenAPI)</summary>\n\n```diff\n+RUN_OPENAPI ?= 0\n+ifeq ($(RUN_OPENAPI),1)\n+ALL_OPENAPI := openapi\n+endif\n+\n-# Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local openapi\n+# Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local $(ALL_OPENAPI)\n \t`@echo` \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 438 - 439, The default \"all\" target currently depends\non \"openapi\", causing the OpenAPI server to run and generate docs during every\nbuild; remove \"openapi\" from the dependency list of the \"all\" target (leave\ntargets like build, check, test-sqlite, e2e-local) and instead add either a\nseparate phony target or a conditional gate (e.g., a MAKE_OPENAPI or\nENABLE_OPENAPI variable checked by the Makefile) so running \"make all\" does not\ninvoke the \"openapi\" target unless the user explicitly opts in (e.g., \"make\nopenapi\" or \"MAKE_OPENAPI=1 make all\"); update any README/Makefile comments to\ndocument the opt‑in behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T04:16:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T06:15:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780504996","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780504996"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780504996"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780504996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":438,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":439,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780507297","pull_request_review_id":3771072490,"id":2780507297,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6luyyh","diff_hunk":"@@ -435,5 +435,5 @@ build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n # Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local openapi","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"c8193b5a50be8f4ee72f73124b09ffdf22c93601","original_commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n1\\. Orphan server via openapi <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code>\n\n<pre>\n• <b><i>make all</i></b> now runs the <b><i>openapi</i></b> target, which starts <b><i>hyperspot-server</i></b> in the background but\n  captures <b><i>$$!</i></b> (PID) on a *different* recipe line; with Make’s default behavior (each recipe line =\n  separate shell), <b><i>SERVER_PID</i></b> is empty/incorrect and cleanup doesn’t happen.\n• This can leave a long-running server on <b><i>127.0.0.1:8087</i></b>, causing port conflicts and flaky/failed\n  subsequent runs on developer machines (and potentially in automation).\n• <b><i>openapi</i></b> also hard-requires <b><i>curl</i></b>, so <b><i>make all</i></b> now fails on systems where <b><i>curl</i></b> isn’t\n  installed, even though <b><i>all</i></b> is documented as the general “run all checks” entrypoint.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n## Issue description\n`make all` now runs `openapi`, but the `openapi` recipe starts `hyperspot-server` in the background on one Make recipe line and attempts to capture/kill the PID (`$$!`) on a subsequent line. Because Make runs each recipe line in a new shell by default, PID capture and cleanup are ineffective, leaving an orphan server process.\n\n## Issue Context\nThis issue becomes much more impactful now that `all` depends on `openapi`.\n\n## Fix Focus Areas\n- Makefile[241-266]\n- Makefile[437-439]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-09T04:17:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T04:17:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780507297","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780507297"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780507297"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780507297/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":431,"original_line":438,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780807959","pull_request_review_id":3771381763,"id":2780807959,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lv8MX","diff_hunk":"@@ -435,5 +435,5 @@ build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n # Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local openapi\n \t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","original_commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","user":{"login":"dominic1988-lgtm","id":206866400,"node_id":"U_kgDODFSH4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206866400?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm","html_url":"https://github.com/dominic1988-lgtm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/followers","following_url":"h