cessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local openapi\n \t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","original_commit_id":"f420023e538a745c3e615353b0ae80d126ae71ac","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Question: \nit is default required inside make all to build binary locally\n\n### Answer:\nYou can steer Qodo Merge away from suggesting “make OpenAPI opt-in” changes by adding a repo-level instruction that treats `make all` as a required local build contract, and by asking it not to propose changes that weaken default build targets.\n\nAdd to your `.pr_agent.toml` (repo root or wiki config):\n\n```toml\n[pr_code_suggestions]\nextra_instructions=\"\"\"\\\nWhen reviewing build tooling (Makefile/CI scripts):\n- Treat `make all` as the canonical local build entrypoint and DO NOT suggest removing existing dependencies from it (e.g., do not make steps opt-in via flags) unless there is a clear functional bug.\n- If a target like `openapi` is required for producing the local binary/release artifacts in this repo, assume it must remain part of the default build path.\n- Prefer suggestions that improve determinism (documentation, clearer prerequisites, cleanup targets) without changing the default target graph.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nIf you want to fully avoid Makefile-related suggestions, you can also ignore it from analysis:\n\n```toml\n[ignore]\nglob = [\"Makefile\", \"**/Makefile\"]\n```\n\n(Use this only if you’re okay with losing Makefile feedback entirely.)\n\n#### Relevant Sources:\n\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/tools/improve#extra-instructions-and-best-practices\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#extra-instructions\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#ignoring-files-from-analysis\n","created_at":"2026-02-09T06:15:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T06:15:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780808497","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780808497"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780808497"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780808497/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":438,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":439,"side":"RIGH