i.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dominic1988-lgtm`, understood! I've noted that `openapi` is intentionally part of the default `all` target for local builds. Thank you for clarifying the requirement.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: dominic1988-lgtm\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 519\nFile: Makefile:438-439\nTimestamp: 2026-02-09T06:16:16.976Z\nLearning: In the Makefile for cyberfabric-core, the `openapi` target is intentionally included as a dependency of the `all` target because OpenAPI generation is required by default as part of the local build process.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T06:16:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T06:16:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780810068","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780810068"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780810068"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780810068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":438,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":439,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2780504996,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780830811","pull_request_review_id":3771405901,"id":2780830811,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lwBxb","diff_hunk":"@@ -434,6 +435,11 @@ ci: check\n build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n-# Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n-\t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"\n+# Build all release artifacts\n+build-artifacts: build openapi\n+\n+# Verify the build works locally\n+verify: check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+\n+# Default target\n+all: build-artifacts verify","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"4d09ca80eb5e06eafd3e3820bf2fb1ae5d1fd900","original_commit_id":"4d09ca80eb5e06eafd3e3820bf2fb1ae5d1fd900","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add PHONY declarations for new targets.**\n\nThe new `build-artifacts` and `verify` targets are not declared as `.PHONY` on line 409. Since they don't produce files, they should be declared phony to ensure they always run regardless of any file system state.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\nUpdate line 409:\n```diff\n-.PHONY: all check ci build quickstart example\n+.PHONY: all check ci build quickstart example build-artifacts verify\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 checkmake (0.2.2)</summary>\n\n[warning] 442-442: Target \"verify\" should be declared PHONY.\n\n(phonydeclared)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 438 - 445, Add the new non-file targets to the\nMakefile's .PHONY declaration so they always execute: update the existing .PHONY\nline referenced near the current declarations to include build-artifacts and\nverify (and optionally all) so that targets build-artifacts, verify (and all)\nare treated as phony rules rather than files.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T06:22:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T02:37:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780830811","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780830811"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780830811"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780830811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":438,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":445,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":22,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780914389","pull_request_review_id":3771490817,"id":2780914389,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lwWLV","diff_hunk":"@@ -434,6 +434,16 @@ ci: check\n build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n-# Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n-\t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"\n+# Build all release artifacts (openapi only if curl is available)\n+build-artifacts: build\n+\t@if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n+\t\t$(MAKE) openapi; \\\n+\telse \\\n+\t\techo \"WARN: curl not found, skipping OpenAPI spec generation\"; \\\n+\tfi\n+\n+# Verify the build works locally\n+verify: check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+\n+# Default target\n+all: build-artifacts verify","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"773d37b8abd736d831b5c3118a930a94577ade15","original_commit_id":"773d37b8abd736d831b5c3118a930a94577ade15","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Don’t make OpenAPI generation optional in the default build.**\n\n`build-artifacts` currently skips `openapi` when `curl` isn’t present, so `make all` can succeed without generating OpenAPI artifacts. This conflicts with the requirement that OpenAPI runs by default; let the `openapi` target enforce curl availability and fail fast instead.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Suggested change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# Build all release artifacts (openapi only if curl is available)\n-build-artifacts: build\n-\t`@if` command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n-\t\t$(MAKE) openapi; \\\n-\telse \\\n-\t\techo \"WARN: curl not found, skipping OpenAPI spec generation\"; \\\n-\tfi\n+# Build all release artifacts (includes openapi by default)\n+build-artifacts: build openapi\n```\n</details>\n\n\nBased on learnings: \"Ensure that the default 'all' target in every Makefile under cyberfabric-core includes a dependency on the 'openapi' target so OpenAPI generation runs as part of the local build. Verify that an openapi target exists and that including it does not introduce unnecessary rebuilds or circular dependencies.\"\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# Build all release artifacts (includes openapi by default)\nbuild-artifacts: build openapi\n\n# Verify the build works locally\nverify: check test-sqlite e2e-local\n\n# Default target\nall: build-artifacts verify\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 checkmake (0.2.2)</summary>\n\n[warning] 446-446: Target \"verify\" should be declared PHONY.\n\n(phonydeclared)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 437 - 449, The Makefile currently skips running the\nopenapi target when curl is missing; change it to always run openapi so OpenAPI\ngeneration is mandatory: remove the conditional block in the build-artifacts\ntarget and invoke $(MAKE) openapi unconditionally (or add openapi as an explicit\ndependency of the all target), and ensure the openapi target itself checks for\ncurl and fails fast if absent; modify the build-artifacts target (and/or the all\ntarget) to reference the openapi target by name so generation runs as part of\nthe default build.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 23988bc","created_at":"2026-02-09T06:50:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T06:53:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780914389","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780914389"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2780914389"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2780914389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":437,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":449,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":34,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2781459088","pull_request_review_id":3772063909,"id":2781459088,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lybKQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -434,6 +434,11 @@ ci: check\n build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n-# Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n-\t@echo \"consider to run 'make test-db' as well\"\n+# Build all release artifacts (includes openapi by default)\n+build-artifacts: build openapi\n+\n+# Verify the build works locally\n+verify: check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+\n+# Default target\n+all: build-artifacts verify","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"23988bc1e5b1b95ee995c9d3c239d4d70e81132d","original_commit_id":"23988bc1e5b1b95ee995c9d3c239d4d70e81132d","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://a