tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dominic1988-lgtm`, thank you for updating the comment to reflect the fixed port! The configuration is now consistent.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED` for new capabilities that stand alone; use `## MODIFIED` for behavior changes to existing requirements (include full requirement content); use `## REMOVED` for deprecated features; use `## RENAMED` for name-only changes\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:10.527Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/openspec/changes/*/design.md : Create a `design.md` file only when the change involves cross-cutting changes across multiple services/modules, new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions. Include sections: Context, Goals/Non-Goals, Decisions (with alternatives considered), Risks/Trade-offs, Migration Plan, and Open Questions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/*.md : For MODIFIED requirements, paste the complete updated requirement block (header + all scenarios) with behavior changes; the archiver replaces the entire requirement\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/proposal.md : In `proposal.md`, include sections: Why (1-2 sentences on problem/opportunity), What Changes (bullet list with breaking changes marked **BREAKING**), and Impact (affected specs and code)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-12T02:47:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T02:47:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796514083","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796514083"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796514083"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796514083/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":115,"original_start_line":120,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":118,"original_line":123,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2796504979,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":61,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796519448","pull_request_review_id":3788487860,"id":2796519448,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mr4AY","diff_hunk":"@@ -235,7 +227,7 @@ tracing:\n \r\n   # Sampling configuration\r\n   sampler:\r\n-    parent_based_ratio: # parentbased_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\r\n+    parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\r\n       ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\r","path":"config/quickstart-windows.yaml","commit_id":"c8193b5a50be8f4ee72f73124b09ffdf22c93601","original_commit_id":"29288cca3a32f3acaeb051ab0182480295c95177","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Comment-value mismatch: ratio comment says 20% but value is 1.0 (100%).**\n\nThe inline comment states \"Sample 20% of traces\" but the actual ratio is `1.0`, which means 100% sampling. This appears to be a copy-paste artifact from a template.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   sampler:\n     parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n-      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n+      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 100% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n   sampler:\n     parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n       ratio: 1.0  # Sample 100% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/quickstart-windows.yaml` at line 231, The inline comment for the\nconfiguration key \"ratio\" is incorrect: it says \"Sample 20% of traces\" while the\nvalue is 1.0 (100%); update either the numeric value or the comment so they\nmatch—e.g., change the value of ratio to 0.2 if you intend 20% sampling or\nupdate the comment to reflect 100% sampling—make the change next to the \"ratio\"\nkey so the comment and value are consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @dominic1988-lgtm\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-12T02:50:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T02:56:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796519448","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796519448"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796519448"},"pull_request":{"href":"h