line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796617557","pull_request_review_id":3788581409,"id":2796617557,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6msP9V","diff_hunk":"@@ -269,6 +272,24 @@ def check_pytest():\n def kill_existing_server(port):\n     \"\"\"Kill any existing server process on the specified port\"\"\"\n     try:\n+        if is_windows():\n+            # Windows: Use netstat to find PID and taskkill to terminate\n+            result = subprocess.run(\n+                [\"netstat\", \"-ano\"],\n+                capture_output=True,\n+                text=True\n+            )\n+            if result.returncode == 0:\n+                lines = result.stdout.split('\\n')\n+                for line in lines:\n+                    if f\":{port}\" in line and \"LISTENING\" in line:\n+                        parts = line.split()\n+                        if len(parts) >= 5:\n+                            pid = parts[-1]\n+                            print(f\"Killing existing server process {pid} on port {port}\")\n+                            run_cmd_allow_fail([\"taskkill\", \"/F\", \"/PID\", pid])\n+                            time.sleep(1)  # Give it time to die\n+            return  # Windows handling complete","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"c8193b5a50be8f4ee72f73124b09ffdf22c93601","original_commit_id":"6ace66c67643687ce7f6e2304741ae8424322d12","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n scripts/ci.py | sed -n '260,300p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1980\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any other tests or documentation about netstat output\nrg -i \"netstat|taskkill\" --type py -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 814\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check Python documentation and understand netstat -ano format better\n# Also verify if there are any tests for this function\nfd \"test.*ci\" -e py -o -name \"ci_test.py\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 302\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for test files related to ci.py\nfind . -name \"*test*ci*\" -o -name \"*ci*test*\" 2>/dev/null | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for any comments or documentation about netstat output format\nrg \"netstat|LISTENING|Local Address\" --type py -B 5 -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1202\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Windows netstat -ano output format columns local address port`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n`netstat -ano` on Windows prints (typically) these columns:\n\n- **Proto** — protocol (`TCP` or `UDP`). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai))  \n- **Local Address** — the **local** IP/interface and **local port** in the form `IP:Port` (IPv6 is shown like `[addr]:port`). If you *don’t* use `-n`, Windows may show names like `hostname:service` instead of `IP:port`. If a port “is not yet established”, it can show `*`. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai))  \n- **Foreign Address** — the **remote** IP/host and **remote port** in the form `IP:Port` (or name form unless `-n` is used). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai))  \n- **State** — TCP connection state (e.g., `LISTENING`, `ESTABLISHED`, `TIME_WAIT`, etc.). (Not shown for UDP.) ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai))  \n- **PID** — the process ID that owns the socket/connection (`-o`). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/windows-server/performance/determine-which-program-use-block-tcp-ports?utm_source=openai))  \n\nSo, in `Local Address` the “column” is really **address + port together**, separated by a colon (e.g., `127.0.0.1:49274` means local port `49274` on local IP `127.0.0.1`). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai\n- 4: https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai\n- 5: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/windows-server/performance/determine-which-program-use-block-tcp-ports?utm_source=openai\n- 6: https://learn.microsoft.com/tr-tr/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix port matching to avoid terminating unrelated processes.**\n\nThe substring check `f\":{port}\" in line` can match `:8086` when checking for port `:86`, causing incorrect process termination. Extract the port from the Local Address column (`IP:Port` format) and compare as a string instead.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                lines = result.stdout.split('\\n')\n-                for line in lines:\n-                    if f\":{port}\" in line and \"LISTENING\" in line:\n-                        parts = line.split()\n-                        if len(parts) >= 5:\n-                            pid = parts[-1]\n+                port_str = str(port)\n+                for line in result.stdout.splitlines():\n+                    if \"LISTENING\" not in line:\n+                        continue\n+                    parts = line.split()\n+                    if len(parts) < 5:\n+                        continue\n+                    local_addr = parts[1]\n+                    local_port = local_addr.rsplit(\":\", 1)[-1]\n+                    if local_port != port_str:\n+                        continue\n+                    pid = parts[-1]\n                             print(f\"Killing existing server process {pid} on port {port}\")\n                             run_cmd_allow_fail([\"taskkill\", \"/F\", \"/PID\", pid])\n                             time.sleep(1)  # Give it time to die\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.15.0)</summary>\n\n[error] 278-278: Starting a process with a partial executable path\n\n(S607)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 272 - 292, The port-matching logic in\nkill_existing_server is too loose (f\":{port}\" in line) and can match substrings;\nchange the Windows netstat parsing to extract the Local Address column (e.g.,\nparts[1] from netstat output) and isolate the port with local_addr.rsplit(':',\n1)[-1], then compare that extracted port exactly to str(port) before calling\nrun_cmd_allow_fail; also skip header/empty lines and continue using\ntime.sleep(1) after taskkill as before. This touches kill_existing_server and\nuses is_windows, subprocess.run result parsing, and run_cmd_allow_fail.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @dominic1988-lgtm\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-12T03:39:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T03:53:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796617557","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796617557"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#discussion_r2796617557"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796617557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":272,"original_start_line":272,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":298,"original_line":292,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":31,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2796641981","pull_request_review_id":3788604310,"id":2796641981,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6msV69","dif