"-9\", pid])\n>                  time.sleep(1)  # Give it time to die\n>      except Exception:\n>          # If we can't find or kill the process, continue anyway\n>          pass\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3773025310","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3773025310"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-09T12:29:13Z","commit_id":"4534853a13fc321513b3acc6d9f01633db860d3e"},{"id":3788474271,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7hz4ef","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/e2e-local-windows.yaml`:\n- Around line 232-235: The comment next to the sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio\nis inconsistent with the value; update the comment or the value so they match:\neither change ratio: 1.0 to ratio: 0.2 if you intended 20% sampling, or change\nthe inline comment from \"Sample 20% of traces\" to \"Sample 100% of traces\" to\nreflect ratio: 1.0; apply the same correction to the other affected configs\n(config/quickstart.yaml and config/quickstart-windows.yaml) and ensure you edit\nthe keys named sampler -> parent_based_ratio -> ratio.\n\nIn `@config/quickstart-windows.yaml`:\n- Around line 120-123: The comment for grpc-hub's listen_addr is inconsistent\nwith the value: it claims \"Use ephemeral port\" but listen_addr is set to a fixed\naddress \"127.0.0.1:50051\"; either change the comment to reflect the fixed port\nor make the value use an ephemeral port by setting listen_addr to \"127.0.0.1:0\".\nUpdate the comment or the listen_addr value accordingly in the grpc-hub config\n(look for the listen_addr key under grpc-hub) so the comment and the actual\nconfiguration match.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788474271","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788474271"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T02:43:03Z","commit_id":"b64c79172dc31350114830a18ab8d51424198646"},{"id":3788487860,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7hz7y0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/quickstart-windows.yaml`:\n- Line 231: The inline comment for the configuration key \"ratio\" is incorrect:\nit says \"Sample 20% of traces\" while the value is 1.0 (100%); update either the\nnumeric value or the comment so they match—e.g., change the value of ratio to\n0.2 if you intend 20% sampling or update the comment to reflect 100%\nsampling—make the change next to the \"ratio\" key so the comment and value are\nconsistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/openapi.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`20-32`: **Elapsed time tracking doesn't account for request duration.**\n\nThe `elapsed` counter only adds `sleep_time`, not the actual time spent in `urlopen` (which has a 5-second timeout). For a build script this is acceptable, but the actual wait could exceed `max_wait` by up to 5 seconds per iteration.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Optional: Use monotonic clock for accurate timing</summary>\n\n```diff\n def wait_for_server(url: str, max_wait: int = 300) -> bool:\n     \"\"\"Wait for the server to become ready.\"\"\"\n-    elapsed = 0\n+    start = time.monotonic()\n     sleep_time = 1\n-    while elapsed < max_wait:\n+    while (time.monotonic() - start) < max_wait:\n         try:\n             with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=5) as resp:\n                 if resp.status == 200:\n                     return True\n         except (urllib.error.URLError, urllib.error.HTTPError, TimeoutError):\n             pass\n+        elapsed = int(time.monotonic() - start)\n         print(f\"Waiting for server... ({elapsed}s)\")\n         time.sleep(sleep_time)\n-        elapsed += sleep_time\n         sleep_time = min(sleep_time * 2, 8)\n     return False\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`275-292`: **Windows server kill logic relies on specific netstat output format.**\n\nThe parsing assumes `netstat -ano` output has the PID as the last whitespace-separated field. While this is correct for standard Windows netstat, consider adding a check that the parsed PID is numeric to avoid accidentally passing garbage to `taskkill`.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Optional: Validate PID is numeric before kill</summary>\n\n```diff\n                     for line in lines:\n                         if f\":{port}\" in line and \"LISTENING\" in line:\n                             parts = line.split()\n                             if len(parts) >= 5:\n                                 pid = parts[-1]\n+                                if pid.isdigit():\n-                                print(f\"Killing existing server process {pid} on port {port}\")\n-                                run_cmd_allow_fail([\"taskkill\", \"/F\", \"/PID\", pid])\n-                                time.sleep(1)  # Give it time to die\n+                                    print(f\"Killing existing server process {pid} on port {port}\")\n+                                    run_cmd_allow_fail([\"taskkill\", \"/F\", \"/PID\", pid])\n+                                    time.sleep(1)  # Give it time to die\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788487860","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788487860"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T02:50:25Z","commit_id":"29288cca3a32f3acaeb051ab0182480295c95177"},{"id":3788527491,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7h0FeD","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/openapi.py`:\n- Around line 55-71: Add an early existence check for the config file provided\nvia the --config argument: after args = parser.parse_args() validate\nPath(args.config).exists() (similar to the server_bin check) and if missing\nprint a clear error and sys.exit(1). Update any references to the config path\nvariable (args.config) and ensure this check runs before the server startup\nlogic that currently redirects stderr to DEVNULL so the script fails fast with a\nhelpful message.\n- Around line 18-46: Both wait_for_server() and fetch_openapi() currently pass\nuser-controlled URLs directly to urllib.request.urlopen(), which allows unsafe\nschemes like file://; add an allowlist check at the start of each function by\nparsing the URL (urllib.parse.urlparse) and ensuring parsed.scheme is either\n\"http\" or \"https\"; if not, log/print a clear error and return False (or raise\nValueError consistently) before calling urlopen so only HTTP(S) requests are\nallowed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788527491","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788527491"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T03:11:10Z","commit_id":"6edba5f4a6ef013341ac2d9e80b7f90c843b437a"},{"id":3788555157,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7h0MOV","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgD