questreview-3788555157","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788555157"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T03:24:56Z","commit_id":"3828716004a735a116a41e6b2f828d06c7d93dac"},{"id":3788581409,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7h0Soh","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 272-292: The port-matching logic in kill_existing_server is too\nloose (f\":{port}\" in line) and can match substrings; change the Windows netstat\nparsing to extract the Local Address column (e.g., parts[1] from netstat output)\nand isolate the port with local_addr.rsplit(':', 1)[-1], then compare that\nextracted port exactly to str(port) before calling run_cmd_allow_fail; also skip\nheader/empty lines and continue using time.sleep(1) after taskkill as before.\nThis touches kill_existing_server and uses is_windows, subprocess.run result\nparsing, and run_cmd_allow_fail.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788581409","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/519#pullrequestreview-3788581409"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/519"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T03:39:37Z","commit_id":"6ace66c67643687ce7f6e2304741ae8424322d12"}]},{"source_pr_number":477,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/477","source_state":"open","source_author":"hitengajjar","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #477] [WIP] [feat](settings_service): PRD, Design, and ADR documents as per FDD","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feature/settings-service","pr_head_sha":"52159f9abd78d3e881040852f70d96a5b140ebe0","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"hitengajjar","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/477","id":3252532894,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7B3bae","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/477","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/477.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/477.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/477","number":477,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[WIP] [feat](settings_service): PRD, Design, and ADR documents as per FDD","user":{"login":"hitengajjar","id":17683811,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjgzODEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17683811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar","html_url":"https://github.com/hitengajjar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hitengajjar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Settings Service - Multi-Tenant Configuration with GTS Schema & Compliance\r\n\r\nComplete FDD documentation for Hyperspot's Settings Service module providing enterprise-grade configuration management with GTS schema validation, hierarchical tenant inheritance, and compliance features.\r\n\r\n## 🔑 Top Key Features\r\n\r\n1. **Multi-Tenant Hierarchical Inheritance** - Automatic value resolution cascading through 10+ levels of tenant hierarchy with configurable inheritance rules and barrier tenant support\r\n\r\n2. **GTS Schema Validation** - Type-safe configuration with Global Type System schemas, JSON validation, and backward-compatible versioning\r\n\r\n3. **Domain Scoped Settings Support** - Unified settings management across 2 domain types: Tenant, User\r\n\r\n4. **Compliance Mode** - Setting locks, MFA-protected configurations, read-only enforcement, and full audit trail for regulated environments\r\n\r\n5. **High Performance**\r\n\r\n6. **Event-Driven Architecture** - Trait-based audit and notification events with configurable propagation modes (SELF, SUBROOT, NONE)\r\n\r\n7. **Secure by Default** - Automatic tenant scoping, SecurityContext validation, role-based access control, and defense-in-depth architecture\r\n\r\n8. Batch Operations - Efficient bulk updates and multi-tenant bulk get operations with partial success handling and detailed error reporting\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added comprehensive design and PRD for the Settings Service covering architecture, API contracts, deployment, security, caching, value resolution/inheritance, and integration points.\n  * Added 16 ADRs documenting decisions on schema versioning, database selection, caching, event integration, tenant hierarchy, API versioning, performance, registry, trait enforcement, defaults, compliance locks, soft deletion, batch transactions, and related patterns.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-02-06T00:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-03-30T05:19:23Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b6287c24436b5cfc9fb6f072d6b69dc59c8b5611","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.