.github.com/users/Mergifyio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Mergify","description":"Pull requests automation service.","external_url":"https://mergify.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","created_at":"2018-03-30T10:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:02:56Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","deployment_status","issue_comment","member","membership","merge_group","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3857190856","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/477#issuecomment-3857190856","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/477","id":3857190856,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7l6A_I","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T00:54:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T00:54:09Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (2)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Outdated DB security docs <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• The new DESIGN/PRD docs instruct developers to rely on an <b><i>insecure-escape</i></b> flag and to call\n>   <b><i>SecureConn::scoped()</i></b>, but the repository explicitly removed the <b><i>insecure-escape</i></b> feature and\n>   <b><i>SecureConn</i></b>’s public API exposes a different “scoped query” entrypoint.\n>• This mismatch is likely to waste engineering time and can lead to incorrect/unsafe implementation\n>   decisions (e.g., searching for non-existent APIs or assuming raw SQL escape hatches exist).\n>• Because these statements are normative (“MUST…”) they can propagate incorrect platform guidance\n>   beyond this module.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[modules/system/settings_service/docs/DESIGN.md[R123-125]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/477/files#diff-3fb80e678a3329d16dfea3addbb8532e440e27ef7e99ba811bb54096f2e4281fR123-R125)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+All operations MUST require SecurityContext for tenant isolation. Database access MUST use SecureConn with automatic tenant scoping to prevent cross-tenant data leakage. No raw SQL queries allowed except in migrations with explicit `insecure-escape` flag. Authentication MUST validate JWT tokens with tenant context before processing requests. This principle leverages Hyperspot's security infrastructure to enforce defense-in-depth.\n>+\n>+**Implementation Strategy**: Pass `&SecurityContext` to all SDK methods, use `SecureConn::scoped()` for all queries, validate tenant access in domain layer before database operations.\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>DESIGN/PRD prescribe using an <b><i>insecure-escape</i></b> flag and <b><i>SecureConn::scoped()</i></b>. The repo CHANGELOG\n>states the <b><i>insecure-escape</i></b> feature was removed entirely. The <b><i>SecureConn</i></b> implementation\n>documents/exports <b><i>find(scope)</i></b> as the scoped-query entrypoint (and shows the shape of the API\n>developers should use instead).\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[modules/system/settings_service/docs/DESIGN.md[115-126]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/modules/system/settings_service/docs/DESIGN.md/#L115-L126)</code>\n> <code>[modules/system/settings_service/docs/PRD.md[768-777]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/modules/system/settings_service/docs/PRD.md/#L768-L777)</code>\n> <code>[CHANGELOG.md[24-40]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/CHANGELOG.md/#L24-L40)</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-db/src/secure/secure_conn.rs[110-166]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/libs/modkit-db/src/secure/secure_conn.rs/#L110-L166)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>The new Settings Service DESIGN/PRD documents include normative guidance that is inconsistent with the current platform DB/security APIs:\n>- They reference an `insecure-escape` flag as an allowed escape hatch, but the repo changelog states that feature was removed.\n>- They instruct developers to call `SecureConn::scoped()`, but the public `SecureConn` API provides scoped operations via methods like `find(scope: &amp;AccessScope)`.\n>\n>This will mislead implementers and can result in incorrect/unsafe design decisions.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>The platform DB/security layer was recently refactored (see CHANGELOG) and the docs should reflect the current, supported way to scope DB operations.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/DESIGN.md[115-126]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/DESIGN.md[1538-1548]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/PRD.md[768-777]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  2.  ADR path bypasses lint <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• New ADRs are placed under <b><i>modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/...</i></b> (capitalized, singular),\n>   but repo ADR governance/linting is wired to <b><i>modules/**/docs/adrs/**/*.md</i></b>.\n>• As a result, the ADR lint workflow won’t run for these files, and they also diverge from the\n>   documented module ADR location convention.\n>• Additionally, the ADRs don’t follow the repository’s standard ADR template style (YAML\n>   frontmatter), which reduces consistency and toolability.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0001-fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-schema-versioning.md[R1-8]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/477/files#diff-4405072ae22464d0478ff6999d9e19d8222b6561b785fa1cff076b3d63348633R1-R8)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+# ADR-0001: GTS Schema Versioning Strategy\n>+\n>+**Date**: 2026-02-03\n>+\n>+**Status**: Proposed\n>+\n>+**ADR ID**: `fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-schema-versioning`\n>+\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The ADR lint workflow and ADR documentation specify the expected module ADR directory\n>(<b><i>modules/**/docs/adrs/**</i></b>). The new ADRs are stored under a different directory name (<b><i>docs/ADR</i></b>),\n>and the example ADR content shows no YAML frontmatter as used by the repo templates.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/adr-lint.yml[1-29]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/.github/workflows/adr-lint.yml/#L1-L29)</code>\n> <code>[docs/adrs/README.md[48-55]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/docs/adrs/README.md/#L48-L55)</code>\n> <code>[modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0001-fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-schema-versioning.md[1-8]](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/blob/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b/modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0001-fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-schema-versioning.md/#L1-L8)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>Module ADRs were added under `modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/...`, which is not covered by the repository’s ADR lint workflow (`modules/**/docs/adrs/**/*.md`) and diverges from the documented convention. This bypasses ADR linting and reduces consistency/toolability.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>The repo documents ADR conventions and has a dedicated ADR lint workflow. To benefit from that tooling, module ADRs should be placed under `docs/adrs` in the module and follow the standard template format.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0001-fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-schema-versioning.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0002-fdd-settings-service-adr-database-technology.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0003-fdd-settings-service-adr-caching-strategy.md[1-12]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0004-fdd-settings-service-adr-event-bus-integration.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0005-fdd-settings-service-adr-tenant-hierarchy-cache.md[1-12]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0006-fdd-settings-service-adr-api-versioning.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0007-fdd-settings-service-adr-performance-optimization.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0008-fdd-settings-service-adr-gts-registry-implementation.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0009-fdd-settings-service-adr-trait-enforcement.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0010-fdd-settings-service-adr-default-value-resolution.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0011-fdd-settings-service-adr-domain-type-registry.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0012-fdd-settings-service-adr-inheritance-algorithm.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0013-fdd-settings-service-adr-compliance-lock.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0014-fdd-settings-service-adr-soft-deletion.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0015-fdd-settings-service-adr-batch-transactions.md[1-8]\n>- modules/system/settings_service/docs/ADR/general/0016-fdd-settings-service-adr-database-schema-hierarchy.md[1-15]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/commit/aff72ec845dfac72866cafb9e8a5af64ab63891b -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3857190856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discus