38Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004994","pull_request_review_id":3737806467,"id":2753004994,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kF4XC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,674 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — Design Document\n+\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+### 1.1 Purpose\n+\n+The Web Search Gateway is a **Gateway Module** providing a unified, provider-agnostic web search API for HyperSpot. It routes search requests to configurable **Plugin Modules** (provider implementations) while enforcing governance, result normalization, caching, and observability.\n+\n+### 1.2 Module Classification\n+\n+Per [Architecture Manifest](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md):\n+\n+| Attribute | Value |\n+|-----------|-------|\n+| **Module Type** | Gateway Module |\n+| **API Layer** | Yes (REST) |\n+| **Business Logic Layer** | Yes (contract, router, normalization) |\n+| **Infrastructure Layer** | Yes (cache, OAGW client) |\n+| **Gateway Layer** | Yes (plugin connectors) |\n+\n+### 1.3 Key Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | ADR | Summary |\n+|----------|-----|---------|\n+| Stateless Gateway | [ADR-001](./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md) | Gateway holds no state; quota/billing delegated to external service |\n+| Stateless Credential Management | [ADR-002](./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md) | Credentials injected via OAGW; gateway never handles raw secrets |\n+| Settings Service for Tenant Config | [ADR-003](./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md) | Per-tenant provider configuration via Settings Service |\n+| Tenant-Scoped Caching | [ADR-004](./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md) | Cache isolation per tenant prevents data leakage |","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check ADR files in the docs/ADR directory\necho \"=== ADR files in modules/web_search_gateway/docs/ ===\"\nfd -t f '' modules/web_search_gateway/docs/ 2>/dev/null | sort\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Links referenced in Design.md ===\"\nrg '\\[ADR-[^\\]]+\\]\\(' modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md 2>/dev/null || echo \"No matches found with rg\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Manual inspection of Design.md lines 24-29 ===\"\nsed -n '24,29p' modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md 2>/dev/null || echo \"File not found\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1739\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix all four ADR links to match actual file names.**\n\nADR links in the Design.md table are broken. The files use lowercase numbered prefixes without \"ADR-\" (e.g., `001-stateless-gateway.md`), but the links reference uppercase prefixed names (e.g., `ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md`). \n\nUpdate the links as follows:\n- `./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md` → `./001-stateless-gateway.md`\n- `./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md` → `./002-use-oagw-for-credential-management.md`\n- `./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md` → `./003-use-settings-service-for-tenant-config.md`\n- `./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md` → `./004-add-tenant-scoped-caching.md`\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md` around lines 24 - 29, In the\nDesign.md table the ADR links are incorrect; update the four link targets in the\ntable row entries by replacing \"./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md\" with\n\"./001-stateless-gateway.md\", \"./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md\" with\n\"./002-use-oagw-for-credential-management.md\", \"./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md\"\nwith \"./003-use-settings-service-for-tenant-config.md\", and\n\"./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md\" with \"./004-add-tenant-scoped-caching.md\"\nso the table entries for Stateless Gateway, Stateless Credential Management,\nSettings Service for Tenant Config, and Tenant-Scoped Caching point to the\nactual filenames.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753004994","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004994"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753004994"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":24,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":29,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":29,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004995","pull_request_review_id":3737806467,"id":2753004995,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kF4XD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,674 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — Design Document\n+\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+### 1.1 Purpose\n+\n+The Web Search Gateway is a **Gateway Module** providing a unified, provider-agnostic web search API for HyperSpot. It routes search requests to configurable **Plugin Modules** (provider implementations) while enforcing governance, result normalization, caching, and observability.\n+\n+### 1.2 Module Classification\n+\n+Per [Architecture Manifest](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md):\n+\n+| Attribute | Value |\n+|-----------|-------|\n+| **Module Type** | Gateway Module |\n+| **API Layer** | Yes (REST) |\n+| **Business Logic Layer** | Yes (contract, router, normalization) |\n+| **Infrastructure Layer** | Yes (cache, OAGW client) |\n+| **Gateway Layer** | Yes (plugin connectors) |\n+\n+### 1.3 Key Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | ADR | Summary |\n+|----------|-----|---------|\n+| Stateless Gateway | [ADR-001](./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md) | Gateway holds no state; quota/billing delegated to external service |\n+| Stateless Credential Management | [ADR-002](./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md) | Credentials injected via OAGW; gateway never handles raw secrets |\n+| Settings Service for Tenant Config | [ADR-003](./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md) | Per-tenant provider configuration via Settings Service |\n+| Tenant-Scoped Caching | [ADR-004](./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md) | Cache isolation per tenant prevents data leakage |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Architecture\n+\n+### 2.1 High-Level Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                         CONSUMER MODULES                                │\n+│              (AI Chatbots, RAG Systems, Platform Services)              │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    │ hub.get::<dyn WebSearchGatewayApi>()\n+                                    │ or REST: POST /web-search/v1/search\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      WEB SEARCH GATEWAY MODULE                          │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  REST API Layer: /web-search/v1/search, /providers, /health       │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  Domain Layer: SearchService, ProviderRouter, CacheService,       │  │\n+│  │                GovernanceService, CircuitBreaker, Normalizer      │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│                                    │                                    │\n+│                                    │ hub.get_scoped::<dyn WebSearchPluginClient>\n+│                                    ▼                                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+          │                          │                          │\n+          ▼                          ▼                          ▼\n+┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐\n+│  TAVILY PLUGIN  │       │  SERPER PLUGIN  │       │ (FUTURE PLUGIN) │\n+│  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │\n+│  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│\n+│  Client         │       │  Client         │       │  Client         │\n+└────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘\n+         │                         │                         │\n+         └─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘\n+                                   │ HTTPS via OAGW\n+                                   ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│              OUTBOUND API GATEWAY (OAGW) - Credential injection         │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### 2.2 Module Dependencies & Integrations\n+\n+| Dependency | Purpose | Criticality |\n+|------------|---------|-------------|\n+| **Identity & Authorization** | Authentication and authorization of search requests | P0 |\n+| **Outbound API Gateway (OAGW)** | Secure storage and management of provider API credentials | P0 |\n+| **types-registry** | Plugin discovery, capability schemas | P0 |\n+| **Settings Service** | Tenant configuration | P0 |\n+| **Cache backend** | Response caching (Redis or in-memory) | P0 |\n+| **Billing Service** | Quota tracking and usage metering | P0 |\n+| **LLM Gateway** | Query refinement, answer extraction, summarization | P1 |\n+| **Observability stack** | Metrics, logs, traces | P1 |\n+| **Event Manager** | Audit event publishing and observability | P1 |\n+\n+\n+> **Notes**:\n+> - Plugins (e.g., `tavily_plugin`, `serper_plugin`) are **not** listed as dependencies. They are discovered dynamically at runtime via GTS `types-registry`. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md).\n+> - **Billing Service** handles quota tracking and usage metering. Gateway is stateless and delegates quota checks/updates to this service.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Crate Structure\n+\n+### 3.1 Directory Layout\n+\n+```\n+modules/web_search_gateway/\n+├── docs/                            # Documentation\n+├── gts/                             # GTS JSON Schemas (see section 4.3)\n+├── web_search_gateway-sdk/          # SDK crate (public API, plugin API)\n+├── web_search_gateway-gw/           # Gateway implementation\n+│   └── src/\n+│       ├── api/rest/                # REST handlers, DTOs\n+│       ├── domain/                  # SearchService, ProviderRouter, Normalizer\n+│       └── infra/                   # Cache backends, adapters\n+└── plugins/\n+    ├── tavily_plugin/               # Tavily provider (Phase 1)\n+    └── serper_plugin/               # Serper provider (Phase 2)\n+```\n+\n+Follows standard ModKit module layout. See [NEW_MODULE.md](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. SDK Design\n+\n+### 4.1 Public API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchGatewayApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute a web search request\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: SearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<SearchResponse, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// List providers enabled for the requesting tenant\n+    async fn list_providers(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<ProviderInfo>, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Get health status for a specific provider\n+    async fn get_provider_health(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        provider_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<ProviderHealthStatus, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Invalidate cache entries (requires admin permissions)\n+    async fn invalidate_cache(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        pattern: Option<&str>,\n+    ) -> Result<u64, WebSearchError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.2 Plugin API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchPluginClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute search against the provider\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: PluginSearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<PluginSearchResponse, PluginError>;\n+\n+    /// Return plugin's declared capabilities\n+    fn capabilities(&self) -> &PluginCapabilities;\n+\n+    /// Health check for the provider\n+    async fn health_check(&self, ctx: &SecurityCtx) -> Result<HealthStatus, PluginError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.3 Core Models (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Core domain types are defined as GTS JSON Schemas for language-agnostic contracts. Rust SDK types are generated from these schemas.\n+\n+| Schema File | Types | GTS ID |\n+|-------------|-------|--------|\n+| [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json) | `SearchRequest`, `SearchOptions`, `SearchType`, `SafeSearchLevel`, `Freshness`, `DateRange` | `gts.x.web_search.search_request.v1` |\n+| [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json) | `SearchResponse`, `SearchResult`, `ResponseMetadata`, `ContentType`, `AdditionalLink` | `gts.x.web_search.search_response.v1` |\n+| [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json) | `ProviderInfo`, `PluginCapabilities`, `SupportedFilters`, `HealthStatus` | `gts.x.web_search.provider.v1` |\n+| [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) | `TenantWebSearchConfig`, `TenantProviderConfig`, `RateLimitOverride`, `QuotaOverride` | `gts.x.web_search.settings.v1` |\n+\n+### 4.4 Error Codes (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Error codes follow RFC 9457 Problem Details. See [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json).\n+\n+| GTS Code | HTTP | Title |\n+|----------|------|-------|\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_found.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Found |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_enabled.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Enabled |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.capability_not_supported.v1` | 400 | Capability Not Supported |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.validation.v1` | 400 | Validation Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.no_providers_configured.v1` | 400 | No Providers Configured |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.unauthorized.v1` | 401 | Unauthorized |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.forbidden.v1` | 403 | Forbidden |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.rate_limited.v1` | 429 | Rate Limit Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.quota_exceeded.v1` | 429 | Quota Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.internal.v1` | 500 | Internal Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_error.v1` | 502 | Provider Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.providers_unavailable.v1` | 503 | All Providers Unavailable |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.timeout.v1` | 504 | Request Timeout |\n+\n+### 4.5 GTS Plugin Schema\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/gts.rs\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema(\n+    dir_path = \"schemas\",\n+    base = BaseModkitPluginV1,\n+    schema_id = \"gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~\",\n+    description = \"Web Search Gateway provider plugin specification\",\n+    properties = \"\"\n+)]\n+pub struct WebSearchPluginSpecV1;\n+```\n+\n+**GTS Instance ID Pattern**:\n+- Schema: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~`\n+- Instance: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~tavily.web_search.plugin.v1`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Gateway Implementation\n+\n+### 5.1 Module Pattern\n+\n+Web Search Gateway follows the standard Gateway + Plugin pattern. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md) for:\n+- Module declaration with `#[modkit::module]`\n+- Plugin schema registration\n+- Plugin discovery via `types-registry`\n+- Scoped client resolution via `ClientHub`\n+\n+### 5.2 Configuration\n+\n+| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n+|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n+| `default_provider` | string | `\"tavily\"` | Default provider when none specified |\n+| `request_timeout_ms` | u64 | 30000 | Overall request timeout |\n+| `cache.enabled` | bool | true | Enable response caching |\n+| `cache.default_ttl_seconds` | u64 | 3600 | Default cache TTL |\n+| `cache.max_size_mb` | u64 | 1024 | Max cache size |\n+| `rate_limit.*` |  | 100 | Default requests/second |\n+| `quota.default_monthly` |  | 10000 | Default monthly request quota |\n+| `circuit_breaker.failure_threshold` | u32 | 5 | Failures before opening circuit |\n+| `circuit_breaker.reset_timeout_seconds` | u64 | 60 | Half-open retry interval |\n+| `failover.enabled` | bool | true | Enable automatic failover |\n+\n+> **Note**: \n+> - **Rate limits**: Enforced via Redis (stateless). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - **Quotas**: Managed by Billing Service (persistent). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - See [Section 9](#9-governance) for details.\n+\n+### 5.3 Search Service Flow\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Client\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant Plugin\n+    participant Normalizer\n+\n+    Client->>SearchService: search(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService: 1. Validate request\n+    SearchService->>SearchService: validate_request()\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Redis: 2. Check rate limit (Redis)\n+    SearchService->>Redis: check_rate_limit(tenant_id)\n+    Redis-->>SearchService: OK / RateLimitExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 3. Check quota (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: check_quota(ctx)\n+    BillingService-->>SearchService: OK / QuotaExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 4. Check cache (unless bypass)\n+    alt bypass_cache = false\n+        SearchService->>Cache: get(ctx, request)\n+        Cache-->>SearchService: cached_response / miss\n+        alt cache hit\n+            SearchService-->>Client: cached_response\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,ProviderRouter: 5. Select provider\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Plugin: 6. Execute with failover\n+    SearchService->>Plugin: search(ctx, plugin_request)\n+    Plugin-->>SearchService: provider_response / error\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Normalizer: 7. Normalize response\n+    SearchService->>Normalizer: normalize(response, provider_id)\n+    Normalizer-->>SearchService: normalized_response\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 8. Cache result\n+    SearchService->>Cache: store(ctx, request, response)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 9. Record usage (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: record_usage(ctx, 1)\n+    \n+    SearchService-->>Client: normalized_response\n+```\n+\n+### 5.4 Provider Router\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant SettingsService\n+    participant TypesRegistry\n+    participant CircuitBreaker\n+    participant ClientHub\n+\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    alt provider_id specified in request\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use specific provider\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: is_provider_enabled(ctx, provider_id)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: enabled / not_enabled\n+        alt not enabled\n+            ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: ProviderNotEnabled error\n+        end\n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider_id)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+    else no provider_id specified\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use tenant default\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: get_settings(ctx)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+        ProviderRouter->>ProviderRouter: default_provider from config\n+        \n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(default_provider)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+        \n+        alt default unhealthy or capability mismatch\n+            Note over ProviderRouter: Find fallback\n+            loop enabled_providers by priority\n+                ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider)\n+                ProviderRouter->>TypesRegistry: supports_search_type(provider, type)\n+                alt healthy and capable\n+                    break\n+                end\n+            end\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over ProviderRouter,ClientHub: Resolve plugin client\n+    ProviderRouter->>ClientHub: get_scoped(gts_instance_id)\n+    ClientHub-->>ProviderRouter: plugin_client\n+    \n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin_client)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. REST API Design\n+\n+### 6.1 Endpoints\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| POST | `/web-search/v1/search` | Execute search | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers` | List enabled providers | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers/{id}/health` | Provider health | Required |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/cache` | Invalidate cache | Admin |\n+| GET | `/health/live` | Liveness check | Public |\n+| GET | `/health/ready` | Readiness check | Public |\n+\n+### 6.2 Request/Response Schemas\n+\n+REST DTOs are generated from GTS schemas (see section 4.3):\n+- **Request**: [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json)\n+- **Response**: [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json)\n+- **Providers**: [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json)\n+- **Errors**: [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json) (RFC 9457 Problem Details)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. Caching Strategy\n+\n+### 7.1 Cache Key Structure\n+\n+```\n+ws:{tenant_id}:{search_type}:{provider_id}:{sha256(query+options_hash)}\n+```\n+\n+Components:\n+- `tenant_id`: Ensures tenant isolation\n+- `search_type`: web, news, images, etc.\n+- `provider_id`: Different providers may return different results\n+- `sha256(...)`: Hash of normalized query + sorted options\n+\n+### 7.2 TTL Policy\n+\n+TTLs vary by search type (news: shorter, images/video: longer). See [Configuration Example](#12-configuration-example).\n+\n+### 7.3 Cache Bypass\n+\n+- Request header: `Cache-Control: no-cache` or `X-WSG-Cache: bypass`\n+- Request option: `options.bypass_cache: true`\n+- Admin endpoint: `DELETE /web-search/v1/cache?pattern=...`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 8. Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+### 8.1 Overview\n+\n+Tenants configure which providers are enabled via the **Settings Service**. The Web Search Gateway reads tenant-specific provider settings at runtime to determine:\n+- Which providers are enabled for the tenant\n+- The tenant's default provider\n+- Per-provider overrides (e.g., custom rate limits, priority)\n+\n+### 8.2 Configuration Model\n+\n+See [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) for the schema.\n+\n+### 8.3 Configuration Storage\n+\n+Tenant provider configuration is stored via the **Settings Service**:\n+\n+```\n+Key:   tenant:{tenant_id}:web_search.providers\n+Value: TenantWebSearchConfig (JSON)\n+```\n+\n+### 8.4 Admin REST API for Provider Management\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Get tenant provider config | Admin |\n+| PUT | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Replace provider config | Admin |\n+| PATCH | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Update single provider | Admin |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Disable provider for tenant | Admin |\n+\n+Admin request/response schemas use [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) and [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json).\n+\n+### 8.5 Sequence Diagrams\n+\n+#### 8.5.1 Execute Search\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Plugin\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Gateway->>Redis: check_rate_limit()\n+    Redis-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: check_quota()\n+    BillingService-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>Cache: get(key)\n+    Cache-->>Gateway: MISS\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get_enabled_providers()\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Plugin: search(request)\n+    Plugin-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize(response)\n+    Gateway->>Cache: store(key, response)\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: record_usage(1)\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (results)\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.2 Execute Search with Failover\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant CB as CircuitBreaker\n+    participant PluginA as Plugin-A (Tavily)\n+    participant PluginB as Plugin-B (Serper)\n+    participant OAGW\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Note over Gateway: governance, cache checks pass\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginA: search()\n+    PluginA->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginA: timeout\n+    PluginA-->>Gateway: ERROR\n+    Gateway->>CB: record_failure(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: threshold reached → OPEN\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"serper\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginB: search()\n+    PluginB->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginB: OK\n+    PluginB-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize, cache, quota\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (metadata.failover_from: \"tavily\")\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.3 List Enabled Providers\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Registry as TypesRegistry\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: GET /providers\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get(\"web_search.providers\")\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Registry: query(WebSearchPluginSpec)\n+    Registry-->>Gateway: [all registered plugins]\n+    Note over Gateway: filter, enrich health, sort by priority\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK [providers]\n+```\n+\n+### 9.7 Default Behavior\n+\n+| Scenario | Behavior |\n+|----------|----------|\n+| No tenant config exists | Use gateway default config (Tavily enabled) |\n+| Requested provider not enabled | Return `WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED` error |\n+| No enabled providers | Return `WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED` error |\n+| Default provider unhealthy | Failover to next enabled provider by priority |\n+","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Section numbering error: \"9.7 Default Behavior\" is misplaced.**\n\nThis section appears between 8.5.3 and 9 (Governance). Based on its content about tenant configuration defaults, it should likely be \"8.6 Default Behavior\" or moved into section 8.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-### 9.7 Default Behavior\n+### 8.6 Default Behavior\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n### 8.6 Default Behavior\n\n| Scenario | Behavior |\n|----------|----------|\n| No tenant config exists | Use gateway default config (Tavily enabled) |\n| Requested provider not enabled | Return `WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED` error |\n| No enabled providers | Return `WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED` error |\n| Default provider unhealthy | Failover to next enabled provider by priority |\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md` around lines 529 - 537, The\nsection titled \"9.7 Default Behavior\" is misnumbered and misplaced between\nsections 8.5.3 and 9 (Governance); rename and/or move it into the section 8\nblock so numbering and context align (e.g., change the heading to \"8.6 Default\nBehavior\" or relocate the entire paragraph/table under the appropriate 8.x\nsubsection). Update the heading text \"9.7 Default Behavior\" and any\ncross-references to reflect \"8.6 Default Behavior\" so the tenant configuration\ndefaults (Tavily enabled, WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED, WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED,\nfailover behavior) are documented within the configuration section rather than\nunder Governance.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @akshatjhalani\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:10:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753004995","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004995"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753004995"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753004995/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":529,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":537,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":537,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005001","pull_request_review_id":3737806467,"id":2753005001,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kF4XJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — PRD\n+\n+**Unified, Provider-Agnostic Search API with Plugin-Based Extensibility**\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: The Web Search Gateway is HyperSpot's centralized web search service that provides a unified API for web search operations, routing requests to configurable provider plugins while enforcing governance, normalization, and observability.\n+\n+Web search integration must be consistent across all modules without embedding provider-specific logic in each consumer. The Web Search Gateway achieves this by providing a common search API and delegating provider calls to configurable plugins via the Outbound API Gateway (OAGW).\n+\n+Phase 1 focuses on tenant-scoped web search with a single provider (Tavily), result normalization, and core governance (authN/Z, quotas, rate limits). It does not implement LLM-powered features (query refinement, answer extraction), additional search types (news, images), or advanced features (semantic caching, ML re-ranking); those are planned for Phase 2 and beyond.\n+\n+**Target Users**: Platform engineers integrating search into AI agents and RAG pipelines. Tenant admins configuring provider selection, quotas, and policies.\n+\n+**Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n+- **LLM hallucinations**: Make chatbots more accurate by providing real-time web context.\n+- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API interface abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n+- **Duplicated integration code**: A single gateway eliminates redundant provider integrations across modules.\n+- **Centralized governance**: Unified quotas, rate limits, and audit logging across all search consumers.\n+\n+**Success Criteria**:\n+\n+- All search requests resolve using tenant scope from SecurityContext; requests can specify provider or use tenant's default.\n+- Consumers can query enabled providers for their tenant via gateway endpoint.\n+- Provider plugins are discovered via types-registry and can be added without gateway code changes.\n+\n+**Capabilities**:\n+\n+- Tenant-scoped web search with per-request provider selection from tenant-enabled providers\n+- Normalized `SearchResponse` schema regardless of underlying provider\n+- Response caching with tenant isolation and configurable TTL\n+- Plugin-based provider integration via types-registry (GTS)\n+- Provider failover with circuit breaker pattern\n+- Governance: authentication, authorization, quotas, rate limiting\n+- Observability: metrics, structured logging, distributed tracing, audit events\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| **Platform Engineer** | Integrates search into AI agents and RAG systems via the Web Search Gateway |\n+| **Tenant Admin** | Configures provider selection, monitors quota usage, and manages cost controls for their tenant |\n+| **Plugin Developer** | Implements new search provider plugins using the plugin contract, and registration process |\n+\n+---","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Section numbering gap: Missing sections 2-4.**\n\nThe document jumps from \"## 1. Overview\" directly to \"## 5. Actors\". This creates a confusing structure and may indicate missing content or a copy-paste issue.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 42 - 50, The headings\njump from \"## 1. Overview\" to \"## 5. Actors\" indicating missing or misnumbered\nsections 2–4; either restore the omitted sections' content if it was\naccidentally removed or renumber the \"## 5. Actors\" header (and any subsequent\nheaders) to maintain a consecutive sequence (e.g., change \"## 5. Actors\" to \"##\n2. Actors\"), and verify other headers in the document follow the corrected\nnumbering to keep the table of contents and structure consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 831d9f8","created_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:30:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753005001","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005001"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753005001"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005001/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":42,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":50,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":50,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005007","pull_request_review_id":3737806467,"id":2753005007,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kF4XP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — PRD\n+\n+**Unified, Provider-Agnostic Search API with Plugin-Based Extensibility**\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: The Web Search Gateway is HyperSpot's centralized web search service that provides a unified API for web search operations, routing requests to configurable provider plugins while enforcing governance, normalization, and observability.\n+\n+Web search integration must be consistent across all modules without embedding provider-specific logic in each consumer. The Web Search Gateway achieves this by providing a common search API and delegating provider calls to configurable plugins via the Outbound API Gateway (OAGW).\n+\n+Phase 1 focuses on tenant-scoped web search with a single provider (Tavily), result normalization, and core governance (authN/Z, quotas, rate limits). It does not implement LLM-powered features (query refinement, answer extraction), additional search types (news, images), or advanced features (semantic caching, ML re-ranking); those are planned for Phase 2 and beyond.\n+\n+**Target Users**: Platform engineers integrating search into AI agents and RAG pipelines. Tenant admins configuring provider selection, quotas, and policies.\n+\n+**Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n+- **LLM hallucinations**: Make chatbots more accurate by providing real-time web context.\n+- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API interface abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n+- **Duplicated integration code**: A single gateway eliminates redundant provider integrations across modules.\n+- **Centralized governance**: Unified quotas, rate limits, and audit logging across all search consumers.\n+\n+**Success Criteria**:\n+\n+- All search requests resolve using tenant scope from SecurityContext; requests can specify provider or use tenant's default.\n+- Consumers can query enabled providers for their tenant via gateway endpoint.\n+- Provider plugins are discovered via types-registry and can be added without gateway code changes.\n+\n+**Capabilities**:\n+\n+- Tenant-scoped web search with per-request provider selection from tenant-enabled providers\n+- Normalized `SearchResponse` schema regardless of underlying provider\n+- Response caching with tenant isolation and configurable TTL\n+- Plugin-based provider integration via types-registry (GTS)\n+- Provider failover with circuit breaker pattern\n+- Governance: authentication, authorization, quotas, rate limiting\n+- Observability: metrics, structured logging, distributed tracing, audit events\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| **Platform Engineer** | Integrates search into AI agents and RAG systems via the Web Search Gateway |\n+| **Tenant Admin** | Configures provider selection, monitors quota usage, and manages cost controls for their tenant |\n+| **Plugin Developer** | Implements new search provider plugins using the plugin contract, and registration process |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. Primary Use Cases\n+\n+### UC1: Basic Web Search\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant is onboarded; at least one provider is enabled for tenant  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends `POST /web-search/v1/search` with query, parameters, and optional `provider_id`\n+2. Gateway authenticates request via bearer token\n+3. Gateway authorizes against tenant's search permissions\n+4. Gateway checks rate limit and quota\n+5. Gateway checks cache; if hit, returns cached response with `from_cache: true`\n+6. If cache miss:\n+   - If `provider_id` specified: verify provider is enabled for tenant; if not, return 400\n+   - If `provider_id` not specified: use tenant's configured default provider\n+7. Gateway invokes provider plugin, receives raw results\n+8. Gateway normalizes results into `SearchResponse` schema\n+9. Gateway caches response (if cacheable)\n+10. Gateway returns response with latency headers\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Response logged; metrics emitted; quota decremented\n+\n+### UC2: Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+**Actor**: Tenant Admin  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin queries available providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers` (platform-wide list)\n+2. Admin updates tenant configuration in Settings Service to:\n+   - Enable specific providers for the tenant (e.g., `[\"tavily\", \"serper\"]`)\n+   - Set a default provider (e.g., `\"tavily\"`)\n+   - Configure auto-failover behavior (enabled/disabled)\n+3. Subsequent requests from that tenant can specify any enabled provider via `provider_id`\n+4. Requests without `provider_id` use the tenant's default provider\n+\n+### UC2a: Per-Request Provider Selection\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has multiple providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service queries enabled providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers`\n+2. Service sends search request with `provider_id: \"serper\"` for a specific use case\n+3. Gateway verifies \"serper\" is enabled for the tenant\n+4. Gateway routes request to Serper plugin\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used: \"serper\"`\n+\n+### UC3: Provider Failover\n+\n+**Actor**: System (automatic)  \n+**Trigger**: Requested provider returns 5xx, 429, or times out  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has auto-failover enabled; tenant has other providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition on requested provider\n+2. Circuit breaker opens for failed provider\n+3. Gateway selects another enabled provider from tenant's list based on plugin priority\n+4. Gateway retries request with fallback provider\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used` (fallback) and `metadata.failover_from` (original)\n+6. Metrics record failover event\n+\n+**Alternative Flow** (auto-failover disabled):\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition\n+2. Gateway returns error response with Problem Details\n+3. Consumer can retry with different `provider_id` if desired\n+\n+### UC4: Quota Exhaustion\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Trigger**: Tenant quota exceeded  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Request arrives; gateway checks quota\n+2. Quota check fails; request rejected with `429 Too Many Requests`\n+3. Response includes `Retry-After` header and Problem Details body\n+4. Metrics record quota denial\n+\n+### UC5: Adding a New Provider Plugin\n+\n+**Actor**: Plugin Developer  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Plugin developer implements `WebSearchPluginClient` trait\n+2. Plugin developer registers plugin instance in types-registry with capability declaration\n+3. Gateway discovers new plugin on next startup or config reload\n+4. Tenant Admin enables new provider for specific tenants\n+5. Gateway routes matching requests to new provider\n+\n+### UC6: LLM-Enhanced Search with Answer Extraction\n+\n+**Actor**: AI Chatbot (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: LLM Gateway available; tenant has LLM features enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Chatbot sends search request with `options.extract_answer: true`\n+2. Gateway executes web search via provider\n+3. Gateway invokes LLM Gateway to extract direct answer from top results\n+4. Response includes `answer` object with concise text, source URLs, and confidence\n+5. Chatbot uses extracted answer to ground its response, reducing hallucination risk\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Answer extraction logged; LLM cost tracked\n+\n+### UC7: Query Refinement for Ambiguous Searches\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends search with `options.refine_query: true`\n+2. Gateway invokes LLM to refine query (spelling correction, expansion, intent detection)\n+3. Gateway searches with refined query\n+4. Response includes original and refined query in metadata\n+5. Improved search results returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. Scope\n+\n+### 7.1 In Scope\n+\n+| Category | Items |\n+|----------|-------|\n+| **Search modalities** | Web search (MVP); news, images, video, academic as extensions |\n+| **Provider plugins** | Plugin architecture with stable contract; initial plugins: Tavily |\n+| **Multi-tenancy** | Per-tenant provider config, quotas, rate limits, cache policies |\n+| **API** | REST API with OpenAPI documentation; gRPC MAY be added later |\n+| **Normalization** | Unified `SearchResponse` schema for all providers |\n+| **Caching** | Response caching with configurable TTL, tenant isolation |\n+| **Governance** | AuthN (bearer tokens, service-to-service), AuthZ, quotas, rate limits |\n+| **Observability** | Metrics, structured logs, distributed tracing, audit events |\n+| **Error handling** | RFC 9457 Problem Details for all error responses |\n+| **Admin operations** | Provider health status, cache invalidation, quota management |\n+| **LLM integration** | Query refinement, answer extraction, result summarization (opt-in via LLM Gateway) |\n+| **Safe search** | Configurable content filtering (off, moderate, strict) with tenant-level enforcement |\n+\n+### 7.2 Out of Scope\n+\n+| Item | Rationale |\n+|------|-----------|\n+| Web crawling / scraping | Gateway is for Search API execution, not for deep scraping or crawling |\n+| Search result storage | Gateway is stateless for results; caching is ephemeral |\n+| Billing integration | Cost metrics are emitted; billing is a separate platform concern |\n+| BYO-Key Management | Users do not supply their own API keys; keys are managed centrally by the platform  |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 8. Functional Requirements\n+\n+| ID | Priority | Category | Requirement | Rationale | Acceptance Criteria |\n+|----|----------|----------|-------------|-----------|---------------------|\n+| **FR-001** | P0 | API | Gateway MUST provide a unified `Search` endpoint accepting `SearchRequest` and returning `SearchResponse` | Single entry point for all search operations | Endpoint returns 200 with valid `SearchResponse` for valid requests |\n+| **FR-002** | P0 | Routing | Gateway MUST route requests to provider based on: (1) `provider_id` in request if specified, (2) tenant's default provider if not specified; Gateway MUST verify requested provider is enabled for tenant | Per-request provider flexibility with tenant governance | Request with valid `provider_id` routes to that provider; request with invalid/disabled provider returns 400; request without `provider_id` uses tenant default |\n+| **FR-003** | P0 | Discovery | Gateway MUST expose a provider discovery endpoint returning list of providers enabled for the requesting tenant | Consumer awareness of available providers | Endpoint returns array of provider objects with `id`, `name`, `capabilities`; list filtered to tenant's enabled providers |\n+| **FR-004** | P0 | Normalization | Gateway MUST transform all provider responses into a unified response schema | Provider-agnostic responses for consumers | All fields populated correctly regardless of provider; provider-specific data isolated |\n+| **FR-005** | P0 | AuthN | Gateway MUST authenticate all requests | Security: no anonymous access | Requests without valid auth return 401; valid tokens extract tenant and user context |\n+| **FR-006** | P0 | AuthZ | Gateway MUST authorize requests against tenant's search permissions | Enforce access control | Unauthorized requests return 403; authorized requests proceed |\n+| **FR-007** | P0 | Rate Limiting | Gateway MUST enforce per-tenant rate limits | Protect providers and ensure fair usage | Rate limit hit returns 429 with retry information |\n+| **FR-008** | P0 | Quota | Gateway MUST track and enforce per-tenant quotas (requests per period) | Cost control and fair usage | Quota exhaustion returns error; quota resets at configured cadence |\n+| **FR-009** | P0 | Errors | Gateway MUST return consistent, machine-readable error responses | Uniform error handling for consumers | All error responses follow consistent structure with error code, message, and details |\n+| **FR-010** | P0 | Failover | Gateway MUST support configurable auto-failover per tenant; when enabled and provider fails, gateway attempts another enabled provider; when disabled, gateway returns error | Tenant control over failover behavior | Auto-failover enabled: failure triggers fallback; Auto-failover disabled: failure returns error |\n+| **FR-011** | P1 | Caching | Gateway SHOULD cache responses with tenant isolation and configurable TTL | Cost reduction, latency improvement | Identical requests return cached response; cache isolated per tenant; TTL configurable |\n+| **FR-012** | P1 | Caching | Gateway SHOULD support cache bypass on request | Allow fresh results when needed | Cache bypass returns fresh provider response |\n+| **FR-013** | P1 | Observability | Gateway SHOULD emit structured logs with correlation IDs for all requests | Debugging and audit | Logs contain correlation ID, tenant ID, provider used, latency; PII redacted |\n+| **FR-014** | P1 | Observability | Gateway SHOULD support distributed tracing | End-to-end request tracing | Trace context propagated to provider calls; spans visible in tracing backend |\n+| **FR-015** | P1 | Audit | Gateway SHOULD emit audit events for: config changes, quota/rate actions, provider selection | Compliance and incident investigation | Audit events contain timestamp, actor, action, resource, outcome |\n+| **FR-016** | P1 | Admin | Gateway SHOULD expose health and cache management endpoints for operators | Operational visibility and control | Health status per provider; cache invalidation capability |\n+| **FR-017** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support news search with freshness, category, and sort parameters | Real-time information for chatbots | News search returns results with freshness filter; category filtering works |\n+| **FR-018** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support image search with size, color, type, and license filters | Content discovery use cases | Image results include thumbnails, dimensions, license info |\n+| **FR-019** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support video search with duration and quality filters | Video research use cases | Video results include duration, quality, platform info |\n+| **FR-020** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support academic/scholarly search with publication type, year range, and citation count | Research and fact-checking | Academic results include citation count, publication type, authors |\n+| **FR-021** | P1 | Safe Search | Gateway MUST enforce safe search filtering with configurable levels (off, moderate, strict) per tenant | Content safety and compliance | Safe search level enforced; platform-wide minimum level can override tenant settings |","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Priority/keyword mismatch: FR-021 uses \"MUST\" but is P1.**\n\nFR-021 states \"Gateway MUST enforce safe search filtering\" but is marked as P1 priority. Typically, \"MUST\" requirements are P0 (critical). Either downgrade to \"SHOULD\" for P1 consistency, or promote to P0 if this is truly mandatory.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md` at line 214, FR-021 in the PRD\ndeclares \"Gateway MUST enforce safe search filtering\" but is labeled P1; update\nthe requirement to ensure consistency between priority and obligation: either\nchange the normative keyword \"MUST\" to \"SHOULD\" if this is a P1 (non-critical)\nrequirement, or change the priority from P1 to P0 if enforcement is truly\nmandatory; locate and edit the FR-021 entry (Safe Search) in the PRD to apply\nthe chosen correction and ensure the acceptance criteria and any platform-wide\noverride text reflect the revised obligation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 831d9f8","created_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:30:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753005007","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005007"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753005007"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753005007/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":214,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":214,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529001","pull_request_review_id":3738425771,"id":2753529001,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kH4Sp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — PRD\n+\n+**Unified, Provider-Agnostic Search API with Plugin-Based Extensibility**\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: The Web Search Gateway is HyperSpot's centralized web search service that provides a unified API for web search operations, routing requests to configurable provider plugins while enforcing governance, normalization, and observability.\n+\n+Web search integration must be consistent across all modules without embedding provider-specific logic in each consumer. The Web Search Gateway achieves this by providing a common search API and delegating provider calls to configurable plugins via the Outbound API Gateway (OAGW).\n+\n+Phase 1 focuses on tenant-scoped web search with a single provider (Tavily), result normalization, and core governance (authN/Z, quotas, rate limits). It does not implement LLM-powered features (query refinement, answer extraction), additional search types (news, images), or advanced features (semantic caching, ML re-ranking); those are planned for Phase 2 and beyond.\n+\n+**Target Users**: Platform engineers integrating search into AI agents and RAG pipelines. Tenant admins configuring provider selection, quotas, and policies.\n+\n+**Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n+- **LLM hallucinations**: Make chatbots more accurate by providing real-time web context.\n+- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API interface abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n+- **Duplicated integration code**: A single gateway eliminates redundant provider integrations across modules.\n+- **Centralized governance**: Unified quotas, rate limits, and audit logging across all search consumers.\n+\n+**Success Criteria**:\n+\n+- All search requests resolve using tenant scope from SecurityContext; requests can specify provider or use tenant's default.\n+- Consumers can query enabled providers for their tenant via gateway endpoint.\n+- Provider plugins are discovered via types-registry and can be added without gateway code changes.\n+\n+**Capabilities**:\n+\n+- Tenant-scoped web search with per-request provider selection from tenant-enabled providers\n+- Normalized `SearchResponse` schema regardless of underlying provider\n+- Response caching with tenant isolation and configurable TTL\n+- Plugin-based provider integration via types-registry (GTS)\n+- Provider failover with circuit breaker pattern\n+- Governance: authentication, authorization, quotas, rate limiting\n+- Observability: metrics, structured logging, distributed tracing, audit events\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| **Platform Engineer** | Integrates search into AI agents and RAG systems via the Web Search Gateway |\n+| **Tenant Admin** | Configures provider selection, monitors quota usage, and manages cost controls for their tenant |\n+| **Plugin Developer** | Implements new search provider plugins using the plugin contract, and registration process |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. Primary Use Cases\n+\n+### UC1: Basic Web Search\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant is onboarded; at least one provider is enabled for tenant  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends `POST /web-search/v1/search` with query, parameters, and optional `provider_id`\n+2. Gateway authenticates request via bearer token\n+3. Gateway authorizes against tenant's search permissions\n+4. Gateway checks rate limit and quota\n+5. Gateway checks cache; if hit, returns cached response with `from_cache: true`\n+6. If cache miss:\n+   - If `provider_id` specified: verify provider is enabled for tenant; if not, return 400\n+   - If `provider_id` not specified: use tenant's configured default provider\n+7. Gateway invokes provider plugin, receives raw results\n+8. Gateway normalizes results into `SearchResponse` schema\n+9. Gateway caches response (if cacheable)\n+10. Gateway returns response with latency headers\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Response logged; metrics emitted; quota decremented\n+\n+### UC2: Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+**Actor**: Tenant Admin  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin queries available providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers` (platform-wide list)\n+2. Admin updates tenant configuration in Settings Service to:\n+   - Enable specific providers for the tenant (e.g., `[\"tavily\", \"serper\"]`)\n+   - Set a default provider (e.g., `\"tavily\"`)\n+   - Configure auto-failover behavior (enabled/disabled)\n+3. Subsequent requests from that tenant can specify any enabled provider via `provider_id`\n+4. Requests without `provider_id` use the tenant's default provider\n+\n+### UC2a: Per-Request Provider Selection\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has multiple providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service queries enabled providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers`\n+2. Service sends search request with `provider_id: \"serper\"` for a specific use case\n+3. Gateway verifies \"serper\" is enabled for the tenant\n+4. Gateway routes request to Serper plugin\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used: \"serper\"`\n+\n+### UC3: Provider Failover\n+\n+**Actor**: System (automatic)  \n+**Trigger**: Requested provider returns 5xx, 429, or times out  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has auto-failover enabled; tenant has other providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition on requested provider\n+2. Circuit breaker opens for failed provider\n+3. Gateway selects another enabled provider from tenant's list based on plugin priority\n+4. Gateway retries request with fallback provider\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used` (fallback) and `metadata.failover_from` (original)\n+6. Metrics record failover event\n+\n+**Alternative Flow** (auto-failover disabled):\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition\n+2. Gateway returns error response with Problem Details\n+3. Consumer can retry with different `provider_id` if desired\n+\n+### UC4: Quota Exhaustion\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Trigger**: Tenant quota exceeded  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Request arrives; gateway checks quota\n+2. Quota check fails; request rejected with `429 Too Many Requests`\n+3. Response includes `Retry-After` header and Problem Details body\n+4. Metrics record quota denial\n+\n+### UC5: Adding a New Provider Plugin\n+\n+**Actor**: Plugin Developer  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Plugin developer implements `WebSearchPluginClient` trait\n+2. Plugin developer registers plugin instance in types-registry with capability declaration\n+3. Gateway discovers new plugin on next startup or config reload\n+4. Tenant Admin enables new provider for specific tenants\n+5. Gateway routes matching requests to new provider\n+\n+### UC6: LLM-Enhanced Search with Answer Extraction\n+\n+**Actor**: AI Chatbot (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: LLM Gateway available; tenant has LLM features enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Chatbot sends search request with `options.extract_answer: true`\n+2. Gateway executes web search via provider\n+3. Gateway invokes LLM Gateway to extract direct answer from top results\n+4. Response includes `answer` object with concise text, source URLs, and confidence\n+5. Chatbot uses extracted answer to ground its response, reducing hallucination risk\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Answer extraction logged; LLM cost tracked\n+\n+### UC7: Query Refinement for Ambiguous Searches\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends search with `options.refine_query: true`\n+2. Gateway invokes LLM to refine query (spelling correction, expansion, intent detection)\n+3. Gateway searches with refined query\n+4. Response includes original and refined query in metadata","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"8af9588dc0a4b2752bc18bbd5b54df0d630b8b23","original_commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Call out that UC6/UC7 fields are future-facing (not in v1 schema).**\n\nUC6/UC7 use `options.extract_answer` and `options.refine_query`, but these fields are not present in `search_request.v1.json`. To avoid confusion, annotate these as Phase 2 fields or note that they require a future schema revision.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-1. Chatbot sends search request with `options.extract_answer: true`\n+1. Chatbot sends search request with `options.extract_answer: true` (Phase 2; requires schema extension)\n...\n-1. Service sends search with `options.refine_query: true`\n+1. Service sends search with `options.refine_query: true` (Phase 2; requires schema extension)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 135 - 155, Update the\nPRD to mark UC6 and UC7 fields as future/Phase-2 features: explicitly state that\noptions.extract_answer and options.refine_query are not part of the current v1\nschema (search_request.v1.json) and require a future schema revision; add a\nbrief note in the UC6/UC7 sections indicating these fields are “Phase 2 / not in\nv1” and suggest where to document the planned schema change (e.g., reference\nsearch_request.v1.json) so readers won’t assume they exist in the current API.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 831d9f8","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:03:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:30:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529001","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529001"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529001"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529001/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":135,"original_start_line":135,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":155,"original_line":155,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":155,"position":155,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529010","pull_request_review_id":3738425771,"id":2753529010,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kH4Sy","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.search_request.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"SearchRequest\",\n+  \"description\": \"Web search request parameters\",\n+  \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"required\": [\"query\"],\n+  \"properties\": {\n+    \"query\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"description\": \"Search query text\",\n+      \"minLength\": 1,\n+      \"maxLength\": 2000\n+    },\n+    \"search_type\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SearchType\"\n+    },\n+    \"provider_id\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"description\": \"Specific provider ID, or tenant default if omitted\"\n+    },\n+    \"options\": {\n+      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SearchOptions\"\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"$defs\": {\n+    \"SearchType\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"description\": \"Type of search to perform\",\n+      \"enum\": [\"web\", \"news\", \"images\", \"video\", \"academic\"],\n+      \"default\": \"web\"\n+    },\n+    \"SearchOptions\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Optional search parameters\",\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"max_results\": {\n+          \"type\": \"integer\",\n+          \"description\": \"Maximum results to return\",\n+          \"minimum\": 1,\n+          \"maximum\": 100,\n+          \"default\": 10\n+        },\n+        \"language\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"ISO 639-1 language code\",\n+          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z]{2}$\"\n+        },\n+        \"region\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 region code\",\n+          \"pattern\": \"^[A-Z]{2}$\"\n+        },\n+        \"safe_search\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SafeSearchLevel\"\n+        },\n+        \"include_domains\": {\n+          \"type\": \"array\",\n+          \"description\": \"Domains to include in results\",\n+          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        },\n+        \"exclude_domains\": {\n+          \"type\": \"array\",\n+          \"description\": \"Domains to exclude from results\",\n+          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        },\n+        \"date_range\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DateRange\"\n+        },\n+        \"bypass_cache\": {\n+          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n+          \"description\": \"Skip cache lookup\",\n+          \"default\": false\n+        }\n+      }\n+    },\n+    \"SafeSearchLevel\": {\n+      \"type\": \"string\",\n+      \"description\": \"Safe search filtering level\",\n+      \"enum\": [\"off\", \"moderate\", \"strict\"],\n+      \"default\": \"moderate\"\n+    },\n+    \"DateRange\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Custom date range filter\",\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"start\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"format\": \"date\",\n+          \"description\": \"Start date (ISO 8601)\"\n+        },\n+        \"end\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"format\": \"date\",\n+          \"description\": \"End date (ISO 8601)\"\n+        }\n+      }","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_request.v1.json","commit_id":"8af9588dc0a4b2752bc18bbd5b54df0d630b8b23","original_commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Require a non-empty date range and validate ordering in the service.**\n\n`DateRange` currently permits `{}`. Also, `start` could be after `end` without any guard. Consider requiring at least one boundary here and enforcing ordering in request validation. Line 83 currently defines an unconstrained object.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested schema tightening</summary>\n\n```diff\n     \"DateRange\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"description\": \"Custom date range filter\",\n+      \"minProperties\": 1,\n+      \"anyOf\": [\n+        { \"required\": [\"start\"] },\n+        { \"required\": [\"end\"] }\n+      ],\n       \"properties\": {\n         \"start\": {\n           \"type\": \"string\",\n           \"format\": \"date\",\n           \"description\": \"Start date (ISO 8601)\"\n         },\n         \"end\": {\n           \"type\": \"string\",\n           \"format\": \"date\",\n           \"description\": \"End date (ISO 8601)\"\n         }\n       }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_request.v1.json` around lines 83 - 97,\nThe DateRange schema currently allows an empty object and does not guard\nordering; update the DateRange definition to require at least one of \"start\" or\n\"end\" (use \"oneOf\" or \"minProperties\":1) and keep \"start\" and \"end\" as \"string\"\nwith \"format\":\"date\", and then add validation in the search request validation\nlogic (the service-level request validator that consumes DateRange) to reject or\nnormalize requests where both bounds are present but start > end (compare parsed\nISO dates) returning a 400 error or normalized swap per API policy; reference\nthe DateRange schema and its \"start\"/\"end\" properties and the request validator\nthat validates incoming search requests.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:03:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:03:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529010","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529010"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529010"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":83,"original_start_line":83,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":98,"original_line":97,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":97,"position":98,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529016","pull_request_review_id":3738425771,"id":2753529016,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kH4S4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.tenant_config.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"TenantWebSearchConfig\",","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/settings.v1.json","commit_id":"8af9588dc0a4b2752bc18bbd5b54df0d630b8b23","original_commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Align the schema `$id` with the module naming convention.**\n\nThe `$id` uses `tenant_config` while other schemas (and the design doc table) use the `settings` naming. This inconsistency can break schema registry lookups or code generation. Line 3 should align with `gts.x.web_search.settings.v1`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.tenant_config.v1\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.settings.v1\",\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.settings.v1\",\n  \"title\": \"TenantWebSearchConfig\",\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/gts/settings.v1.json` around lines 2 - 4, Update\nthe JSON schema $id to follow the module naming convention by replacing\n\"gts.x.web_search.tenant_config.v1\" with \"gts.x.web_search.settings.v1\" in the\nschema for TenantWebSearchConfig; locate the $id field in\nmodules/web_search_gateway/gts/settings.v1.json (the schema with \"title\":\n\"TenantWebSearchConfig\") and change the identifier so registry lookups and\ncodegen use the consistent settings namespace.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 831d9f8","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:03:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:30:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529016","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529016"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753529016"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753529016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":2,"original_start_line":2,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":4,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753555206","pull_request_review_id":3738458859,"id":2753555206,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kH-sG","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,674 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — Design Document\n+\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+### 1.1 Purpose\n+\n+The Web Search Gateway is a **Gateway Module** providing a unified, provider-agnostic web search API for HyperSpot. It routes search requests to configurable **Plugin Modules** (provider implementations) while enforcing governance, result normalization, caching, and observability.\n+\n+### 1.2 Module Classification\n+\n+Per [Architecture Manifest](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md):\n+\n+| Attribute | Value |\n+|-----------|-------|\n+| **Module Type** | Gateway Module |\n+| **API Layer** | Yes (REST) |\n+| **Business Logic Layer** | Yes (contract, router, normalization) |\n+| **Infrastructure Layer** | Yes (cache, OAGW client) |\n+| **Gateway Layer** | Yes (plugin connectors) |\n+\n+### 1.3 Key Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | ADR | Summary |\n+|----------|-----|---------|\n+| Stateless Gateway | [ADR-001](./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md) | Gateway holds no state; quota/billing delegated to external service |\n+| Stateless Credential Management | [ADR-002](./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md) | Credentials injected via OAGW; gateway never handles raw secrets |\n+| Settings Service for Tenant Config | [ADR-003](./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md) | Per-tenant provider configuration via Settings Service |\n+| Tenant-Scoped Caching | [ADR-004](./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md) | Cache isolation per tenant prevents data leakage |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Architecture\n+\n+### 2.1 High-Level Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                         CONSUMER MODULES                                │\n+│              (AI Chatbots, RAG Systems, Platform Services)              │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    │ hub.get::<dyn WebSearchGatewayApi>()\n+                                    │ or REST: POST /web-search/v1/search\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      WEB SEARCH GATEWAY MODULE                          │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  REST API Layer: /web-search/v1/search, /providers, /health       │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  Domain Layer: SearchService, ProviderRouter, CacheService,       │  │\n+│  │                GovernanceService, CircuitBreaker, Normalizer      │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│                                    │                                    │\n+│                                    │ hub.get_scoped::<dyn WebSearchPluginClient>\n+│                                    ▼                                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+          │                          │                          │\n+          ▼                          ▼                          ▼\n+┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐\n+│  TAVILY PLUGIN  │       │  SERPER PLUGIN  │       │ (FUTURE PLUGIN) │\n+│  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │\n+│  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│\n+│  Client         │       │  Client         │       │  Client         │\n+└────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘\n+         │                         │                         │\n+         └─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘\n+                                   │ HTTPS via OAGW\n+                                   ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│              OUTBOUND API GATEWAY (OAGW) - Credential injection         │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### 2.2 Module Dependencies & Integrations\n+\n+| Dependency | Purpose | Criticality |\n+|------------|---------|-------------|\n+| **Identity & Authorization** | Authentication and authorization of search requests | P0 |\n+| **Outbound API Gateway (OAGW)** | Secure storage and management of provider API credentials | P0 |\n+| **types-registry** | Plugin discovery, capability schemas | P0 |\n+| **Settings Service** | Tenant configuration | P0 |\n+| **Cache backend** | Response caching (Redis or in-memory) | P0 |\n+| **Billing Service** | Quota tracking and usage metering | P0 |\n+| **LLM Gateway** | Query refinement, answer extraction, summarization | P1 |\n+| **Observability stack** | Metrics, logs, traces | P1 |\n+| **Event Manager** | Audit event publishing and observability | P1 |\n+\n+\n+> **Notes**:\n+> - Plugins (e.g., `tavily_plugin`, `serper_plugin`) are **not** listed as dependencies. They are discovered dynamically at runtime via GTS `types-registry`. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md).\n+> - **Billing Service** handles quota tracking and usage metering. Gateway is stateless and delegates quota checks/updates to this service.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Crate Structure\n+\n+### 3.1 Directory Layout\n+\n+```\n+modules/web_search_gateway/\n+├── docs/                            # Documentation\n+├── gts/                             # GTS JSON Schemas (see section 4.3)\n+├── web_search_gateway-sdk/          # SDK crate (public API, plugin API)\n+├── web_search_gateway-gw/           # Gateway implementation\n+│   └── src/\n+│       ├── api/rest/                # REST handlers, DTOs\n+│       ├── domain/                  # SearchService, ProviderRouter, Normalizer\n+│       └── infra/                   # Cache backends, adapters\n+└── plugins/\n+    ├── tavily_plugin/               # Tavily provider (Phase 1)\n+    └── serper_plugin/               # Serper provider (Phase 2)\n+```\n+\n+Follows standard ModKit module layout. See [NEW_MODULE.md](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. SDK Design\n+\n+### 4.1 Public API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchGatewayApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute a web search request\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: SearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<SearchResponse, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// List providers enabled for the requesting tenant\n+    async fn list_providers(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<ProviderInfo>, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Get health status for a specific provider\n+    async fn get_provider_health(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        provider_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<ProviderHealthStatus, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Invalidate cache entries (requires admin permissions)\n+    async fn invalidate_cache(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        pattern: Option<&str>,\n+    ) -> Result<u64, WebSearchError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.2 Plugin API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchPluginClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute search against the provider\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: PluginSearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<PluginSearchResponse, PluginError>;\n+\n+    /// Return plugin's declared capabilities\n+    fn capabilities(&self) -> &PluginCapabilities;\n+\n+    /// Health check for the provider\n+    async fn health_check(&self, ctx: &SecurityCtx) -> Result<HealthStatus, PluginError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.3 Core Models (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Core domain types are defined as GTS JSON Schemas for language-agnostic contracts. Rust SDK types are generated from these schemas.\n+\n+| Schema File | Types | GTS ID |\n+|-------------|-------|--------|\n+| [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json) | `SearchRequest`, `SearchOptions`, `SearchType`, `SafeSearchLevel`, `Freshness`, `DateRange` | `gts.x.web_search.search_request.v1` |\n+| [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json) | `SearchResponse`, `SearchResult`, `ResponseMetadata`, `ContentType`, `AdditionalLink` | `gts.x.web_search.search_response.v1` |\n+| [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json) | `ProviderInfo`, `PluginCapabilities`, `SupportedFilters`, `HealthStatus` | `gts.x.web_search.provider.v1` |\n+| [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) | `TenantWebSearchConfig`, `TenantProviderConfig`, `RateLimitOverride`, `QuotaOverride` | `gts.x.web_search.settings.v1` |\n+\n+### 4.4 Error Codes (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Error codes follow RFC 9457 Problem Details. See [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json).\n+\n+| GTS Code | HTTP | Title |\n+|----------|------|-------|\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_found.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Found |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_enabled.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Enabled |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.capability_not_supported.v1` | 400 | Capability Not Supported |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.validation.v1` | 400 | Validation Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.no_providers_configured.v1` | 400 | No Providers Configured |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.unauthorized.v1` | 401 | Unauthorized |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.forbidden.v1` | 403 | Forbidden |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.rate_limited.v1` | 429 | Rate Limit Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.quota_exceeded.v1` | 429 | Quota Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.internal.v1` | 500 | Internal Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_error.v1` | 502 | Provider Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.providers_unavailable.v1` | 503 | All Providers Unavailable |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.timeout.v1` | 504 | Request Timeout |\n+\n+### 4.5 GTS Plugin Schema\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/gts.rs\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema(\n+    dir_path = \"schemas\",\n+    base = BaseModkitPluginV1,\n+    schema_id = \"gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~\",\n+    description = \"Web Search Gateway provider plugin specification\",\n+    properties = \"\"\n+)]\n+pub struct WebSearchPluginSpecV1;\n+```\n+\n+**GTS Instance ID Pattern**:\n+- Schema: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~`\n+- Instance: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~tavily.web_search.plugin.v1`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Gateway Implementation\n+\n+### 5.1 Module Pattern\n+\n+Web Search Gateway follows the standard Gateway + Plugin pattern. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md) for:\n+- Module declaration with `#[modkit::module]`\n+- Plugin schema registration\n+- Plugin discovery via `types-registry`\n+- Scoped client resolution via `ClientHub`\n+\n+### 5.2 Configuration\n+\n+| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n+|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n+| `default_provider` | string | `\"tavily\"` | Default provider when none specified |\n+| `request_timeout_ms` | u64 | 30000 | Overall request timeout |\n+| `cache.enabled` | bool | true | Enable response caching |\n+| `cache.default_ttl_seconds` | u64 | 3600 | Default cache TTL |\n+| `cache.max_size_mb` | u64 | 1024 | Max cache size |\n+| `rate_limit.*` |  | 100 | Default requests/second |\n+| `quota.default_monthly` |  | 10000 | Default monthly request quota |\n+| `circuit_breaker.failure_threshold` | u32 | 5 | Failures before opening circuit |\n+| `circuit_breaker.reset_timeout_seconds` | u64 | 60 | Half-open retry interval |\n+| `failover.enabled` | bool | true | Enable automatic failover |\n+\n+> **Note**: \n+> - **Rate limits**: Enforced via Redis (stateless). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - **Quotas**: Managed by Billing Service (persistent). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - See [Section 9](#9-governance) for details.\n+\n+### 5.3 Search Service Flow\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Client\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant Plugin\n+    participant Normalizer\n+\n+    Client->>SearchService: search(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService: 1. Validate request\n+    SearchService->>SearchService: validate_request()\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Redis: 2. Check rate limit (Redis)\n+    SearchService->>Redis: check_rate_limit(tenant_id)\n+    Redis-->>SearchService: OK / RateLimitExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 3. Check quota (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: check_quota(ctx)\n+    BillingService-->>SearchService: OK / QuotaExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 4. Check cache (unless bypass)\n+    alt bypass_cache = false\n+        SearchService->>Cache: get(ctx, request)\n+        Cache-->>SearchService: cached_response / miss\n+        alt cache hit\n+            SearchService-->>Client: cached_response\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,ProviderRouter: 5. Select provider\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Plugin: 6. Execute with failover\n+    SearchService->>Plugin: search(ctx, plugin_request)\n+    Plugin-->>SearchService: provider_response / error\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Normalizer: 7. Normalize response\n+    SearchService->>Normalizer: normalize(response, provider_id)\n+    Normalizer-->>SearchService: normalized_response\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 8. Cache result\n+    SearchService->>Cache: store(ctx, request, response)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 9. Record usage (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: record_usage(ctx, 1)\n+    \n+    SearchService-->>Client: normalized_response\n+```\n+\n+### 5.4 Provider Router\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant SettingsService\n+    participant TypesRegistry\n+    participant CircuitBreaker\n+    participant ClientHub\n+\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    alt provider_id specified in request\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use specific provider\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: is_provider_enabled(ctx, provider_id)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: enabled / not_enabled\n+        alt not enabled\n+            ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: ProviderNotEnabled error\n+        end\n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider_id)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+    else no provider_id specified\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use tenant default\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: get_settings(ctx)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+        ProviderRouter->>ProviderRouter: default_provider from config\n+        \n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(default_provider)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+        \n+        alt default unhealthy or capability mismatch\n+            Note over ProviderRouter: Find fallback\n+            loop enabled_providers by priority\n+                ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider)\n+                ProviderRouter->>TypesRegistry: supports_search_type(provider, type)\n+                alt healthy and capable\n+                    break\n+                end\n+            end\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over ProviderRouter,ClientHub: Resolve plugin client\n+    ProviderRouter->>ClientHub: get_scoped(gts_instance_id)\n+    ClientHub-->>ProviderRouter: plugin_client\n+    \n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin_client)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. REST API Design\n+\n+### 6.1 Endpoints\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| POST | `/web-search/v1/search` | Execute search | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers` | List enabled providers | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers/{id}/health` | Provider health | Required |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/cache` | Invalidate cache | Admin |\n+| GET | `/health/live` | Liveness check | Public |\n+| GET | `/health/ready` | Readiness check | Public |\n+\n+### 6.2 Request/Response Schemas\n+\n+REST DTOs are generated from GTS schemas (see section 4.3):\n+- **Request**: [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json)\n+- **Response**: [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json)\n+- **Providers**: [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json)\n+- **Errors**: [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json) (RFC 9457 Problem Details)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. Caching Strategy\n+\n+### 7.1 Cache Key Structure\n+\n+```\n+ws:{tenant_id}:{search_type}:{provider_id}:{sha256(query+options_hash)}\n+```\n+\n+Components:\n+- `tenant_id`: Ensures tenant isolation\n+- `search_type`: web, news, images, etc.\n+- `provider_id`: Different providers may return different results\n+- `sha256(...)`: Hash of normalized query + sorted options\n+\n+### 7.2 TTL Policy\n+\n+TTLs vary by search type (news: shorter, images/video: longer). See [Configuration Example](#12-configuration-example).\n+\n+### 7.3 Cache Bypass\n+\n+- Request header: `Cache-Control: no-cache` or `X-WSG-Cache: bypass`\n+- Request option: `options.bypass_cache: true`\n+- Admin endpoint: `DELETE /web-search/v1/cache?pattern=...`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 8. Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+### 8.1 Overview\n+\n+Tenants configure which providers are enabled via the **Settings Service**. The Web Search Gateway reads tenant-specific provider settings at runtime to determine:\n+- Which providers are enabled for the tenant\n+- The tenant's default provider\n+- Per-provider overrides (e.g., custom rate limits, priority)\n+\n+### 8.2 Configuration Model\n+\n+See [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) for the schema.\n+\n+### 8.3 Configuration Storage\n+\n+Tenant provider configuration is stored via the **Settings Service**:\n+\n+```\n+Key:   tenant:{tenant_id}:web_search.providers\n+Value: TenantWebSearchConfig (JSON)\n+```\n+\n+### 8.4 Admin REST API for Provider Management\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Get tenant provider config | Admin |\n+| PUT | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Replace provider config | Admin |\n+| PATCH | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Update single provider | Admin |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Disable provider for tenant | Admin |\n+\n+Admin request/response schemas use [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) and [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json).\n+\n+### 8.5 Sequence Diagrams\n+\n+#### 8.5.1 Execute Search\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Plugin\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Gateway->>Redis: check_rate_limit()\n+    Redis-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: check_quota()\n+    BillingService-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>Cache: get(key)\n+    Cache-->>Gateway: MISS\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get_enabled_providers()\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Plugin: search(request)\n+    Plugin-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize(response)\n+    Gateway->>Cache: store(key, response)\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: record_usage(1)\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (results)\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.2 Execute Search with Failover\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant CB as CircuitBreaker\n+    participant PluginA as Plugin-A (Tavily)\n+    participant PluginB as Plugin-B (Serper)\n+    participant OAGW\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Note over Gateway: governance, cache checks pass\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginA: search()\n+    PluginA->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginA: timeout\n+    PluginA-->>Gateway: ERROR\n+    Gateway->>CB: record_failure(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: threshold reached → OPEN\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"serper\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginB: search()\n+    PluginB->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginB: OK\n+    PluginB-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize, cache, quota\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (metadata.failover_from: \"tavily\")\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.3 List Enabled Providers\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Registry as TypesRegistry\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: GET /providers\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get(\"web_search.providers\")\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Registry: query(WebSearchPluginSpec)\n+    Registry-->>Gateway: [all registered plugins]\n+    Note over Gateway: filter, enrich health, sort by priority\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK [providers]\n+```\n+\n+### 9.7 Default Behavior\n+\n+| Scenario | Behavior |\n+|----------|----------|\n+| No tenant config exists | Use gateway default config (Tavily enabled) |\n+| Requested provider not enabled | Return `WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED` error |\n+| No enabled providers | Return `WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED` error |\n+| Default provider unhealthy | Failover to next enabled provider by priority |\n+","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"akshatjhalani","id":6149183,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNDkxODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6149183?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani","html_url":"https://github.com/akshatjhalani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akshatjhalani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:10:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:10:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753555206","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753555206"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753555206"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753555206/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":529,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":537,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2753004995,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":537,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753557753","pull_request_review_id":3738461827,"id":2753557753,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kH_T5","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,674 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — Design Document\n+\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+### 1.1 Purpose\n+\n+The Web Search Gateway is a **Gateway Module** providing a unified, provider-agnostic web search API for HyperSpot. It routes search requests to configurable **Plugin Modules** (provider implementations) while enforcing governance, result normalization, caching, and observability.\n+\n+### 1.2 Module Classification\n+\n+Per [Architecture Manifest](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md):\n+\n+| Attribute | Value |\n+|-----------|-------|\n+| **Module Type** | Gateway Module |\n+| **API Layer** | Yes (REST) |\n+| **Business Logic Layer** | Yes (contract, router, normalization) |\n+| **Infrastructure Layer** | Yes (cache, OAGW client) |\n+| **Gateway Layer** | Yes (plugin connectors) |\n+\n+### 1.3 Key Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | ADR | Summary |\n+|----------|-----|---------|\n+| Stateless Gateway | [ADR-001](./ADR-001-Stateless-Gateway.md) | Gateway holds no state; quota/billing delegated to external service |\n+| Stateless Credential Management | [ADR-002](./ADR-002-Credential-Management.md) | Credentials injected via OAGW; gateway never handles raw secrets |\n+| Settings Service for Tenant Config | [ADR-003](./ADR-003-Settings-Service.md) | Per-tenant provider configuration via Settings Service |\n+| Tenant-Scoped Caching | [ADR-004](./ADR-004-Tenant-Scoped-Caching.md) | Cache isolation per tenant prevents data leakage |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Architecture\n+\n+### 2.1 High-Level Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                         CONSUMER MODULES                                │\n+│              (AI Chatbots, RAG Systems, Platform Services)              │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    │ hub.get::<dyn WebSearchGatewayApi>()\n+                                    │ or REST: POST /web-search/v1/search\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      WEB SEARCH GATEWAY MODULE                          │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  REST API Layer: /web-search/v1/search, /providers, /health       │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n+│  │  Domain Layer: SearchService, ProviderRouter, CacheService,       │  │\n+│  │                GovernanceService, CircuitBreaker, Normalizer      │  │\n+│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n+│                                    │                                    │\n+│                                    │ hub.get_scoped::<dyn WebSearchPluginClient>\n+│                                    ▼                                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+          │                          │                          │\n+          ▼                          ▼                          ▼\n+┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐\n+│  TAVILY PLUGIN  │       │  SERPER PLUGIN  │       │ (FUTURE PLUGIN) │\n+│  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │       │  Implements:    │\n+│  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│       │  WebSearchPlugin│\n+│  Client         │       │  Client         │       │  Client         │\n+└────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘       └────────┬────────┘\n+         │                         │                         │\n+         └─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┘\n+                                   │ HTTPS via OAGW\n+                                   ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│              OUTBOUND API GATEWAY (OAGW) - Credential injection         │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### 2.2 Module Dependencies & Integrations\n+\n+| Dependency | Purpose | Criticality |\n+|------------|---------|-------------|\n+| **Identity & Authorization** | Authentication and authorization of search requests | P0 |\n+| **Outbound API Gateway (OAGW)** | Secure storage and management of provider API credentials | P0 |\n+| **types-registry** | Plugin discovery, capability schemas | P0 |\n+| **Settings Service** | Tenant configuration | P0 |\n+| **Cache backend** | Response caching (Redis or in-memory) | P0 |\n+| **Billing Service** | Quota tracking and usage metering | P0 |\n+| **LLM Gateway** | Query refinement, answer extraction, summarization | P1 |\n+| **Observability stack** | Metrics, logs, traces | P1 |\n+| **Event Manager** | Audit event publishing and observability | P1 |\n+\n+\n+> **Notes**:\n+> - Plugins (e.g., `tavily_plugin`, `serper_plugin`) are **not** listed as dependencies. They are discovered dynamically at runtime via GTS `types-registry`. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md).\n+> - **Billing Service** handles quota tracking and usage metering. Gateway is stateless and delegates quota checks/updates to this service.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Crate Structure\n+\n+### 3.1 Directory Layout\n+\n+```\n+modules/web_search_gateway/\n+├── docs/                            # Documentation\n+├── gts/                             # GTS JSON Schemas (see section 4.3)\n+├── web_search_gateway-sdk/          # SDK crate (public API, plugin API)\n+├── web_search_gateway-gw/           # Gateway implementation\n+│   └── src/\n+│       ├── api/rest/                # REST handlers, DTOs\n+│       ├── domain/                  # SearchService, ProviderRouter, Normalizer\n+│       └── infra/                   # Cache backends, adapters\n+└── plugins/\n+    ├── tavily_plugin/               # Tavily provider (Phase 1)\n+    └── serper_plugin/               # Serper provider (Phase 2)\n+```\n+\n+Follows standard ModKit module layout. See [NEW_MODULE.md](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. SDK Design\n+\n+### 4.1 Public API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchGatewayApi: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute a web search request\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: SearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<SearchResponse, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// List providers enabled for the requesting tenant\n+    async fn list_providers(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<ProviderInfo>, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Get health status for a specific provider\n+    async fn get_provider_health(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        provider_id: &str,\n+    ) -> Result<ProviderHealthStatus, WebSearchError>;\n+\n+    /// Invalidate cache entries (requires admin permissions)\n+    async fn invalidate_cache(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        pattern: Option<&str>,\n+    ) -> Result<u64, WebSearchError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.2 Plugin API Trait\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait WebSearchPluginClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Execute search against the provider\n+    async fn search(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityCtx,\n+        request: PluginSearchRequest,\n+    ) -> Result<PluginSearchResponse, PluginError>;\n+\n+    /// Return plugin's declared capabilities\n+    fn capabilities(&self) -> &PluginCapabilities;\n+\n+    /// Health check for the provider\n+    async fn health_check(&self, ctx: &SecurityCtx) -> Result<HealthStatus, PluginError>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### 4.3 Core Models (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Core domain types are defined as GTS JSON Schemas for language-agnostic contracts. Rust SDK types are generated from these schemas.\n+\n+| Schema File | Types | GTS ID |\n+|-------------|-------|--------|\n+| [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json) | `SearchRequest`, `SearchOptions`, `SearchType`, `SafeSearchLevel`, `Freshness`, `DateRange` | `gts.x.web_search.search_request.v1` |\n+| [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json) | `SearchResponse`, `SearchResult`, `ResponseMetadata`, `ContentType`, `AdditionalLink` | `gts.x.web_search.search_response.v1` |\n+| [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json) | `ProviderInfo`, `PluginCapabilities`, `SupportedFilters`, `HealthStatus` | `gts.x.web_search.provider.v1` |\n+| [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) | `TenantWebSearchConfig`, `TenantProviderConfig`, `RateLimitOverride`, `QuotaOverride` | `gts.x.web_search.settings.v1` |\n+\n+### 4.4 Error Codes (GTS JSON Schema)\n+\n+Error codes follow RFC 9457 Problem Details. See [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json).\n+\n+| GTS Code | HTTP | Title |\n+|----------|------|-------|\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_found.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Found |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_not_enabled.v1` | 400 | Provider Not Enabled |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.capability_not_supported.v1` | 400 | Capability Not Supported |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.validation.v1` | 400 | Validation Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.no_providers_configured.v1` | 400 | No Providers Configured |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.unauthorized.v1` | 401 | Unauthorized |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.forbidden.v1` | 403 | Forbidden |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.rate_limited.v1` | 429 | Rate Limit Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.quota_exceeded.v1` | 429 | Quota Exceeded |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.internal.v1` | 500 | Internal Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.provider_error.v1` | 502 | Provider Error |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.providers_unavailable.v1` | 503 | All Providers Unavailable |\n+| `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.web_search.timeout.v1` | 504 | Request Timeout |\n+\n+### 4.5 GTS Plugin Schema\n+\n+```rust\n+// web_search_gateway-sdk/src/gts.rs\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema(\n+    dir_path = \"schemas\",\n+    base = BaseModkitPluginV1,\n+    schema_id = \"gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~\",\n+    description = \"Web Search Gateway provider plugin specification\",\n+    properties = \"\"\n+)]\n+pub struct WebSearchPluginSpecV1;\n+```\n+\n+**GTS Instance ID Pattern**:\n+- Schema: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~`\n+- Instance: `gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~x.web_search.web_search.plugin.v1~tavily.web_search.plugin.v1`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Gateway Implementation\n+\n+### 5.1 Module Pattern\n+\n+Web Search Gateway follows the standard Gateway + Plugin pattern. See [MODKIT_PLUGINS.md](../../../docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md) for:\n+- Module declaration with `#[modkit::module]`\n+- Plugin schema registration\n+- Plugin discovery via `types-registry`\n+- Scoped client resolution via `ClientHub`\n+\n+### 5.2 Configuration\n+\n+| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\n+|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n+| `default_provider` | string | `\"tavily\"` | Default provider when none specified |\n+| `request_timeout_ms` | u64 | 30000 | Overall request timeout |\n+| `cache.enabled` | bool | true | Enable response caching |\n+| `cache.default_ttl_seconds` | u64 | 3600 | Default cache TTL |\n+| `cache.max_size_mb` | u64 | 1024 | Max cache size |\n+| `rate_limit.*` |  | 100 | Default requests/second |\n+| `quota.default_monthly` |  | 10000 | Default monthly request quota |\n+| `circuit_breaker.failure_threshold` | u32 | 5 | Failures before opening circuit |\n+| `circuit_breaker.reset_timeout_seconds` | u64 | 60 | Half-open retry interval |\n+| `failover.enabled` | bool | true | Enable automatic failover |\n+\n+> **Note**: \n+> - **Rate limits**: Enforced via Redis (stateless). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - **Quotas**: Managed by Billing Service (persistent). Per-tenant overrides via Settings Service.\n+> - See [Section 9](#9-governance) for details.\n+\n+### 5.3 Search Service Flow\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Client\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant Plugin\n+    participant Normalizer\n+\n+    Client->>SearchService: search(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService: 1. Validate request\n+    SearchService->>SearchService: validate_request()\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Redis: 2. Check rate limit (Redis)\n+    SearchService->>Redis: check_rate_limit(tenant_id)\n+    Redis-->>SearchService: OK / RateLimitExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 3. Check quota (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: check_quota(ctx)\n+    BillingService-->>SearchService: OK / QuotaExceeded\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 4. Check cache (unless bypass)\n+    alt bypass_cache = false\n+        SearchService->>Cache: get(ctx, request)\n+        Cache-->>SearchService: cached_response / miss\n+        alt cache hit\n+            SearchService-->>Client: cached_response\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,ProviderRouter: 5. Select provider\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Plugin: 6. Execute with failover\n+    SearchService->>Plugin: search(ctx, plugin_request)\n+    Plugin-->>SearchService: provider_response / error\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Normalizer: 7. Normalize response\n+    SearchService->>Normalizer: normalize(response, provider_id)\n+    Normalizer-->>SearchService: normalized_response\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,Cache: 8. Cache result\n+    SearchService->>Cache: store(ctx, request, response)\n+    \n+    Note over SearchService,BillingService: 9. Record usage (Billing Service)\n+    SearchService->>BillingService: record_usage(ctx, 1)\n+    \n+    SearchService-->>Client: normalized_response\n+```\n+\n+### 5.4 Provider Router\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant SearchService\n+    participant ProviderRouter\n+    participant SettingsService\n+    participant TypesRegistry\n+    participant CircuitBreaker\n+    participant ClientHub\n+\n+    SearchService->>ProviderRouter: select_provider(ctx, request)\n+    \n+    alt provider_id specified in request\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use specific provider\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: is_provider_enabled(ctx, provider_id)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: enabled / not_enabled\n+        alt not enabled\n+            ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: ProviderNotEnabled error\n+        end\n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider_id)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+    else no provider_id specified\n+        Note over ProviderRouter: Use tenant default\n+        ProviderRouter->>SettingsService: get_settings(ctx)\n+        SettingsService-->>ProviderRouter: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+        ProviderRouter->>ProviderRouter: default_provider from config\n+        \n+        ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(default_provider)\n+        CircuitBreaker-->>ProviderRouter: healthy / unhealthy\n+        \n+        alt default unhealthy or capability mismatch\n+            Note over ProviderRouter: Find fallback\n+            loop enabled_providers by priority\n+                ProviderRouter->>CircuitBreaker: is_healthy(provider)\n+                ProviderRouter->>TypesRegistry: supports_search_type(provider, type)\n+                alt healthy and capable\n+                    break\n+                end\n+            end\n+        end\n+    end\n+    \n+    Note over ProviderRouter,ClientHub: Resolve plugin client\n+    ProviderRouter->>ClientHub: get_scoped(gts_instance_id)\n+    ClientHub-->>ProviderRouter: plugin_client\n+    \n+    ProviderRouter-->>SearchService: (provider_id, plugin_client)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. REST API Design\n+\n+### 6.1 Endpoints\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| POST | `/web-search/v1/search` | Execute search | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers` | List enabled providers | Required |\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/providers/{id}/health` | Provider health | Required |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/cache` | Invalidate cache | Admin |\n+| GET | `/health/live` | Liveness check | Public |\n+| GET | `/health/ready` | Readiness check | Public |\n+\n+### 6.2 Request/Response Schemas\n+\n+REST DTOs are generated from GTS schemas (see section 4.3):\n+- **Request**: [`search_request.v1.json`](../gts/search_request.v1.json)\n+- **Response**: [`search_response.v1.json`](../gts/search_response.v1.json)\n+- **Providers**: [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json)\n+- **Errors**: [`errors.v1.json`](../gts/errors.v1.json) (RFC 9457 Problem Details)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. Caching Strategy\n+\n+### 7.1 Cache Key Structure\n+\n+```\n+ws:{tenant_id}:{search_type}:{provider_id}:{sha256(query+options_hash)}\n+```\n+\n+Components:\n+- `tenant_id`: Ensures tenant isolation\n+- `search_type`: web, news, images, etc.\n+- `provider_id`: Different providers may return different results\n+- `sha256(...)`: Hash of normalized query + sorted options\n+\n+### 7.2 TTL Policy\n+\n+TTLs vary by search type (news: shorter, images/video: longer). See [Configuration Example](#12-configuration-example).\n+\n+### 7.3 Cache Bypass\n+\n+- Request header: `Cache-Control: no-cache` or `X-WSG-Cache: bypass`\n+- Request option: `options.bypass_cache: true`\n+- Admin endpoint: `DELETE /web-search/v1/cache?pattern=...`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 8. Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+### 8.1 Overview\n+\n+Tenants configure which providers are enabled via the **Settings Service**. The Web Search Gateway reads tenant-specific provider settings at runtime to determine:\n+- Which providers are enabled for the tenant\n+- The tenant's default provider\n+- Per-provider overrides (e.g., custom rate limits, priority)\n+\n+### 8.2 Configuration Model\n+\n+See [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) for the schema.\n+\n+### 8.3 Configuration Storage\n+\n+Tenant provider configuration is stored via the **Settings Service**:\n+\n+```\n+Key:   tenant:{tenant_id}:web_search.providers\n+Value: TenantWebSearchConfig (JSON)\n+```\n+\n+### 8.4 Admin REST API for Provider Management\n+\n+| Method | Path | Description | Auth |\n+|--------|------|-------------|------|\n+| GET | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Get tenant provider config | Admin |\n+| PUT | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers` | Replace provider config | Admin |\n+| PATCH | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Update single provider | Admin |\n+| DELETE | `/web-search/v1/admin/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider_id}` | Disable provider for tenant | Admin |\n+\n+Admin request/response schemas use [`settings.v1.json`](../gts/settings.v1.json) and [`provider.v1.json`](../gts/provider.v1.json).\n+\n+### 8.5 Sequence Diagrams\n+\n+#### 8.5.1 Execute Search\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Redis\n+    participant BillingService\n+    participant Cache\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Plugin\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Gateway->>Redis: check_rate_limit()\n+    Redis-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: check_quota()\n+    BillingService-->>Gateway: OK\n+    Gateway->>Cache: get(key)\n+    Cache-->>Gateway: MISS\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get_enabled_providers()\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Plugin: search(request)\n+    Plugin-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize(response)\n+    Gateway->>Cache: store(key, response)\n+    Gateway->>BillingService: record_usage(1)\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (results)\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.2 Execute Search with Failover\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant CB as CircuitBreaker\n+    participant PluginA as Plugin-A (Tavily)\n+    participant PluginB as Plugin-B (Serper)\n+    participant OAGW\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: POST /search\n+    Note over Gateway: governance, cache checks pass\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginA: search()\n+    PluginA->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginA: timeout\n+    PluginA-->>Gateway: ERROR\n+    Gateway->>CB: record_failure(\"tavily\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: threshold reached → OPEN\n+    Gateway->>CB: is_healthy(\"serper\")\n+    CB-->>Gateway: CLOSED (healthy)\n+    Gateway->>PluginB: search()\n+    PluginB->>OAGW: call_api()\n+    OAGW-->>PluginB: OK\n+    PluginB-->>Gateway: ProviderResponse\n+    Note over Gateway: normalize, cache, quota\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK (metadata.failover_from: \"tavily\")\n+```\n+\n+#### 8.5.3 List Enabled Providers\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant Consumer\n+    participant Gateway\n+    participant Settings as SettingsService\n+    participant Registry as TypesRegistry\n+\n+    Consumer->>Gateway: GET /providers\n+    Gateway->>Settings: get(\"web_search.providers\")\n+    Settings-->>Gateway: TenantWebSearchConfig\n+    Gateway->>Registry: query(WebSearchPluginSpec)\n+    Registry-->>Gateway: [all registered plugins]\n+    Note over Gateway: filter, enrich health, sort by priority\n+    Gateway-->>Consumer: 200 OK [providers]\n+```\n+\n+### 9.7 Default Behavior\n+\n+| Scenario | Behavior |\n+|----------|----------|\n+| No tenant config exists | Use gateway default config (Tavily enabled) |\n+| Requested provider not enabled | Return `WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED` error |\n+| No enabled providers | Return `WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED` error |\n+| Default provider unhealthy | Failover to next enabled provider by priority |\n+","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md","commit_id":"67a4dc9e09da42ddeb93bb7b9cd00548ae79f16b","original_commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@akshatjhalani`, thank you for fixing the section numbering! 🎉\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.753Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.844Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: hyphen-2025\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 385\nFile: modules/system/license_enforcer/docs/DESIGN.md:156-170\nTimestamp: 2026-01-30T18:21:25.258Z\nLearning: In the hypernetix/hyperspot repository, design documents (DESIGN.md, ADRs) are intentionally conceptual and may show semantic types (e.g., HashSet) rather than exact type aliases (e.g., EnabledGlobalFeatures) used in implementation. Minor discrepancies between design doc signatures and SDK implementation are acceptable when they improve clarity of intent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=Rename%2Fmove%20%229.7%20Default%20Behavior%22%20%E2%86%92%20%228.6%20Default%20Behavior%22%20into%20config.%20Clarifies%20tenant%20defaults%20(Tavily%20enabled)%2C%20errors%20(WSG_PROVIDER_NOT_ENABLED%2C%20WSG_NO_PROVIDERS_CONFIGURED)%20%2B%20priority%20failover.%20Try%20%40coderabbitai%20%E2%9A%99%EF%B8%8F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhypernetix%2Fhyperspot%2Fpull%2F402%23discussion_r2753004995)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:10:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:10:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753557753","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753557753"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753557753"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753557753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":529,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":537,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2753004995,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":537,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667797","pull_request_review_id":3738598724,"id":2753667797,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kIaLV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@\n+# Web Search Gateway — PRD\n+\n+**Unified, Provider-Agnostic Search API with Plugin-Based Extensibility**\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: The Web Search Gateway is HyperSpot's centralized web search service that provides a unified API for web search operations, routing requests to configurable provider plugins while enforcing governance, normalization, and observability.\n+\n+Web search integration must be consistent across all modules without embedding provider-specific logic in each consumer. The Web Search Gateway achieves this by providing a common search API and delegating provider calls to configurable plugins via the Outbound API Gateway (OAGW).\n+\n+Phase 1 focuses on tenant-scoped web search with a single provider (Tavily), result normalization, and core governance (authN/Z, quotas, rate limits). It does not implement LLM-powered features (query refinement, answer extraction), additional search types (news, images), or advanced features (semantic caching, ML re-ranking); those are planned for Phase 2 and beyond.\n+\n+**Target Users**: Platform engineers integrating search into AI agents and RAG pipelines. Tenant admins configuring provider selection, quotas, and policies.\n+\n+**Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n+- **LLM hallucinations**: Make chatbots more accurate by providing real-time web context.\n+- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n+- **Duplicated integration code**: A single gateway eliminates redundant provider integrations across modules.\n+- **Centralized governance**: Unified quotas, rate limits, and audit logging across all search consumers.\n+\n+**Success Criteria**:\n+\n+- All search requests resolve using tenant scope from SecurityContext; requests can specify provider or use tenant's default.\n+- Consumers can query enabled providers for their tenant via gateway endpoint.\n+- Provider plugins are discovered via types-registry and can be added without gateway code changes.\n+\n+**Capabilities**:\n+\n+- Tenant-scoped web search with per-request provider selection from tenant-enabled providers\n+- Normalized `SearchResponse` schema regardless of underlying provider\n+- Response caching with tenant isolation and configurable TTL\n+- Plugin-based provider integration via types-registry (GTS)\n+- Provider failover with circuit breaker pattern\n+- Governance: authentication, authorization, quotas, rate limiting\n+- Observability: metrics, structured logging, distributed tracing, audit events\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Actors\n+\n+| Actor | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| **Platform Engineer** | Integrates search into AI agents and RAG systems via the Web Search Gateway |\n+| **Tenant Admin** | Configures provider selection, monitors quota usage, and manages cost controls for their tenant |\n+| **Plugin Developer** | Implements new search provider plugins using the plugin contract, and registration process |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Primary Use Cases\n+\n+### UC1: Basic Web Search\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant is onboarded; at least one provider is enabled for tenant  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends `POST /web-search/v1/search` with query, parameters, and optional `provider_id`\n+2. Gateway authenticates request via bearer token\n+3. Gateway authorizes against tenant's search permissions\n+4. Gateway checks rate limit and quota\n+5. Gateway checks cache; if hit, returns cached response with `from_cache: true`\n+6. If cache miss:\n+   - If `provider_id` specified: verify provider is enabled for tenant; if not, return 400\n+   - If `provider_id` not specified: use tenant's configured default provider\n+7. Gateway invokes provider plugin, receives raw results\n+8. Gateway normalizes results into `SearchResponse` schema\n+9. Gateway caches response (if cacheable)\n+10. Gateway returns response with latency headers\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Response logged; metrics emitted; quota decremented\n+\n+### UC2: Tenant Provider Configuration\n+\n+**Actor**: Tenant Admin  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin queries available providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers` (platform-wide list)\n+2. Admin updates tenant configuration in Settings Service to:\n+   - Enable specific providers for the tenant (e.g., `[\"tavily\", \"serper\"]`)\n+   - Set a default provider (e.g., `\"tavily\"`)\n+   - Configure auto-failover behavior (enabled/disabled)\n+3. Subsequent requests from that tenant can specify any enabled provider via `provider_id`\n+4. Requests without `provider_id` use the tenant's default provider\n+\n+### UC2a: Per-Request Provider Selection\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has multiple providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service queries enabled providers via `GET /web-search/v1/providers`\n+2. Service sends search request with `provider_id: \"serper\"` for a specific use case\n+3. Gateway verifies \"serper\" is enabled for the tenant\n+4. Gateway routes request to Serper plugin\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used: \"serper\"`\n+\n+### UC3: Provider Failover\n+\n+**Actor**: System (automatic)  \n+**Trigger**: Requested provider returns 5xx, 429, or times out  \n+**Preconditions**: Tenant has auto-failover enabled; tenant has other providers enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition on requested provider\n+2. Circuit breaker opens for failed provider\n+3. Gateway selects another enabled provider from tenant's list based on plugin priority\n+4. Gateway retries request with fallback provider\n+5. Response includes `metadata.provider_used` (fallback) and `metadata.failover_from` (original)\n+6. Metrics record failover event\n+\n+**Alternative Flow** (auto-failover disabled):\n+1. Gateway detects failure condition\n+2. Gateway returns error response with Problem Details\n+3. Consumer can retry with different `provider_id` if desired\n+\n+### UC4: Quota Exhaustion\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Trigger**: Tenant quota exceeded  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Request arrives; gateway checks quota\n+2. Quota check fails; request rejected with `429 Too Many Requests`\n+3. Response includes `Retry-After` header and Problem Details body\n+4. Metrics record quota denial\n+\n+### UC5: Adding a New Provider Plugin\n+\n+**Actor**: Plugin Developer  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Plugin developer implements `WebSearchPluginClient` trait\n+2. Plugin developer registers plugin instance in types-registry with capability declaration\n+3. Gateway discovers new plugin on next startup or config reload\n+4. Tenant Admin enables new provider for specific tenants\n+5. Gateway routes matching requests to new provider\n+\n+### UC6: LLM-Enhanced Search with Answer Extraction\n+\n+**Actor**: AI Chatbot (via service)  \n+**Preconditions**: LLM Gateway available; tenant has LLM features enabled  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Chatbot sends search request with `options.extract_answer: true`\n+2. Gateway executes web search via provider\n+3. Gateway invokes LLM Gateway to extract direct answer from top results\n+4. Response includes `answer` object with concise text, source URLs, and confidence\n+5. Chatbot uses extracted answer to ground its response, reducing hallucination risk\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Answer extraction logged; LLM cost tracked\n+\n+### UC7: Query Refinement for Ambiguous Searches\n+\n+**Actor**: Platform Engineer (via service)  \n+**Flow**:\n+1. Service sends search with `options.refine_query: true`\n+2. Gateway invokes LLM to refine query (spelling correction, expansion, intent detection)\n+3. Gateway searches with refined query\n+4. Response includes original and refined query in metadata\n+5. Improved search results returned\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. Scope\n+\n+### 4.1 In Scope\n+\n+| Category | Items |\n+|----------|-------|\n+| **Search modalities** | Web search (MVP); news, images, video, academic as extensions |\n+| **Provider plugins** | Plugin architecture with stable contract; initial plugins: Tavily |\n+| **Multi-tenancy** | Per-tenant provider config, quotas, rate limits, cache policies |\n+| **API** | REST API with OpenAPI documentation; gRPC MAY be added later |\n+| **Normalization** | Unified `SearchResponse` schema for all providers |\n+| **Caching** | Response caching with configurable TTL, tenant isolation |\n+| **Governance** | AuthN (bearer tokens, service-to-service), AuthZ, quotas, rate limits |\n+| **Observability** | Metrics, structured logs, distributed tracing, audit events |\n+| **Error handling** | RFC 9457 Problem Details for all error responses |\n+| **Admin operations** | Provider health status, cache invalidation, quota management |\n+| **LLM integration** | Query refinement, answer extraction, result summarization (opt-in via LLM Gateway) |\n+| **Safe search** | Configurable content filtering (off, moderate, strict) with tenant-level enforcement |\n+\n+### 4.2 Out of Scope\n+\n+| Item | Rationale |\n+|------|-----------|\n+| Web crawling / scraping | Gateway is for Search API execution, not for deep scraping or crawling |\n+| Search result storage | Gateway is stateless for results; caching is ephemeral |\n+| Billing integration | Cost metrics are emitted; billing is a separate platform concern |\n+| BYO-Key Management | Users do not supply their own API keys; keys are managed centrally by the platform  |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 5. Functional Requirements\n+\n+| ID | Priority | Category | Requirement | Rationale | Acceptance Criteria |\n+|----|----------|----------|-------------|-----------|---------------------|\n+| **FR-001** | P0 | API | Gateway MUST provide a unified `Search` endpoint accepting `SearchRequest` and returning `SearchResponse` | Single entry point for all search operations | Endpoint returns 200 with valid `SearchResponse` for valid requests |\n+| **FR-002** | P0 | Routing | Gateway MUST route requests to provider based on: (1) `provider_id` in request if specified, (2) tenant's default provider if not specified; Gateway MUST verify requested provider is enabled for tenant | Per-request provider flexibility with tenant governance | Request with valid `provider_id` routes to that provider; request with invalid/disabled provider returns 400; request without `provider_id` uses tenant default |\n+| **FR-003** | P0 | Discovery | Gateway MUST expose a provider discovery endpoint returning list of providers enabled for the requesting tenant | Consumer awareness of available providers | Endpoint returns array of provider objects with `id`, `name`, `capabilities`; list filtered to tenant's enabled providers |\n+| **FR-004** | P0 | Normalization | Gateway MUST transform all provider responses into a unified response schema | Provider-agnostic responses for consumers | All fields populated correctly regardless of provider; provider-specific data isolated |\n+| **FR-005** | P0 | AuthN | Gateway MUST authenticate all requests | Security: no anonymous access | Requests without valid auth return 401; valid tokens extract tenant and user context |\n+| **FR-006** | P0 | AuthZ | Gateway MUST authorize requests against tenant's search permissions | Enforce access control | Unauthorized requests return 403; authorized requests proceed |\n+| **FR-007** | P0 | Rate Limiting | Gateway MUST enforce per-tenant rate limits | Protect providers and ensure fair usage | Rate limit hit returns 429 with retry information |\n+| **FR-008** | P0 | Quota | Gateway MUST track and enforce per-tenant quotas (requests per period) | Cost control and fair usage | Quota exhaustion returns error; quota resets at configured cadence |\n+| **FR-009** | P0 | Errors | Gateway MUST return consistent, machine-readable error responses | Uniform error handling for consumers | All error responses follow consistent structure with error code, message, and details |\n+| **FR-010** | P0 | Failover | Gateway MUST support configurable auto-failover per tenant; when enabled and provider fails, gateway attempts another enabled provider; when disabled, gateway returns error | Tenant control over failover behavior | Auto-failover enabled: failure triggers fallback; Auto-failover disabled: failure returns error |\n+| **FR-011** | P1 | Caching | Gateway SHOULD cache responses with tenant isolation and configurable TTL | Cost reduction, latency improvement | Identical requests return cached response; cache isolated per tenant; TTL configurable |\n+| **FR-012** | P1 | Caching | Gateway SHOULD support cache bypass on request | Allow fresh results when needed | Cache bypass returns fresh provider response |\n+| **FR-013** | P1 | Observability | Gateway SHOULD emit structured logs with correlation IDs for all requests | Debugging and audit | Logs contain correlation ID, tenant ID, provider used, latency; PII redacted |\n+| **FR-014** | P1 | Observability | Gateway SHOULD support distributed tracing | End-to-end request tracing | Trace context propagated to provider calls; spans visible in tracing backend |\n+| **FR-015** | P1 | Audit | Gateway SHOULD emit audit events for: config changes, quota/rate actions, provider selection | Compliance and incident investigation | Audit events contain timestamp, actor, action, resource, outcome |\n+| **FR-016** | P1 | Admin | Gateway SHOULD expose health and cache management endpoints for operators | Operational visibility and control | Health status per provider; cache invalidation capability |\n+| **FR-017** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support news search with freshness, category, and sort parameters | Real-time information for chatbots | News search returns results with freshness filter; category filtering works |\n+| **FR-018** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support image search with size, color, type, and license filters | Content discovery use cases | Image results include thumbnails, dimensions, license info |\n+| **FR-019** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support video search with duration and quality filters | Video research use cases | Video results include duration, quality, platform info |\n+| **FR-020** | P1 | Search Types | Gateway SHOULD support academic/scholarly search with publication type, year range, and citation count | Research and fact-checking | Academic results include citation count, publication type, authors |\n+| **FR-021** | P1 | Safe Search | Gateway SHOULD enforce safe search filtering with configurable levels (off, moderate, strict) per tenant | Content safety and compliance | Safe search level enforced; platform-wide minimum level can override tenant settings |\n+| **FR-022** | P1 | LLM Integration | Gateway SHOULD support optional LLM-based query refinement (spelling correction, query expansion, intent detection) | Improve search quality | Refinement opt-in per request; refined query logged in metadata; original preserved |\n+| **FR-023** | P1 | LLM Integration | Gateway SHOULD support LLM-based answer extraction from search results | Reduce hallucinations in AI chatbots | Answer includes text, type (fact/definition/summary), source URL, confidence score |\n+| **FR-024** | P1 | LLM Integration | Gateway SHOULD support LLM-based summarization of top search results | Concise context for RAG pipelines | Summary includes configurable length, source URLs |\n+| **FR-025** | P1 | Aggregation | Gateway SHOULD support multi-provider aggregation with deduplication and score merging | Comprehensive result coverage | Aggregation opt-in per request; results deduplicated by URL; provider source tracked per result |\n+| **FR-026** | P1 | Filters | Gateway SHOULD support comprehensive filtering: domain include/exclude, file type, freshness, date range | Refined search results | Filters mapped to provider syntax; unsupported filters indicated in response metadata |\n+| **FR-027** | P1 | Provider Health | Gateway SHOULD track provider health and availability to inform routing decisions | Intelligent provider selection | Health includes error rates, response time trends, rate limit status, circuit breaker state |\n+| **FR-028** | P1 | Cost Tracking | Gateway SHOULD track actual monetary costs per provider with budget alerts | Cost visibility and control | Cost per query by provider tracked; monthly totals per tenant available; alerts on thresholds |\n+| **FR-029** | P1 | Streaming | Gateway SHOULD support streaming search results as they become available | Improved perceived latency | SSE endpoint returns results incrementally; final response aggregates all |\n+| **FR-030** | P1 | Cache Warming | Gateway SHOULD support pre-populating cache with common/trending queries | Improve cache hit rates | Admin API accepts query list for warming; warming jobs logged |\n+| **FR-031** | P1 | Re-ranking | Gateway SHOULD support re-ranking search results based on tenant preferences, quality signals, and recency | Result quality improvement | Re-ranking configurable per tenant; ranking factors logged |\n+| **FR-032** | P1 | History | Gateway SHOULD support configurable retention of search history for analytics (default 30 days) | Usage analytics and quality improvement | History queryable by tenant admin; retention configurable; PII rules applied |\n+| **FR-033** | P1 | Export | Gateway SHOULD support exporting search results in multiple formats (JSON, CSV) | Offline analysis | Export endpoint accepts result set; formats validated |\n+| **FR-034** | P2 | MCP Tool | Gateway MAY expose search as an MCP tool interface for LLM function calling | LLM agent integration | MCP tool schema published; tool callable by LLM agents |\n+| **FR-035** | P2 | Semantic Cache | Gateway MAY support embeddings for semantic caching and result enrichment | Improve cache hit rates for paraphrased queries; enable downstream semantic operations | Similar queries return cached results; embeddings optionally returned in response |\n+| **FR-036** | P2 | Pagination | Gateway MAY support pagination for large result sets via `offset` parameter | Navigate through large result sets | Request accepts `offset`; response includes `has_more` indicator |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 6. Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs)\n+\n+### 6.1 Performance\n+\n+| Metric | Target | Measurement |\n+|--------|--------|-------------|\n+| **p95 latency** | ≤800ms (excluding provider latency) | Gateway processing time only |\n+| **p99 latency** | ≤1200ms (excluding provider latency) | Gateway processing time only |\n+\n+---\n+## 7. Gateway Constraints\n+\n+### 7.1 Multi-Tenancy Requirements\n+\n+| Constraint | Description |\n+|------------|-------------|\n+| **Tenant isolation** | Tenant A's configuration, cache, quotas MUST NOT affect Tenant B |\n+| **Provider enablement** | Tenant Admin enables specific providers from the platform-wide available list; requests can only use enabled providers |\n+\n+### 10.2 Provider Contract Constraints\n+\n+| Constraint | Description |\n+|------------|-------------|\n+| **Capability mismatch** | If request requires capability provider lacks, return 400 with `capability_not_supported` error |","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"831d9f83fe0bfdf26cbc34bac913c8ff88f45552","original_commit_id":"831d9f83fe0bfdf26cbc34bac913c8ff88f45552","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix section numbering (\"10.2\" should be \"7.2\").**\n\nThis subsection sits under section 7 but is labeled 10.2, which breaks the document structure.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-### 10.2 Provider Contract Constraints\n+### 7.2 Provider Contract Constraints\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n### 7.2 Provider Contract Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Description |\n|------------|-------------|\n| **Capability mismatch** | If request requires capability provider lacks, return 400 with `capability_not_supported` error |\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 252 - 256, The\nsubsection heading \"### 10.2 Provider Contract Constraints\" is misnumbered and\nshould be \"### 7.2 Provider Contract Constraints\"; update that heading text to\n\"7.2\" (referencing the heading string \"Provider Contract Constraints\") so the\nsubsection correctly sits under section 7 and the document structure is\npreserved.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 8af9588","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T11:21:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667797","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667797"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667797"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":252,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":256,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":256,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667808","pull_request_review_id":3738598724,"id":2753667808,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kIaLg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.provider.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Provider\",\n+  \"description\": \"Web search provider types\",\n+  \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"$defs\": {\n+    \"ProviderInfo\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Provider information returned to clients\",\n+      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"version\", \"is_default\", \"capabilities\", \"health\"],\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"id\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider GTS identifier\"\n+        },\n+        \"name\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider display name\"\n+        },\n+        \"version\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider plugin version\"\n+        },\n+        \"priority\": {\n+          \"type\": \"integer\",\n+          \"description\": \"Failover priority (lower = higher priority)\"\n+        },\n+        \"capabilities\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PluginCapabilities\"\n+        },\n+        \"health\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HealthStatus\"\n+        }\n+      }","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/provider.v1.json","commit_id":"8af9588dc0a4b2752bc18bbd5b54df0d630b8b23","original_commit_id":"831d9f83fe0bfdf26cbc34bac913c8ff88f45552","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add `is_default` property to `ProviderInfo`.**\n\n`is_default` is required but not defined, which makes it untyped and can break schema-driven clients.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"version\": {\n           \"type\": \"string\",\n           \"description\": \"Provider plugin version\"\n         },\n+        \"is_default\": {\n+          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n+          \"description\": \"Whether this provider is the tenant default\"\n+        },\n         \"priority\": {\n           \"type\": \"integer\",\n           \"description\": \"Failover priority (lower = higher priority)\"\n         },\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/gts/provider.v1.json` around lines 8 - 35,\nProviderInfo declares is_default as required but the property is missing; add an\nis_default boolean property to the ProviderInfo schema so schema-driven clients\nhave a type for it. Update the \"properties\" object inside the ProviderInfo\ndefinition to include \"is_default\" with \"type\": \"boolean\" and a short\n\"description\" (e.g., \"Whether this provider is the default\"), ensuring it\nmatches the required entry and keeps existing properties like id, name, version,\npriority, capabilities, and health.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @akshatjhalani\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T12:05:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667808","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667808"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667808"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":8,"original_start_line":8,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":35,"original_line":35,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":35,"position":35,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667815","pull_request_review_id":3738598724,"id":2753667815,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kIaLn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.provider.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Provider\",\n+  \"description\": \"Web search provider types\",\n+  \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"$defs\": {\n+    \"ProviderInfo\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Provider information returned to clients\",\n+      \"required\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"version\", \"is_default\", \"capabilities\", \"health\"],\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"id\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider GTS identifier\"\n+        },\n+        \"name\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider display name\"\n+        },\n+        \"version\": {\n+          \"type\": \"string\",\n+          \"description\": \"Provider plugin version\"\n+        },\n+        \"priority\": {\n+          \"type\": \"integer\",\n+          \"description\": \"Failover priority (lower = higher priority)\"\n+        },\n+        \"capabilities\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PluginCapabilities\"\n+        },\n+        \"health\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HealthStatus\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    },\n+    \"PluginCapabilities\": {\n+      \"type\": \"object\",\n+      \"description\": \"Provider capability declaration\",\n+      \"required\": [\"provider_id\", \"search_types\", \"max_results_per_request\"],\n+      \"properties\": {\n+        \"search_types\": {\n+          \"type\": \"array\",\n+          \"description\": \"Supported search types\",\n+          \"items\": {\n+            \"type\": \"string\",\n+            \"enum\": [\"web\", \"news\", \"images\", \"video\", \"academic\"]\n+          }\n+        },\n+        \"supported_filters\": {\n+          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SupportedFilters\"\n+        },\n+        \"max_results_per_request\": {\n+          \"type\": \"integer\",\n+          \"description\": \"Maximum results per request\"\n+        },\n+        \"data_residency\": {\n+          \"type\": \"array\",\n+          \"description\": \"Data residency regions\",\n+          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        }\n+      }","path":"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/provider.v1.json","commit_id":"8af9588dc0a4b2752bc18bbd5b54df0d630b8b23","original_commit_id":"831d9f83fe0bfdf26cbc34bac913c8ff88f45552","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{