t: 380\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for \"image\" references in schema files\necho \"=== Searching for 'image' (singular) in schema files ===\"\ngrep -r '\"image\"' modules/web_search_gateway/gts/*.json 2>/dev/null || echo \"No matches for singular 'image'\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Searching for 'images' (plural) in schema files ===\"\ngrep -r '\"images\"' modules/web_search_gateway/gts/*.json 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Full search_response.v1.json structure ===\"\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\n\nwith open(\"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_response.v1.json\") as f:\n    response = json.load(f)\n\n# Check if any $defs reference search types\nprint(\"All keys in response:\", list(response.keys()))\nprint(\"\\nFull $defs structure:\")\nfor key, value in response.get(\"$defs\", {}).items():\n    print(f\"  {key}: {list(value.keys()) if isinstance(value, dict) else type(value)}\")\n\n# Check if any property references SearchType or search_types\nprint(\"\\nLooking for searchType/search_type/SearchType references...\")\nimport json as j\ncontent = json.dumps(response)\nif \"SearchType\" in content:\n    print(\"  Found 'SearchType' reference\")\nif \"search_type\" in content:\n    print(\"  Found 'search_type' reference\")\nif \"searchType\" in content:\n    print(\"  Found 'searchType' reference\")\nif \"enum\" in content and \"image\" in content.lower():\n    print(\"  Found enum with 'image' references\")\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1088\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Get detailed context for ContentType definition (used in response)\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\n\n# Check response schema\nwith open(\"modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_response.v1.json\") as f:\n    response = json.load(f)\n\nprint(\"=== ContentType enum (in response) ===\")\nprint(response[\"$defs\"][\"ContentType\"][\"enum\"])\n\n# Check where search_type is used in response\nprint(\"\\n=== SearchResult properties ===\")\nsearch_result = response[\"$defs\"][\"SearchResult\"][\"properties\"]\nfor prop_name, prop_def in search_result.items():\n    print(f\"{prop_name}:\")\n    if \"$ref\" in prop_def:\n        print(f\"  $ref: {prop_def['$ref']}\")\n    else:\n        for k, v in prop_def.items():\n            if k != \"description\":\n                print(f\"  {k}: {v}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Summary ===\")\nprint(\"Request search_types enum: ['web', 'news', 'images', 'video', 'academic']\")\nprint(\"Response ContentType enum: ['webpage', 'news', 'image', 'video', 'pdf', 'academic', 'other']\")\nprint(\"\\nConflicts:\")\nprint(\"  - 'images' vs 'image'\")\nprint(\"  - Request has 'academic', Response doesn't\")\nprint(\"  - Response has 'webpage', 'pdf', 'other' not in request\")\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 821\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Align `search_types` enum with `content_type` enum across schemas.**\n\nThe request schema (`search_request.v1.json`) defines search types as `['web', 'news', 'images', 'video', 'academic']`, but the response schema (`search_response.v1.json`) defines `content_type` as `['webpage', 'news', 'image', 'video', 'pdf', 'academic', 'other']`. The mismatch between `\"images\"` (plural, in request) and `\"image\"` (singular, in response) will break capability validation when matching request parameters to response results. Additionally, the response enum includes extra types (`webpage`, `pdf`, `other`) that cannot be requested, creating semantic inconsistency in the API contract. Update the enums to align both the naming (singular/plural) and the set of supported values.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/gts/provider.v1.json` around lines 42 - 48, The\nenums for search_types and content_type are inconsistent; update the enum values\nso naming and sets match across schemas: change search_types (currently\ncontaining \"images\") to the singular form \"image\" and add any missing values\npresent in content_type (or remove extras from content_type) so both enums use\nthe same normalized set (e.g., [\"webpage\" or \"web\" choice must be agreed],\n\"news\", \"image\", \"video\", \"pdf\", \"academic\", \"other\" or a reduced matching\nsubset). Edit the search_types enum and the content_type enum (referencing the\nsearch_types and content_type symbols) to use the identical list and\nsingular/plural form consistently so request parameters can validly map to\nresponse results.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T10:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:35:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667818","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667818"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#discussion_r2753667818"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":42,"original_start_line":42,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":48,"original_line":48,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":48,"position":48,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2753667825","pull_request_review_id":3738598724,"id":2753667825,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kIaLx","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n+  \"$id\": \"gts.x.web_search.search_response.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Sea