tion\nls -la ./modules/web_search_gateway/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 340\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for any validation happening on settings objects in the codebase\nrg \"enabled_providers|default_provider\" --type rust --type go --type ts -B 3 -A 3 | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Address the missing cross-field constraint during Settings Service implementation.**\n\nThe `default_provider` description says it \"must be in `enabled_providers`\", but the schema doesn't enforce this membership rule. Any string will pass schema validation. Decide during implementation whether to:\n\n1. Add schema-level validation using `allOf` + `contains` + `$data` (supported by JSON Schema Draft 2020-12), or  \n2. Implement this check in the Settings Service validation layer when the service handles this schema.\n\nReference ADR-003 for the validation responsibility assignment.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/web_search_gateway/gts/settings.v1.json` around lines 7 - 17, The\nschema currently declares \"default_provider\" and \"enabled_providers\" but does\nnot enforce that the default_provider value is a member of enabled_providers;\nupdate implementation to enforce this cross-field constraint either by adding a\nschema-level rule (use JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 features such as allOf +\ncontains + $data to assert default_provider exists in enabled_providers) or by\nimplementing the check in the Settings Service validation layer (validate after\nJSON Schema validation that settings.default_provider is included in\nsettings.enabled_providers), and follow ADR-003 to decide which layer owns the\nvalidation; reference the symbols default_provider, enabled_providers,\nTenantProviderConfig, and the Settings Service when making the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- 