 ensure consistency\nbetween priority and obligation: either change the normative keyword \"MUST\" to\n\"SHOULD\" if this is a P1 (non-critical) requirement, or change the priority from\nP1 to P0 if enforcement is truly mandatory; locate and edit the FR-021 entry\n(Safe Search) in the PRD to apply the chosen correction and ensure the\nacceptance criteria and any platform-wide override text reflect the revised\nobligation.\n- Around line 42-50: The headings jump from \"## 1. Overview\" to \"## 5. Actors\"\nindicating missing or misnumbered sections 2–4; either restore the omitted\nsections' content if it was accidentally removed or renumber the \"## 5. Actors\"\nheader (and any subsequent headers) to maintain a consecutive sequence (e.g.,\nchange \"## 5. Actors\" to \"## 2. Actors\"), and verify other headers in the\ndocument follow the corrected numbering to keep the table of contents and\nstructure consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (9)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/gts/errors.v1.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2-6`: **Consider using 404 for \"Provider Not Found\".**\n\nHTTP 404 might be more semantically accurate for a resource not found scenario. However, 400 is acceptable if interpreted as \"invalid provider_id in request.\"\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_request.v1.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`57-66`: **Consider adding domain format validation.**\n\nThe `include_domains` and `exclude_domains` arrays accept any string. Consider adding a pattern or format constraint to validate domain structure (e.g., basic hostname pattern) to catch invalid inputs early.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Example pattern for domain validation</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"include_domains\": {\n           \"type\": \"array\",\n           \"description\": \"Domains to include in results\",\n-          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+          \"items\": { \n+            \"type\": \"string\",\n+            \"pattern\": \"^[a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?(\\\\.[a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*$\"\n+          }\n         },\n         \"exclude_domains\": {\n           \"type\": \"array\",\n           \"description\": \"Domains to exclude from results\",\n-          \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+          \"items\": { \n+            \"type\": \"string\",\n+            \"pattern\": \"^[a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?(\\\\.[a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*$\"\n+          }\n         },\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/gts/provider.v1.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`121-124`: **Add minimum constraint for `latency_p99_ms`.**\n\nLatency values should not be negative. Consider adding `\"minimum\": 0` for consistency with other bounded numeric fields.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"latency_p99_ms\": {\n           \"type\": \"integer\",\n-          \"description\": \"P99 latency in milliseconds\"\n+          \"description\": \"P99 latency in milliseconds\",\n+          \"minimum\": 0\n         },\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/gts/settings.v1.json (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`51-67`: **Consider making `requests_per_minute` required in RateLimitOverride.**\n\nCurrently, `RateLimitOverride` has no required fields, allowing an empty object `{}`. If a rate limit override is specified, it likely needs at least `requests_per_minute` to be meaningful.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     \"RateLimitOverride\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"description\": \"Tenant rate limit override\",\n+      \"required\": [\"requests_per_minute\"],\n       \"properties\": {\n         \"requests_per_minute\": {\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`68-78`: **Consider making `monthly_limit` required in QuotaOverride.**\n\nSimilarly, `QuotaOverride` allows an empty object. If a quota override is specified, `monthly_limit` should likely be required.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     \"QuotaOverride\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"description\": \"Tenant quota override\",\n+      \"required\": [\"monthly_limit\"],\n       \"properties\": {\n         \"monthly_limit\": {\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/docs/PRD.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`20-20`: **Minor style nit: \"API interface\" is redundant.**\n\n\"API\" already stands for \"Application Programming Interface\", so \"API interface\" is tautological. Consider using just \"Unified API\" or \"Unified interface\".\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API interface abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n+- **Provider fragmentation**: Unified API abstracts differences in provider APIs, enabling seamless provider switching without consumer code changes.\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/gts/search_response.v1.json (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-25`: **Consider adding `minimum: 0` constraints to count fields.**\n\n`total_results` and `returned_count` cannot be negative. Adding explicit constraints improves schema validation and documentation.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested enhancement</summary>\n\n```diff\n     \"total_results\": {\n       \"type\": \"integer\",\n-      \"description\": \"Estimated total results available\"\n+      \"description\": \"Estimated total results available\",\n+      \"minimum\": 0\n     },\n     \"returned_count\": {\n       \"type\": \"integer\",\n-      \"description\": \"Number of results in this response\"\n+      \"description\": \"Number of results in this response\",\n+      \"minimum\": 0\n     },\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`113-116`: **Consider adding `minimum: 0` to `latency_ms`.**\n\nLatency cannot be negative; an explicit constraint improves schema clarity.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested enhancement</summary>\n\n```diff\n         \"latency_ms\": {\n           \"type\": \"integer\",\n-          \"description\": \"Request latency in milliseconds\"\n+          \"description\": \"Request latency in milliseconds\",\n+          \"minimum\": 0\n         },\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/web_search_gateway/docs/Design.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`248-249`: **Incomplete table entries: Type column is empty for rate_limit and quota parameters.**\n\nLines 248-249 have empty Type columns. Specify the types for clarity (e.g., `u64` or similar).\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `rate_limit.*` |  | 100 | Default requests/second |\n-| `quota.default_monthly` |  | 10000 | Default monthly request quota |\n+| `rate_limit.*` | u64 | 100 | Default requests/second |\n+| `quota.default_monthly` | u64 | 10000 | Default monthly request quota |\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#pullrequestreview-3737806467","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/402#pullrequestreview-3737806467"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/402"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-02T07:50:05Z","commit_id":"749863c0e229b4fcb30c00d33d7322f9adb8ed61"},{"id":3738425771,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7e09mr","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent