oderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Database feature flags don't make SQLite conditional.**\n\nThe new feature flags add database backends, but the base `sea-orm` dependency at lines 35-41 unconditionally includes `\"sqlx-sqlite\"`. This means SQLite is always compiled regardless of which `db-*` feature is selected.\n\nTo properly gate database drivers, remove `\"sqlx-sqlite\"` from the base dependency and rely solely on the feature flags:\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n [features]\n # Database driver selection - choose one at build time\n db-sqlite = [\"sea-orm/sqlx-sqlite\", \"sea-orm-migration/sqlx-sqlite\"]\n db-pg = [\"sea-orm/sqlx-postgres\", \"sea-orm-migration/sqlx-postgres\"]\n db-mysql = [\"sea-orm/sqlx-mysql\", \"sea-orm-migration/sqlx-mysql\"]\n\n [dependencies]\n ...\n sea-orm = { workspace = true, features = [\n-    \"sqlx-sqlite\",\n     \"runtime-tokio-rustls\",\n     \"macros\",\n     \"with-time\",\n     \"with-uuid\",\n ] }\n-sea-orm-migration = { workspace = true }\n+sea-orm-migration = { workspace = true, features = [] }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/Cargo.toml` around lines 15\n- 20, The Cargo.toml currently leaves the \"sqlx-sqlite\" feature enabled\nunconditionally on the sea-orm dependency, so SQLite is always compiled; update\nCargo.toml to remove \"sqlx-sqlite\" from the base sea-orm dependency and instead\nonly enable \"sqlx-sqlite\" when the db-sqlite feature is selected (i.e., move\nthat feature flag into the db-sqlite feature group), and ensure other\ndependencies like sea-orm-migration/sqlx-sqlite are similarly gated by db-sqlite\nso each db-* feature (db-sqlite, db-pg, db-mysql) fully controls its SQLX flags\nfor sea-orm and sea-orm-migration.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 6c63b51","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:15:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:33:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730778455","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730778455"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730778455"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730778455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":15,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":9,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730778459","pull_request_review_id":3709713864,"id":2730778459,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixF9b","diff_hunk":"@@ -272,26 +272,35 @@ def cmd_e2e(args):\n             \"hyperspot-api:e2e\",\n         ]\n         \n-        # Add build args for cargo features if specified\n-        if args.features:\n-            build_cmd.extend([\"--build-arg\", f\"CARGO_FEATURES={args.features}\"])\n+        # Add build args for cargo arguments if specified\n+        if args.cargo_build_args:\n+            build_cmd.extend([\"--build-arg\", f\"CARGO_BUILD_ARGS={args.cargo_build_args}\"])\n         \n         build_cmd.append(\".\")\n         run_cmd(build_cmd)\n \n         # Start environment\n         step(\"Starting E2E docker-compose environment\")\n-        run_cmd(\n-            [\n-                \"docker\",\n-                \"compose\",\n-                \"-f\",\n-                \"testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\",\n-                \"up\",\n-                \"--force-recreate\",\n-                \"-d\",\n-            ]\n-        )\n+        compose_cmd = [\n+            \"docker\",\n+            \"compose\",\n+            \"-f\",\n+            \"testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\",\n+        ]\n+        \n+        # Add profile if specified, otherwise use 'default'\n+        if args.profile:\n+            if args.profile not in ['default', 'postgres', 'mariadb']:\n+                print(f\"ERROR: Invalid profile '{args.profile}'. Must be 'default', 'postgres' or 'mariadb'\")\n+                sys.exit(1)\n+            compose_cmd.extend([\"--profile\", args.profile])\n+            print(f\"Using profile: {args.profile}\")\n+        else:\n+            compose_cmd.extend([\"--profile\", \"default\"])\n+            print(\"Using profile: default (no database)\")\n+\n+        compose_cmd.extend([\"up\", \"-d\", \"--force-recreate\"])\n+        run_cmd(compose_cmd)","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"96961423e65f58ee94d5cdd9084efc7d45d9a9b9","original_commit_id":"9c084cde2f8fd42f50476f7d2cb0a6f2203241fd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Inconsistent profile handling between `up` and `down` commands.**\n\nWhen starting the Docker environment, if `args.profile` is not set, the code explicitly passes `--profile default` (lines 298-300). However, during teardown (lines 397-398), the profile is only added if `args.profile` is truthy, meaning `--profile default` won't be passed when the user didn't explicitly specify a profile.\n\nThis inconsistency may cause unexpected behavior during cleanup, as Docker Compose may not properly identify which services to stop.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix to use consistent profile handling</summary>\n\n```diff\n     if args.docker and docker_env_started:\n         step(\"Stopping E2E docker-compose environment\")\n+        # Use same profile logic as startup: default to \"default\" if not specified\n+        profile = args.profile if args.profile else \"default\"\n         down_cmd = [\n             \"docker\",\n             \"compose\",\n             \"-f\",\n             \"testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\",\n+            \"--profile\",\n+            profile,\n+            \"down\",\n+            \"-v\",\n         ]\n-        if args.profile:\n-            down_cmd.extend([\"--profile\", args.profile])\n-        down_cmd.extend([\"down\", \"-v\"])\n         run_cmd_allow_fail(down_cmd)\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 391-400\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 291 - 303, The teardown logic is inconsistent\nwith startup: when building the compose command for stopping/removing services\n(the same pattern used with compose_cmd and run_cmd), ensure you apply the same\nprofile handling as in the startup block that checks args.profile; specifically,\nin the teardown branch that currently only adds \"--profile\" when args.profile is\ntruthy, change it to add [\"--profile\", args.profile] if args.profile is set,\notherwise add [\"--profile\", \"default\"] so the down/stop/remove compose_cmd uses\nthe same profile selection as the up path (reference args.profile, compose_cmd,\nand run_cmd to locate the code).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 6c63b51","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:15:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:33:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730778459","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730778459"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730778459"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730778459/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":413,"original_start_line":291,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":425,"original_line":303,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":46,"position":86,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730865233","pull_request_review_id":3709820465,"id":2730865233,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixbJR","diff_hunk":"@@ -30,7 +36,7 @@ path = \"src/main.rs\"\n mimalloc = { version = \"0.1\" }\n # Local crates\n modkit = { workspace = true, features = [\"otel\", \"bootstrap\"] }\n-modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\"] }\n+modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"] }","path":"apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"6c63b5122a93d9475a3918dfac22b2bc37eb9298","original_commit_id":"6c63b5122a93d9475a3918dfac22b2bc37eb9298","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The dependency unconditionally enables all database features `[\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"]`, which conflicts with the conditional feature flags defined above (lines 16-18). This means all three database drivers will always be compiled in regardless of which `db-*` feature is selected.\n\n**Impact**: Defeats the purpose of conditional compilation, increases binary size, and may cause runtime conflicts if the code assumes only one driver is active.\n\n**Fix**:\n```toml\nmodkit-db = { workspace = true, default-features = false }\n```\n\nThe feature propagation in lines 16-18 will handle enabling the correct driver.\n```suggestion\nmodkit-db = { workspace = true, default-features = false }\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/320?chatWithGeneratedComment=302dc5b2-a842-483d-9cd5-5c228e06c189\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:36:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:36:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730865233","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730865233"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730865233"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730865233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":39,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889240","pull_request_rev