-db/Cargo.toml for mysql references ===\"\ncat libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml | head -100\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking if mysql feature exists in modkit-db ===\"\nrg -n \"mysql\" libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2049\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check users_info/Cargo.toml around line 74 and full feature definitions\necho \"=== users_info/Cargo.toml full content ===\"\ncat examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2998\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add \"mysql\" feature to modkit-db dependency declaration.**\n\nThe `modkit-db` crate defines a `mysql` feature (`mysql = [\"sea-orm/sqlx-mysql\"]`), but the dependency declaration in users_info/Cargo.toml at line 74 doesn't include it: `modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"insecure-escape\"] }`. When building with `--features db-mysql`, the sea-orm driver is enabled at the users_info level, but modkit-db's sea-orm dependency won't have the mysql driver available, causing compilation or runtime failures. Include \"mysql\" in the modkit-db features list.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/Cargo.toml` around lines 17 - 20, The\nmodkit-db dependency in users_info/Cargo.toml is missing the \"mysql\" feature;\nupdate the modkit-db dependency declaration (modkit-db = { workspace = true,\nfeatures = [...] }) to include \"mysql\" alongside \"sqlite\", \"pg\", and\n\"insecure-escape\" so the modkit-db crate enables its mysql feature (mysql =\n[\"sea-orm/sqlx-mysql\"]) when building with --features db-mysql; simply add\n\"mysql\" to the features array for modkit-db.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:04Z","html_url":"https://