2,26p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 743\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check simple_user_settings module to see how it uses database features\ncat -n modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/lib.rs | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 699\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's any feature-gating in the module init\nrg -n \"cfg.*db-pg|cfg.*db-mysql|cfg.*db-sqlite\" modules/simple_user_settings/ -A2 -B2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the users_info example similarly\nrg -n \"cfg.*db-pg|cfg.*db-mysql|cfg.*db-sqlite\" examples/modkit/users_info/ -A2 -B2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check how modules are included as dependencies in hyperspot-server\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml | grep -A2 -B2 \"simple_user_settings\\|users_info\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1318\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at the config files to understand what modules need to be present\nhead -50 config/e2e-local.yaml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2025\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check e2e-local-postgres.yaml to see what it expects\nhead -50 config/e2e-local-postgres.yaml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1955\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if docker-compose ever rebuilds the image or always assumes it's pre-built\ngrep -n \"build\\|docker build\" testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 89\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's any documentation on how to run E2E tests\nfd -e md -e txt | xargs rg -l \"e2e\\|E2E\" | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at what the default build behavior is - what features get built without explicit args\ngrep -n \"default\\|db-sqlite\" apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 185\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me verify the complete picture by checking what happens with the image tag\n# when you use docker-compose with build args\ngrep -n \"image:\" testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 151\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any other variations or if all three services truly share the same image tag\nsed -n '83,128p' testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1294\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's a .dockerignore or any indication of how docker-compose is intended to be used\nfind testing/docker -type f | xargs ls -la\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 479\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for any CI/CD workflows that might show the intended usage pattern\nfd -e yml -e yaml -path \"*/.github/*\" | xargs cat 2>/dev/null | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 232\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's any README or documentation explaining how to use this\nls -la testing/docker/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 516\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the structure more carefully - look for any setup instructions\nfind . -name \"README*\" -o -name \"CONTRIBUTING*\" | xargs cat 2>/dev/null | grep -A20 \"docker\\|E2E\\|e2e\" | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1874\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**The proposed fix cannot work as written—all three services share the same image tag and cannot each build with different features.**\n\nThe core issue is real: `hyperspot_api_pg` and `hyperspot_api_mariadb` use configuration files expecting PostgreSQL and MySQL drivers respectively, but the docker-compose `build` section doesn't specify database-specific `CARGO_BUILD_ARGS`. However, the proposed solution has a critical flaw.\n\nAll three service variants (`hyperspot_api`, `hyperspot_api_pg`, `hyperspot_api_mariadb`) reference the same pre-built image tag `hyperspot-api:e2e`. If each service tries to build with different `CARGO_BUILD_ARGS`, only the last build would persist under that tag—the others would be overwritten. This defeats the purpose.\n\n**Correct approaches:**\n1. Build once with all features: Add `--features db-pg,db-mysql` to a single build step (supports all variants from one image)\n2. Use separate image tags per variant and rebuild for each profile\n3. Document that standalone `docker-compose` usage is unsupported; only use via `ci.py --cargo-build-args`\n\nThe current architecture works correctly through `ci.py`, which builds the image separately with specified features before invoking `docker-compose`. Direct `docker-compose up` usage would fail if database features weren't pre-built.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/docker/docker-compose.yml` around lines 9 - 25, The docker-compose\nsetup is wrong because all three service variants (hyperspot_api,\nhyperspot_api_pg, hyperspot_api_mariadb) share the same image tag\n\"hyperspot-api:e2e\" so different CARGO_BUILD_ARGS would overwrite each other;\nfix by either building one image that includes both DB features (add \"--features\ndb-pg,db-mysql\" to the build step used by the shared image), or give each\nvariant a unique image tag and separate build blocks that pass distinct\nCARGO_BUILD_ARGS, or update documentation to require using ci.py which prebuilds\nimages with the correct CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; modify the build section and image\ntags in the x-hyperspot-api-common and the service entries referencing\n\"hyperspot-api:e2e\" accordingly so each runtime variant has the correct compiled\nfeatures.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 5b6951f","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T10:00:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730889258","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889258"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730889258"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":15,"original_start_line":9,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":31,"original_line":25,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":25,"position":31,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889266","pull_request_review_id":3709853755,"id":2730889266,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixhAy","diff_hunk":"@@ -26,9 +26,9 @@ COPY proto ./proto\n \n # Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\n # Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n-# Features can be customized via CARGO_FEATURES build arg\n-RUN if [ -n \"$CARGO_FEATURES\" ]; then \\\n-        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server --features \"$CARGO_FEATURES\"; \\\n+# Additional cargo args can be customized via CARGO_BUILD_ARGS build arg\n+RUN if [ -n \"$CARGO_BUILD_ARGS\" ]; then \\\n+        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server $CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; \\\n     else \\\n         cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server; \\\n     fi","path":"testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile","commit_id":"edb4135782463e08644a3b2175bc694d3c5417ab","original_commit_id":"6c63b5122a93d9475a3918dfac22b2bc37eb9298","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Comment and behavior mismatch: \"release mode\" vs debug build.**\n\nThe comment at line 27 states \"Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\", but the cargo commands at lines 31 and 33 don't include `--release`, and line 42 copies from `target/debug/`. Either update the comment or add `--release` to the build commands.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Option A: Fix comment to match debug build behavior</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\n+# Build the hyperspot-server binary in debug mode for faster builds\n # Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Option B: Enable release mode for optimized binary</summary>\n\n```diff\n RUN if [ -n \"$CARGO_BUILD_ARGS\" ]; then \\\n-        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server $CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; \\\n+        cargo build --release --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server $CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; \\\n     else \\\n-        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server; \\\n+        cargo build --release --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server; \\\n     fi\n```\n\nAnd update the COPY:\n```diff\n-COPY --from=builder /build/target/debug/hyperspot-server /app/hyperspot-server\n+COPY --from=builder /build/target/release/hyperspot-server /app/hyperspot-server\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# Build the hyperspot-server binary in debug mode for faster builds\n# Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n# Additional cargo args can be customized via CARGO_BUILD_ARGS build arg\nRUN if [ -n \"$CARGO_BUILD_ARGS\" ]; then \\\n        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server $CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; \\\n    else \\\n        cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server; \\\n    fi\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` around lines 27 - 34, The comment claims\nthe build is \"in release mode\" but the Dockerfile runs cargo build without\n--release and later copies from target/debug; either change the comment to\nindicate a debug build or (preferred) enable release mode by adding --release to\nboth cargo build invocations (the lines invoking cargo build --bin\nhyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server and the variant that includes\n$CARGO_BUILD_ARGS) and update the COPY that currently references target/debug/\nto use target/release/ so the built binary and copy step match release mode.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730889266","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889266"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2730889266"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730889266/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":28,"original_start_line":27,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":35,"original_line":34,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":32,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227746","pull_request_review_id":3710261661,"id":2731227746,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iyzpi","diff_hunk":"@@ -10,7 +10,13 @@ authors.workspace = true\n workspace = true\n \n [features]\n-default = []\n+default = [\"db-sqlite\"]\n+\n+# Database driver selection - propagates to all modules\n+db-sqlite = [\"modkit-db/sqlite\", \"simple_user_settings/db-sqlite\", \"users_info?/db-sqlite\"]\n+db-pg = [\"modkit-db/pg\", \"simple_user_settings/db-pg\", \"users_info?/db-pg\"]\n+db-mysql = [\"modkit-db/mysql\", \"simple_user_settings/db-mysql\", \"users_info?/db-mysql\"]","path":"apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"54f8b1e41df9f076d57f0eeba0c5436e9658d924","original_commit_id":"5b6951f1aca6e3b6d1bb1f663afc354f543a7841","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, explore repo structure to find Make targets and CI configs\nfind . -type f \\( -name \"Makefile\" -o -name \"makefile\" -o -name \"*.mk\" \\) | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 74\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for CI configurations\nfind . -type d \\( -name \".github\" -o -name \".gitlab-ci*\" \\) 2>/dev/null | head -10\nls -la .github/workflows/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No .github/workflows found\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 437\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for database-related Make targets and CI configuration\nrg -n 'e2e-docker|--no-default-features|--features.*db' --max-count=50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1258\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the workspace root Cargo.toml for MSRV and Cargo version info\nhead -30 Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 650\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify the exact content and context of apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2374\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for cfg conditionals that check database features\nrg -n 'cfg.*db-(sqlite|pg|mysql)' --type rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for any compile-time validation or conflict detection\nrg -n '#\\[cfg|compile_error|panic.*backend' --type rust | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2640\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's backend feature validation in the main app\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1927\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the Python CI script for any additional build flags\ncat scripts/ci.py | grep -A 10 -B 5 'cargo-build-args\\|no-default-features'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 614\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add `--no-default-features` to Makefile database targets.**\n\nThe `e2e-docker-pg` and `e2e-docker-mysql` targets (Makefile lines 285, 288) do not disable default features. This causes both db-sqlite and the selected backend (db-pg or db-mysql) to be compiled together. With `default = [\"db-sqlite\"]` in Cargo.toml line 13, the Makefile should pass `--no-default-features --features db-pg` (or `db-mysql`) to avoid multi-backend compilation:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile lines 284–288</summary>\n\n```makefile\ne2e-docker-pg:\n\tpython3 scripts/ci.py e2e --docker --cargo-build-args=\"--features db-pg,users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example\" --profile postgres $(E2E_ARGS)\n\ne2e-docker-mysql:\n\tpython3 scripts/ci.py e2e --docker --cargo-build-args=\"--features db-mysql,users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example\" --profile mariadb $(E2E_ARGS)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml` around lines 13 - 18, The Makefile e2e\ntargets e2e-docker-pg and e2e-docker-mysql are not disabling default Cargo\nfeatures, causing db-sqlite to be built alongside db-pg/db-mysql (Cargo.toml has\ndefault = [\"db-sqlite\"]); update the targets so the cargo build args include\n--no-default-features followed by --features db-pg (for e2e-docker-pg) or\n--features db-mysql (for e2e-docker-mysql) when invoking python3 scripts/ci.py\n(i.e., ensure the --cargo-build-args string begins with --no-default-features\nthen the appropriate --features list).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-27T10:08:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T10:08:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2731227746","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227746"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2731227746"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":13,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":10,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227751","pull_request_review_id":3710261661,"id":2731227751,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iyzpn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,247 @@\n+# HyperSpot Server Configuration - E2E MySQL/MariaDB\n+#\n+# Database Architecture Overview:\n+# ===============================\n+#\n+# HyperSpot uses a centralized DbManager that:\n+# 1. Loads global database server templates from `database.servers`\n+# 2. For each module, merges server template with module-specific overrides\n+# 3. Creates isolated database connections per module\n+# 4. Caches DbHandle instances for reuse within the same module\n+#\n+# Key principles:\n+# - Each module gets its own database connection (no sharing)\n+# - MySQL/MariaDB modules use separate databases (settings_db, users_info_db)\n+# - Configuration follows a clear precedence hierarchy\n+# - Environment variables are expanded (${VAR_NAME})\n+# - All paths are resolved relative to server.home_dir\n+\n+# Core server configuration (global section)\n+server:\n+  home_dir: \"~/.hyperspot\"\n+\n+# Database configuration (DbManager architecture)\n+#\n+# The database config has two levels:\n+# 1. Global \"servers\" - shared connection templates that modules can reference\n+# 2. Per-module configs - specific database settings for each module\n+#\n+# Configuration precedence (highest to lowest):\n+# - Module `params` map (highest priority)\n+# - Module DSN query params\n+# - Module fields (host, port, user, etc.)\n+# - Module DSN base\n+# - Server `params` map\n+# - Server DSN query params\n+# - Server fields\n+# - Server DSN base (lowest priority)\n+#\n+database:\n+  # Global server template with shared pool and connection settings\n+  # Modules can reference this server and override only credentials via DSN\n+  servers:\n+    mariadb_base:\n+      # Shared connection pool configuration\n+      pool:\n+        max_conns: 10              # Default pool size for all modules\n+        acquire_timeout: \"30s\"     # Default timeout for acquiring connections\n+        min_conns: 2               # Minimum connections to maintain\n+        idle_timeout: \"10m\"        # Close idle connections after 10 minutes\n+      \n+      # Default host/port (can be overridden by module DSN)\n+      host: \"mariadb\"\n+      port: 3306\n+\n+# Logging configuration (global section)\n+logging:\n+  # global section\n+  default:\n+    console_level: info\n+    file: \"logs/hyperspot-e2e.log\"\n+    file_level: info\n+    max_age_days: 28\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 10\n+  sqlx:\n+    console_level: debug\n+    file: \"logs/sql.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+  api_gateway:\n+    console_level: debug\n+    file: \"logs/api.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+    max_age_days: 28\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 100\n+  types_registry:\n+    console_level: info\n+    file: \"logs/types_registry.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+    max_age_days: 7\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 50\n+\n+\n+# Per-module configurations using MySQL/MariaDB\n+modules:\n+  api_gateway:\n+    # No database needed for api_gateway\n+    config:\n+      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8086\"\n+      enable_docs: true\n+      cors_enabled: false\n+\n+      # OpenAPI Documentation Configuration\n+      openapi:\n+        title: \"HyperSpot API\"\n+        version: \"0.1.0\"\n+        description: \"HyperSpot Server API Documentation\"\n+      defaults:\n+        body_limit_bytes: 64000000\n+        rate_limit:\n+          rps: 1000\n+          burst: 200\n+          in_flight: 64\n+\n+      # Authentication Configuration\n+      auth_disabled: true\n+      require_auth_by_default: true\n+\n+      # JWKS Configuration (replace with your OIDC provider)\n+      jwks_uri: \"http://localhost:8080/realms/dev/protocol/openid-connect/certs\"\n+      issuer: \"http://localhost:8080/realms/dev\"\n+      audience: \"api-gateway\"\n+\n+  # --- Tenant Resolver example (gateway + plugins) ---\n+  types_registry:\n+    config: {}\n+\n+  contoso_tr_plugin:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Contoso\"\n+      priority: 10\n+\n+  fabrikam_tr_plugin:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Fabrikam\"\n+      priority: 20\n+      tenants:\n+        # Root\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          parent_id: null\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 1\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000005\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 2 under 000...02\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000003\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          status: SOFT_DELETED\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: false\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000004\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 2 under 000...05\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000006\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000005\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+\n+  tenant_resolver_gateway:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Fabrikam\"\n+\n+  grpc_hub:\n+    config:\n+      listen_addr: \"uds:///tmp/hyperspot-grpc-e2e\"\n+\n+  users_info:\n+    # Module-specific database configuration using DSN\n+    # Inherits pool settings from mariadb_base server template\n+    database:\n+      server: \"mariadb_base\"      # Inherits pool and params from global template\n+      \n+      # Module-specific DSN overrides user, password, and database name\n+      dsn: \"mysql://users_info_user:${USERS_INFO_DB_PASSWORD}@mariadb:3306/users_info_db\"\n+      \n+      # Optional: Override specific pool settings for this module\n+      # pool:\n+      #   max_conns: 15            # Would override the global 10 connections\n+      \n+      # Alternative: Use fields instead of DSN to override only credentials\n+      # user: \"users_info_user\"\n+      # password: \"${USERS_INFO_DB_PASSWORD}\"\n+      # dbname: \"users_info_db\"\n+    \n+    # Module-specific application configuration\n+    config:\n+      default_page_size: 5\n+      max_page_size: 100\n+\n+  simple-user-settings:\n+    # Module-specific database configuration using DSN\n+    # Inherits pool settings from mariadb_base server template\n+    database:\n+      server: \"mariadb_base\"      # Inherits pool and params from global template\n+      \n+      # Module-specific DSN overrides user, password, and database name\n+      dsn: \"mysql://settings_user:${SETTINGS_DB_PASSWORD}@mariadb:3306/settings_db\"\n+      \n+      # Optional: Override specific pool settings for this module\n+      # pool:\n+      #   max_conns: 5             # Would override the global 10 connections\n+      \n+      # Alternative: Use fields instead of DSN to override only credentials\n+      # user: \"settings_user\"\n+      # password: \"${SETTINGS_DB_PASSWORD}\"\n+      # dbname: \"settings_db\"\n+    \n+    config: {}\n+\n+# OpenTelemetry tracing configuration\n+tracing:\n+  enabled: false\n+  service_name: \"hyperspot-api\"\n+\n+  # OTLP exporter configuration\n+  exporter:\n+    kind: \"otlp_grpc\"  # or \"otlp_http\"\n+    endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:14317\"  # Jaeger OTLP gRPC endpoint\n+    # For HTTP: endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/traces\"\n+    headers:\n+      # Add any required headers, e.g., for authentication\n+      # authorization: \"Bearer your-token\"\n+      uptrace-dsn: \"http://project1_secret@localhost:14318?grpc=14317\"\n+    timeout_ms: 5000\n+\n+  # Sampling configuration\n+  sampler:\n+    parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n+      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)","path":"config/e2e-local-mysql.yaml","commit_id":"3aaa2838f53c4cc41afdab0a9bb1502864ec8922","original_commit_id":"5b6951f1aca6e3b6d1bb1f663afc354f543a7841","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Misleading comment: ratio is 1.0 (100%) but comment says \"20%\".**\n\nThe comment states \"Sample 20% of traces\" but the actual ratio is `1.0`, which samples 100% of traces.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Fix comment</summary>\n\n```diff\n   sampler:\n     parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n-      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n+      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 100% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n  sampler:\n    parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 100% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/e2e-local-mysql.yaml` around lines 226 - 228, The comment next to\nsampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio is incorrect: ratio: 1.0 samples 100% but the\ncomment says \"Sample 20% of traces\"; update the comment to reflect the actual\nvalue (e.g., \"Sample 100% of traces\") or change the ratio to 0.2 if you intend\n20% sampling; edit the line that references sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio to\nkeep the numeric value and its explanatory comment consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-27T10:08:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T10:08:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2731227751","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227751"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2731227751"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731227751/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":226,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":228,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":228,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2732454088","pull_request_review_id":3711733552,"id":2732454088,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6i3fDI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,246 @@\n+# HyperSpot Server Configuration - E2E PostgreSQL\n+#\n+# Database Architecture Overview:\n+# ===============================\n+#\n+# HyperSpot uses a centralized DbManager that:\n+# 1. Loads global database server templates from `database.servers`\n+# 2. For each module, merges server template with module-specific overrides\n+# 3. Creates isolated database connections per module\n+# 4. Caches DbHandle instances for reuse within the same module\n+#\n+# Key principles:\n+# - Each module gets its own database connection (no sharing)\n+# - PostgreSQL modules use separate databases (settings_db, users_info_db)\n+# - Configuration follows a clear precedence hierarchy\n+# - Environment variables are expanded (${VAR_NAME})\n+# - All paths are resolved relative to server.home_dir\n+\n+# Core server configuration (global section)\n+server:\n+  home_dir: \"~/.hyperspot\"\n+\n+# Database configuration (DbManager architecture)\n+#\n+# The database config has two levels:\n+# 1. Global \"servers\" - shared connection templates that modules can reference\n+# 2. Per-module configs - specific database settings for each module\n+#\n+# Configuration precedence (highest to lowest):\n+# - Module `params` map (highest priority)\n+# - Module DSN query params\n+# - Module fields (host, port, user, etc.)\n+# - Module DSN base\n+# - Server `params` map\n+# - Server DSN query params\n+# - Server fields\n+# - Server DSN base (lowest priority)\n+#\n+database:\n+  # Global database servers - reusable connection templates\n+  # These define shared settings that multiple modules can inherit\n+  servers:\n+    postgres_base:\n+      # Shared connection pool configuration\n+      pool:\n+        max_conns: 10              # Default pool size for all modules\n+        acquire_timeout: \"30s\"     # Default timeout for acquiring connections\n+        min_conns: 2               # Minimum connections to maintain\n+        idle_timeout: \"10m\"        # Close idle connections after 10 minutes\n+      \n+      # Shared runtime parameters\n+      params:\n+        application_name: \"hyperspot-e2e\"  # Can be overridden per module\n+      \n+      # Default host/port (can be overridden by module DSN)\n+      host: \"postgres\"\n+      port: 5432\n+\n+# Logging configuration (global section)\n+logging:\n+  # global section\n+  default:\n+    console_level: info\n+    file: \"logs/hyperspot-e2e.log\"\n+    file_level: info\n+    max_age_days: 28\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 10\n+  sqlx:\n+    console_level: debug\n+    file: \"logs/sql.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+  api_gateway:\n+    console_level: debug\n+    file: \"logs/api.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+    max_age_days: 28\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 100\n+  types_registry:\n+    console_level: info\n+    file: \"logs/types_registry.log\"\n+    file_level: debug\n+    max_age_days: 7\n+    max_backups: 3\n+    max_size_mb: 50\n+\n+\n+# Per-module configurations using new structure\n+modules:\n+  api_gateway:\n+    # No database needed for api_gateway\n+    config:\n+      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8086\"\n+      enable_docs: true\n+      cors_enabled: false\n+\n+      # OpenAPI Documentation Configuration\n+      openapi:\n+        title: \"HyperSpot API\"\n+        version: \"0.1.0\"\n+        description: \"HyperSpot Server API Documentation\"\n+      defaults:\n+        body_limit_bytes: 64000000\n+        rate_limit:\n+          rps: 1000\n+          burst: 200\n+          in_flight: 64\n+\n+      # Authentication Configuration\n+      auth_disabled: true\n+      require_auth_by_default: true\n+\n+      # JWKS Configuration (replace with your OIDC provider)\n+      jwks_uri: \"http://localhost:8080/realms/dev/protocol/openid-connect/certs\"\n+      issuer: \"http://localhost:8080/realms/dev\"\n+      audience: \"api-gateway\"\n+\n+  # --- Tenant Resolver example (gateway + plugins) ---\n+  types_registry:\n+    config: {}\n+\n+  contoso_tr_plugin:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Contoso\"\n+      priority: 10\n+\n+  fabrikam_tr_plugin:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Fabrikam\"\n+      priority: 20\n+      tenants:\n+        # Root\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          parent_id: null\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 1\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000005\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 2 under 000...02\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000003\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          status: SOFT_DELETED\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: false\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000004\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+        # Level 2 under 000...05\n+        - id: \"00000000000000000000000000000006\"\n+          parent_id: \"00000000000000000000000000000005\"\n+          status: ACTIVE\n+          is_accessible_by_parent: true\n+\n+  tenant_resolver_gateway:\n+    config:\n+      vendor: \"Fabrikam\"\n+\n+  grpc_hub:\n+    config:\n+      listen_addr: \"uds:///tmp/hyperspot-grpc-e2e\"\n+\n+  users_info:\n+    # Module-specific database configuration\n+    database:\n+      # Reference to global server template defined above\n+      server: \"postgres_base\"\n+      \n+      # Module-specific DSN overrides user, password, and database name\n+      dsn: \"postgres://users_info_user:${USERS_INFO_DB_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/users_info_db?application_name=hyperspot-users-info\"\n+      \n+      # Alternative: Use fields instead of DSN to override only credentials\n+      # user: \"users_info_user\"\n+      # password: \"${USERS_INFO_DB_PASSWORD}\"\n+      # dbname: \"users_info_db\"\n+      # params:\n+      #   application_name: \"hyperspot-users-info\"\n+    \n+    # Module-specific application configuration\n+    config:\n+      default_page_size: 5\n+      max_page_size: 100\n+\n+  simple-user-settings:\n+    # Module-specific database configuration\n+    database:\n+      server: \"postgres_base\"\n+      \n+      # Module-specific DSN overrides user, password, and database name\n+      dsn: \"postgres://settings_user:${SETTINGS_DB_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/settings_db?application_name=hyperspot-settings\"\n+      \n+      # Alternative: Use fields instead of DSN to override only credentials\n+      # user: \"settings_user\"\n+      # password: \"${SETTINGS_DB_PASSWORD}\"\n+      # dbname: \"settings_db\"\n+      # params:\n+      #   application_name: \"hyperspot-settings\"\n+    \n+    config: {}\n+\n+# OpenTelemetry tracing configuration\n+tracing:\n+  enabled: false\n+  service_name: \"hyperspot-api\"\n+\n+  # OTLP exporter configuration\n+  exporter:\n+    kind: \"otlp_grpc\"  # or \"otlp_http\"\n+    endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:14317\"  # Jaeger OTLP gRPC endpoint\n+    # For HTTP: endpoint: \"http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/traces\"\n+    headers:\n+      # Add any required headers, e.g., for authentication\n+      # authorization: \"Bearer your-token\"\n+      uptrace-dsn: \"http://project1_secret@localhost:14318?grpc=14317\"\n+    timeout_ms: 5000\n+\n+  # Sampling configuration\n+  sampler:\n+    parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n+      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)","path":"config/e2e-local-postgres.yaml","commit_id":"3aaa2838f53c4cc41afdab0a9bb1502864ec8922","original_commit_id":"cc94130a3cf2af2fc173b9cd9678c55778e5bd73","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Misleading comment for sampling ratio.**\n\nThe comment states \"Sample 20% of traces\" but the actual ratio is `1.0` (100%).\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   # Sampling configuration\n   sampler:\n     parent_based_ratio: # parent_based_always_on | parent_based_ratio | always_on | always_off\n-      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 20% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n+      ratio: 1.0  # Sample 100% of traces (only used with ratio strategies)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/e2e-local-postgres.yaml` around lines 224 - 227, The comment for the\nsampler configuration is misleading: sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio is set to\n1.0 (100%) but the inline comment says \"Sample 20% of traces\"; update the\ncomment to reflect the actual ratio or change the ratio value to 0.2 depending\non intended behavior. Locate sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio in the config and\neither set ratio: 0.2 to match the \"20%\" comment or change the comment to\n\"Sample 100% of traces\" to match ratio: 1.0.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-27T15:03:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T15:03:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2732454088","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2732454088"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#discussion_r2732454088"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2732454088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":224,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":227,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":227,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2733388638","pull_request_review_id":3712917417,"id":2733388638,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6i7DNe","diff_hunk":"@@ -10,7 +10,13 @@ authors.workspace = true\n workspace = true\n \n [features]\n-default = []\n+default = [\"db-sqlite\"]\n+\n+# Database driv