Sy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 6**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>config/e2e-local.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `204-209`: **Update config/quickstart.yaml to use kebab-case module key.**\n> \n> The module registers itself as `simple-user-settings` (kebab-case), and the e2e-local.yaml change aligns with this. However, config/quickstart.yaml (line 123) still uses `simple_user_settings` (snake_case), creating an inconsistency. Update quickstart.yaml to use `simple-user-settings` to match the module's registered name and other config files.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/e2e-local-mysql.yaml`:\n- Around line 189-197: The DSN for the simple-user-settings module is pointing\nto localhost which will resolve to the API container instead of the MariaDB\nservice; update the dsn value under simple-user-settings (the database.dsn\nentry) to use the mariadb service hostname (e.g., replace \"localhost\" with\n\"mariadb\") so the connection targets the correct container.\n\nIn `@config/e2e-local-postgres.yaml`:\n- Around line 191-198: The simple-user-settings database DSN uses localhost\nwhich, inside the API container, points to itself and prevents connecting to the\nPostgres service; update the dsn value under simple-user-settings -> database to\nuse the Docker service hostname \"postgres\" (i.e. replace \"localhost\" with\n\"postgres\") or remove the explicit host from the DSN so it inherits the server\ntemplate, ensuring the service can reach the postgres container.\n\nIn `@examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 17-20: The Cargo.toml currently hardcodes \"sqlx-sqlite\" in the\nbase sea-orm and sea-orm-migration dependencies making feature flags additive;\nupdate the dependency entries for sea-orm and sea-orm-migration to remove the\n\"sqlx-sqlite\" feature from their default/base dependency lists and instead rely\nsolely on the feature groups db-sqlite, db-pg, and db-mysql (so the db-* feature\nflags become exclusive); locate the sea-orm and sea-orm-migration dependency\nentries referenced alongside the db-sqlite/db-pg/db-mysql feature definitions\nand remove \"sqlx-sqlite\" from those base dependency feature arrays.\n\nIn `@Makefile`:\n- Line 280: Fix the typo in the Makefile comment: change \"sqllite\" to \"sqlite\"\nin the comment string that reads \"## Run E2E tests in Docker environment\n(default: sqllite)\". Update that comment to \"## Run E2E tests in Docker\nenvironment (default: sqlite)\" so the spelling is correct.\n\nIn `@modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 15-20: The Cargo.toml currently leaves the \"sqlx-sqlite\" feature\nenabled unconditionally on the sea-orm dependency, so SQLite is always compiled;\nupdate Cargo.toml to remove \"sqlx-sqlite\" from the base sea-orm dependency and\ninstead only enable \"sqlx-sqlite\" when the db-sqlite feature is selected (i.e.,\nmove that feature flag into the db-sqlite feature group), and ensure other\ndependencies like sea-orm-migration/sqlx-sqlite are similarly gated by db-sqlite\nso each db-* feature (db-sqlite, db-pg, db-mysql) fully controls its SQLX flags\nfor sea-orm and sea-orm-migration.\n\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 291-303: The teardown logic is inconsistent with startup: when\nbuilding the compose command for stopping/removing services (the same pattern\nused with compose_cmd and run_cmd), ensure you apply the same profile handling\nas in the startup block that checks args.profile; specifically, in the teardown\nbranch that currently only adds \"--profile\" when args.profile is truthy, change\nit to add [\"--profile\", args.profile] if args.profile is set, otherwise add\n[\"--profile\", \"default\"] so the down/stop/remove compose_cmd uses the same\nprofile selection as the up path (reference args.profile, compose_cmd, and\nrun_cmd to locate the code).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`39-39`: **Consider gating `modkit-db` features similar to child modules.**\n\nThe `modkit-db` dependency unconditionally enables all three backends (`[\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"]`), while child modules like `simple_user_settings` and `users_info` are feature-gated. For consistency and to reduce compile-time/binary size, consider propagating the selected database feature to `modkit-db` as well.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional: Feature-gate modkit-db</summary>\n\n```diff\n+db-sqlite = [\"modkit-db/sqlite\", \"simple_user_settings/db-sqlite\", \"users_info?/db-sqlite\"]\n+db-pg = [\"modkit-db/pg\", \"simple_user_settings/db-pg\", \"users_info?/db-pg\"]\n+db-mysql = [\"modkit-db/mysql\", \"simple_user_settings/db-mysql\", \"users_info?/db-mysql\"]\n\n [dependencies]\n-modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"] }\n+modkit-db = { workspace = true }\n```\n\nThis would require ensuring at least one `db-*` feature is always enabled.\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`33-97`: **Optional: reduce Pg/Sqlite repo duplication.**  \n`PgSettingsRepository` and `SqliteSettingsRepository` implementations are identical. A shared struct or type alias would reduce maintenance when adding new methods.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`46-51`: **Document the bind_addr override for port 8086.**  \n`EXPOSE 8086` doesn’t guarantee the server binds to 8086. Consider documenting that docker-compose sets `APP__MODULES__api_gateway__CONFIG__BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8086` for E2E to avoid confusion.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n # Expose the HTTP port for E2E tests\n EXPOSE 8086\n \n # Run the binary with minimal config suitable for E2E tests\n+# NOTE: docker-compose overrides bind_addr via APP__MODULES__api_gateway__CONFIG__BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8086\n # Using --mock flag to use in-memory SQLite for any modules that need DB\n CMD [\"/app/hyperspot-server\", \"--config\", \"/app/config/quickstart.yaml\"]\n```\n</details>\nBased on learnings, please keep the 8086 override explicit in the Dockerfile comments.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`293-295`: **Redundant profile validation.**\n\nThe profile validation here duplicates the `choices` constraint already defined in argparse at line 598. Argparse will reject invalid profiles before `cmd_e2e` is called, making this check unreachable for invalid values.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Consider removing redundant validation</summary>\n\n```diff\n         # Add profile if specified, otherwise use 'default'\n         if args.profile:\n-            if args.profile not in ['default', 'postgres', 'mariadb']:\n-                print(f\"ERROR: Invalid profile '{args.profile}'. Must be 'default', 'postgres' or 'mariadb'\")\n-                sys.exit(1)\n             compose_cmd.extend([\"--profile\", args.profile])\n             print(f\"Using profile: {args.profile}\")\n         else:\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3709713864","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3709713864"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-27T08:15:29Z","commit_id":"9c084cde2f8fd42f50476f7d2cb0a6f2203241fd"},{"id":3709853755,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dH-A7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 4**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 17-20: The modkit-db dependency in users_info/Cargo.toml is\nmissing the \"mysql\" feature; update the modkit-db dependency declaration\n(modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [...] }) to include \"mysql\"\nalongside \"sqlite\", \"pg\", and \"insecure-escape\" so the modkit-db crate enables\nits mysql feature (mysql = [\"sea-orm/sqlx-mysql\"]) when building with --features\ndb-mysql; simply add \"mysql\" to the features array for modkit-db.\n\nIn\n`@modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs`:\n- Around line 306-321: The function coalesce_patch_expr_mysql currently builds\ninserted_expr using the deprecated VALUES(?) form; replace that with the\nrow-alias approach for MySQL >= 8.0.20 by producing a raw/custom expression that\nreferences the INSERT row alias (e.g., \"new.col\" or alias you choose) instead of\nVALUES(), or fall back to existing VALUES() only for MariaDB/MySQL < 8.0.20.\nConcretely, update the inserted_expr creation in coalesce_patch_expr_mysql to\nuse Expr::cust_with_exprs with the alias syntax expected in your ON DUPLICATE\nKEY UPDATE clause (or emit raw SQL there) and keep the None branch unchanged;\nensure the new/custom expression references the same column identifier used\nelsewhere so the generated UPDATE uses alias.col rather than VALUES(col).\n\nIn `@testing/docker/docker-compose.yml`:\n- Around line 9-25: The docker-compose setup is wrong because all three service\nvariants (hyperspot_api, hyperspot_api_pg, hyperspot_api_mariadb) share the same\nimage tag \"hyperspot-api:e2e\" so different CARGO_BUILD_ARGS would overwrite each\nother; fix by either building one image that includes both DB features (add\n\"--features db-pg,db-mysql\" to the build step used by the shared image), or give\neach variant a unique image tag and separate build blocks that pass distinct\nCARGO_BUILD_ARGS, or update documentation to require using ci.py which prebuilds\nimages with the correct CARGO_BUILD_ARGS; modify the build section and image\ntags in the x-hyperspot-api-common and the service entries referencing\n\"hyperspot-api:e2e\" accordingly so each runtime variant has the correct compiled\nfeatures.\n\nIn `@testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile`:\n- Around line 27-34: The comment claims the build is \"in release mode\" but the\nDockerfile runs cargo build without --release and later copies from\ntarget/debug; either change the comment to indicate a debug build or (preferred)\nenable release mode by adding --release to both cargo build invocations (the\nlines invoking cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --package=hyperspot-server and\nthe variant that includes $CARGO_BUILD_ARGS) and update the COPY that currently\nreferences target/debug/ to use target/release/ so the built binary and copy\nstep match release mode.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`39-39`: **Consider if all drivers should be unconditionally included.**\n\nLine 39 includes all drivers (`[\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"]`) regardless of which `db-*` feature is selected. This increases compile time and binary size. If runtime selection isn't needed, consider making the modkit-db features conditional:\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional: Make driver features conditional</summary>\n\n```diff\n-modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\", \"mysql\"] }\n+modkit-db = { workspace = true }\n```\n\nThen add to each feature:\n```diff\n-db-sqlite = [\"modkit-db/sqlite\", \"simple_user_settings/db-sqlite\", \"users_info?/db-sqlite\"]\n+db-sqlite = [\"modkit-db/sqlite\", \"simple_user_settings/db-sqlite\", \"users_info?/db-sqlite\"]\n```\n(Already done, but remove base features from the dependency line)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`45-124`: **Consider reducing duplicated repo method delegations.**  \n`find_by_user` and `upsert_full` are identical across Pg/MySql/Sqlite and can drift over time. A shared helper impl or small wrapper struct could keep this DRY.\n\n---\n\n`281-305`: **Doc comment mentions COALESCE, but the code chooses an expression up-front.**  \nThis is minor, but the current wording suggests SQL-level COALESCE when the decision is made in Rust. Consider updating the comments for accuracy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-/// Build COALESCE expression for patch semantics:\n-/// - If patch value is Some: use the new value\n-/// - If patch value is None: keep existing value (COALESCE(excluded.col, table.col))\n+/// Build patch expression:\n+/// - If patch value is Some: use the new value from INSERT\n+/// - If patch value is None: keep existing value (table.col)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3709853755","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3709853755"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-27T08:43:04Z","commit_id":"6c63b5122a93d9475a3918dfac22b2bc37eb9298"},{"id":3710261661,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dJhmd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 13-18: The Makefile e2e targets e2e-docker-pg and e2e-docker-mysql\nare not disabling default Cargo features, causing db-sqlite to be built\nalongside db-pg/db-mysql (Cargo.toml has default = [\"db-sqlite\"]); update the\ntargets so the cargo build args include --no-default-features followed by\n--features db-pg (for e2e-docker-pg) or --features db-mysql (for\ne2e-docker-mysql) when invoking python3 scripts/ci.py (i.e., ensure the\n--cargo-build-args string begins with --no-default-features then the appropriate\n--features list).\n\nIn `@config/e2e-local-mysql.yaml`:\n- Around line 226-228: The comment next to sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio is\nincorrect: ratio: 1.0 samples 100% but the comment says \"Sample 20% of traces\";\nupdate the comment to reflect the actual value (e.g., \"Sample 100% of traces\")\nor change the ratio to 0.2 if you intend 20% sampling; edit the line that\nreferences sampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio to keep the numeric value and its\nexplanatory comment consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`284-288`: **Missing help comments for new Make targets.**\n\nThe new `e2e-docker-pg` and `e2e-docker-mysql` targets lack the `##` comment prefix used by `make help` (via `scripts/make_help.py`). Other documented targets like `test-sqlite` (line 250) use this pattern.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Add help comments</summary>\n\n```diff\n+## Run E2E tests in Docker with PostgreSQL\n e2e-docker-pg:\n \tpython3 scripts/ci.py e2e --docker --cargo-build-args=\"--features db-pg,users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example\" --profile postgres $(E2E_ARGS)\n \n+## Run E2E tests in Docker with MariaDB\n e2e-docker-mysql:\n \tpython3 scripts/ci.py e2e --docker --cargo-build-args=\"--features db-mysql,users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example\" --profile mariadb $(E2E_ARGS)\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`271-271`: **Add new targets to `.PHONY` declaration.**\n\nThe new `e2e-docker-pg` and `e2e-docker-mysql` targets should be declared as phony to ensure they always run regardless of file existence.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Update .PHONY</summary>\n\n```diff\n-.PHONY: e2e e2e-local e2e-docker\n+.PHONY: e2e e2e-local e2e-docker e2e-docker-pg e2e-docker-mysql\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`172-186`: **Consider removing these unnecessary wrapper functions.**\n\n`upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl` and `upsert_patch_mysql_impl` simply delegate to `upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite` and `upsert_patch_impl_mysql` respectively. The trait implementations could call the `_impl` functions directly.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n #[async_trait]\n impl SettingsRepository for PgSettingsRepository {\n     // ...\n     async fn upsert_patch(\n         &self,\n         ctx: &SecurityContext,\n         patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n     ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n-        upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n+        upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n     }\n }\n```\n\nThen remove the wrapper functions at lines 172-186.\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`188-279`: **Reduce duplication between PostgreSQL/SQLite and MySQL implementations.**\n\nThese two functions are nearly identical—the only difference is which `coalesce_patch_expr_*` function is called. Consider extracting the common logic into a single function that accepts the COALESCE builder as a parameter.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n+type CoalesceBuilder = fn(entity::Column, Option<&String>) -> SimpleExpr;\n+\n+async fn upsert_patch_impl(\n+    db: &SecureConn,\n+    ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+    patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n+    coalesce_fn: CoalesceBuilder,\n+) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n+    let user_id = ctx.subject_id();\n+    let tenant_id = ctx.tenant_id();\n+\n+    let theme_expr = coalesce_fn(entity::Column::Theme, patch.theme.as_ref());\n+    let language_expr = coalesce_fn(entity::Column::Language, patch.language.as_ref());\n+\n+    let active_model = entity::ActiveModel {\n+        tenant_id: ActiveValue::Set(tenant_id),\n+        user_id: ActiveValue::Set(user_id),\n+        theme: ActiveValue::Set(patch.theme.clone()),\n+        language: ActiveValue::Set(patch.language.clone()),\n+    };\n+\n+    SettingsEntity::insert(active_model)\n+        .on_conflict(\n+            OnConflict::columns([entity::Column::TenantId, entity::Column::UserId])\n+                .value(entity::Column::Theme, theme_expr)\n+                .value(entity::Column::Language, language_expr)\n+                .to_owned(),\n+        )\n+        .exec(db.conn())\n+        .await?;\n+\n+    let scope = AccessScope::both(vec![tenant_id], vec![user_id]);\n+    let result = db\n+        .find::<SettingsEntity>(&scope)\n+        .one(db.conn())\n+        .await?\n+        .map(Into::into)\n+        .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(\"row must exist after successful upsert\"))?;\n+\n+    Ok(result)\n+}\n```\n\nThen call with:\n- `upsert_patch_impl(db, ctx, patch, coalesce_patch_expr_pg_sqlite).await` for Pg/SQLite\n- `upsert_patch_impl(db, ctx, patch, coalesce_patch_expr_mysql).await` for MySQL\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`281-301`: **Doc comment mentions COALESCE but the function doesn't use it.**\n\nThe docstring says \"COALESCE(excluded.col, table.col)\" but the implementation returns either the `excluded.col` expression directly (when `Some`) or `table.col` (when `None`)—no actual `COALESCE` SQL function is involved. Consider updating the comment to accurately describe the conditional expression logic.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-/// Build COALESCE expression for patch semantics:\n+/// Build conditional expression for patch semantics:\n /// - If patch value is Some: use the new value\n-/// - If patch value is None: keep existing value (COALESCE(excluded.col, table.col))\n+/// - If patch value is None: keep existing value (table.col)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3710261661","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3710261661"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-27T10:08:23Z","commit_id":"5b6951f1aca6e3b6d1bb1f663afc354f543a7841"},{"id":3711733552,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dPI8w","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@config/e2e-local-postgres.yaml`:\n- Around line 224-227: The comment for the sampler configuration is misleading:\nsampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio is set to 1.0 (100%) but the inline comment\nsays \"Sample 20% of traces\"; update the comment to reflect the actual ratio or\nchange the ratio value to 0.2 depending on intended behavior. Locate\nsampler.parent_based_ratio.ratio in the config and either set ratio: 0.2 to\nmatch the \"20%\" comment or change the comment to \"Sample 100% of traces\" to\nmatch ratio: 1.0.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`540-543`: **Missing `profile` and `cargo_build_args` attributes in `cmd_all` invocation.**\n\n`cmd_all` creates an `argparse.Namespace` with only `docker=False` and `pytest_args=[]`, but `cmd_e2e` may access `args.profile` (line 266, 293) and `args.cargo_build_args` (line 277). While these code paths are guarded by `args.docker`, future refactoring could introduce an `AttributeError` if the guards change.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix for defensive consistency</summary>\n\n```diff\n     step(\"Running e2e-local\")\n-    cmd_e2e(argparse.Namespace(docker=False, pytest_args=[]))\n+    cmd_e2e(argparse.Namespace(docker=False, pytest_args=[], profile=None, cargo_build_args=None))\n     print(\"All (full pipeline) completed\")\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`172-186`: **Consider removing unnecessary wrapper functions.**\n\n`upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl` and `upsert_patch_mysql_impl` are single-line wrappers that directly call `upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite` and `upsert_patch_impl_mysql` respectively, adding indirection without value.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed simplification</summary>\n\nCall the implementation functions directly from the trait impls:\n\n```diff\n #[async_trait]\n impl SettingsRepository for PgSettingsRepository {\n     // ...\n     async fn upsert_patch(\n         &self,\n         ctx: &SecurityContext,\n         patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n     ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n-        upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n+        upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n     }\n }\n```\n\nThen remove the wrapper functions at lines 172-186.\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-20`: **Consider enforcing a single `db-*` feature at compile time.**\n\nMultiple db features can be enabled together, which may pull multiple SQLx drivers and make runtime selection ambiguous. A small `compile_error!` guard in the crate root helps keep the configuration explicit.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Example guard (place in crate root, e.g., src/lib.rs)</summary>\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(all(feature = \"db-sqlite\", any(feature = \"db-pg\", feature = \"db-mysql\")))]\ncompile_error!(\"Select only one of: db-sqlite, db-pg, db-mysql.\");\n\n#[cfg(all(feature = \"db-pg\", feature = \"db-mysql\"))]\ncompile_error!(\"Select only one of: db-sqlite, db-pg, db-mysql.\");\n\n#[cfg(not(any(feature = \"db-sqlite\", feature = \"db-pg\", feature = \"db-mysql\")))]\ncompile_error!(\"Select one of: db-sqlite, db-pg, db-mysql.\");\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3711733552","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3711733552"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-27T15:03:06Z","commit_id":"cc94130a3cf2af2fc173b9cd9678c55778e5bd73"},{"id":3715115530,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dcCoK","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D"