ents (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`172-186`: **Consider removing unnecessary wrapper functions.**\n\n`upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl` and `upsert_patch_mysql_impl` are single-line wrappers that just call `upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite` and `upsert_patch_impl_mysql` respectively. The trait methods could call the `_impl` functions directly.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n #[async_trait]\n impl SettingsRepository for PgSettingsRepository {\n     // ...\n     async fn upsert_patch(\n         &self,\n         ctx: &SecurityContext,\n         patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n     ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n-        upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n+        upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite(&self.db, ctx, patch).await\n     }\n }\n \n-async fn upsert_patch_pg_sqlite_impl(\n-    db: &SecureConn,\n-    ctx: &SecurityContext,\n-    patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n-) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n-    upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite(db, ctx, patch).await\n-}\n-\n-async fn upsert_patch_mysql_impl(\n-    db: &SecureConn,\n-    ctx: &SecurityContext,\n-    patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n-) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n-    upsert_patch_impl_mysql(db, ctx, patch).await\n-}\n```\n\nApply similar changes to `SqliteSettingsRepository` and `MySqlSettingsRepository`.\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`188-279`: **Consider extracting common upsert_patch logic to reduce duplication.**\n\n`upsert_patch_impl_pg_sqlite` and `upsert_patch_impl_mysql` are nearly identical (~90% shared code). The only difference is the `coalesce_patch_expr_*` function called. Consider refactoring to a single parameterized function.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactoring approach</summary>\n\n```rust\nasync fn upsert_patch_impl<F>(\n    db: &SecureConn,\n    ctx: &SecurityContext,\n    patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n    coalesce_fn: F,\n) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings>\nwhere\n    F: Fn(entity::Column, Option<&String>) -> SimpleExpr,\n{\n    let user_id = ctx.subject_id();\n    let tenant_id = ctx.tenant_id();\n\n    let theme_expr = coalesce_fn(entity::Column::Theme, patch.theme.as_ref());\n    let language_expr = coalesce_fn(entity::Column::Language, patch.language.as_ref());\n\n    let active_model = entity::ActiveModel {\n        tenant_id: ActiveValue::Set(tenant_id),\n        user_id: ActiveValue::Set(user_id),\n        theme: ActiveValue::Set(patch.theme.clone()),\n        language: ActiveValue::Set(patch.language.clone()),\n    };\n\n    SettingsEntity::insert(active_model)\n        .on_conflict(\n            OnConflict::columns([entity::Column::TenantId, entity::Column::UserId])\n                .value(entity::Column::Theme, theme_expr)\n                .value(entity::Column::Language, language_expr)\n                .to_owned(),\n        )\n        .exec(db.conn())\n        .await?;\n\n    let scope = AccessScope::both(vec![tenant_id], vec![user_id]);\n    let result = db\n        .find::<SettingsEntity>(&scope)\n        .one(db.conn())\n        .await?\n        .map(Into::into)\n        .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(\"row must exist after successful upsert\"))?;\n\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\nThen call it with the appropriate coalesce function:\n```rust\nupsert_patch_impl(db, ctx, patch, coalesce_patch_expr_pg_sqlite).await\nupsert_patch_impl(db, ctx, patch, coalesce_patch_expr_mysql).await\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715115530","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715115530"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-28T07:57:43Z","commit_id":"c1dcd23bc027571f63645292c0ff470960a700ac"},{"id":3715288206,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dcsyO","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_types_registry_list.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `221-224`: **Update remaining `gtsId` references to `gts_id`.**\n> \n> These assertions still use the old camelCase field name, which will raise `KeyError` once the API response is snake_case. Please update all remaining uses to `gts_id`.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -        for entity in entities:\n> -            assert entity.get(\"package\") == \"list\" or \".list.\" in entity[\"gtsId\"], (\n> -                f\"Entity should have package 'list': {entity['gtsId']}\"\n> -            )\n> +        for entity in entities:\n> +            assert entity.get(\"package\") == \"list\" or \".list.\" in entity[\"gts_id\"], (\n> +                f\"Entity should have package 'list': {entity['gts_id']}\"\n> +            )\n> ...\n> -        for entity in entities:\n> -            assert entity.get(\"namespace\") == \"acme\" or \".acme.\" in entity[\"gtsId\"], (\n> -                f\"Entity should have namespace 'acme': {entity['gtsId']}\"\n> -            )\n> +        for entity in entities:\n> +            assert entity.get(\"namespace\") == \"acme\" or \".acme.\" in entity[\"gts_id\"], (\n> +                f\"Entity should have namespace 'acme': {entity['gts_id']}\"\n> +            )\n> ...\n> -        for entity in entities:\n> -            assert entity[\"gtsId\"].startswith(\"gts.e2e.list.acme.\"), (\n> -                f\"Entity should match pattern 'gts.e2e.list.acme.*': {entity['gtsId']}\"\n> -            )\n> +        for entity in entities:\n> +            assert entity[\"gts_id\"].startswith(\"gts.e2e.list.acme.\"), (\n> +                f\"Entity should match pattern 'gts.e2e.list.acme.*': {entity['gts_id']}\"\n> +            )\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 256-259, 291-294\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 266-274: The image tag creation logic treats \"--profile default\"\nlike any other profile and adds \"-default\" to profile_suffix, causing tags like\n\"hyperspot-api-default:e2e\" while compose expects \"hyperspot-api:e2e\"; update\nthe conditional that sets profile_suffix (the variable using args.profile) so it\nonly appends \"-{args.profile}\" when args.profile is truthy and not equal to the\nstring \"default\", leaving profile_suffix as an empty string for the default\nprofile so the build_cmd tag f\"hyperspot-api{profile_suffix}:e2e\" matches\ncompose.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715288206","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715288206"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-28T08:38:17Z","commit_id":"dce8bcaf4537a5731dd64d59f09e3250e8bed5e5"},{"id":3715453710,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7ddVMO","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 0**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/infra/storage/migrations/initial_001.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `13-47`: **Avoid editing an already-applied migration; add a new migration for type changes.**\n> \n> If this migration has already run in any environment, changing it in place won’t update existing schemas (the migration is marked applied and `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` is a no‑op). That leaves old VARCHAR/TEXT columns while the code now expects binary UUIDs. Please add a new forward migration to alter/rebuild the table per backend (and plan for data conversion), rather than modifying the initial migration in place.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`271-288`: **Add new E2E targets to `.PHONY`.**  \nPrevents name collisions if files with those names appear.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-.PHONY: e2e e2e-local e2e-docker\n+.PHONY: e2e e2e-local e2e-docker e2e-docker-pg e2e-docker-mysql\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>config/e2e-local-mysql.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-53`: **Well-structured database architecture documentation and global template.**\n\nThe configuration header clearly documents the DbManager architecture and precedence hierarchy. The `mariadb_base` server template provides sensible pool defaults.\n\nOne minor inconsistency: the PostgreSQL config includes a `params` section with `application_name` in the server template, but this MariaDB config omits it. Consider adding a similar `params` block for consistency if MariaDB supports application-level naming.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715453710","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715453710"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-28T09:11:09Z","commit_id":"b785933afac0b45a303280ac0fe806eb1e6cb93c"},{"id":3715852885,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7de2pV","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/docker/docker-compose.yml`:\n- Around line 32-35: Ensure all hardcoded DB credentials in docker-compose.yml\nare consistent with the DSNs and config variables used by the test modules:\nverify POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_PASSWORD/POSTGRES_DB, the MariaDB password entries\n(e.g., root_pass and hyperspot_pass), and the module-specific credentials\nusers_info_pass and settings_pass match the environment variables referenced as\n${USERS_INFO_DB_PASSWORD} and ${SETTINGS_DB_PASSWORD} in e2e-local-postgres.yaml\nand e2e-local-mysql.yaml; if any mismatch, update the values in\ndocker-compose.yml (POSTGRES_PASSWORD, MariaDB password envs, and\nusers_info_pass/settings_pass) to match the DSN/config variable values so the\nE2E services authenticate correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715852885","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/320#pullrequestreview-3715852885"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/320"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-28T10:16:30Z","commit_id":"b4b05009b99b27188cb755c895f2225364794394"}]},{"source_pr_number":244,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/244","source_state":"open","source_author":"binarycode","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #244] [WIP] docs(workflow_engine): add PRD and ADRs for Workflow Engine","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"workflow-engine-prd-and-adrs","pr_head_sha":"1c48223410242c5fedd2b765219b76d85953916d","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"binarycode","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/244","id":3176236597,"node