s://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T05:40:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T05:40:42Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ## Review skipped\n> \n> Draft detected.\n> \n> Please check the settings in the CodeRabbit UI or the `.coderabbit.yaml` file in this repository. To trigger a single review, invoke the `@coderabbitai review` command.\n> \n> You can disable this status message by setting the `reviews.review_status` to `false` in the CodeRabbit configuration file.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3752987271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3802306967","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/243#issuecomment-3802306967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/243","id":3802306967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7iopmX","user":{"login":"ainetx","id":244471386,"node_id":"U_kgDODpJWWg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244471386?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx","html_url":"https://github.com/ainetx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T23:44:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:46:26Z","body":"FDD Style Overall Design\r\n\r\n# Technical Design: Hyperspot — Serverless Runtime\r\n\r\n## A. Architecture Overview\r\n\r\n### Architectural Vision\r\n\r\nHyperspot Serverless Runtime provides a unified, tenant-safe execution surface for compute entrypoints that can behave as short-lived functions or durable workflows. The design centers on a single **entrypoint definition model** identified by stable **GTS type IDs** (JSON Schemas) and a single **invocation API** that returns a consistent **InvocationRecord** across sync and async execution.\r\n\r\nThe system prioritizes operability and correctness under multi-tenant conditions: every invocation is tracked via an `invocation_id`, observability metadata is carried end-to-end, and failures are represented via a structured error taxonomy. Runtime implementations (e.g., Starlark) may determine whether a given entrypoint should be executed with workflow semantics (durable suspend/resume) by validating code for durability primitives.\r\n\r\nThis document intentionally defines system-wide constraints, principles, and authoritative contract surfaces. Decision rationale and debates are captured in ADRs (see references in Section B).\r\n\r\n### Architecture drivers\r\n\r\n#### Product requirements\r\n\r\n| FDD ID | Solution short description |\r\n|--------|----------------------------|\r\n| `fdd-hyperspot-fr-entrypoint-definitions` | Use GTS-identified JSON Schema types to define entrypoints (base + derived types). |\r\n| `fdd-hyperspot-fr-unified-invocation-api` | Expose a single invocation surface returning a stable `InvocationRecord` for both sync and async modes. |\r\n| `fdd-hyperspot-fr-observability` | Include correlation/tracing identifiers and execution metrics in invocation responses. |\r\n| `fdd-hyperspot-fr-structured-errors` | Standardize errors via a base envelope plus derived error classes (upstream, transport, runtime, code). |\r\n| `fdd-hyperspot-fr-cancel-and-timeline` | Support cancelation and timeline history endpoints for operational control and debugging. |\r\n\r\n### Architecture Layers\r\n\r\n| Layer | Responsibility | Technology |\r\n|-------|---------------|------------|\r\n| Presentation | External control plane API surface for registration and invocation; authentication and authorization entry points | HTTP API (REST/JSON) |\r\n| Application | Invocation orchestration, policy enforcement (tenant scoping, throttling), lifecycle management (queued/running/suspended/finished) | Runtime control-plane services |\r\n| Domain | Core domain concepts: EntrypointDefinition, InvocationRecord, Error taxonomy, Status lifecycle, Observability | GTS IDs + JSON Schema-driven models |\r\n| Infrastructure | Durable storage, queues, execution backends/runtimes, tracing/metrics sinks | DB/Queue/Runtime adapters (implementation-dependent) |\r\n\r\n## B. Principles & Constraints\r\n\r\n### B.1: Design Principles\r\n\r\n#### Unified Invocation Surface\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-principle-unified-invocation-surface`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nAll entrypoints (functions and workflows) MUST be invocable through a single consistent API surface and MUST return a consistent invocation record shape. This reduces client complexity, enables consistent tooling, and enforces uniform operational semantics across runtimes.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n#### Tenant-Scoped Everything\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-principle-tenant-scoped-everything`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nInvocation records, caching hints, observability fields, and debug data MUST be scoped by tenant and protected by authorization. No API response or cache reuse behavior may cross tenant boundaries.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n#### Structured Errors Over Strings\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-principle-structured-errors`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nErrors MUST be represented using a base envelope and derived typed classes with structured `details` payloads. Clients SHOULD be able to implement stable retry policies, UIs, and telemetry aggregation without parsing unstructured strings.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n#### Operability First\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-principle-operability-first`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nEvery invocation MUST be observable: correlation identifiers, trace identifiers, and key execution metrics MUST be available. Debugging MUST be possible without relying exclusively on logs, via status, timeline, and debug/call-trace APIs.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n### B.2: Constraints\r\n\r\n#### URL Input Compatibility (Async by Default)\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-constraint-async-default`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nThe platform MUST support asynchronous invocation as the default mode to avoid coupling correctness to HTTP gateway timeouts. Synchronous mode MAY exist for short-lived operations but MUST remain bounded by platform limits and operational safeguards.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n#### Authorization on Observability Surfaces\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-constraint-authz-on-debug`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nAll observability endpoints (`/invocations/{id}`, `/timeline`, `/debug`, `/debug/calls`) MUST enforce strict authorization and MUST prevent data leakage. Debug fields MUST be considered sensitive and MUST be subject to auditing and access controls.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n#### Runtime-Defined Semantics Must Be Validated\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-constraint-runtime-validation-required`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints`\r\n\r\nWorkflow-like semantics (durable suspend/resume, checkpoints, event waiting) MUST be enabled only when the runtime validates that the entrypoint code uses durability primitives correctly. Invalid code MUST fail fast via a typed code error.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n\r\n## C. Technical Architecture\r\n\r\n### C.1: Domain Model\r\n\r\n**Technology**: GTS / JSON Schema (type-identified schemas)  \r\n**Location**: [modules/serverless_runtime/docs/2_ADR_ENTRYPOINT.md](../modules/serverless_runtime/docs/2_ADR_ENTRYPOINT.md)\r\n\r\n**Core Entities**:\r\n\r\n- **EntrypointDefinition**\r\n  - Identified by a GTS type `$id` (e.g., `gts://gts.x.core.faas.func.v1~vendor.app.namespace.func_name.v1~`)\r\n  - Contains `params`, `returns`, `errors`, and `traits` (timeouts, resources, invocation modes, caching hints, runtime selector)\r\n  - Contains `implementation` with runtime language + inline or referenced source\r\n\r\n- **InvocationRecord**\r\n  - Identified by `invocation_id` (opaque)\r\n  - Tracks `entrypoint_id`, `status`, timestamps, `result` or `error`, and `observability` metrics\r\n  - Represents both pending and completed invocations\r\n\r\n- **Error (base + derived types)**\r\n  - Base envelope: `gts.x.core.faas.err.v1~` with `id`, `message`, `details`\r\n  - Derived classes include:\r\n    - Upstream HTTP error\r\n    - Upstream transport errors (timeout / no connection)\r\n    - Runtime resource errors (timeout, memory, CPU, canceled)\r\n    - Code validation/compile/execute errors\r\n\r\n- **InvocationStatus**\r\n  - Lifecycle identifiers:\r\n    - queued, running, suspended, succeeded, failed, canceled\r\n\r\n- **TimelineItem**\r\n  - Time-ordered history of invocation lifecycle and step execution events\r\n  - Supports pagination via cursor\r\n\r\n- **DebugInfo**\r\n  - Runtime-provided diagnostic location and stack information\r\n  - Optional call-trace page describing downstream calls with duration and responses\r\n\r\n**Relationships**:\r\n\r\n- EntrypointDefinition 1..N → InvocationRecord (many invocations per entrypoint)\r\n- InvocationRecord 0..1 → Error (only when failed)\r\n- InvocationRecord 0..N → TimelineItem (history stream)\r\n- InvocationRecord 0..1 → DebugInfo (current or last-known debug snapshot)\r\n\r\n### C.2: Component Model\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nflowchart LR\r\n  Client[Client / Control Plane Caller] -->|HTTP| API[Serverless Runtime API]\r\n\r\n  API --> Auth[AuthN/AuthZ]\r\n  API --> Registry[Entrypoint Registry]\r\n  API --> Invocations[Invocation Manager]\r\n\r\n  Invocations --> Queue[Work Queue / Scheduler]\r\n  Queue --> Executor[\"Runtime Executor - Starlark\"]\r\n\r\n  Executor --> Store[Invocation Store]\r\n  Invocations --> Store\r\n\r\n  Invocations --> Obs[Observability Sink]\r\n  Executor --> Obs\r\n\r\n  Invocations --> Timeline[Timeline Service]\r\n  Timeline --> Store\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Components**:\r\n\r\n- **Serverless Runtime API**\r\n  - Handles requests for invocation start/status/cancel/timeline/debug\r\n  - Enforces request validation, rate limiting, and tenant scoping\r\n\r\n- **AuthN/AuthZ**\r\n  - Validates caller identity and tenant scope\r\n  - Enforces access control for debug and status endpoints\r\n\r\n- **Entrypoint Registry**\r\n  - Stores and retrieves entrypoint definitions by GTS ID\r\n  - Enforces that definitions pin required traits (runtime, limits, invocation modes)\r\n\r\n- **Invocation Manager**\r\n  - Creates durable invocation records (unless dry-run)\r\n  - Transitions statuses and coordinates execution scheduling\r\n  - Implements idempotency start semantics (Idempotency-Key)\r\n\r\n- **Work Queue / Scheduler**\r\n  - Buffers async work and drives worker concurrency\r\n  - Enables throttling and per-tenant limits\r\n\r\n- **Runtime Executor**\r\n  - Validates code (validate/compile/execute phases)\r\n  - Executes entrypoint code and produces result/errors\r\n  - May emit workflow semantics (suspend/resume) based on runtime primitives\r\n\r\n- **Invocation Store**\r\n  - Persistent source of truth for InvocationRecord and timeline\r\n  - Supports query by invocation_id, tenant, entrypoint_id\r\n\r\n- **Timeline Service**\r\n  - Provides paginated timeline endpoints\r\n  - Normalizes internal events into a stable external representation\r\n\r\n- **Observability Sink**\r\n  - Exposes tracing identifiers and metrics for monitoring\r\n  - Ensures observability output does not leak cross-tenant data\r\n\r\n**Interactions**:\r\n\r\n- API → AuthN/AuthZ: authorize call and tenant scope\r\n- API → Invocation Manager: start invocation, fetch status, cancel invocation\r\n- Invocation Manager → Store: persist records and state transitions\r\n- Invocation Manager → Scheduler: enqueue async work\r\n- Executor → Store: write results/errors and debug snapshots\r\n- API → Timeline Service: read time-ordered history\r\n\r\n### C.3: API Contracts\r\n\r\n**Technology**: REST/JSON (contract shape defined in ADR; to be extracted into machine-readable OpenAPI in repo)  \r\n**Location**: [modules/serverless_runtime/docs/2_ADR_ENTRYPOINT.md](../modules/serverless_runtime/docs/2_ADR_ENTRYPOINT.md)\r\n\r\n**Endpoints Overview**:\r\n\r\n- `POST /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations`\r\n  - Starts an invocation (sync or async) or performs `dry_run` validation\r\n  - Returns `InvocationRecord` (completed for sync, pending for async)\r\n\r\n- `GET /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations/{invocation_id}`\r\n  - Returns current `InvocationRecord` state\r\n\r\n- `POST /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations/{invocation_id}:cancel`\r\n  - Requests cancellation of a running or queued invocation\r\n\r\n- `GET /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations/{invocation_id}/timeline`\r\n  - Returns paginated invocation timeline items\r\n\r\n- `GET /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations/{invocation_id}/debug`\r\n  - Returns `InvocationRecord` plus debug location/stack when available\r\n\r\n- `GET /api/serverless-runtime/v1/invocations/{invocation_id}/debug/calls`\r\n  - Returns paginated ordered call list with params, duration, and responses\r\n\r\n**Error Handling Expectations**:\r\n\r\n- All errors returned as typed envelopes (base + derived)\r\n- HTTP status codes MUST reflect lifecycle-level semantics (e.g., 202 for async accepted)\r\n- Throttling MUST return 429 with Retry-After when applicable\r\n\r\n**AuthN/AuthZ Entry Points**:\r\n\r\n- Caller identity MUST be validated on every endpoint\r\n- Debug endpoints MUST require stronger authorization than status retrieval in most deployments\r\n\r\n### C.4: Interactions & Sequences\r\n\r\n**Async invocation start and status polling**:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n  participant Client\r\n  participant API as Serverless Runtime API\r\n  participant Inv as Invocation Manager\r\n  participant Q as Scheduler/Queue\r\n  participant Exec as Runtime Executor\r\n  participant Store as Invocation Store\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: POST /invocations (mode=async)\r\n  API->>Inv: create invocation record\r\n  Inv->>Store: persist status=queued\r\n  Inv->>Q: enqueue job(invocation_id)\r\n  API-->>Client: 202 InvocationRecord(queued)\r\n\r\n  Q->>Exec: dispatch job(invocation_id)\r\n  Exec->>Store: update status=running\r\n  Exec->>Store: update status=succeeded/failed + result/error\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: GET /invocations/{id}\r\n  API->>Store: read InvocationRecord\r\n  API-->>Client: 200 InvocationRecord(current)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Cancel execution**:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n  participant Client\r\n  participant API as Serverless Runtime API\r\n  participant Inv as Invocation Manager\r\n  participant Store as Invocation Store\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: POST /invocations/{id}:cancel\r\n  API->>Inv: request cancel(id)\r\n  Inv->>Store: mark cancel requested / status transition\r\n  API-->>Client: 202 Accepted\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Timeline retrieval**:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n  participant Client\r\n  participant API as Serverless Runtime API\r\n  participant Timeline as Timeline Service\r\n  participant Store as Invocation Store\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: GET /invocations/{id}/timeline?limit=25\r\n  API->>Timeline: query timeline\r\n  Timeline->>Store: read timeline items\r\n  API-->>Client: 200 items + page_info\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Debug and call-trace retrieval**:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n  participant Client\r\n  participant API as Serverless Runtime API\r\n  participant Store as Invocation Store\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: GET /invocations/{id}/debug\r\n  API->>Store: read InvocationRecord + debug snapshot\r\n  API-->>Client: 200 InvocationRecord + debug(location,stack)\r\n\r\n  Client->>API: GET /invocations/{id}/debug/calls?limit=25\r\n  API->>Store: read call trace page\r\n  API-->>Client: 200 InvocationRecord + debug.page(items,page_info)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## D. Additional Context\r\n\r\n**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-design-context-content-only-initial`\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\nThis DESIGN.md was generated in a content-only mode without access to a local repository root, adapter configuration, or PRD.md content. Therefore:\r\n- The `fdd-hyperspot-fr-*` IDs in Section A are provisional placeholders for PRD-aligned requirement/capability IDs and MUST be reconciled with the actual PRD once available.\r\n- The ADR reference `fdd-hyperspot-adr-serverless-runtime-entrypoints` is expected to exist in the ADR set; if the repo uses different ADR numbering/IDs, references MUST be updated.\r\n- File links in Section C intentionally reference an existing repo document path (`modules/serverless_runtime/docs/2_ADR_ENTRYPOINT.md`) as the authoritative source for schema/API details until machine-readable contracts (OpenAPI/JSON Schema files) are extracted into dedicated contract directories.\r\n<!-- fdd-id-content -->\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3802306967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3807796470","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/243#issuecomment-3807796470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/243","id":3807796470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7i9lz2","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T22:16:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T22:16:23Z","body":"There are unresolved review comments awaiting response.\n\nUnanswered human review threads: 55\nUnresolved comments: 55","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3807796470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u