Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4578046871","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1982#issuecomment-4578046871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1982","id":4578046871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABEN9zlw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T17:36:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T17:36:56Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `dab16912-f3af-40d8-ad29-92a49a90ff6a`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 39a05154eb71c475bb3fd324f45e01a36a626fab and e06ab439d61ebc7a79acfd3f1c91a63f194a367b.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (5)</summary>\n\n* `Makefile`\n* `libs/modkit-http/src/builder.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-http/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-http/tests/no_crypto_provider_fips.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR restructures TLS error handling in `modkit-http` to support explicit FIPS provider management with fail-closed semantics. `TlsConfigError` transitions from a boxed error type alias to a discriminated enum with FIPS-specific variants, the client config builder auto-installs the test FIPS provider and requires a pre-installed provider in production, and new integration tests validate the fail-closed behavior.\n\n## Changes\n\n**FIPS TLS Configuration Error and Provider Handling**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**TlsConfigError enum definition with test FIPS provider auto-install** <br> `libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs`|TlsConfigError is now a structured enum with variants `NoCryptoProvider`, `FipsHardeningFailed(String)`, and `Other(...)` for foreign errors. A test-only module auto-installs the platform FIPS provider during in-crate unit tests.|\n|**FIPS-aware TLS client config builder with fail-closed semantics** <br> `libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs`|The build_client_config function auto-installs the test FIPS provider, requires CryptoProvider::get_default() when --features fips is active, fails closed with NoCryptoProvider if absent, and wraps all error cases as the new TlsConfigError variants.|\n|**Public API adaptation: TlsConfigError re-export and error boxing** <br> `libs/modkit-http/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-http/src/builder.rs`|TlsConfigError is re-exported at the crate root and explicitly boxed when mapped into HttpError::Tls in build_https_connector, preserving the error source chain.|\n|**FIPS integration test for fail-closed provider absence scenario** <br> `libs/modkit-http/tests/no_crypto_provider_fips.rs`|New #[test] validates that building HttpClient fails with HttpError::Tls → TlsConfigError::NoCryptoProvider when no CryptoProvider is installed before the build attempt.|\n|**Makefile test-fips target expansion for dual-package coverage** <br> `Makefile`|The test-fips target now runs cargo nextest for both cyberware-modkit and cyberware-modkit-http in a single invocation using per-package feature syntax.|\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n> 🐰 *Error enums now fail closed, like a bunny tucked safe inside,*  \n> *FIPS providers installed during tests with trusty guide,*  \n> *No crypto? We catch it swift—no surprises to hide!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4578046871/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3328900871","pull_request_review_id":4395530909,"id":3328900871,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Gav8H","diff_hunk":"@@ -178,17 +275,16 @@ fn build_client_config(\n fn apply_fips_hardening(cfg: &mut rustls::ClientConfig) -> Result<(), TlsConfigError> {\n     cfg.require_ems = true;\n     if !cfg.fips() {\n-        return Err(\n+        return Err(TlsConfigError::FipsHardeningFailed(","path":"libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs","commit_id":"e06ab439d61ebc7a79acfd3f1c91a63f194a367b","original_commit_id":"e06ab439d61ebc7a79acfd3f1c91a63f194a367b","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**LOW**\r\n\r\nThe rewritten `FipsHardeningFailed` message attributes `fips() == false` solely to the macOS corecrypto OE witness, but this branch is now only reachable when a provider *is* installed yet is not FIPS-capable.\r\n\r\nOn Linux/Windows the most likely trigger is that a non-FIPS provider (e.g. plain `aws_lc_rs::default_provider`) was installed instead of the FIPS one — the macOS-only wording is misleading there, and the old \"wrong provider installed\" cause was dropped.\r\n\r\nAdd a platform-neutral cause to the message: state that an installed-but-non-FIPS `CryptoProvider` also produces this error, so operators on non-macOS targets are not misdirected to `CYBERWARE_FIPS_OE_OVERRIDE`.\r\n\r\nAnyway we can merge it but please check all platforms in advance.","created_at":"2026-05-30T14:56:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T14:58:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1982#discussion_r3328900871","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1982","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3328900871"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1982#discussion_r3328900871"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1982"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3328900871/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":278,"original_line":278,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":149,"position":149,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1981,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1981","source_state":"closed","source_author":"asmith987","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1981] feat(modkit-auth): enforce FIPS algorithm allow-list on JWT verification","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/modkit-auth-fips-algorithm-allow-list","pr_head_sha":"5076475fa407532eb27088be8906d8a526cd679b","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"asmith987","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1981","id":3769865827,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7gs5Zj","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1981","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1981.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1981.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1981","number":1981,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(modkit-auth): enforce FIPS algorithm allow-list on JWT verification","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/