 [Learn more →](https://docs.qodo.ai/subscription-plans#what-you%E2%80%99ll-see-when-reviews-are-paused)\n\n\n**On a Teams plan?**\nReviews resume once this user has a paid seat *and* their Git account is linked in Qodo.\n[Link Git account →](https://docs.qodo.ai/subscription-plans#linking-a-git-account)\n\n**Using GitHub Enterprise Server, GitLab Self-Managed, or Bitbucket Data Center?**\nThese require an Enterprise plan - Contact us\n[Contact us →](https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-support#support)\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4576887869/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4576889466","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1981#issuecomment-4576889466","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1981","id":4576889466,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABEM3Keg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T15:22:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T15:23:15Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `26878731-c5c9-4b56-988d-5f6f333daeaf`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 39a05154eb71c475bb3fd324f45e01a36a626fab and 5076475fa407532eb27088be8906d8a526cd679b.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (3)</summary>\n\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/claims_error.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/errors.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/providers/jwks.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR hardens JWT signature algorithm validation by enforcing FIPS-140-3 approved algorithms. New error variants signal unsupported algorithms, an internal allow-list helper gates verification, and tests confirm rejection of disallowed algorithms including EdDSA.\n\n## Changes\n\n**FIPS-140-3 JWT Algorithm Validation**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Unsupported algorithm error types and conversion** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/claims_error.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/errors.rs` | `ClaimsError` and `AuthError` enums each gain a new `UnsupportedAlgorithm(String)` variant. The conversion from `ClaimsError` to `AuthError` explicitly maps this variant instead of falling through to a generic handler. |\n| **JWKS validation with FIPS algorithm allow-list** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/providers/jwks.rs` | Token validation imports `Algorithm` and enforces an early FIPS algorithm allow-list check via a new `fips_allow_alg` helper before signature verification. The helper implements an exhaustive match over `jsonwebtoken::Algorithm` variants, approving RSA, ECDSA, and HMAC families while rejecting EdDSA and others. Comprehensive unit tests validate all approved algorithms, EdDSA rejection, error type conversion, and end-to-end token validation behavior. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A hop through algorithms secure,*  \n> *FIPS-compliant paths endure.*  \n> *EdDSA is out, RSA stays in,*  \n> *Testing confirms each validation win!* 🔐\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4576889466/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1980,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980","source_state":"closed","source_author":"diffora","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1980] feat(account-management): IdP vendor selection, ROOT guards, InvalidInput 400","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"am/idp-vendor-selection","pr_head_sha":"7ded4dbad8faeadcae80550da7272d3913c36571","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"diffora","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1980","id":3762593844,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7gRKA0","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1980","number":1980,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(account-management): IdP vendor selection, ROOT guards, InvalidInput 400","user":{"login":"diffora","id":272209596,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDmWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272209596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora","html_url":"https://github.com/diffora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThree thematically related changes on the AM module + its IdP plugin contract.\n\n### 1. Vendor-based IdP plugin selection\n\nCloses the half-built pattern where IdP plugins advertised `vendor` + `priority` to types-registry but resolution still went through unscoped `ClientHub::get::<dyn IdpPluginClient>` — two coexisting IdP plugins silently overwrote each other in the hub HashMap.\n\n- New `IdpConfig::vendor` knob (default `\"cf\"`, aligns with `StaticIdpPluginConfig::default()`).\n- `LazyIdpProvider` wrapper defers resolution to first call (types-registry catalogue isn't ready at AM `Module::init` — `post_init` of types-registry settles it after every module's init returns). Pattern is symmetric with AuthN Resolver's `GtsPluginSelector`.\n- `static-idp-plugin` switched from unscoped to `register_scoped::<dyn IdpPluginClient>(ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id))`.\n- Vendor selection runs through the shared `choose_plugin_instance` (filter by `cfg.idp.vendor`, priority tiebreak).\n\n**Behavioural shift:** under `idp.required = true`, a misconfigured `idp.vendor` now surfaces at the first IdP-touching API call (503 `service_unavailable`, retryable shape) instead of `Module::init` failure. Documented in `LazyIdpProvider` module docs — necessary because the catalogue cannot be probed at init time.\n\n### 2. ROOT-tenant guards for suspend / unsuspend / PATCH\n\nPre-fix, `DELETE /tenants/{ROOT}` correctly returned 400, but `POST /suspend`, `POST /unsuspend`, and `PATCH /tenants/{ROOT}` all returned 200 and actually mutated the root row (status flipped to `suspended`, name overwritten).\n\n- Two new `DomainError` / SDK variants: `RootTenantCannotChangeStatus` (covers suspend + unsuspend via the shared `set_status_internal`) and `RootTenantCannotUpdate` (covers PATCH).\n- Guard shape mirrors `RootTenantCannotDelete`: `tenant.parent_id.is_none()` (root identified by absence of parent, not by hard-coded UUID).\n- Guards fire AFTER `find_by_id` so a caller targeting a non-existent id still gets 404 — the 'not found' surface stays distinguishable from the 'is the root' surface.\n\n### 3. `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput` → 400 with structured `field_violations`\n\nPreviously every malformed `provisioning_metadata` shape surfaced as 503 `service_unavailable` (plugin `PluginError::Config`/`MetadataDecode` → `CleanFailure` → `service_unavailable`). Wrong status (clients see \"retry later\" for a permanent client error) and wasted KC compensation cycles.\n\n- New SDK variant `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput { detail, field: Option<String> }` (additive, `#[non_exhaustive]`).\n- AM-side: dedicated `DomainError::IdpInvalidInput` + `AccountManagementError::IdpInvalidInput` carrying the dotted-path `field` as a structured attribute — surfaced on the canonical envelope as `field_violations[0].field` with `reason = \"IDP_INVALID_INPUT\"`. When the plugin can't localise the violation (`field: None`), the canonical mapping falls back to the shared `\"provisioning_metadata\"` field key.\n- Saga compensates the `provisioning` row (same shape as `CleanFailure` — nothing on the IdP side to undo).\n\n## Wire delta examples\n\n### Root tenant suspend (was 200, now 400)\n```json\nHTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\nContent-Type: application/problem+json\n{\n  \"type\": \"gts://gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~cf.core.err.invalid_argument.v1~\",\n  \"title\": \"Invalid Argument\",\n  \"status\": 400,\n  \"detail\": \"Request validation failed\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"field_violations\": [{\n      \"field\": \"tenant_id\",\n      \"description\": \"root tenant status cannot be changed\",\n      \"reason\": \"ROOT_TENANT_CANNOT_CHANGE_STATUS\"\n    }],\n    \"resource_type\": \"gts.cf.core.am.tenant.v1~\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### IdP malformed metadata (was 503, now 400 with field attribution)\n```json\nHTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\nContent-Type: application/problem+json\n{\n  \"type\": \"gts://gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~cf.core.err.invalid_argument.v1~\",\n  \"title\": \"Invalid Argument\",\n  \"status\": 400,\n  \"detail\": \"Request validation failed\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"field_violations\": [{\n      \"field\": \"provisioning_metadata.realm_name\",\n      \"description\": \"realm_name must be non-empty\",\n      \"reason\": \"IDP_INVALID_INPUT\"\n    }],\n    \"resource_type\": \"gts.cf.core.am.tenant.v1~\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Migration notes\n\n- `StaticIdpPluginConfig` default `vendor` changed from `\"cyberfabric\"` → `\"cf\"`. Deploys that explicitly pinned `vendor: \"cyberfabric\"` need to update either the plugin section or `idp.vendor`.\n- Deployment-specific plugins integrating with a real IdP must override `account_management.idp.vendor` to match the plugin's advertised vendor; otherwise `LazyIdpProvider` surfaces `CleanFailure` (503) on every IdP-touching call (when `idp.required = true`).\n- Downstream plugins should reclassify their wire-shape rejections from `PluginError::Config` / `MetadataDecode` to `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput { detail, field }` to get the new 400 surface; existing classifications stay 503.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo build` clean (AM + AM-SDK + static-idp-plugin)\n- [x] `cargo test -p cyberware-account-management --lib` — **762 passed**\n- [x] `cargo test -p cyberware-account-management-sdk` — **60 passed**\n- [x] `cargo test -p cyberware-static-idp-plugin --lib --tests` — **24 passed**\n- [x] `cargo clippy --all-targets` — clean\n- [x] `cargo fmt --all --check` — clean\n- [x] `make dylint` — clean\n- [ ] E2e regression against an environment with a real IdP plugin (requires the matching downstream-plugin reclassification to ship)\n- [ ] Verify behavioural shift under `idp.required = true` with a misconfigured `idp.vendor` — confirm 503 on first IdP-touching call instead of init failure\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- No `force` flag to bypass ROOT-tenant guards (no legitimate use case today).\n- Downstream-plugin reclassification (`PluginError::Config` / `MetadataDecode` → `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput`) ships in deployment-specific plugin crates, not here.\n- No restoration of the pre-existing \"fail closed at config time\" property under `required = true` — a `post_init` probe after types-registry settles could restore it as a follow-up, but is not in this PR.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Root-tenant protection: platform root tenant’s lifecycle/status cannot be changed.\n  * Lazy IdP selection: IdP plugins are resolved on first use with safe fallbacks.\n  * Explicit IdP invalid-input error: malformed IdP input reported as a distinct invalid-input result.\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * Standardized IdP vendor defaults and scoped plugin registration behavior.\n  * REST list endpoints now reject non-OData query params with clear validation errors.\n  * Canonical error mapping includes field violations for IdP invalid input.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added/extended coverage for IdP invalid-input, lazy provider behavior, tenant guards, and 