ile changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4564957429","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980#issuecomment-4564957429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1980","id":4564957429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABEBe49Q","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T14:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T16:37:18Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `100f64f8-29f0-4140-92a2-ff6acdaa2f52`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between e25172f1b82814912aa8672ae8fe20a2cfc746d9 and 7ded4dbad8faeadcae80550da7272d3913c36571.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (22)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/error.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/conversions.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/config.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/bootstrap/service.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/idp/mod.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/service/mod.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/service/service_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/test_support/idp.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/lazy.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/lazy_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/mod.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/sdk_error_mapping.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/sdk_error_mapping_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/module.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/config.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/module.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (14)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp_tests.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/idp/mod.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/module.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/mod.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/test_support/idp.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/module.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/conversions.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common_tests.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/config.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/config.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/lazy.rs\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/bootstrap/service.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds Domain/SDK variants for root-tenant and IdP invalid-input, enforces root-tenant lifecycle immutability, introduces LazyIdpProvider with scoped vendor selection and caching, validates listing query keys, and maps new errors through SDK → REST canonical envelopes with tests.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Root-tenant protection and lazy IdP vendor resolution**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**SDK error variants for root-tenant and IdP validation** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/error.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/idp_tests.rs`|Adds `AccountManagementError::RootTenantCannotChangeStatus` and `AccountManagementError::IdpInvalidInput { detail, field }`; adds `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput { detail, field }`; updates metric label/detail/display and validation categorization.|\n|**REST listing query validation** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/common_tests.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/api/rest/handlers/conversions.rs`|Adds `reject_non_odata_params` helper and tests; listing handlers accept `Query<HashMap<String,String>>` extras and call the validator before OData pagination.|\n|**IdpConfig defaults and StaticIdpPlugin vendor alignment** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/config.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/config.rs`|Removes derived `Default` for `IdpConfig` and provides explicit `Default` (vendor = `\"cf\"`, required = false). Aligns static plugin default vendor to `\"cf\"`.|\n|**Domain error types and HTTP boundary mappings** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error_tests.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/sdk_error_mapping.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/sdk_error_mapping_tests.rs`|Adds `DomainError::RootTenantCannotChangeStatus` and `DomainError::IdpInvalidInput { detail, field }`; extends test-only `code()`/`http_status()` mappings; maps new variants through SDK boundary to `AccountManagementError` and into canonical `InvalidArgument` envelopes (IdP invalid-input yields `IDP_INVALID_INPUT` field violation with fallback key `provisioning_metadata`).|\n|**IdP invalid input handling through services and fixtures** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/bootstrap/service.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/service/mod.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/idp/mod.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/test_support/idp.rs`|Bootstrap and tenant services handle `IdpProvisionFailure::InvalidInput` with best-effort saga compensation and convert it to `DomainError::IdpInvalidInput`; adds `FakeOutcome::InvalidInput` test variant.|\n|**Root-tenant lifecycle guards in tenant service** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/service/mod.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/tenant/service/service_tests.rs`|Adds runtime guard rejecting suspend/unsuspend for platform root tenant (`parent_id.is_none()`), updates docs, and adds tests asserting the guard error.|\n|**LazyIdpProvider and infra wiring** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/lazy.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/lazy_tests.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/infra/idp/mod.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/module.rs`, `modules/system/account-management/plugins/static-idp-plugin/src/module.rs`|Implements `LazyIdpProvider` that defers vendor-based plugin selection to first call, selects by vendor+priority from types-registry, performs scoped `ClientHub` lookup, caches successful resolutions only, and falls back to unavailable or `NoopIdpProvider` behavior based on `required`. Updates module wiring to register scoped plugin clients and use the lazy wrapper. Comprehensive tests added.|\n|**Test updates and small cleanups** <br> multiple test files |Adjusts tests to use `IdpConfig::default()` expansion where required and extends coverage for new error mappings and lazy-provider behaviors.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant LazyIdpProvider\n    participant GtsPluginSelector\n    participant TypesRegistry\n    participant ClientHub\n    participant SelectedPlugin\n    participant NoopIdpProvider\n\n    Client->>LazyIdpProvider: provision_tenant()\n    LazyIdpProvider->>GtsPluginSelector: get_or_init()\n    GtsPluginSelector->>TypesRegistry: list_instances(IdpPluginSpecV1)\n    TypesRegistry-->>GtsPluginSelector: plugin list\n    Note over GtsPluginSelector: choose_plugin_instance by vendor + priority\n    GtsPluginSelector-->>LazyIdpProvider: gts_id\n    LazyIdpProvider->>ClientHub: try_get_scoped(gts_id)\n    alt scoped client exists\n      ClientHub-->>LazyIdpProvider: IdpPluginClient\n      LazyIdpProvider->>SelectedPlugin: provision_tenant()\n      SelectedPlugin-->>LazyIdpProvider: result\n      LazyIdpProvider-->>Client: result\n    else Vendor missing + required=true\n      LazyIdpProvider-->>Client: TenantProvisionFailure::Unavailable\n    else Vendor missing + required=false\n      LazyIdpProvider->>NoopIdpProvider: provision_tenant()\n      NoopIdpProvider-->>LazyIdpProvider: UnsupportedOperation\n      LazyIdpProvider-->>Client: UnsupportedOperation\n    end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> A rabbit hops through vendor lanes,  \n> Lazily selecting IdP chains,  \n> Root tenants stand firm and still,  \n> Invalid inputs get a quill,  \n> Errors traced and routed cleanly. 🐰✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4564957429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319182792","pull_request_review_id":4382723397,"id":3319182792,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7F1rXI","diff_hunk":"@@ -75,6 +75,42 @@ pub enum AccountManagementError {\n     #[error(\"root tenant cannot be converted\")]\n     RootTenantCannotConvert,\n \n+    /// Root tenant status is immutable — `suspend` / `unsuspend` refused.\n+    /// Symmetric with [`Self::RootTenantCannotDelete`]: the platform\n+    /// root is a singleton whose lifecycle state must not flip from\n+    /// the public API. Downstream modules that branch on\n+    /// `root.status` may take unexpected paths (read-only mode,\n+    /// refuse provisioning, etc.) without a documented recovery\n+    /// runbook.\n+    #[error(\"root tenant status cannot be changed\")]\n+    RootTenantCannotChangeStatus,\n+\n+    /// Root tenant mutable fields (today: `name`) cannot be updated\n+    /// via PATCH. The root's name is referenced in admin UIs, audit\n+    /// feeds, and `IdP` realm display strings — silently renamable\n+    /// by any admin token is a configuration-drift hazard. Symmetric\n+    /// with [`Self::RootTenantCannotDelete`].\n+    #[error(\"root tenant cannot be updated\")]\n+    RootTenantCannotUpdate,","path":"modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/error.rs","commit_id":"e25172f1b82814912aa8672ae8fe20a2cfc746d9","original_commit_id":"e25172f1b82814912aa8672ae8fe20a2cfc746d9","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Do we really need to don't allow updating root tenant?","created_at":"2026-05-28T16:16:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T16:16:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980#discussion_r3319182792","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1980","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319182792"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980#discussion_r3319182792"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1980"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319182792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":94,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319306632","pull_request_review_id":4382883028,"id":3319306632,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7F2JmI","diff_hunk":"@@ -75,6 +75,42 @@ pub enum AccountManagementError {\n     #[error(\"root tenant cannot be converted\")]\n     RootTenantCannotConvert,\n \n+    /// Root tenant status is immutable — `suspend` / `unsuspend` refused.\n+    /// Symmetric with [`Self::RootTenantCannotDelete`]: the platform\n+    /// root is a singleton whose lifecycle state must not flip from\n+    /// the public API. Downstream modules that branch on\n+    /// `root.status` may take unexpected paths (read-only mode,\n+    /// refuse provisioning, etc.) without a documented recovery\n+    /// runbook.\n+    #[error(\"root tenant status cannot be changed\")]\n+    RootTenantCannotChangeStatus,\n+\n+    /// Root tenant mutable fields (today: `name`) cannot be updated\n+    /// via PATCH. The root's name is referenced in admin UIs, audit\n+    /// feeds, and `IdP` realm display strings — silently renamable\n+    /// by any admin token is a configuration-drift hazard. Symmetric\n+    /// with [`Self::RootTenantCannotDelete`].\n+    #[error(\"root tenant cannot be updated\")]\n+    RootTenantCannotUpdate,","path":"modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/src/error.rs","commit_id":"e25172f1b82814912aa8672ae8fe20a2cfc746d9","original_commit_id":"e25172f1b82814912aa8672ae8fe20a2cfc746d9","user":{"login":"diffora","id":272209596,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDmWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272209596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora","html_url":"https://github.com/diffora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Agree with you. Reverted.","created_at":"2026-05-28T16:36:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T16:36:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980#discussion_r3319306632","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1980","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319306632"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1980#discussion_r3319306632"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1980"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3319306632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":94,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3319182792,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1976,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1976","source_state":"closed","source_author":"striped-zebra-dev","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1976] fix(quickstart): make example bootable (#1971)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/bug-1971-quickstart-credstore-owner","pr_head_sha":"beb90a365ade49b4bdc532d440e7321666283166","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"striped-zebra-dev","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1976","id":3755587988,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7f2bmU","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1976","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1976.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1976.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1976","number":1976,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(quickstart): make example bootable (#1971)","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Two changes required to get `make example` past startup:\r\n\r\n1. static-credstore-plugin: drop `owner_id` from the openai-key / azure-openai-key entries. With both `tenant_id` and `owner_id` set, `SecretConfig::resolve_sharing` maps the entries to `Private`, which keys them on `(tenant_id, owner_id, key)`. At OAGW upstream registration time mini-chat resolves credentials with a `SecurityContext` built from the static-authn S2S identity for `mini-chat`, whose `subject_id` falls back to `DEFAULT_SUBJECT_ID` (`11111111-6a88-4768-9dfc-6bcd5187d9ed`) — different from the tenant-uuid that was copy-pasted into `owner_id`. The Private lookup misses and no fallback map holds the secret, so OAGW reports \"upstream registration failed for provider 'openai'\". Without `owner_id` the entry resolves as Tenant-mode, keyed on `(tenant_id, key)`, which is what an LLM provider key in a single- tenant example should be: usable by any subject within the e2e tenant.\r\n\r\n2. account-management: add an explicit config block (bootstrap root + `idp.required=true`) so AM seeds the same `e2e-root` the platform middleware already knows about and refuses to start with the silent 501-returning Noop IdP fallback when static-idp-plugin is wired in.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * New account management module with dedicated local storage and identity provider integration\n  * Identity provider configuration is now required during setup\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Credential storage entries simplified to remove owner identifier for streamlined credential handling\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1976?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T14:01:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T14:21:38Z","closed_at":"2026-05-27T14:21:38Z","merged_at":"2026-05-27T14:21:38Z","merge_commit_sha":"543a190d1ad2301798df46a599d1eb33a591d642","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1976/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1976/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1976/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/beb90a365ade49b4bdc532d440e7321666283166","head":{"label":"striped-zebra-dev:fix/bug-1971-quickstart-credstore-owner","ref":"fix/bug-1971-quickstart-credstore-owner","sha":"beb90a365ade49b4bdc532d440e7321666283166","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stri