ity/fips/adrs/0005-fips-dependency-policy.md`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/docs/design.md`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/docs/modkit-auth-client-impl.md`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/error.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/fetch.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/mod.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token_watcher.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/crypto.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-oauth2-client-credentials-auth-plugin.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes (1)</summary>\n\n* libs/modkit-auth/docs/modkit-auth-client-impl.md\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR replaces the `aliri_tokens` dependency with an in-house OAuth2 token watcher implementation. The refactoring introduces `TokenWatcher` with lock-free caching via `ArcSwap`, background refresh with jitter and exponential backoff, and refactors `OAuthTokenSource` to provide token fetching independent of trait implementations. Related documentation and security posture descriptions are updated accordingly.\n\n## Changes\n\n**OAuth2 Token Lifecycle Refactor**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Dependency swap and error types** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/error.rs`|Removes `aliri_tokens` and `aliri_clock` from workspace and modkit-auth dependencies, adds `rand`. New `TokenError::InvalidTokenLifetime(String)` variant with test coverage.|\n|**Token watcher core module** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/mod.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token_watcher.rs`|Introduces `TokenStatus` (Fresh/Stale/Expired), `CachedToken` with time-based freshness/expiry computation and redacted debug output, `WatcherConfig` with validated construction, `FetchedToken` payload type. Core `TokenWatcher` with `spawn` performing initial fetch and spawning background refresh loop using jitter and exponential backoff; shutdown via `oneshot` channel; `valid_token()` returns cached token or `TokenError::Unavailable` when expired.|\n|**OAuthTokenSource refactoring** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs`|Removes `AsyncTokenSource` trait impl; adds crate-visible `request_token` performing OAuth2 client-credentials exchange via `HttpClient`, conditional Basic/Form authentication, bearer token_type validation, returning `FetchedToken`. Refactors `refresh_params` to return `(f64, u64)` and work with plain `u64` lifetimes. Updates all 14 unit tests to assert on `FetchedToken` fields instead of `TokenWithLifetime` accessors.|\n|**Token handle and test integration** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/fetch.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs`|`Token` struct imports switch to `token_watcher` types; `WatcherConfig::new(...)` used for validated construction; `Token::get` delegates to `watcher.valid_token()` for cached reads and error propagation; `spawn_watcher` delegates to `TokenWatcher::spawn`. `fetch.rs` updated to use `FetchedToken` fields directly; `layer.rs` test timing adjusted.|\n|**Design and security documentation** <br> `docs/adrs/modkit/0002-modkit-auth-oauth2-client.md`, `docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md`, `docs/security/SECURITY.md`, `docs/security/fips/PRD.md`, `docs/security/fips/adrs/0005-fips-dependency-policy.md`, `libs/modkit-auth/docs/design.md`, `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/crypto.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-oauth2-client-credentials-auth-plugin.md`, `deny-fips.toml`|ADRs updated to document in-house `token_watcher` instead of `aliri_tokens` with jitter/backoff behavior and `ArcSwap` lock-free caching. Security documentation revised to clarify JWT validation backend (`jsonwebtoken`) and updated FIPS-140-3 transitive crypto crate attribution (removing `aliri` path). Design doc expanded on token lifecycle states and refresh scheduling. Deny-fips and crypto bootstrap docs reflect new transitive dependency paths.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 Away with aliri, we craft our own way,  \n> TokenWatcher now stands in the light of the day,  \n> Fresh tokens and stale ones, with jitter so sweet,  \n> ArcSwap reads racing fast through the refresh heartbeat!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4549966301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1969,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1969","source_state":"closed","source_author":"asmith987","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1969] feat(oagw): emit basic proxy metrics","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/oagw-proxy-metrics","pr_head_sha":"204b7ed7e521722697034998455958ac90be93c9","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"asmith987","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1969","id":3750972451,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7fk0wj","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1969","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1969.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1969.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1969","number":1969,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(oagw): emit basic proxy metrics","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * OpenTelemetry-backed metrics in the data plane: request/error counters, request-duration histograms, in‑flight gauges, rate‑limit counters/gauges, WebSocket session metrics, and auth‑phase timings; metric name prefix configurable via config.\n  * HTTP method normalization (unknown → _OTHER) and numeric HTTP response status code labeling.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Comprehensive tests validating metric emission, prefix behavior, status-code labeling, in‑flight accounting, rate‑limit usage/clamping, and WebSocket metrics.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated docs to use OTel-aligned labels and clarified metric cardinality rules.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1969?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-26T21:05:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T06:16:57Z","closed_at":"2026-05-28T06:16:57Z","merged_at":"2026-05-28T06:16:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"7dd797f1355ebbff2805afbecb8b0c4d3cbf8aa2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1969/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1969/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1969/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/204b7ed7e521722697034998455958ac90be93c9","head":{"label":"asmith987:feat/oagw-proxy-metrics","ref":"feat/oagw-proxy-metrics","sha":"204b7ed7e521722697034998455958ac90be93c9","user":{"login":"asmith98