/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/ports/metrics.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/ports/mod.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/mod.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/scenarios/INDEX.md\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/module.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/config.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/websocket.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/metrics.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/metrics_tests.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/test_support.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nIntegrates OpenTelemetry-backed metrics: adds deps and MetricsConfig; defines domain metrics port and label constants; implements OagwMetricsMeter with tests; and wires metrics into proxy request timing, rate-limits, and websocket sessions.\n\n## Changes\n\n**OpenTelemetry Metrics Integration**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Dependencies and metrics configuration** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/Cargo.toml`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/config.rs`|OpenTelemetry (`opentelemetry`) and `heck` deps added; `MetricsConfig` and `effective_prefix()` introduced and wired into `OagwConfig::default()`.|\n|**Domain metrics port and label constants** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/mod.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/ports/*`|`OagwMetricsPort` trait defined; centralized metric label key constants and `phase` values added; `NoopMetrics` no-op implementation provided and re-exported.|\n|**OpenTelemetry metrics implementation and helpers** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/metrics.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/mod.rs`|`OagwMetricsMeter` builds OTel instruments (counters, histograms, up/down counters, gauge), implements `OagwMetricsPort`, adds `normalize_method`, fixed histogram buckets, and registers infra::metrics.|\n|**Metrics implementation test suite** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/metrics_tests.rs`|In-memory OTel SDK test harness and extractors; tests validate counters, histograms, in-flight up/down balances, gauge last-value/clamping, prefix behavior, OTel label keys, and `normalize_method`.|\n|**Data plane request and rate-limit metrics recording** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs`|`DataPlaneServiceImpl` now holds `Arc<dyn OagwMetricsPort>`; `RequestMetricsGuard` records timings/labels, auth-phase timing recorded, success/error counters emitted, and `check_rate_limits` records usage/exceeded metrics.|\n|**WebSocket session metrics** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/websocket.rs`|WebSocket bridge IO carries optional metrics and host label; `WsSessionGuard` RAII increments/decrements active sessions and records session duration; guard installed in `websocket_bridge`.|\n|**Module initialization and docs** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/module.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/*` docs|`OutboundApiGatewayModule::init()` creates an OTel instrumentation scope and `OagwMetricsMeter` behind `Arc<dyn OagwMetricsPort>` and passes it into `DataPlaneServiceImpl::new(...)`; DESIGN/features/scenarios/docs updated to use OTel semantic labels including numeric `http.response.status_code`.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~75 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I nibble metrics, stitch each trace,  \n> > Prefix tidy, labels find their place,  \n> > Histograms hum, gauges rise and fall,  \n> > In-flight counts climb, then settle all,  \n> > The gateway hops — observability for all.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4548839804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312539011","pull_request_review_id":4374482017,"id":3312539011,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7FcVWD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@\n+//! Centralized constants for OAGW metric label keys and values.\n+//!\n+//! Keeps magic strings out of service code and ensures consistent naming\n+//! across recording sites and dashboards.\n+\n+// ── Label keys (OpenTelemetry attribute names) ───────────────────────────\n+\n+pub mod key {\n+    /// Upstream alias (stable, low-cardinality identifier of the destination service).\n+    pub const HOST: &str = \"host\";\n+    /// Route match pattern (NOT raw request path — cardinality control).\n+    pub const PATH: &str = \"path\";\n+    /// HTTP method.\n+    pub const METHOD: &str = \"method\";\n+    /// HTTP status class (`2xx`, `3xx`, `4xx`, `5xx`).\n+    pub const STATUS_CLASS: &str = \"status_class\";","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src