est_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4519377866","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1966#issuecomment-4519377866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1966","id":4519377866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABDWA7yg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-22T14:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T20:08:07Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `6a07f105-982f-43c8-9de1-0171f873bca3`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between ed49efb3755141cb2f6ada980e31d792a7ae0237 and bb08a2a39e6c2ca2ce640b7faaa5f49a24394d0d.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (34)</summary>\n\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/aead.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/aead_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hash.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hash_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hkdf.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hkdf_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hmac.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hmac_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/kx.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/kx_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/oe.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/oe_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/provider.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/provider_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/signer/ec.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/signer/ec_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/signer/rsa.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/signer/rsa_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/tls12.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/tls12_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/tls13.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/tls13_tests.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/verify.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/verify_tests.rs`\n* `modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/ports/knowledge_retriever.rs`\n* `modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/service/stream_service/provider_task.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/account-management/account-management/tests/api_metadata_test.rs`\n* `modules/system/authn-resolver/plugins/oidc-authn-plugin/docs/DESIGN.md`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/Cargo.toml`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/test_support.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/gts.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (9)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/tests/api_metadata_test.rs\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hmac.rs\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/hkdf.rs\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/tls13.rs\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/verify.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/Cargo.toml\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/oe.rs\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/src/aead.rs\n* modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR externalizes test modules from inline definitions to separate files across the rustls-corecrypto-provider cryptography library, while adding domain model annotations to mini-chat and updating infrastructure in oagw and usage-collector modules. The refactoring moves ~2,500 lines of test code into dedicated `*_tests.rs` files without altering production logic.\n\n## Changes\n\n**rustls-corecrypto-provider test file externalization**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Symmetric crypto primitives** <br> `src/aead.rs`, `src/aead_tests.rs`, `src/hash.rs`, `src/hash_tests.rs`, `src/hkdf.rs`, `src/hkdf_tests.rs`, `src/hmac.rs`, `src/hmac_tests.rs` | AEAD AES-GCM tests include NIST CAVS vectors, authentication failure modes, and input validation. Hash tests cover SHA-256/SHA-384 known-answer tests, streaming equivalence, and fork behavior. HKDF tests validate RFC 5869 vectors and multi-block output semantics. HMAC tests cover RFC 4231 vectors and concurrent signing. |\n| **Key agreement** <br> `src/kx.rs`, `src/kx_tests.rs` | ECDH tests validate P-256 and P-384 public key generation, commutativity, malformed peer key rejection, and accessor contracts. |\n| **Signing operations** <br> `src/signer/ec.rs`, `src/signer/ec_tests.rs`, `src/signer/rsa.rs`, `src/signer/rsa_tests.rs` | ECDSA and RSA signing tests cover key loading from PKCS#8 and SEC1/PKCS#1 encodings, curve detection, FIPS-4 minimum key size validation, PSS salt-length regression testing, and concurrent signing via shared signing keys. |\n| **TLS record operations** <br> `src/tls12.rs`, `src/tls12_tests.rs`, `src/tls13.rs`, `src/tls13_tests.rs` | TLS 1.2 tests validate AES-GCM record roundtrips, explicit-nonce wire format matching `extra XOR seq`, PRF determinism, and FIPS claims. TLS 1.3 tests cover payload roundtrips, sequence number validation, and key extraction variant selection. |\n| **Signature verification** <br> `src/verify.rs`, `src/verify_tests.rs` | Verification tests cover ECDSA (P-256/384/521) and RSA (PSS/PKCS#1 v1.5) roundtrips, tampered signature/key rejection, and signature-scheme mapping completeness. |\n| **macOS policy and provider** <br> `src/oe.rs`, `src/oe_tests.rs`, `src/provider.rs`, `src/provider_tests.rs` | OE tests validate macOS version parsing, whitelist enforcement, and FIPS witness computation under override and error conditions. Provider tests verify cipher suite exposure, key loading rejection of malformed input, FIPS claims propagation, and AES-GCM confidentiality limits. |\n\n**Domain model macro annotations and infrastructure updates**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Mini-chat domain model macros** <br> `modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/ports/knowledge_retriever.rs`, `modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/service/stream_service/provider_task.rs` | Adds `#[domain_model]` macro annotations to `RetrievedChunk`, `RetrievalRequest`, `RetrievalError`, and `KnowledgeSearchParams`. |\n| **OAGW crypto provider initialization** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/Cargo.toml`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/test_support.rs` | Adds `modkit/bootstrap` feature to `test-utils` feature list and dev-dependencies; updates `test_server_config` to call idempotent `modkit::bootstrap::init_crypto_provider()` instead of feature-gated manual provider installation. |\n| **Usage-collector schema updates** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/gts.rs` | Refactors `USAGE_RECORD` to use `ResourceType::from_static()` constructor; updates test assertions to use accessor methods (`name()`, `supported_properties()`); changes `UsageCollectorPluginSpecV1` GTS schema base from `BaseModkitPluginV1` to `PluginV1`. |\n| **Account management test formatting** <br> `modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error_tests.rs` | Reformats `MetadataEntryNotFound` assertion string across multiple lines without functional change. |\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n> 🐰 *A thousand tests now scattered wide,*  \n> *From inline blocks to files, safely side by side,*  \n> *Each vector checked, each crypto call,*  \n> *Organized and clean—no chaos at all!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/c