 guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4513510049","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1963#issuecomment-4513510049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1963","id":4513510049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABDQayoQ","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T23:13:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T23:14:28Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `15c0674f-5273-481a-8498-07d5468f29ce`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between fb6b88f1401b69a81c30ab8fe2d70874bc51135c and c633b0f3f3125270fcb0d4a3dc9a00c5ca2040eb.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (8)</summary>\n\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/pr-review.toml`\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/code-review.md`\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/design-review.md`\n* `.cypilot/config/pr-review.toml`\n* `docs/checklists/CODING.md`\n* `docs/checklists/DESIGN.md`\n* `docs/pr-review/modkit-rust-review.md`\n* `guidelines/GTS.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces comprehensive GTS (Global Type System) documentation as a canonical authoring and review guide, then integrates it throughout the SDLC review toolchain: TOML configuration, pr-review prompts, and existing code/design/Rust review checklists.\n\n## Changes\n\n**GTS Guidelines & SDLC Integration**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**GTS Definition & Authoring Guide** <br> `guidelines/GTS.md`|New 1200-line guide documenting GTS identifier format (base/derived/well-known/anonymous), component semantics (vendor/package/namespace/type/version), type vs instance usage, hybrid storage patterns, JSON Schema conventions (Draft-07, `gts://` URIs), Rust authoring practices (`type_id`/`GtsTypeId`, macro-driven schema), well-known instance rationale vs string constants, heterogeneous dispatch via `try_narrow`, design guidelines for base/derived/abstract/final types and traits, and a Quick Review Checklist for PR/design validation.|\n|**SDLC Tool Configuration & Prompts** <br> `.cypilot/config/pr-review.toml`, `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/pr-review.toml`, `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/code-review.md`, `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/scripts/prompts/pr/design-review.md`|Wire `gts_guidelines = \"guidelines/GTS.md\"` into pr-review configuration (both primary and kit-specific TOML files), and update code-review and design-review prompt templates to direct reviewers to consult the guideline when PRs introduce GTS identifiers, schemas, traits, registries, authorization, or extension-point contracts.|\n|**Review Checklist Integration** <br> `docs/checklists/CODING.md`, `docs/checklists/DESIGN.md`, `docs/pr-review/modkit-rust-review.md`|Add GTS validation bullets to code review checklist (SEM-CODE-006 for identifier/type/trait/authorization changes; SEM-CODE-007 for GTS-based modeling), design review checklist (6 bullets across domain modeling, API contracts, extensibility, authorization/security, integration architecture, and PR review focus), and Rust-specific review guide (clarifying intro sentence and GTS rule, plus formatting adjustment in sample output).|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n_No sequence diagram applies here. The changes are documentation-only and do not introduce new runtime interactions or request/response flows._\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~12 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> A rabbit hops through types so clear,  \n> GTS rules both far and near,  \n> Well-known instances, schemas tight,  \n> Identifiers burning bright~ 🌟  \n> Global type system, done just right! 🐰\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4513510049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1962,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962","source_state":"closed","source_author":"asmith987","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1962] feat(canonical-errors): SDK canonical-projection pattern (ADR 0005)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/sdk-canonical-projection","pr_head_sha":"067ee36ccd50df28982c8d373792b092d2ea6e2e","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"asmith987","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","id":3724430801,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7d_k3R","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1962","number":1962,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(canonical-errors): SDK canonical-projection pattern (ADR 0005)","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Establish the canonical-at-boundary + opt-in typed projection pattern for in-process SDK consumers. OAGW is the reference implementation.\r\n\r\n- docs(adr): add 0005 — SDK trait methods return Result<_, CanonicalError>; per-SDK projection enums (From<CanonicalError>) are an opt-in consumer convenience, not part of the trait contract. Includes conformance map against ADR 0001 / DESIGN §3.2 / PRD acceptance criteria.\r\n\r\n- libs/modkit-canonical-errors: implement TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError plus ProblemConversionError (closes DECOMPOSITION 1.2.5). Enables out-of-process round-trip: network bytes → Problem → CanonicalError → (optional) SdkError.\r\n\r\n- oagw-sdk: ServiceGatewayClientV1 trait now returns CanonicalError. ServiceGatewayError becomes a 14-variant typed projection with an Other { canonical } catch-all. Co-locate wire-string constants with typed sub-enums in field.rs (TargetHostCode), gts.rs (Resource), quota.rs, reason.rs (auth::FailureReason, permission::DenialReason). Round-trip Problem tests pin every wire constant to its JSON path.\r\n\r\n- oagw: delete the parallel From<DomainError> for ServiceGatewayError ladder. The single AIP-193 mapping lives in api/rest/error.rs as From<DomainError> for CanonicalError. Impl-side facade calls .map_err(CanonicalError::from) once per method.\r\n\r\n- mini-chat: From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError chains through ServiceGatewayError internally so consumer call sites stay as plain `?` propagation without per-call .map_err boilerplate.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Platform-wide canonical error surface with optional SDK-facing projections, standardized reason/resource/quota vocabularies, and explicit retry-after hints for quota/unavailability.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added ADR describing canonical-at-the-boundary error contract, integration patterns, migration guidance, and conformance expectations.\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * SDKs and services unified to emit/propagate CanonicalError at boundaries.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Comprehensive round-trip and projection tests for Problem↔CanonicalError serialization and mappings.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-21T15:14:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T06:17:23Z","closed_at":"2026-05-28T06:17:23Z","merged_at":"2026-05-28T06:17:23Z","merge_commit_sha":"811a1aed67393e6ff7a761556bd15bdb30897605","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1962/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/067ee36ccd50df28982c8d373792b092d2ea6e2e","head":{"label":"asmith987:feat/sdk-canonical-projection","ref":"feat/sdk-canonical-projection","sha":"067ee36ccd50df28982c8d373792b092d2ea6e2e","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/