gs-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/api/rest/extractors.rs\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/lib.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/error.rs\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (34)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/lib.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/quota.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/provider_resolver.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/gts_helpers.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/lib.rs\n* modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/local_client.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/api/rest/handlers/proxy.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/request_builder.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/lib.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/gts.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/tests/third_party_custom_transport.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/tests/usage.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/reason.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/service/test_helpers.rs\n* modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/api.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/mod.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/tests/third_party_in_process.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/domain/service/attachment_service_test.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/providers/rag_http_client.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/api.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/headers.rs\n* docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md\n* modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/lib.rs\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/field.rs\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/builder.rs\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors/tests/problem.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/mod_tests.rs\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/problem.rs\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/providers/openai_responses_tests.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/api/rest/error.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nADR 0005 recorded: SDK trait boundaries return CanonicalError. Canonical-errors crate adds Deserialize, retry-after hints, ProblemConversionError, TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError, and round-trip tests. SDK adds vocabulary modules and a canonical-projection ServiceGatewayError; implementations, facades, and tests migrated to CanonicalError.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Canonical Error Library & ADR Foundation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**ADR 0005 Canonical Projection** <br> `docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md`|ADR defines SDK error boundary: trait methods return `CanonicalError`, optional typed projections via `From<CanonicalError>`, co-located wire constants + typed enums, and round-trip `Problem` tests.|\n|**Workspace deps & builder helper** <br> `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/builder.rs`|Adds workspace `thiserror` dependency and `ResourceErrorBuilder::with_quota_violation_retry_after_seconds(...)` helper to set per-violation retry hints.|\n|**Context types and Deserialize** <br> `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs`|Adds `Deserialize` derives to V1 context types and `retry_after_seconds: Option<u64>` to `QuotaViolationV1` (initialized to None).|\n|**Problem conversion & re-export** <br> `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/problem.rs`|Adds `ProblemConversionError` re-export and implements `TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` with parsing helpers and category-specific context deserialization.|\n|**Problem round-trip tests** <br> `libs/modkit-canonical-errors/tests/problem.rs`|Comprehensive tests exercising CanonicalError → Problem → JSON → Problem → CanonicalError round-trips, including negative cases for unknown problem types and malformed contexts.|\n\n**SDK Vocabulary & Error Projection Surface**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**SDK vocabulary modules** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/field.rs`, `.../gts.rs`, `.../quota.rs`, `.../reason.rs`, `.../lib.rs`|Adds stable wire-string constants and typed discriminators (`TargetHostCode`, `Resource`, `FailureReason`, `DenialReason`) with `from_wire`/`as_wire` and unit tests; expands SDK root exports.|\n|**ServiceGatewayError canonical projection** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/error.rs`|Replaces prior gateway-specific enum with a canonical-projection `ServiceGatewayError` and implements `From<CanonicalError> for ServiceGatewayError`, including invalid-argument projection logic and projection tests.|\n|**ServiceGatewayClientV1 canonical trait** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/api.rs`|Updates `ServiceGatewayClientV1` fallible methods to return `Result<_, CanonicalError>` and documents optional projection patterns for consumers.|\n|**SDK lib & Cargo** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/Cargo.toml`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/src/lib.rs`|Adds `modkit-canonical-errors` dependency and new pub modules; re-exports `ServiceGatewayError` from SDK root.|\n\n**OAGW Domain, REST, & Facade Implementation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Domain & REST integration** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/*`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/api/rest/*`|Domain error constructors and REST mapping use `oagw_sdk::{field,quota,reason,gts}` constants; validations and tests updated to assert structured constants.|\n|**ServiceGatewayClientV1Facade canonical implementation** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/client.rs`|Facade methods now return `CanonicalError` and map DomainError via `CanonicalError::from`; local mapping helper removed and tests adjusted.|\n|**OAGW SDK Cargo & lib updates** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/Cargo.toml`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/lib.rs`|Adds `modkit-canonical-errors` dependency and re-exports `ServiceGatewayError` from SDK root.|\n\n**Test Mocks & Consumer Updates**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Test mocks & helpers** <br> `modules/mini-chat/.../test_helpers.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/tests/*`, `modules/mini-chat/.../provider_resolver.rs`, `.../openai_responses_tests.rs`, `.../rag_http_client.rs`|All ServiceGatewayClientV1 test mocks updated to use `CanonicalError`; constructors and helpers accept CanonicalError for injected failures.|\n|**LLM provider mapping & tests** <br> `modules/mini-chat/mini-chat/src/infra/llm/mod.rs`, `mod_tests.rs`|Adds `From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError` (via ServiceGatewayError projection) and updates tests to assert rate-limit, timeout, unavailable, and auth-failure mappings, including retry-after preservation and sanitization.|\n|**Simple-user-settings SDK & impl** <br> `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/*`, `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/*`|Removes `SettingsError`, updates SDK trait to return `CanonicalError`, updates implementations and re-exports accordingly.|\n|**Integration tests & fixtures** <br> `modules/mini-chat/.../attachment_service_test.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/proxy_integration.rs`|Attachment and proxy integration tests switched to assert CanonicalError variants and use canonical error builders/helpers for simulated provider failures.|\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n> 🐇 *A hop, skip, and jump through error boundaries,*  \n> *The canonical path now serves all callers,*  \n> *With constants co-located, round-trips complete,*  \n> *Traits return CanonicalError and projections meet,*  \n> *A tidy surface, one error per boundary!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4509659599/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3285042325","pull_request_review_id":4341561357,"id":3285042325,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7DzcSV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,357 @@\n+---\n+status: accepted\n+date: 2026-05-20\n+---\n+\n+# SDK Error Surface: Canonical at the Boundary, Opt-in Typed Projection\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-errors-adr-sdk-canonical-projection`\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+Cyber Ware ships per-module SDK crates (`oagw-sdk`, `credstore-sdk`, `tenant-resolver-sdk`, …) that ClientHub consumers use to call other modules in-process. Each SDK historically exposed a hand-rolled error enum (`ServiceGatewayError`, `CredStoreError`, …) that the impl crate populated through a parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder, distinct from the `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` ladder used on the REST boundary.\n+\n+This caused three concrete problems:\n+\n+1. **Contract is hostage to internal taxonomy.** Adding a new domain variant means an SDK contract break.\n+2. **Two parallel boundary mappings.** Each impl crate maintains `From<DomainError> for SdkError` for ClientHub consumers *and* `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` for REST. They classify the same variants, can disagree, and must update in lockstep.\n+3. **Consumers learn impl vocabulary.** Pattern matching on `ServiceGatewayError::PayloadTooLarge` couples the consumer to the impl crate's word for that concept.\n+\n+A pure-alias approach (`pub use CanonicalError as XxxError`) fixes all three but pushes context-walking onto consumers who want sub-category dispatch. Putting a typed projection in the trait signature gives flat dispatch but makes the projection variant set part of the SDK contract — variant changes become breaking, and consumers using multiple SDKs see N different SDK-specific names for the same canonical category.\n+\n+What's the right shape for the SDK error surface?\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+* Single authoritative AIP-193 categorization — domain → canonical mapping must live in exactly one place per module\n+* Information fidelity at the SDK boundary — projection loss should be a consumer-side opt-in, not a default\n+* Stable SDK contract — variant changes in the projection must not be SDK semver-major events\n+* Cross-SDK uniformity — consumers using multiple SDKs should see a uniform error type at trait boundaries\n+* Ergonomic typed dispatch when consumers want it — flat match arms, typed sub-enums for context discriminators\n+* Conformance with `cpt-cf-errors-adr-canonical-error-categories` — finite vocabulary, no module-specific error categories\n+* `cpt-cf-errors-principle-single-error-gateway` — REST path goes through `CanonicalError` unchanged\n+\n+## Decision Outcome\n+\n+SDKs expose errors in **two layers**:\n+\n+- **At the trait boundary**: `Result<_, CanonicalError>`. Every SDK trait returns the platform's canonical error type — no SDK-specific error type in the trait contract.\n+- **As an opt-in consumer convenience**: SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) for consumers that want flat typed dispatch. Consumers project at the call site via `.map_err(SdkError::from)?`, or chain transparently through a `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError` impl.\n+\n+The trait signature is uniform across all SDKs. The projection lives in the SDK as a typed view over canonical — not as the wire contract or the trait contract — and individual SDKs add it only when their consumers benefit from it. Future projection variant changes (adding, splitting, refining) are non-breaking on the trait contract; only consumers that opted into typed dispatch are affected, and only at sites that pattern-matched on the changed variants.\n+\n+### Consequences\n+\n+* The SDK trait returns `Result<_, CanonicalError>` for every fallible method. No SDK-specific error type appears in the trait signature.\n+* The impl crate keeps **only** `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in its REST error module. Any parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` is deleted; the facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)` once per method.\n+* SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) as a documented consumer convenience. The projection is **not** part of the trait contract:\n+   - Adding a variant is non-breaking\n+   - Refining a variant's payload is breaking only for consumers that destructure that variant\n+   - Removing a variant is breaking only for consumers that pattern-match on it\n+   - The trait signature is unaffected by any of these changes\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST also ship the typed sub-enum vocabulary (`field::TargetHostCode`, `reason::auth::FailureReason`, `gts::Resource`, …) co-located with the wire-string constants they project from, each with `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire` helpers. Round-trip `Problem` tests pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant so the conversion is infallible and forward-compatible (new canonical categories surface with full fidelity).\n+* The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"...\")]` proc-macro literals are the one exception (proc macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip Problem tests pin them.\n+* SDK error types must not carry transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) — those belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+* Trait method rustdoc MUST cross-link to the SDK's projection type (when one exists) so the typed surface is discoverable.\n+\n+### Confirmation\n+\n+The OAGW SDK demonstrates the pattern end-to-end:\n+\n+(a) `ServiceGatewayClientV1` trait methods return `Result<_, CanonicalError>`.\n+\n+(b) `oagw-sdk` ships `ServiceGatewayError` — a 14-variant projection with `From<CanonicalError>` — as a consumer convenience. Variants: `RateLimited`, `Timeout`, `Unavailable`, `AuthFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `InvalidTargetHost`, `Validation`, `NotFound`, `AlreadyExists`, `FailedPrecondition`, `Aborted`, `Internal`, `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }`.\n+\n+(c) Typed sub-enums are co-located with their wire-string constants:\n+- `field::TargetHostCode` next to `MISSING_TARGET_HOST` / `INVALID_TARGET_HOST` / `UNKNOWN_TARGET_HOST`\n+- `reason::auth::FailureReason` next to `PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND` / `PLUGIN_FAILED` / `PLUGIN_INTERNAL`\n+- `reason::permission::DenialReason` next to `AUTHZ_DENIED` / `TENANT_*` / `CORS_*`\n+- `gts::Resource` next to the six `*_SCHEMA` constants\n+\n+(d) The impl crate's parallel `From<DomainError> for ServiceGatewayError` ladder is deleted (~110 lines + 4 tests). The single AIP-193 mapping is `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in `oagw/src/api/rest/error.rs`.\n+\n+(e) Round-trip `Problem` tests in `oagw-sdk/src/error.rs::tests` pin all 26 `field::*` constants, 8 `reason::*` constants, 1 `quota::*` constant, and 6 `gts::*` constants to their wire JSON paths.\n+\n+(f) Mini-chat (OAGW's only current consumer) defines `From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError` that chains through `ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()` internally, so every call site stays as plain `?` propagation without `.map_err` boilerplate.\n+\n+(g) Out-of-process consumers can use `TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) to reconstruct typed errors from wire bytes. The full chain is `Problem JSON → Problem → CanonicalError → (optional) SdkError`.\n+\n+(h) Workspace `cargo test` passes (~1,800 tests across `oagw-sdk`, `oagw`, `mini-chat`, `modkit-canonical-errors`).\n+\n+## The Pattern\n+\n+### Trait signature — canonical at the boundary\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait XxxClientV1: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+        -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>;\n+    // every fallible method returns CanonicalError\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Impl-side facade — single `.map_err`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+    -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>\n+{\n+    self.inner.do_thing(&ctx, req)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(CanonicalError::from)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The single AIP-193 ladder lives in `{impl}/src/api/rest/error.rs`:\n+\n+```rust\n+impl From<DomainError> for CanonicalError {\n+    fn from(err: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => UserResourceError::not_found(/* … */)\n+                .with_resource(id.to_string())\n+                .create(),\n+            // … one arm per domain variant, AIP-193 mapping\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Optional projection — typed view over canonical\n+\n+When an SDK's consumers benefit from flat typed dispatch, the SDK ships a `From<CanonicalError>`-driven enum **alongside** the trait — not in the trait signature:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs\n+\n+use modkit_canonical_errors::CanonicalError;\n+use crate::field::TargetHostCode;\n+use crate::gts::Resource;\n+use crate::reason::auth::FailureReason as AuthFailureReason;\n+use crate::reason::permission::DenialReason as PermissionDenialReason;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Error)]\n+pub enum ServiceGatewayError {\n+    #[error(\"rate limit exceeded\")]\n+    RateLimited { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request timed out\")]\n+    Timeout,\n+\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable\")]\n+    Unavailable { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"authentication failed [{reason}]: {detail}\")]\n+    AuthFailed { reason: AuthFailureReason, detail: String },\n+\n+    // … one variant per dispatch case, driven by consumer needs …\n+\n+    /// Catch-all for canonical categories the SDK does not model.\n+    /// Preserves full canonical context for inspection / forward-compat.\n+    #[error(\"[{}] {}\", canonical.gts_type(), canonical.detail())]\n+    Other { canonical: CanonicalError },\n+}\n+\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for ServiceGatewayError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        match &err {\n+            CanonicalError::ResourceExhausted { .. } => Self::RateLimited { retry_after_secs: None },\n+            CanonicalError::DeadlineExceeded { .. } => Self::Timeout,\n+            // … one arm per canonical variant the SDK models, plus\n+            // `_ => Self::Other { canonical: err.clone() }` catch-all\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Co-located vocabulary\n+\n+Wire-string constants and their typed sub-enums live together. Example for `Unauthenticated.ctx.reason`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/reason.rs\n+pub mod auth {\n+    pub const PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND: &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_FAILED:    &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_FAILED\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_INTERNAL:  &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_INTERNAL\";\n+\n+    /// Typed view of the wire `reason` strings above.\n+    #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+    pub enum FailureReason {\n+        PluginNotFound,\n+        PluginFailed,\n+        PluginInternal,\n+        Unknown(String),\n+    }\n+\n+    impl FailureReason {\n+        pub fn from_wire(s: Option<&str>) -> Self { /* … */ }\n+        pub fn as_wire(&self) -> &str { /* … */ }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Same pattern in `field.rs` (`TargetHostCode` etc.), `gts.rs` (`Resource`), `reason::permission` (`DenialReason`).\n+\n+### Round-trip tests pin the vocabulary\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs::tests\n+#[test]\n+fn auth_reason_constants_round_trip() {\n+    for r in [reason::auth::PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND, /* … */] {\n+        let err = CanonicalError::unauthenticated().with_reason(r).create();\n+        let json = serde_json::to_value(&Problem::from(err)).unwrap();\n+        assert_eq!(json[\"context\"][\"reason\"], r);\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception (macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip tests pin them.\n+\n+## Consumer Integration\n+\n+Three patterns, all valid:\n+\n+### Pattern 1 — pure propagation (no projection)\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;  // ? propagates CanonicalError\n+```\n+\n+Caller's own error type implements `From<CanonicalError>`. The projection isn't used. Right choice when the consumer only propagates or dispatches on broad canonical category.\n+\n+### Pattern 2 — explicit projection at the call site\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(ServiceGatewayError::from)?;\n+\n+match err {\n+    ServiceGatewayError::RateLimited { retry_after_secs } => /* backoff */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::Timeout                          => /* retry */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::AuthFailed {\n+        reason: AuthFailureReason::PluginInternal, ..\n+    } => /* gateway-side auth broken — transient */,\n+    _ => /* fallback */,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Explicit about projecting. Caller's error type implements `From<ServiceGatewayError>`. Right choice for one-off typed-dispatch sites scattered across a codebase that otherwise propagates canonical.\n+\n+### Pattern 3 — transparent chaining via `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError`\n+\n+```rust\n+// Define once in the consumer crate:\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for OwnConsumerError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        // Route through the SDK's typed projection internally.\n+        ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Then every call site stays plain `?`:\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;\n+```\n+\n+Eliminates per-call-site boilerplate while keeping the typed dispatch surface. **Recommended** for consumers that always want typed dispatch. Mini-chat uses this pattern.\n+\n+### Reverse direction (consumer wraps SDK failure in its own canonical)\n+\n+Often a consumer wants to catch an SDK failure and re-emit it as a canonical error in its own resource scope (e.g. `account-management` catching an OAGW call and re-emitting it as a tenant-management failure). The canonical-at-boundary contract makes this trivial — the consumer already has `CanonicalError` from the `?`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(|canonical| {\n+        AccountMgmtResourceError::failed_precondition()\n+            .with_precondition_violation(/* … */)\n+            .create()\n+    })?;\n+```\n+\n+No reverse `From<SdkError> for CanonicalError` impl is needed — canonical is already at the boundary.\n+\n+### Cross-process round-trip\n+\n+`TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) closes the out-of-process loop. An HTTP/REST consumer's full chain:\n+\n+```\n+network bytes\n+  → serde_json::from_slice → Problem\n+  → CanonicalError::try_from(problem) → CanonicalError\n+  → (optional) ServiceGatewayError::from(canonical) → ServiceGatewayError\n+```\n+\n+The first two hops are mandatory and lossless (modulo wire-strip fields like `Internal.description` which are `#[serde(skip)]` by design — production wire never carries the diagnostic). The third hop is opt-in.\n+\n+## Design Rules\n+\n+1. **Trait signature returns `CanonicalError`** for every fallible method. Document this in the trait's top-level rustdoc and cross-link the optional projection.\n+2. **Impl-side facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)`** once per method. No parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder.\n+3. **SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection** as a consumer convenience. When shipped:\n+   - MUST be infallible (`From<CanonicalError>`, not `TryFrom`)\n+   - MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant for forward-compat\n+   - Variant set is driven by consumer dispatch — audit workspace `match` arms before designing\n+   - Variant names encode consumer intent, not impl vocabulary\n+4. **When a projection is shipped, co-locate typed sub-enums with wire-string constants**:\n+   - `gts.rs` — `*_SCHEMA` constants + typed `Resource` enum for `NotFound` / `AlreadyExists.ctx.resource_type`\n+   - `reason.rs` — submodules per canonical category, each holding both `pub const` reason values and a typed enum\n+   - `field.rs` — `pub const` constants for `InvalidArgument.ctx.field_violations[].reason`, plus typed sub-enums for families consumers dispatch on\n+   - `quota.rs` — `pub const` `subject` values for `ResourceExhausted.ctx.violations[].subject`\n+5. **Each typed sub-enum exposes `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire`** (`from_wire` returns `Self` with an `Unknown(String)` catch-all when every wire value is meaningful, or `Option<Self>` when only a few wire strings are valid).\n+6. **Impl crate references the SDK constants** at every site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception; the round-trip tests pin them.\n+7. **Round-trip `Problem` tests** in `{sdk}/src/error.rs::tests` pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+8. **No transport fields in the projection**: `instance` and `trace_id` belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+9. **Document the projection** in the SDK's `error.rs` module rustdoc: state it is an opt-in convenience, show the three consumer integration patterns, include a consumer-dispatch reference table, and link to this ADR.\n+\n+## Per-SDK Migration\n+\n+Every SDK uses the same trait-contract migration. Whether to **also** ship a projection is a separate per-SDK decision based on consumer dispatch needs.\n+\n+| SDK | `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError`? | Ship projection? | Effort |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| `simple-user-settings-sdk` | yes | no | ~30 min (delete parallel ladder, switch trait to `CanonicalError`) |\n+| `nodes-registry-sdk` | yes | no | ~30 min |\n+| `mini-chat-sdk` | yes | no | ~1 hr (plugin-SPI enums separate, do not migrate) |\n+| `resource-group-sdk` | yes | re-evaluate if consumers want typed cycle/limit dispatch | ~1–2 hr |\n+| `file-parser` | yes | no | ~1 hr |\n+| `types-registry-sdk` | yes | likely yes (typed `ValidationError` payload) | ~half day |\n+| `oagw-sdk` | yes | **yes** | **done** (reference implementation) |\n+| `credstore-sdk` | **no** | TBD after consumer audit | ~1 day (author canonical boundary first) |\n+| `authn-resolver-sdk` | **no** | no | ~1 day |\n+| `tenant-resolver-sdk` | **no** | no | ~1 day |\n+| `authz-resolver-sdk` | **no** | likely yes (`EnforcerError::Denied { deny_reason }` — typed payload) | ~1–2 days |\n+\n+For the four resolver SDKs at the bottom, the canonical boundary mapping is the real cost. The trait-contract switch is trivial once that lands.\n+\n+## Known Gaps\n+\n+1. **`retry_after_seconds` on `ResourceExhausted`.** The canonical `ResourceExhausted` context type does not yet carry `retry_after_seconds` (see [`libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs`](../../../../libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs)). The retry hint only lands in the HTTP `Retry-After` header; in-process callers see `None`. The semantically correct fix is to add `retry_after_seconds: Option<u64>` to `QuotaViolation` (per-violation, not per-category — memory exhaustion has no retry window while rate-limit does).","path":"docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md","commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"mattgarmon","id":22921875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTIxODc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22921875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon","html_url":"https://github.com/mattgarmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Let's implement this before merge","created_at":"2026-05-22T00:06:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T00:06:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3285042325","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3285042325"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3285042325"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3285042325/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":331,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":331,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312464800","pull_request_review_id":4374392531,"id":3312464800,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7FcDOg","diff_hunk":"@@ -140,6 +145,208 @@ impl From<CanonicalError> for Problem {\n     }\n }\n \n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Round-trip: Problem → CanonicalError\n+//\n+// Reverse direction of `From<CanonicalError> for Problem`. Out-of-process SDK\n+// consumers receive `application/problem+json` over the wire, deserialize into\n+// `Problem`, and reconstruct the typed `CanonicalError` via this `TryFrom`.\n+// In-process consumers do not need this hop — they hold `CanonicalError`\n+// directly from the ClientHub call.\n+//\n+// Lossy by design:\n+// * `Internal.description` and `Unknown.description` are `#[serde(skip)]` on\n+//   the wire, so they reconstruct as empty strings. This is intentional —\n+//   production wire responses never carry the server-side diagnostic.\n+// * Transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) live on `Problem`, not on\n+//   `CanonicalError`. Callers that need them should read them off the\n+//   `Problem` before converting.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+/// Prefix on `Problem.problem_type` produced by the forward conversion.\n+const PROBLEM_TYPE_PREFIX: &str = \"gts://\";\n+\n+/// Reasons a `Problem` cannot be reconstructed as a `CanonicalError`.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum ProblemConversionError {\n+    /// The `problem_type` URI does not match any of the 16 canonical\n+    /// category identifiers. Either the server emitted a non-canonical\n+    /// problem or the wire format has drifted.\n+    #[error(\"unknown canonical problem_type: {0}\")]","path":"libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/problem.rs","commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If that is unknown, then why it is canonical? I feel like we overused `canonical` a bit.","created_at":"2026-05-27T17:00:54Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T17:00:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3312464800","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312464800"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3312464800"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312464800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312521240","pull_request_review_id":4374461081,"id":3312521240,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7FcRAY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,357 @@\n+---\n+status: accepted\n+date: 2026-05-20\n+---\n+\n+# SDK Error Surface: Canonical at the Boundary, Opt-in Typed Projection\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-errors-adr-sdk-canonical-projection`\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+Cyber Ware ships per-module SDK crates (`oagw-sdk`, `credstore-sdk`, `tenant-resolver-sdk`, …) that ClientHub consumers use to call other modules in-process. Each SDK historically exposed a hand-rolled error enum (`ServiceGatewayError`, `CredStoreError`, …) that the impl crate populated through a parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder, distinct from the `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` ladder used on the REST boundary.\n+\n+This caused three concrete problems:\n+\n+1. **Contract is hostage to internal taxonomy.** Adding a new domain variant means an SDK contract break.\n+2. **Two parallel boundary mappings.** Each impl crate maintains `From<DomainError> for SdkError` for ClientHub consumers *and* `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` for REST. They classify the same variants, can disagree, and must update in lockstep.\n+3. **Consumers learn impl vocabulary.** Pattern matching on `ServiceGatewayError::PayloadTooLarge` couples the consumer to the impl crate's word for that concept.\n+\n+A pure-alias approach (`pub use CanonicalError as XxxError`) fixes all three but pushes context-walking onto consumers who want sub-category dispatch. Putting a typed projection in the trait signature gives flat dispatch but makes the projection variant set part of the SDK contract — variant changes become breaking, and consumers using multiple SDKs see N different SDK-specific names for the same canonical category.\n+\n+What's the right shape for the SDK error surface?\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+* Single authoritative AIP-193 categorization — domain → canonical mapping must live in exactly one place per module\n+* Information fidelity at the SDK boundary — projection loss should be a consumer-side opt-in, not a default\n+* Stable SDK contract — variant changes in the projection must not be SDK semver-major events\n+* Cross-SDK uniformity — consumers using multiple SDKs should see a uniform error type at trait boundaries\n+* Ergonomic typed dispatch when consumers want it — flat match arms, typed sub-enums for context discriminators\n+* Conformance with `cpt-cf-errors-adr-canonical-error-categories` — finite vocabulary, no module-specific error categories\n+* `cpt-cf-errors-principle-single-error-gateway` — REST path goes through `CanonicalError` unchanged\n+\n+## Decision Outcome\n+\n+SDKs expose errors in **two layers**:\n+\n+- **At the trait boundary**: `Result<_, CanonicalError>`. Every SDK trait returns the platform's canonical error type — no SDK-specific error type in the trait contract.\n+- **As an opt-in consumer convenience**: SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) for consumers that want flat typed dispatch. Consumers project at the call site via `.map_err(SdkError::from)?`, or chain transparently through a `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError` impl.\n+\n+The trait signature is uniform across all SDKs. The projection lives in the SDK as a typed view over canonical — not as the wire contract or the trait contract — and individual SDKs add it only when their consumers benefit from it. Future projection variant changes (adding, splitting, refining) are non-breaking on the trait contract; only consumers that opted into typed dispatch are affected, and only at sites that pattern-matched on the changed variants.\n+\n+### Consequences\n+\n+* The SDK trait returns `Result<_, CanonicalError>` for every fallible method. No SDK-specific error type appears in the trait signature.\n+* The impl crate keeps **only** `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in its REST error module. Any parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` is deleted; the facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)` once per method.\n+* SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) as a documented consumer convenience. The projection is **not** part of the trait contract:\n+   - Adding a variant is non-breaking\n+   - Refining a variant's payload is breaking only for consumers that destructure that variant\n+   - Removing a variant is breaking only for consumers that pattern-match on it\n+   - The trait signature is unaffected by any of these changes\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST also ship the typed sub-enum vocabulary (`field::TargetHostCode`, `reason::auth::FailureReason`, `gts::Resource`, …) co-located with the wire-string constants they project from, each with `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire` helpers. Round-trip `Problem` tests pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant so the conversion is infallible and forward-compatible (new canonical categories surface with full fidelity).\n+* The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"...\")]` proc-macro literals are the one exception (proc macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip Problem tests pin them.\n+* SDK error types must not carry transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) — those belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+* Trait method rustdoc MUST cross-link to the SDK's projection type (when one exists) so the typed surface is discoverable.\n+\n+### Confirmation\n+\n+The OAGW SDK demonstrates the pattern end-to-end:\n+\n+(a) `ServiceGatewayClientV1` trait methods return `Result<_, CanonicalError>`.\n+\n+(b) `oagw-sdk` ships `ServiceGatewayError` — a 14-variant projection with `From<CanonicalError>` — as a consumer convenience. Variants: `RateLimited`, `Timeout`, `Unavailable`, `AuthFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `InvalidTargetHost`, `Validation`, `NotFound`, `AlreadyExists`, `FailedPrecondition`, `Aborted`, `Internal`, `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }`.\n+\n+(c) Typed sub-enums are co-located with their wire-string constants:\n+- `field::TargetHostCode` next to `MISSING_TARGET_HOST` / `INVALID_TARGET_HOST` / `UNKNOWN_TARGET_HOST`\n+- `reason::auth::FailureReason` next to `PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND` / `PLUGIN_FAILED` / `PLUGIN_INTERNAL`\n+- `reason::permission::DenialReason` next to `AUTHZ_DENIED` / `TENANT_*` / `CORS_*`\n+- `gts::Resource` next to the six `*_SCHEMA` constants\n+\n+(d) The impl crate's parallel `From<DomainError> for ServiceGatewayError` ladder is deleted (~110 lines + 4 tests). The single AIP-193 mapping is `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in `oagw/src/api/rest/error.rs`.\n+\n+(e) Round-trip `Problem` tests in `oagw-sdk/src/error.rs::tests` pin all 26 `field::*` constants, 8 `reason::*` constants, 1 `quota::*` constant, and 6 `gts::*` constants to their wire JSON paths.\n+\n+(f) Mini-chat (OAGW's only current consumer) defines `From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError` that chains through `ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()` internally, so every call site stays as plain `?` propagation without `.map_err` boilerplate.\n+\n+(g) Out-of-process consumers can use `TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) to reconstruct typed errors from wire bytes. The full chain is `Problem JSON → Problem → CanonicalError → (optional) SdkError`.\n+\n+(h) Workspace `cargo test` passes (~1,800 tests across `oagw-sdk`, `oagw`, `mini-chat`, `modkit-canonical-errors`).\n+\n+## The Pattern\n+\n+### Trait signature — canonical at the boundary\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait XxxClientV1: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+        -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>;\n+    // every fallible method returns CanonicalError\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Impl-side facade — single `.map_err`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+    -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>\n+{\n+    self.inner.do_thing(&ctx, req)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(CanonicalError::from)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The single AIP-193 ladder lives in `{impl}/src/api/rest/error.rs`:\n+\n+```rust\n+impl From<DomainError> for CanonicalError {\n+    fn from(err: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => UserResourceError::not_found(/* … */)\n+                .with_resource(id.to_string())\n+                .create(),\n+            // … one arm per domain variant, AIP-193 mapping\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Optional projection — typed view over canonical\n+\n+When an SDK's consumers benefit from flat typed dispatch, the SDK ships a `From<CanonicalError>`-driven enum **alongside** the trait — not in the trait signature:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs\n+\n+use modkit_canonical_errors::CanonicalError;\n+use crate::field::TargetHostCode;\n+use crate::gts::Resource;\n+use crate::reason::auth::FailureReason as AuthFailureReason;\n+use crate::reason::permission::DenialReason as PermissionDenialReason;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Error)]\n+pub enum ServiceGatewayError {\n+    #[error(\"rate limit exceeded\")]\n+    RateLimited { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request timed out\")]\n+    Timeout,\n+\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable\")]\n+    Unavailable { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"authentication failed [{reason}]: {detail}\")]\n+    AuthFailed { reason: AuthFailureReason, detail: String },\n+\n+    // … one variant per dispatch case, driven by consumer needs …\n+\n+    /// Catch-all for canonical categories the SDK does not model.\n+    /// Preserves full canonical context for inspection / forward-compat.\n+    #[error(\"[{}] {}\", canonical.gts_type(), canonical.detail())]\n+    Other { canonical: CanonicalError },\n+}\n+\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for ServiceGatewayError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        match &err {\n+            CanonicalError::ResourceExhausted { .. } => Self::RateLimited { retry_after_secs: None },\n+            CanonicalError::DeadlineExceeded { .. } => Self::Timeout,\n+            // … one arm per canonical variant the SDK models, plus\n+            // `_ => Self::Other { canonical: err.clone() }` catch-all\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Co-located vocabulary\n+\n+Wire-string constants and their typed sub-enums live together. Example for `Unauthenticated.ctx.reason`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/reason.rs\n+pub mod auth {\n+    pub const PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND: &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_FAILED:    &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_FAILED\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_INTERNAL:  &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_INTERNAL\";\n+\n+    /// Typed view of the wire `reason` strings above.\n+    #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+    pub enum FailureReason {\n+        PluginNotFound,\n+        PluginFailed,\n+        PluginInternal,\n+        Unknown(String),\n+    }\n+\n+    impl FailureReason {\n+        pub fn from_wire(s: Option<&str>) -> Self { /* … */ }\n+        pub fn as_wire(&self) -> &str { /* … */ }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Same pattern in `field.rs` (`TargetHostCode` etc.), `gts.rs` (`Resource`), `reason::permission` (`DenialReason`).\n+\n+### Round-trip tests pin the vocabulary\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs::tests\n+#[test]\n+fn auth_reason_constants_round_trip() {\n+    for r in [reason::auth::PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND, /* … */] {\n+        let err = CanonicalError::unauthenticated().with_reason(r).create();\n+        let json = serde_json::to_value(&Problem::from(err)).unwrap();\n+        assert_eq!(json[\"context\"][\"reason\"], r);\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception (macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip tests pin them.\n+\n+## Consumer Integration\n+\n+Three patterns, all valid:\n+\n+### Pattern 1 — pure propagation (no projection)\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;  // ? propagates CanonicalError\n+```\n+\n+Caller's own error type implements `From<CanonicalError>`. The projection isn't used. Right choice when the consumer only propagates or dispatches on broad canonical category.\n+\n+### Pattern 2 — explicit projection at the call site\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(ServiceGatewayError::from)?;\n+\n+match err {\n+    ServiceGatewayError::RateLimited { retry_after_secs } => /* backoff */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::Timeout                          => /* retry */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::AuthFailed {\n+        reason: AuthFailureReason::PluginInternal, ..\n+    } => /* gateway-side auth broken — transient */,\n+    _ => /* fallback */,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Explicit about projecting. Caller's error type implements `From<ServiceGatewayError>`. Right choice for one-off typed-dispatch sites scattered across a codebase that otherwise propagates canonical.\n+\n+### Pattern 3 — transparent chaining via `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError`\n+\n+```rust\n+// Define once in the consumer crate:\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for OwnConsumerError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        // Route through the SDK's typed projection internally.\n+        ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Then every call site stays plain `?`:\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;\n+```\n+\n+Eliminates per-call-site boilerplate while keeping the typed dispatch surface. **Recommended** for consumers that always want typed dispatch. Mini-chat uses this pattern.\n+\n+### Reverse direction (consumer wraps SDK failure in its own canonical)\n+\n+Often a consumer wants to catch an SDK failure and re-emit it as a canonical error in its own resource scope (e.g. `account-management` catching an OAGW call and re-emitting it as a tenant-management failure). The canonical-at-boundary contract makes this trivial — the consumer already has `CanonicalError` from the `?`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(|canonical| {\n+        AccountMgmtResourceError::failed_precondition()\n+            .with_precondition_violation(/* … */)\n+            .create()\n+    })?;\n+```\n+\n+No reverse `From<SdkError> for CanonicalError` impl is needed — canonical is already at the boundary.\n+\n+### Cross-process round-trip\n+\n+`TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) closes the out-of-process loop. An HTTP/REST consumer's full chain:\n+\n+```\n+network bytes\n+  → serde_json::from_slice → Problem\n+  → CanonicalError::try_from(problem) → CanonicalError\n+  → (optional) ServiceGatewayError::from(canonical) → ServiceGatewayError\n+```\n+\n+The first two hops are mandatory and lossless (modulo wire-strip fields like `Internal.description` which are `#[serde(skip)]` by design — production wire never carries the diagnostic). The third hop is opt-in.\n+\n+## Design Rules","path":"docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md","commit_id":"067ee36ccd50df28982c8d373792b092d2ea6e2e","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Worth to mention the reason why someone can be interested in shipping the specific error, from the top of my mind: if the method can only return one of of two error types - then it is better to use the specific, narrowed error.\n\nAnother thing to consider: not every method of the SDK must return `CanonicalError`-compatible error, reason: some of the SDKs will provide local in-process functionality with no need to be transported and probably more specific error types.","created_at":"2026-05-27T17:11:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T17:11:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3312521240","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312521240"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3312521240"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3312521240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":309,"original_line":289,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":289,"position":309,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313415150","pull_request_review_id":4375535179,"id":3313415150,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7FfrPu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,357 @@\n+---\n+status: accepted\n+date: 2026-05-20\n+---\n+\n+# SDK Error Surface: Canonical at the Boundary, Opt-in Typed Projection\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-errors-adr-sdk-canonical-projection`\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+Cyber Ware ships per-module SDK crates (`oagw-sdk`, `credstore-sdk`, `tenant-resolver-sdk`, …) that ClientHub consumers use to call other modules in-process. Each SDK historically exposed a hand-rolled error enum (`ServiceGatewayError`, `CredStoreError`, …) that the impl crate populated through a parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder, distinct from the `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` ladder used on the REST boundary.\n+\n+This caused three concrete problems:\n+\n+1. **Contract is hostage to internal taxonomy.** Adding a new domain variant means an SDK contract break.\n+2. **Two parallel boundary mappings.** Each impl crate maintains `From<DomainError> for SdkError` for ClientHub consumers *and* `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` for REST. They classify the same variants, can disagree, and must update in lockstep.\n+3. **Consumers learn impl vocabulary.** Pattern matching on `ServiceGatewayError::PayloadTooLarge` couples the consumer to the impl crate's word for that concept.\n+\n+A pure-alias approach (`pub use CanonicalError as XxxError`) fixes all three but pushes context-walking onto consumers who want sub-category dispatch. Putting a typed projection in the trait signature gives flat dispatch but makes the projection variant set part of the SDK contract — variant changes become breaking, and consumers using multiple SDKs see N different SDK-specific names for the same canonical category.\n+\n+What's the right shape for the SDK error surface?\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+* Single authoritative AIP-193 categorization — domain → canonical mapping must live in exactly one place per module\n+* Information fidelity at the SDK boundary — projection loss should be a consumer-side opt-in, not a default\n+* Stable SDK contract — variant changes in the projection must not be SDK semver-major events\n+* Cross-SDK uniformity — consumers using multiple SDKs should see a uniform error type at trait boundaries\n+* Ergonomic typed dispatch when consumers want it — flat match arms, typed sub-enums for context discriminators\n+* Conformance with `cpt-cf-errors-adr-canonical-error-categories` — finite vocabulary, no module-specific error categories\n+* `cpt-cf-errors-principle-single-error-gateway` — REST path goes through `CanonicalError` unchanged\n+\n+## Decision Outcome\n+\n+SDKs expose errors in **two layers**:\n+\n+- **At the trait boundary**: `Result<_, CanonicalError>`. Every SDK trait returns the platform's canonical error type — no SDK-specific error type in the trait contract.\n+- **As an opt-in consumer convenience**: SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) for consumers that want flat typed dispatch. Consumers project at the call site via `.map_err(SdkError::from)?`, or chain transparently through a `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError` impl.\n+\n+The trait signature is uniform across all SDKs. The projection lives in the SDK as a typed view over canonical — not as the wire contract or the trait contract — and individual SDKs add it only when their consumers benefit from it. Future projection variant changes (adding, splitting, refining) are non-breaking on the trait contract; only consumers that opted into typed dispatch are affected, and only at sites that pattern-matched on the changed variants.\n+\n+### Consequences\n+\n+* The SDK trait returns `Result<_, CanonicalError>` for every fallible method. No SDK-specific error type appears in the trait signature.\n+* The impl crate keeps **only** `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in its REST error module. Any parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` is deleted; the facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)` once per method.\n+* SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) as a documented consumer convenience. The projection is **not** part of the trait contract:\n+   - Adding a variant is non-breaking\n+   - Refining a variant's payload is breaking only for consumers that destructure that variant\n+   - Removing a variant is breaking only for consumers that pattern-match on it\n+   - The trait signature is unaffected by any of these changes\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST also ship the typed sub-enum vocabulary (`field::TargetHostCode`, `reason::auth::FailureReason`, `gts::Resource`, …) co-located with the wire-string constants they project from, each with `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire` helpers. Round-trip `Problem` tests pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant so the conversion is infallible and forward-compatible (new canonical categories surface with full fidelity).\n+* The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"...\")]` proc-macro literals are the one exception (proc macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip Problem tests pin them.\n+* SDK error types must not carry transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) — those belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+* Trait method rustdoc MUST cross-link to the SDK's projection type (when one exists) so the typed surface is discoverable.\n+\n+### Confirmation\n+\n+The OAGW SDK demonstrates the pattern end-to-end:\n+\n+(a) `ServiceGatewayClientV1` trait methods return `Result<_, CanonicalError>`.\n+\n+(b) `oagw-sdk` ships `ServiceGatewayError` — a 14-variant projection with `From<CanonicalError>` — as a consumer convenience. Variants: `RateLimited`, `Timeout`, `Unavailable`, `AuthFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `InvalidTargetHost`, `Validation`, `NotFound`, `AlreadyExists`, `FailedPrecondition`, `Aborted`, `Internal`, `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }`.\n+\n+(c) Typed sub-enums are co-located with their wire-string constants:\n+- `field::TargetHostCode` next to `MISSING_TARGET_HOST` / `INVALID_TARGET_HOST` / `UNKNOWN_TARGET_HOST`\n+- `reason::auth::FailureReason` next to `PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND` / `PLUGIN_FAILED` / `PLUGIN_INTERNAL`\n+- `reason::permission::DenialReason` next to `AUTHZ_DENIED` / `TENANT_*` / `CORS_*`\n+- `gts::Resource` next to the six `*_SCHEMA` constants\n+\n+(d) The impl crate's parallel `From<DomainError> for ServiceGatewayError` ladder is deleted (~110 lines + 4 tests). The single AIP-193 mapping is `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in `oagw/src/api/rest/error.rs`.\n+\n+(e) Round-trip `Problem` tests in `oagw-sdk/src/error.rs::tests` pin all 26 `field::*` constants, 8 `reason::*` constants, 1 `quota::*` constant, and 6 `gts::*` constants to their wire JSON paths.\n+\n+(f) Mini-chat (OAGW's only current consumer) defines `From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError` that chains through `ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()` internally, so every call site stays as plain `?` propagation without `.map_err` boilerplate.\n+\n+(g) Out-of-process consumers can use `TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) to reconstruct typed errors from wire bytes. The full chain is `Problem JSON → Problem → CanonicalError → (optional) SdkError`.\n+\n+(h) Workspace `cargo test` passes (~1,800 tests across `oagw-sdk`, `oagw`, `mini-chat`, `modkit-canonical-errors`).\n+\n+## The Pattern\n+\n+### Trait signature — canonical at the boundary\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait XxxClientV1: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+        -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>;\n+    // every fallible method returns CanonicalError\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Impl-side facade — single `.map_err`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+    -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>\n+{\n+    self.inner.do_thing(&ctx, req)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(CanonicalError::from)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The single AIP-193 ladder lives in `{impl}/src/api/rest/error.rs`:\n+\n+```rust\n+impl From<DomainError> for CanonicalError {\n+    fn from(err: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => UserResourceError::not_found(/* … */)\n+                .with_resource(id.to_string())\n+                .create(),\n+            // … one arm per domain variant, AIP-193 mapping\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Optional projection — typed view over canonical\n+\n+When an SDK's consumers benefit from flat typed dispatch, the SDK ships a `From<CanonicalError>`-driven enum **alongside** the trait — not in the trait signature:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs\n+\n+use modkit_canonical_errors::CanonicalError;\n+use crate::field::TargetHostCode;\n+use crate::gts::Resource;\n+use crate::reason::auth::FailureReason as AuthFailureReason;\n+use crate::reason::permission::DenialReason as PermissionDenialReason;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Error)]\n+pub enum ServiceGatewayError {\n+    #[error(\"rate limit exceeded\")]\n+    RateLimited { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request timed out\")]\n+    Timeout,\n+\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable\")]\n+    Unavailable { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"authentication failed [{reason}]: {detail}\")]\n+    AuthFailed { reason: AuthFailureReason, detail: String },\n+\n+    // … one variant per dispatch case, driven by consumer needs …\n+\n+    /// Catch-all for canonical categories the SDK does not model.\n+    /// Preserves full canonical context for inspection / forward-compat.\n+    #[error(\"[{}] {}\", canonical.gts_type(), canonical.detail())]\n+    Other { canonical: CanonicalError },\n+}\n+\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for ServiceGatewayError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        match &err {\n+            CanonicalError::ResourceExhausted { .. } => Self::RateLimited { retry_after_secs: None },\n+            CanonicalError::DeadlineExceeded { .. } => Self::Timeout,\n+            // … one arm per canonical variant the SDK models, plus\n+            // `_ => Self::Other { canonical: err.clone() }` catch-all\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Co-located vocabulary\n+\n+Wire-string constants and their typed sub-enums live together. Example for `Unauthenticated.ctx.reason`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/reason.rs\n+pub mod auth {\n+    pub const PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND: &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_FAILED:    &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_FAILED\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_INTERNAL:  &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_INTERNAL\";\n+\n+    /// Typed view of the wire `reason` strings above.\n+    #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+    pub enum FailureReason {\n+        PluginNotFound,\n+        PluginFailed,\n+        PluginInternal,\n+        Unknown(String),\n+    }\n+\n+    impl FailureReason {\n+        pub fn from_wire(s: Option<&str>) -> Self { /* … */ }\n+        pub fn as_wire(&self) -> &str { /* … */ }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Same pattern in `field.rs` (`TargetHostCode` etc.), `gts.rs` (`Resource`), `reason::permission` (`DenialReason`).\n+\n+### Round-trip tests pin the vocabulary\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs::tests\n+#[test]\n+fn auth_reason_constants_round_trip() {\n+    for r in [reason::auth::PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND, /* … */] {\n+        let err = CanonicalError::unauthenticated().with_reason(r).create();\n+        let json = serde_json::to_value(&Problem::from(err)).unwrap();\n+        assert_eq!(json[\"context\"][\"reason\"], r);\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception (macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip tests pin them.\n+\n+## Consumer Integration\n+\n+Three patterns, all valid:\n+\n+### Pattern 1 — pure propagation (no projection)\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;  // ? propagates CanonicalError\n+```\n+\n+Caller's own error type implements `From<CanonicalError>`. The projection isn't used. Right choice when the consumer only propagates or dispatches on broad canonical category.\n+\n+### Pattern 2 — explicit projection at the call site\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(ServiceGatewayError::from)?;\n+\n+match err {\n+    ServiceGatewayError::RateLimited { retry_after_secs } => /* backoff */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::Timeout                          => /* retry */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::AuthFailed {\n+        reason: AuthFailureReason::PluginInternal, ..\n+    } => /* gateway-side auth broken — transient */,\n+    _ => /* fallback */,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Explicit about projecting. Caller's error type implements `From<ServiceGatewayError>`. Right choice for one-off typed-dispatch sites scattered across a codebase that otherwise propagates canonical.\n+\n+### Pattern 3 — transparent chaining via `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError`\n+\n+```rust\n+// Define once in the consumer crate:\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for OwnConsumerError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        // Route through the SDK's typed projection internally.\n+        ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Then every call site stays plain `?`:\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;\n+```\n+\n+Eliminates per-call-site boilerplate while keeping the typed dispatch surface. **Recommended** for consumers that always want typed dispatch. Mini-chat uses this pattern.\n+\n+### Reverse direction (consumer wraps SDK failure in its own canonical)\n+\n+Often a consumer wants to catch an SDK failure and re-emit it as a canonical error in its own resource scope (e.g. `account-management` catching an OAGW call and re-emitting it as a tenant-management failure). The canonical-at-boundary contract makes this trivial — the consumer already has `CanonicalError` from the `?`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(|canonical| {\n+        AccountMgmtResourceError::failed_precondition()\n+            .with_precondition_violation(/* … */)\n+            .create()\n+    })?;\n+```\n+\n+No reverse `From<SdkError> for CanonicalError` impl is needed — canonical is already at the boundary.\n+\n+### Cross-process round-trip\n+\n+`TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) closes the out-of-process loop. An HTTP/REST consumer's full chain:\n+\n+```\n+network bytes\n+  → serde_json::from_slice → Problem\n+  → CanonicalError::try_from(problem) → CanonicalError\n+  → (optional) ServiceGatewayError::from(canonical) → ServiceGatewayError\n+```\n+\n+The first two hops are mandatory and lossless (modulo wire-strip fields like `Internal.description` which are `#[serde(skip)]` by design — production wire never carries the diagnostic). The third hop is opt-in.\n+\n+## Design Rules\n+\n+1. **Trait signature returns `CanonicalError`** for every fallible method. Document this in the trait's top-level rustdoc and cross-link the optional projection.\n+2. **Impl-side facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)`** once per method. No parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder.\n+3. **SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection** as a consumer convenience. When shipped:\n+   - MUST be infallible (`From<CanonicalError>`, not `TryFrom`)\n+   - MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant for forward-compat\n+   - Variant set is driven by consumer dispatch — audit workspace `match` arms before designing\n+   - Variant names encode consumer intent, not impl vocabulary\n+4. **When a projection is shipped, co-locate typed sub-enums with wire-string constants**:\n+   - `gts.rs` — `*_SCHEMA` constants + typed `Resource` enum for `NotFound` / `AlreadyExists.ctx.resource_type`\n+   - `reason.rs` — submodules per canonical category, each holding both `pub const` reason values and a typed enum\n+   - `field.rs` — `pub const` constants for `InvalidArgument.ctx.field_violations[].reason`, plus typed sub-enums for families consumers dispatch on\n+   - `quota.rs` — `pub const` `subject` values for `ResourceExhausted.ctx.violations[].subject`\n+5. **Each typed sub-enum exposes `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire`** (`from_wire` returns `Self` with an `Unknown(String)` catch-all when every wire value is meaningful, or `Option<Self>` when only a few wire strings are valid).\n+6. **Impl crate references the SDK constants** at every site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception; the round-trip tests pin them.\n+7. **Round-trip `Problem` tests** in `{sdk}/src/error.rs::tests` pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+8. **No transport fields in the projection**: `instance` and `trace_id` belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+9. **Document the projection** in the SDK's `error.rs` module rustdoc: state it is an opt-in convenience, show the three consumer integration patterns, include a consumer-dispatch reference table, and link to this ADR.\n+\n+## Per-SDK Migration\n+\n+Every SDK uses the same trait-contract migration. Whether to **also** ship a projection is a separate per-SDK decision based on consumer dispatch needs.\n+\n+| SDK | `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError`? | Ship projection? | Effort |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| `simple-user-settings-sdk` | yes | no | ~30 min (delete parallel ladder, switch trait to `CanonicalError`) |\n+| `nodes-registry-sdk` | yes | no | ~30 min |\n+| `mini-chat-sdk` | yes | no | ~1 hr (plugin-SPI enums separate, do not migrate) |\n+| `resource-group-sdk` | yes | re-evaluate if consumers want typed cycle/limit dispatch | ~1–2 hr |\n+| `file-parser` | yes | no | ~1 hr |\n+| `types-registry-sdk` | yes | likely yes (typed `ValidationError` payload) | ~half day |\n+| `oagw-sdk` | yes | **yes** | **done** (reference implementation) |\n+| `credstore-sdk` | **no** | TBD after consumer audit | ~1 day (author canonical boundary first) |\n+| `authn-resolver-sdk` | **no** | no | ~1 day |\n+| `tenant-resolver-sdk` | **no** | no | ~1 day |\n+| `authz-resolver-sdk` | **no** | likely yes (`EnforcerError::Denied { deny_reason }` — typed payload) | ~1–2 days |\n+\n+For the four resolver SDKs at the bottom, the canonical boundary mapping is the real cost. The trait-contract switch is trivial once that lands.\n+\n+## Known Gaps\n+\n+1. **`retry_after_seconds` on `ResourceExhausted`.** The canonical `ResourceExhausted` context type does not yet carry `retry_after_seconds` (see [`libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs`](../../../../libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/context.rs)). The retry hint only lands in the HTTP `Retry-After` header; in-process callers see `None`. The semantically correct fix is to add `retry_after_seconds: Option<u64>` to `QuotaViolation` (per-violation, not per-category — memory exhaustion has no retry window while rate-limit does).","path":"docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md","commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I went ahead and implemented this","created_at":"2026-05-27T19:42:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T19:42:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313415150","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313415150"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313415150"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313415150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":331,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3285042325,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":331,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313418403","pull_request_review_id":4375539320,"id":3313418403,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7FfsCj","diff_hunk":"@@ -140,6 +145,208 @@ impl From<CanonicalError> for Problem {\n     }\n }\n \n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+// Round-trip: Problem → CanonicalError\n+//\n+// Reverse direction of `From<CanonicalError> for Problem`. Out-of-process SDK\n+// consumers receive `application/problem+json` over the wire, deserialize into\n+// `Problem`, and reconstruct the typed `CanonicalError` via this `TryFrom`.\n+// In-process consumers do not need this hop — they hold `CanonicalError`\n+// directly from the ClientHub call.\n+//\n+// Lossy by design:\n+// * `Internal.description` and `Unknown.description` are `#[serde(skip)]` on\n+//   the wire, so they reconstruct as empty strings. This is intentional —\n+//   production wire responses never carry the server-side diagnostic.\n+// * Transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) live on `Problem`, not on\n+//   `CanonicalError`. Callers that need them should read them off the\n+//   `Problem` before converting.\n+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+/// Prefix on `Problem.problem_type` produced by the forward conversion.\n+const PROBLEM_TYPE_PREFIX: &str = \"gts://\";\n+\n+/// Reasons a `Problem` cannot be reconstructed as a `CanonicalError`.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum ProblemConversionError {\n+    /// The `problem_type` URI does not match any of the 16 canonical\n+    /// category identifiers. Either the server emitted a non-canonical\n+    /// problem or the wire format has drifted.\n+    #[error(\"unknown canonical problem_type: {0}\")]","path":"libs/modkit-canonical-errors/src/problem.rs","commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I updated the verbage to not use \"canonical\" in this scenario.","created_at":"2026-05-27T19:43:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T19:43:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313418403","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313418403"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313418403"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313418403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3312464800,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313463960","pull_request_review_id":4375593682,"id":3313463960,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Ff3KY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,357 @@\n+---\n+status: accepted\n+date: 2026-05-20\n+---\n+\n+# SDK Error Surface: Canonical at the Boundary, Opt-in Typed Projection\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-errors-adr-sdk-canonical-projection`\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+Cyber Ware ships per-module SDK crates (`oagw-sdk`, `credstore-sdk`, `tenant-resolver-sdk`, …) that ClientHub consumers use to call other modules in-process. Each SDK historically exposed a hand-rolled error enum (`ServiceGatewayError`, `CredStoreError`, …) that the impl crate populated through a parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` ladder, distinct from the `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` ladder used on the REST boundary.\n+\n+This caused three concrete problems:\n+\n+1. **Contract is hostage to internal taxonomy.** Adding a new domain variant means an SDK contract break.\n+2. **Two parallel boundary mappings.** Each impl crate maintains `From<DomainError> for SdkError` for ClientHub consumers *and* `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` for REST. They classify the same variants, can disagree, and must update in lockstep.\n+3. **Consumers learn impl vocabulary.** Pattern matching on `ServiceGatewayError::PayloadTooLarge` couples the consumer to the impl crate's word for that concept.\n+\n+A pure-alias approach (`pub use CanonicalError as XxxError`) fixes all three but pushes context-walking onto consumers who want sub-category dispatch. Putting a typed projection in the trait signature gives flat dispatch but makes the projection variant set part of the SDK contract — variant changes become breaking, and consumers using multiple SDKs see N different SDK-specific names for the same canonical category.\n+\n+What's the right shape for the SDK error surface?\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+* Single authoritative AIP-193 categorization — domain → canonical mapping must live in exactly one place per module\n+* Information fidelity at the SDK boundary — projection loss should be a consumer-side opt-in, not a default\n+* Stable SDK contract — variant changes in the projection must not be SDK semver-major events\n+* Cross-SDK uniformity — consumers using multiple SDKs should see a uniform error type at trait boundaries\n+* Ergonomic typed dispatch when consumers want it — flat match arms, typed sub-enums for context discriminators\n+* Conformance with `cpt-cf-errors-adr-canonical-error-categories` — finite vocabulary, no module-specific error categories\n+* `cpt-cf-errors-principle-single-error-gateway` — REST path goes through `CanonicalError` unchanged\n+\n+## Decision Outcome\n+\n+SDKs expose errors in **two layers**:\n+\n+- **At the trait boundary**: `Result<_, CanonicalError>`. Every SDK trait returns the platform's canonical error type — no SDK-specific error type in the trait contract.\n+- **As an opt-in consumer convenience**: SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) for consumers that want flat typed dispatch. Consumers project at the call site via `.map_err(SdkError::from)?`, or chain transparently through a `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError` impl.\n+\n+The trait signature is uniform across all SDKs. The projection lives in the SDK as a typed view over canonical — not as the wire contract or the trait contract — and individual SDKs add it only when their consumers benefit from it. Future projection variant changes (adding, splitting, refining) are non-breaking on the trait contract; only consumers that opted into typed dispatch are affected, and only at sites that pattern-matched on the changed variants.\n+\n+### Consequences\n+\n+* The SDK trait returns `Result<_, CanonicalError>` for every fallible method. No SDK-specific error type appears in the trait signature.\n+* The impl crate keeps **only** `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in its REST error module. Any parallel `From<DomainError> for SdkError` is deleted; the facade calls `.map_err(CanonicalError::from)` once per method.\n+* SDKs MAY ship a typed `SdkError` projection enum (with `From<CanonicalError>`) as a documented consumer convenience. The projection is **not** part of the trait contract:\n+   - Adding a variant is non-breaking\n+   - Refining a variant's payload is breaking only for consumers that destructure that variant\n+   - Removing a variant is breaking only for consumers that pattern-match on it\n+   - The trait signature is unaffected by any of these changes\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST also ship the typed sub-enum vocabulary (`field::TargetHostCode`, `reason::auth::FailureReason`, `gts::Resource`, …) co-located with the wire-string constants they project from, each with `pub fn from_wire` and `pub fn as_wire` helpers. Round-trip `Problem` tests pin every wire-string constant to its expected JSON path.\n+* When an SDK ships a projection, it MUST include a catch-all `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }` variant so the conversion is infallible and forward-compatible (new canonical categories surface with full fidelity).\n+* The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"...\")]` proc-macro literals are the one exception (proc macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip Problem tests pin them.\n+* SDK error types must not carry transport fields (`instance`, `trace_id`) — those belong to the `Problem` envelope.\n+* Trait method rustdoc MUST cross-link to the SDK's projection type (when one exists) so the typed surface is discoverable.\n+\n+### Confirmation\n+\n+The OAGW SDK demonstrates the pattern end-to-end:\n+\n+(a) `ServiceGatewayClientV1` trait methods return `Result<_, CanonicalError>`.\n+\n+(b) `oagw-sdk` ships `ServiceGatewayError` — a 14-variant projection with `From<CanonicalError>` — as a consumer convenience. Variants: `RateLimited`, `Timeout`, `Unavailable`, `AuthFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `InvalidTargetHost`, `Validation`, `NotFound`, `AlreadyExists`, `FailedPrecondition`, `Aborted`, `Internal`, `Other { canonical: CanonicalError }`.\n+\n+(c) Typed sub-enums are co-located with their wire-string constants:\n+- `field::TargetHostCode` next to `MISSING_TARGET_HOST` / `INVALID_TARGET_HOST` / `UNKNOWN_TARGET_HOST`\n+- `reason::auth::FailureReason` next to `PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND` / `PLUGIN_FAILED` / `PLUGIN_INTERNAL`\n+- `reason::permission::DenialReason` next to `AUTHZ_DENIED` / `TENANT_*` / `CORS_*`\n+- `gts::Resource` next to the six `*_SCHEMA` constants\n+\n+(d) The impl crate's parallel `From<DomainError> for ServiceGatewayError` ladder is deleted (~110 lines + 4 tests). The single AIP-193 mapping is `From<DomainError> for CanonicalError` in `oagw/src/api/rest/error.rs`.\n+\n+(e) Round-trip `Problem` tests in `oagw-sdk/src/error.rs::tests` pin all 26 `field::*` constants, 8 `reason::*` constants, 1 `quota::*` constant, and 6 `gts::*` constants to their wire JSON paths.\n+\n+(f) Mini-chat (OAGW's only current consumer) defines `From<CanonicalError> for LlmProviderError` that chains through `ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()` internally, so every call site stays as plain `?` propagation without `.map_err` boilerplate.\n+\n+(g) Out-of-process consumers can use `TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) to reconstruct typed errors from wire bytes. The full chain is `Problem JSON → Problem → CanonicalError → (optional) SdkError`.\n+\n+(h) Workspace `cargo test` passes (~1,800 tests across `oagw-sdk`, `oagw`, `mini-chat`, `modkit-canonical-errors`).\n+\n+## The Pattern\n+\n+### Trait signature — canonical at the boundary\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait XxxClientV1: Send + Sync {\n+    async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+        -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>;\n+    // every fallible method returns CanonicalError\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Impl-side facade — single `.map_err`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn do_thing(&self, ctx: SecurityContext, req: Request)\n+    -> Result<Response, CanonicalError>\n+{\n+    self.inner.do_thing(&ctx, req)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(CanonicalError::from)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The single AIP-193 ladder lives in `{impl}/src/api/rest/error.rs`:\n+\n+```rust\n+impl From<DomainError> for CanonicalError {\n+    fn from(err: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => UserResourceError::not_found(/* … */)\n+                .with_resource(id.to_string())\n+                .create(),\n+            // … one arm per domain variant, AIP-193 mapping\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Optional projection — typed view over canonical\n+\n+When an SDK's consumers benefit from flat typed dispatch, the SDK ships a `From<CanonicalError>`-driven enum **alongside** the trait — not in the trait signature:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs\n+\n+use modkit_canonical_errors::CanonicalError;\n+use crate::field::TargetHostCode;\n+use crate::gts::Resource;\n+use crate::reason::auth::FailureReason as AuthFailureReason;\n+use crate::reason::permission::DenialReason as PermissionDenialReason;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Error)]\n+pub enum ServiceGatewayError {\n+    #[error(\"rate limit exceeded\")]\n+    RateLimited { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request timed out\")]\n+    Timeout,\n+\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable\")]\n+    Unavailable { retry_after_secs: Option<u64> },\n+\n+    #[error(\"authentication failed [{reason}]: {detail}\")]\n+    AuthFailed { reason: AuthFailureReason, detail: String },\n+\n+    // … one variant per dispatch case, driven by consumer needs …\n+\n+    /// Catch-all for canonical categories the SDK does not model.\n+    /// Preserves full canonical context for inspection / forward-compat.\n+    #[error(\"[{}] {}\", canonical.gts_type(), canonical.detail())]\n+    Other { canonical: CanonicalError },\n+}\n+\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for ServiceGatewayError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        match &err {\n+            CanonicalError::ResourceExhausted { .. } => Self::RateLimited { retry_after_secs: None },\n+            CanonicalError::DeadlineExceeded { .. } => Self::Timeout,\n+            // … one arm per canonical variant the SDK models, plus\n+            // `_ => Self::Other { canonical: err.clone() }` catch-all\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Co-located vocabulary\n+\n+Wire-string constants and their typed sub-enums live together. Example for `Unauthenticated.ctx.reason`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/reason.rs\n+pub mod auth {\n+    pub const PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND: &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_FAILED:    &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_FAILED\";\n+    pub const PLUGIN_INTERNAL:  &str = \"AUTH_PLUGIN_INTERNAL\";\n+\n+    /// Typed view of the wire `reason` strings above.\n+    #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+    pub enum FailureReason {\n+        PluginNotFound,\n+        PluginFailed,\n+        PluginInternal,\n+        Unknown(String),\n+    }\n+\n+    impl FailureReason {\n+        pub fn from_wire(s: Option<&str>) -> Self { /* … */ }\n+        pub fn as_wire(&self) -> &str { /* … */ }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Same pattern in `field.rs` (`TargetHostCode` etc.), `gts.rs` (`Resource`), `reason::permission` (`DenialReason`).\n+\n+### Round-trip tests pin the vocabulary\n+\n+```rust\n+// {sdk}/src/error.rs::tests\n+#[test]\n+fn auth_reason_constants_round_trip() {\n+    for r in [reason::auth::PLUGIN_NOT_FOUND, /* … */] {\n+        let err = CanonicalError::unauthenticated().with_reason(r).create();\n+        let json = serde_json::to_value(&Problem::from(err)).unwrap();\n+        assert_eq!(json[\"context\"][\"reason\"], r);\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The impl crate references the SDK constants at every construction site that previously hardcoded a wire literal. The `#[resource_error(\"…\")]` proc-macro literals are the exception (macros cannot resolve constants); the round-trip tests pin them.\n+\n+## Consumer Integration\n+\n+Three patterns, all valid:\n+\n+### Pattern 1 — pure propagation (no projection)\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;  // ? propagates CanonicalError\n+```\n+\n+Caller's own error type implements `From<CanonicalError>`. The projection isn't used. Right choice when the consumer only propagates or dispatches on broad canonical category.\n+\n+### Pattern 2 — explicit projection at the call site\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(ServiceGatewayError::from)?;\n+\n+match err {\n+    ServiceGatewayError::RateLimited { retry_after_secs } => /* backoff */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::Timeout                          => /* retry */,\n+    ServiceGatewayError::AuthFailed {\n+        reason: AuthFailureReason::PluginInternal, ..\n+    } => /* gateway-side auth broken — transient */,\n+    _ => /* fallback */,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Explicit about projecting. Caller's error type implements `From<ServiceGatewayError>`. Right choice for one-off typed-dispatch sites scattered across a codebase that otherwise propagates canonical.\n+\n+### Pattern 3 — transparent chaining via `From<CanonicalError> for OwnError`\n+\n+```rust\n+// Define once in the consumer crate:\n+impl From<CanonicalError> for OwnConsumerError {\n+    fn from(err: CanonicalError) -> Self {\n+        // Route through the SDK's typed projection internally.\n+        ServiceGatewayError::from(err).into()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Then every call site stays plain `?`:\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await?;\n+```\n+\n+Eliminates per-call-site boilerplate while keeping the typed dispatch surface. **Recommended** for consumers that always want typed dispatch. Mini-chat uses this pattern.\n+\n+### Reverse direction (consumer wraps SDK failure in its own canonical)\n+\n+Often a consumer wants to catch an SDK failure and re-emit it as a canonical error in its own resource scope (e.g. `account-management` catching an OAGW call and re-emitting it as a tenant-management failure). The canonical-at-boundary contract makes this trivial — the consumer already has `CanonicalError` from the `?`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let upstream = gateway.get_upstream(&ctx, id).await\n+    .map_err(|canonical| {\n+        AccountMgmtResourceError::failed_precondition()\n+            .with_precondition_violation(/* … */)\n+            .create()\n+    })?;\n+```\n+\n+No reverse `From<SdkError> for CanonicalError` impl is needed — canonical is already at the boundary.\n+\n+### Cross-process round-trip\n+\n+`TryFrom<Problem> for CanonicalError` (in `modkit-canonical-errors`) closes the out-of-process loop. An HTTP/REST consumer's full chain:\n+\n+```\n+network bytes\n+  → serde_json::from_slice → Problem\n+  → CanonicalError::try_from(problem) → CanonicalError\n+  → (optional) ServiceGatewayError::from(canonical) → ServiceGatewayError\n+```\n+\n+The first two hops are mandatory and lossless (modulo wire-strip fields like `Internal.description` which are `#[serde(skip)]` by design — production wire never carries the diagnostic). The third hop is opt-in.\n+\n+## Design Rules","path":"docs/arch/errors/ADR/0005-cpt-cf-adr-sdk-canonical-projection.md","commit_id":"067ee36ccd50df28982c8d373792b092d2ea6e2e","original_commit_id":"00a8f90253c53f63dbbea1ffa954c1d849b7717d","user":{"login":"asmith987","id":260502008,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4bx-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260502008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987","html_url":"https://github.com/asmith987","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmith987/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I added two additional sections that:\n- Explain when to ship a projection and when to skip one\n- Explain that not all SDKs must return CanonicalError since as you mentioned, the SDKs will only expose local in-process functionality. ","created_at":"2026-05-27T19:52:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T19:52:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313463960","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313463960"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1962#discussion_r3313463960"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1962"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3313463960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":309,"original_line":289,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3312521240,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":289,"position":309,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1961,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1961","source_state":"closed","source_author":"fluiderson","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1961] feat(dylint): enforce `docs.rs.all-features` for publishable crates","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"docs-all-feats","pr_head_sha":"5e341b19cac95a5904ff8da35666478d7424e5f7","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"fluiderson","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url"