r/authz-resolver-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/tenant-resolver/plugins/static-tr-plugin/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/nodes-registry/nodes-registry-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/authz-resolver/plugins/tr-authz-plugin/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/grpc-hub/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/tenant-resolver/tenant-resolver-sdk/Cargo.toml\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (25)</summary>\n\n* modules/file-parser/Cargo.toml\n* modules/mini-chat/mini-chat-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-sdk/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-macros/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-http/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-canonical-errors-macro/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-odata/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-node-info/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-gts/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-gts-macro/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-db-macros/Cargo.toml\n* modules/credstore/credstore/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-odata-macros/Cargo.toml\n* libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/src/domain/error_tests.rs\n* libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-utils/Cargo.toml\n* libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-transport-grpc/Cargo.toml\n* modules/credstore/plugins/static-credstore-plugin/Cargo.toml\n* modules/system/account-management/account-management-sdk/Cargo.toml\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces a new Dylint linter (DE1201) that enforces `metadata.docs.rs.all-features = true` on publishable crates, applies the setting to approximately 50 crates workspace-wide, and includes comprehensive validation through integration tests and fixture-based scenarios.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Documentation Feature Lint (DE1201) and Workspace Enforcement**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Lint Crate Manifest and Configuration** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de12_documentation/de1201_docs_rs_all_features/Cargo.toml`, `src/lib.rs` (lines 1–30) | Defines the new `de1201_docs_rs_all_features` lint crate as a cdylib with dependencies on `cargo_metadata`, `serde`, and `serde_json`. Configuration struct deserializes `excluded_crates` list from `dylint.toml`. |\n| **Lint Registration and Check Implementation** <br> `src/lib.rs` (lines 32–115) | Registers `DE1201_DOCS_RS_ALL_FEATURES` via `impl_late_lint!` and implements `check_crate` to read Cargo metadata, locate the current package by manifest path, check publishability and exclusion status, detect missing or disabled `metadata.docs.rs.all-features`, and emit a diagnostic with help text. |\n| **Path Utilities, Gating Logic, and Status Parsing** <br> `src/lib.rs` (lines 117–332) | Helper functions for manifest path resolution, package lookup, and path normalization; publishability gating (treats omitted `publish` as publishable); `DocsRsAllFeaturesStatus` enum and JSON parsing to distinguish enabled, disabled, missing key, missing table, and non-boolean cases; unit tests covering all branches. |\n| **Integration Test Harness and Fixtures** <br> `tests/cargo_fixtures.rs`, `tests/fixtures/*` | Integration test that runs `cargo dylint` against four fixture crates: one passing (all-features enabled), one excluded via `dylint.toml`, one missing metadata, and one unpublishable. Includes command execution, environment setup, path resolution, assertion helpers, and Cargo.lock cleanup. |\n| **Linter Registration and Documentation** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/Cargo.toml`, `tools/dylint_lints/README.md` | Registers the new lint crate in workspace members and documents the DE1201 requirement in the Dylint README under the DE12xx documentation checklist. |\n| **Workspace Crate Manifest Updates** <br> `libs/modkit-*/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`, `libs/rustls-corecrypto-provider/Cargo.toml`, `libs/system-sdks/*/Cargo.toml`, `modules/credstore/*/Cargo.toml`, `modules/file-parser/Cargo.toml`, `modules/mini-chat/*/Cargo.toml`, `modules/system/*/Cargo.toml` | Applied `metadata.docs.rs.all-features = true` to approximately 50 publishable crates across libs, modules, and system submodules to enable docs.rs documentation builds with all Cargo feature flags enabled. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n> 🐰 *A linter hops into the fray,* \n> *Checking metadata day by day,*\n> *docs.rs shines with features wide,*\n> *Fifty crates now unified with pride!* 🎉\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4508000405/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4510426177","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1961#issuecomment-4510426177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1961","id":4510426177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABDNekQQ","user":{"login":"fluiderson","id":90795031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzk1MDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90795031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson","html_url":"https://github.com/fluiderson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T16:36:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T16:38:02Z","body":"> This kind of checking is outside of rust source code, and dylint rules are expensive.\r\n\r\nI see. For context, I've took [existing `Cargo.toml` lints from Clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy/tree/5663c0285499201205479b3f6dba116cdce7afed/clippy_lints/src/cargo) as references. If we don't want any lints that enforce rules on more than just Rust source files, we should probably add this restriction to the docs under `tools/dylint_lints`.\r\n\r\n> this approach can be easily solved once the CLI is done(WIP)\r\n\r\nI'm not well-informed on the plans for our CLI. Do I understand correctly that `package.metadata.docs.rs.all-features = true` could be enforced with it in the future without using Dylint? If so, we can close this PR and wait for the CLI.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4510426177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4511257155","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1961#issuecomment-4511257155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1961","id":4511257155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABDORSQw","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T18:11:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T18:11:52Z","body":"> > This kind of checking is outside of rust source code, and dylint rules are expensive.\r\n> \r\n> I see. For context, I've took [existing `Cargo.toml` lints from Clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy/tree/5663c0285499201205479b3f6dba116cdce7afed/clippy_lints/src/cargo) as references. If we don't want any lints that enforce rules on more than just Rust source files, we should probably add this restriction to the docs under `tools/dylint_lints`.\r\n> \r\n> > this approach can be easily solved once the CLI is done(WIP)\r\n> \r\n> I'm not well-informed on the plans for our CLI. Do I understand correctly that `package.metadata.docs.rs.all-features = true` could be enforced with it in the future without using Dylint? If so, we can close this PR and wait for the CLI.\r\n\r\nI see, let me propose to merge this changes and once the CLI is ready, we can deprecate certain lints that can be enforced outside of the scope of analysing rust source code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4511257155/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4555023640","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1961#issuecomment-4555023640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1961","id":4555023640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABD4AlGA","user":{"login":"fluiderson","id":90795031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzk1MDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90795031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson","html_url":"https://github.com/fluiderson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.githu