l request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `0822d432-33b5-4b8b-8bd2-05ce39886bfa`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 5e004716109082218f5848175c4cb3b20c06aa4c and 77bd54d5947d7a2fb8fff7533490bce9cf4542a0.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (4)</summary>\n\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/README.md`\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/constraints.toml`\n* `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/rules.md`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/hello_world/__init__.py`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR systematically renames the SDLC kit identifier from `cf-sdlc` to `cyberware-sdlc` across configuration and documentation files. The kit's structure and artifact constraints remain unchanged; only the naming label is updated throughout.\n\n## Changes\n\n**SDLC Kit Identifier Rename**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **SDLC kit configuration and metadata** <br> `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/README.md`, `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/constraints.toml`, `.cypilot/config/kits/sdlc/rules.md` | Kit identifier renamed from `cf-sdlc` to `cyberware-sdlc` in the README, all six artifact constraint sections (PRD, ADR, DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION, FEATURE, UPSTREAM_REQS) in the constraints configuration, and the rules documentation header. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~3 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A kit rebrands from cf to cw,\n> Through README, rules, and constraints too—\n> Same structure shines, now with new name,\n> The cyberware-sdlc stakes its claim! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start --