k/src/authz.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR adds a workspace `url` dev-dependency, updates HttpClient doctest examples to use `.send().await?` and include doctest scaffolding, refactors `USAGE_RECORD` construction to `ResourceType::from_static(...)`, updates tests to use accessors, and changes a GTS schema macro base type and its `schema_id`.\n\n## Changes\n\n**HTTP Client Documentation and Dependencies**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Fetch example and dependency addition** <br> `libs/modkit-http/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-http/src/client.rs`|The `HttpClient::fetch` documentation example now uses `.send().await?.json().await`, and the `url` workspace dependency is added to `dev-dependencies`.|\n|**HTTP method doctest scaffolding** <br> `libs/modkit-http/src/client.rs`|All HTTP method doc examples (`get`, `post`, `put`, `patch`, `delete`, `head`, `options`) were rewritten with hidden imports/async scaffolding and `Ok(())` terminators so they compile as standalone doctests.|\n\n**Usage Collector SDK Refactoring**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**ResourceType initialization and test updates** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs`|`USAGE_RECORD` is constructed with `ResourceType::from_static(...)` instead of a struct literal; tests now call `USAGE_RECORD.name()` and `USAGE_RECORD.supported_properties()` rather than accessing fields.|\n|**GTS schema configuration update** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/gts.rs`|The `#[struct_to_gts_schema]` for `UsageCollectorPluginSpecV1` changes `base` to `PluginV1` and updates the generated `schema_id` to `gts.cf.modkit.plugins.plugin.v1~cf.core.usage.plugin.v1~`.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hop through docs with tidy care,  \n> Hidden imports placed with flair,  \n> `.send().await` now sings,  \n> ResourceTypes wear new strings,  \n> Schemas twirl a brand-new pair.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4496130875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1954,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954","source_state":"closed","source_author":"aviator5","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1954] feat(modkit): add error_502/503/504 OperationBuilder helpers","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"issue-1921","pr_head_sha":"e64498678a8ca55f421235243741b968ba28a8ea","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"aviator5","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1954","id":3714450130,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7dZgLS","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1954","number":1954,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(modkit): add error_502/503/504 OperationBuilder helpers","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1921.\r\n\r\nOperationBuilder exposed convenience wrappers for the common 4xx codes and 500, but had no helper for 502/503/504. 503 in particular is reachable across most modules on PDP/IdP/upstream transport failure, so handlers had to fall back to the verbose problem_response() form to declare it in OpenAPI. Add three thin wrappers matching the existing error_4xx pattern.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## New Features\n\n* Added convenience methods for declaring RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` error responses for three additional HTTP status codes: 502 (Bad Gateway), 503 (Service Unavailable), and 504 (Gateway Timeout). These methods streamline error handling in API operation definitions.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-20T06:59:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T10:58:42Z","closed_at":"2026-05-22T10:58:42Z","merged_at":"2026-05-22T10:58:42Z","merge_commit_sha":"cb39e761d837b31579b5894c6c1a48d47e1b48a5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1954/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1954/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1954/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/e64498678a8ca55f421235243741b968ba28a8ea","head":{"label":"aviator5:issue-1921","ref":"issue-1921","sha":"e64498678a8ca55f421235243741b968ba28a8ea","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://ap