 review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4495486554","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1954#issuecomment-4495486554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1954","id":4495486554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABC_OuWg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T06:59:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T06:59:50Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `124995c9-9a91-4154-962b-c97f65e91bc7`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 4e87c10fd4e67a3cd313663c7bef624be84806df and e64498678a8ca55f421235243741b968ba28a8ea.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/operation_builder.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR adds three convenience methods to `OperationBuilder` for declaring 502 Bad Gateway, 503 Service Unavailable, and 504 Gateway Timeout error responses. Each method wraps the existing `problem_response` method with the appropriate HTTP status code and description.\n\n## Changes\n\n**API Operation Builder Error Responses**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**5xx error response convenience methods** <br> `libs/modkit/src/api/operation_builder.rs`|Added `error_502`, `error_503`, and `error_504` methods to register additional RFC 9457 problem+json error responses by delegating to `problem_response` with the corresponding status codes.|\n\n## Estimated Code Review Effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~3 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 Three gateway errors hop in line,  \n> Five-oh-two, three, four align!  \n> Problem responses, clean and neat,  \n> Convenience methods, can't be beat!  \n> ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4495486554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1953,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1953","source_state":"closed","source_author":"diffora","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1953] feat(account-management): public v1 REST surface + plugins + e2e","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"am/06-rest-handlers","pr_head_sha":"376aa11b6f0adb4424fc58ebe663d010f540b94a","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"diffora","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1953","id":3711438492,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7dOA6c","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1953","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1953.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1953.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1953","number":1953,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(account-management): public v1 REST surface + plugins + e2e","user":{"login":"diffora","id":272209596,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDmWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272209596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora","html_url":"https://github.com/diffora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diffora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nLands the public v1 REST surface of Account Management together with the\r\nco-located **Tenant Resolver plugin**, a permissive **static IdP plugin**\r\nfor dev/E2E, and end-to-end test coverage across Rust + Python.\r\n\r\n## What's landed\r\n\r\n### REST surface v1\r\n\r\n18 endpoints across 4 families, wired via `OperationBuilder` so the\r\nOpenAPI spec is generated from the same source as the runtime router.\r\n\r\n| Family | Endpoints | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| **Tenants** | `POST /tenants`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /tenants/{id}`, `GET /tenants/{id}/children` | OData `$filter`/`$orderby`/cursor pagination; subtree-clamp at DB JOIN; `Location` header on create |\r\n| **Custom methods** | `POST /tenants/{id}/suspend`, `POST /tenants/{id}/unsuspend` | AIP-136 sub-resource fallback (axum/matchit constraint, tracked) |\r\n| **Metadata** | `GET/PUT/DELETE /tenants/{id}/metadata/{schema_id}`, `GET .../resolved`, `GET .../metadata` | GTS-validated; inheritance walk-up with self-managed barriers; `resolved=false` for empty walks (200, not 404); distinct `resource_type` per 404 variant |\r\n| **Users** | `GET/POST /tenants/{id}/users`, `DELETE /tenants/{id}/users/{user_id}` | IdP-delegated; `?user_id=…` existence-check shape |\r\n| **Conversions** | `POST/GET/PATCH /tenants/{id}/conversions[/{request_id}]` + parent-side `child-conversions/*` mirror | Dual-consent; cross-barrier minimal projection on parent side |\r\n\r\nOData filter values for categorical columns (`status`, `target_mode`,\r\n`initiator_side`) accept the public enum strings (e.g.\r\n`?$filter=status eq 'pending'`) and are translated to the storage\r\n`SMALLINT` ordinal via `FieldToColumn::map_value`. Ordered operators and\r\n`$orderby` are rejected on these columns (no consistent ordering across\r\nwire and storage shapes).\r\n\r\n### Tenant Resolver plugin (in-process)\r\n\r\n`src/tr_plugin/` (~2.7k LOC) implements\r\n`tenant_resolver_sdk::TenantResolverPluginClient` directly over AM-owned\r\n`tenants` + `tenant_closure`. Co-located with AM so the plugin relies\r\non AM-writer invariants (transactional `(tenants, tenant_closure)`\r\nmaintenance, barrier materialization, provisioning-invisibility).\r\n\r\n- `queries.rs` — `get_tenant` / `get_root_tenant` / `get_tenants` /\r\n  `get_ancestors` / `get_descendants` / `is_ancestor`. 1–2 indexed\r\n  reads per call; tenant-type reverse-hydration batched via\r\n  `TypesRegistryClient`.\r\n- Fail-closed corruption defenses: parent_id cycles / closure↔tenants\r\n  hydration mismatch / multi-root invariant violations surface as\r\n  `Internal` rather than partial result.\r\n- Audit-log channel `tr_plugin.audit` for `BarrierMode::Ignore` use.\r\n\r\n### Static IdP plugin (new crate)\r\n\r\n`plugins/static-idp-plugin/` — permissive echo `IdpPluginClient` for\r\ndev/E2E. In-memory per-tenant user cache, deterministic `UUIDv5` IDs\r\nfrom `(tenant_id, username)`. NOT for production — production fallback\r\nis `NoopIdpProvider` returning `UnsupportedOperation`.\r\n\r\n### GTS envelopes\r\n\r\n`account-management-sdk/src/gts_envelopes.rs` registers\r\n`gts.cf.core.am.tenant_type.v1~` and `gts.cf.core.am.tenant_metadata.v1~`\r\nbase envelopes via `inventory::submit!` at boot. Drift-guard test diffs\r\ninline literals against `docs/schemas/*.schema.json`. Inline form is a\r\nworkaround until the `#[gts_type_schema]` macro grows\r\n`x-gts-traits-schema` support (tracked in\r\n[#1928](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1928),\r\nblocked upstream by\r\n[GTS-rust/#85](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust/issues/85)).\r\n\r\nNew `TENANT_METADATA_SCHEMA_RESOURCE_TYPE` so schema-level 404\r\n(`MetadataSchemaNotRegistered`) is structurally distinct from\r\nentry-level 404 (`MetadataEntryNotFound`) — clients branch on\r\n`resource_type` without parsing prose.\r\n\r\n### SDK additions\r\n\r\n- New `MetadataInvalidRequest` variant (canonical envelope carries the\r\n  metadata resource type).\r\n- New `is_already_exists()` classifier.\r\n- `PendingConversionExists` now maps to AIP-193 `AlreadyExists` (HTTP\r\n  409, not 400 failed_precondition) per the YAML contract.\r\n\r\n### Storage layer\r\n\r\n- m0006 migration — `conversion_audit_comments` rationale columns.\r\n- Repo updates across `lifecycle`, `metadata`, `conversion`,\r\n  `retention`, `integrity` for the new REST flows + closure invariants.\r\n- Types-registry metadata-schema registry: orphan rejection +\r\n  `effective_traits()` resolution.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\n| Layer | Files | LOC |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Rust unit (handler/route/dto/tr_plugin) | `*_tests.rs` siblings + `tr_plugin/tests.rs` | ~4.5k |\r\n| Rust e2e (Axum oneshot + sqlite) | `api_{tenants,children,metadata,users,conversions,envelope}_test.rs` | ~2.6k |\r\n| Python e2e (real gateway + IdP plugin) | `testing/e2e/modules/account_management/` | ~1k |\r\n\r\nRust e2e covers: lifecycle, idempotency (incl. unsuspend on active),\r\n404/cross-tenant/unauthenticated, OData filter+order pagination, RFC\r\n9457 envelope shape, conversion dual-consent dispatch, metadata\r\ndistinct 404 codes.\r\n\r\nPython e2e covers: real `static-authz-plugin` PEP scope clamping\r\n(token A vs token B baseline+clamp), IdP plugin round-trip, gateway\r\nmiddleware ordering, counterparty-only rule on conversion approve.\r\n\r\n### Docs\r\n\r\n- `docs/account-management-v1.yaml` — full path set + new\r\n  `tenant_metadata_schema.v1~` distinction.\r\n- `docs/tr-plugin/{DESIGN,PRD}.md` in sync with the co-located impl.\r\n- `feature-tenant-resolver-plugin.md`,\r\n  `feature-managed-self-managed-modes.md` refreshed.\r\n\r\n## Wiring\r\n\r\n- `account_management` and `static-idp-plugin` are **optional** crates\r\n  in `apps/cyberware-example-server` (default features = `[]`). Not\r\n  in non-e2e builds.\r\n- `config/e2e-features.txt` enables `account-management,static-idp`\r\n  for CI/e2e — same as before this PR.\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n\r\n- AIP-136 colon-method shape (`{id}:suspend`) — blocked on\r\n  axum/matchit bump; sub-resource fallback documented inline.\r\n\r\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added comprehensive REST API for account management: tenant CRUD operations, metadata management with inheritance, user provisioning/deprovisioning, and tenant conversion workflows.\n  * Introduced tenant hierarchy with parent-child relationships and soft-delete support.\n  * Added configurable in-process tenant resolver plugin registration.\n  * Enhanced metadata schema validation and registration support.\n  * New audit comment fields for conversion requests tracking rationale.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Corrected metadata deletion to be idempotent on missing entries.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated configuration documentation and error handling contracts.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1953?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T19:28:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T12:59:55Z","closed_at":"2026-05-21T12:59:54Z","merged_at":"2026-05-21T12:59:54Z","merge_commit_sha":"14b5e90caabdc9cd8a286df3af73dfdf96296e2e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1953/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1953/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1953/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/376aa11b6f0adb4424fc58ebe663d010f540b94a","head":{"label":"diffora:am/06-rest-handlers","ref":"am/06-rest-handlers","sha":"376aa11b6f0adb4424