"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T15:03:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T15:04:34Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `c5ca6fc6-30f4-4427-8031-d46effe290f6`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a49c65ce7b9ca7b2f51f8a8c4ec6dd5f41865bdc and 85b0885a05122050d30a677505e0dfff46f04671.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (2)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (36)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `docs/api/api.json`\n* `docs/arch/errors/DESIGN.md`\n* `dylint.toml`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/Cargo.toml`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/src/client.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/src/gts.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/src/lib.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/gts/errors.json`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/domain/error.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/domain/local_client/addresses.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/domain/local_client/cities.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/domain/local_client/users.rs`\n* `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/errors.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-errors-macro/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit-errors-macro/README.md`\n* `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-errors-macro/tests/gts_validation.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-errors/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit-errors/README.md`\n* `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-errors/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/api_dto.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/openapi_registry.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/operation_builder.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/problem.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/trace_layer.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/errors.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/result.rs`\n* `modules/system/module-orchestrator/src/api/rest/handlers.rs`\n* `release-plz.toml`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes (22)</summary>\n\n* libs/modkit/src/errors.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit/src/result.rs\n* examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/gts/errors.json\n* dylint.toml\n* libs/modkit-errors-macro/tests/gts_validation.rs\n* libs/modkit/src/api/problem.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors/README.md\n* libs/modkit-errors/src/lib.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors-macro/README.md\n* Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit-errors-macro/Cargo.toml\n* examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/errors.rs\n* examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/src/errors.rs\n* libs/modkit/src/api/trace_layer.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs\n* libs/modkit/Cargo.toml\n* examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/domain/error.rs\n* libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs\n* release-plz.toml\n* libs/modkit/src/lib.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR removes the legacy `modkit-errors` and `modkit-errors-macro` crates and migrates the entire codebase to use `modkit-canonical-errors`. The migration updates workspace configuration, core library dependencies and APIs, removes old error helper types and functions, introduces canonical error envelopes in the example users-info crate, and updates OpenAPI documentation to reflect the new simplified Problem schema.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Error System Migration**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Workspace and configuration cleanup** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `dylint.toml`, `release-plz.toml`|Legacy error crates are removed from workspace members, shared dependencies, lint exclusions, and release configuration.|\n|**Core modkit library migration** <br> `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit/src/api/{mod.rs, api_dto.rs, openapi_registry.rs, operation_builder.rs}`, `libs/modkit/src/{errors.rs, lib.rs, result.rs}`|Dependency switches to canonical errors; API module re-exports legacy prelude with new canonical prelude; convenience constructors and trace helpers are removed; library root exports are cleaned up.|\n|**Users-info SDK error integration** <br> `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info-sdk/{Cargo.toml, src/gts.rs, src/lib.rs, src/client.rs}`|UsersInfoError enum is replaced with re-exported CanonicalError; GTS resource-type constants are introduced and exported; crate re-exports canonical error types alongside models.|\n|**Users-info impl error mapping** <br> `examples/modkit/users-info/users-info/src/{domain/error.rs, domain/local_client/*.rs}`|DomainError-to-UsersInfoError conversion removed; streaming clients map errors via canonical internal error with formatted message instead of streaming variant.|\n|**Module-orchestrator handler update** <br> `modules/system/module-orchestrator/src/api/rest/handlers.rs`|Handler prelude import switches from legacy to canonical prelude.|\n|**OpenAPI documentation update** <br> `docs/api/api.json`|Problem schema simplified to RFC 9457 form; ValidationViolation schema removed; 422 Unprocessable Entity responses removed from all endpoints.|\n|**Architecture documentation** <br> `docs/arch/errors/DESIGN.md`|Error system implementation references updated from modkit-errors to modkit-canonical-errors paths.|\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n> 🐰 *Hops with glee at the cleanup spree!*  \n> *Old errors hop away, canonical ways are here to stay,*  \n> *Schemas simplified, migrations unified,*  \n> *The codebase now refined, a cleaner design!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4478964164/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1945,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1945","source_state":"closed","source_author":"aviator5","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1945] refactor(authz-resolver-sdk): accept runtime resource type names","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"issue-1920","pr_head_sha":"da9bf7967d18fde15a3b784358fe98622b3ac48c","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"aviator5","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1945","id":3702769998,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7cs8lO","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1945","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1945.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1945.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1945","number":1945,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"refactor(authz-resolver-sdk): accept runtime resource type names","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Change ResourceType.name from &'static str to Cow<'static, str> so PEP callers can pass runtime-built resource type ids (e.g. chained GTS schema ids like gts.cf.core.am.tenant_metadata.v1~vendor.app.branding.v1~) without leaking strings via Box::leak or routing through a global intern table.\r\n\r\nThe 'static bound provided no wire-level benefit — build_request_with immediately copies the name into an owned String for the EvaluationRequest payload. Cow keeps the const-declaration ergonomics (Cow::Borrowed in const context, zero allocation, clone is a pointer copy) while unlocking Cow::Owned for runtime-derived names.\r\n\r\nRefs: #1920\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * Standardized how resource-type descriptors are defined across authorization components for consistency and reliability.\n  * Internal resource descriptor representation and APIs were modernized (no behavior changes), improving maintainability.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Authorization tests and examples updated to align with the new resource descriptor form and accessors.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1945?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-18T14:58:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T19:59:48Z","closed_at":"2026-05-18T19:59:48Z","merged_at":"2026-05-18T19:59:48Z","merge_commit_sha":"a83bca716d9939694e64738e4d777ceb62bbb848","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"http