 = group_by\n>                     .iter()\n>                     .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n>             {\n>                 let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n>                 select_cols.push(format!(\n>                     \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n>                 ));\n>                 group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n>             }\n>             if has_usage_type {\n>                 select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n>                 group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n>             }\n>             if has_subject {\n>                 select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n>                 group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n>             }\n>             if has_resource {\n>                 select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n> \n> ```\n> \n> ---\n> \n> Script executed:\n> \n> ```shell\n> # Final verification: confirm no bucket_size checks in routing\n> echo \"=== Full routing decision context ===\"\n> sed -n '95,105p' modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs\n> \n> echo\n> echo \"=== Confirm bucket_size is never referenced in use_raw_path logic ===\"\n> grep -n \"query.bucket_size\\|bucket_size\" modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs | head -5\n> ```\n> \n> Repository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n> \n> ---\n> \n> Repository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n> Exit code: 0\n> \n> \n> stdout:\n> ```\n> === Full routing decision context ===\n> \n>         let group_by = &query.group_by;\n> \n>         // `@cpt-begin`:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n>         let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n>             || query.subject_id.is_some()\n>             || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n>             || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n>         tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");\n>         // `@cpt-end`:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n> \n> \n> === Confirm bucket_size is never referenced in use_raw_path logic ===\n> 70:fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n> 147:                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n> 250:                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n> \n> ```\n> \n> ---\n> \n> \n> \n> </details>\n> \n> **Routing to `usage_agg_1h` must verify the query time range falls entirely within materialized data.**\n> \n> The current routing logic at lines 98–103 ignores whether the requested time range includes the current non-materialized hour. With `end_offset => INTERVAL '1 hour'` (continuous_aggregate.rs:61), only data older than 1 hour is available in `usage_agg_1h`. Queries that span the current hour (e.g., a 2-hour window starting 30 minutes ago) will silently return incomplete aggregates from cagg instead of falling back to `usage_records`. Additionally, the routing decision does not consider the requested bucket size; a query for minute-level granularity via `BucketSize::Minute` in `group_by` should always use raw records, not hourly re-bucketing.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>          let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n>              || query.subject_id.is_some()\n>              || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n>              || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject)\n> +            || group_by.iter().any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(BucketSize::Minute)))\n> +            || query.time_range.1 > now() - Duration::hours(1);\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In\n> `@modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs`\n> around lines 98 - 103, The routing decision for use_raw_path must also ensure\n> the requested time window is fully covered by the materialized hourly aggregate\n> and honor bucket granularity: check that the query's end time is <= (now() -\n> INTERVAL '1 hour') given continuous_aggregate.rs's end_offset and that the\n> entire [start, end) falls before that boundary; if any part of the requested\n> range overlaps the current non-materialized hour, set use_raw_path = true so we\n> query raw usage_records instead of usage_agg_1h. Also force use_raw_path = true\n> whenever the requested bucket size includes minute-level granularity\n> (BucketSize::Minute) or other sub-hour buckets in group_by; keep existing checks\n> for query.resource_id, query.subject_id, and GroupByDimension::Resource/Subject\n> and combine them with these new time-range and bucket-size conditions when\n> computing use_raw_path.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot:1c0b977e-62db-442d-a749-837ed1795dba -->\n> \n> <!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:04:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:33:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266096489","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266096489"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266096489"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266096489/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":103,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":103,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266098480","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266098480,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrLUw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n+    let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n+    let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n+    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n+    loop {\n+        interval.tick().await;\n+        if pool.is_closed() {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+        health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n+    }","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"coderabbitai commented:\n\n> _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n> \n> **Emit an unhealthy sample before breaking the health loop.**\n> \n> Line 172 exits as soon as the pool is closed, so `storage_health_status` never records `0.0` on shutdown and can stay stuck at the previous healthy value.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n>      let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n>      let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n>      let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n>      loop {\n>          interval.tick().await;\n>          if pool.is_closed() {\n> +            gauge.record(0.0, &[]);\n>              break;\n>          }\n>          health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n>      }\n>  }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <!-- suggestion_start -->\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n> \n> > ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> > Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n> \n> ```suggestion\n> async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n>     let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n>     let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n>     let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n>     loop {\n>         interval.tick().await;\n>         if pool.is_closed() {\n>             gauge.record(0.0, &[]);\n>             break;\n>         }\n>         health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n>     }\n> }\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <!-- suggestion_end -->\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In\n> `@modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs`\n> around lines 166 - 176, The loop in run_health_check_loop exits immediately when\n> pool.is_closed() returns true, so storage_health_status never records an\n> unhealthy 0.0 on shutdown; before breaking out of the loop in\n> run_health_check_loop (right after detecting pool.is_closed()), record an\n> explicit unhealthy sample (e.g., call gauge.record(0.0, &[]) or otherwise emit\n> 0.0 via the same mechanism health_check uses) so the metric is set to 0.0 prior\n> to exiting; reference the run_health_check_loop function, the pool.is_closed()\n> check, the gauge built from meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\"), and the\n> existing health_check(&pool, &gauge) call to keep behavior consistent.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:d2d15a0a-03f2-4e8e-92e9-093f1a6aa48c -->\n> \n> <!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:05:14Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:31:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266098480","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266098480"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266098480"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266098480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":176,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":176,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266101536","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266101536,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrMEg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **CRITICAL**\n> \n> The routing decision ignores `query.bucket_size` and the `TimeBucket(BucketSize)` granularity in `group_by`, so an aggregation request like `BucketSize::Minute` with no `resource_id`/`subject_id` filter is silently routed to `usage_agg_1h` and rewritten as `time_bucket('1 minute', bucket)` over already 1-hour-pre-aggregated rows.\n> \n> This returns billing/reporting numbers at the wrong granularity without any error — the PR description and FEATURE doc both state the cagg path is valid only when bucket size ≥ 1 h.\n> \n> Fix: extend `use_raw_path` to also be true whenever a `TimeBucket` GROUP BY is sub-hourly (`BucketSize::Minute`) or whenever `query.bucket_size` is set to a sub-hour value, so those queries fall back to `usage_records`.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:05:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266101536","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266101536"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266101536"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266101536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":102,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":102,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266103659","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266103659,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrMlr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+\n+        let mut args = PgArguments::default();\n+        let mut param_idx: usize = 0;\n+\n+        for sv in &scope_params {\n+            param_idx += 1;\n+            match sv {\n+                SqlValue::Uuid(u) => add_arg(&mut args, *u)?,\n+                SqlValue::UuidArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::Text(s) => add_arg(&mut args, s.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::TextArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let time_start_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.0)?;\n+        let time_end_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.1)?;\n+\n+        let has_time_bucket = group_by\n+            .iter()\n+            .any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)));\n+        let has_usage_type = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::UsageType);\n+        let has_subject = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        let has_resource = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource);\n+        let has_source = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Source);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+        let sql = if use_raw_path {\n+            let time_col = \"timestamp\";\n+            let agg_expr = raw_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(resource_id) = query.resource_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(subject_id) = query.subject_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_records WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+        } else {\n+            let time_col = \"bucket\";\n+            let agg_expr = cagg_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_agg_1h WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        };\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-5\n+        let rows = sqlx::query_with(&sql, args)\n+            .fetch_all(&self.pool)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if is_transient_error(&e) {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::unavailable(format!(\"transient error: {e}\"))\n+                } else {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"storage error: {e}\"))\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-5\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-6\n+        let results: Vec<AggregationResult> = rows\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(|row| -> Result<AggregationResult, UsageCollectorError> {\n+                let value = row.try_get::<f64, _>(\"agg_value\").map_err(|e| {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row decode error (agg_value): {e}\"))\n+                })?;\n+                let bucket_start = if has_time_bucket {\n+                    row.try_get(\"bucket_start\").ok()","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **HIGH**\n> \n> `row.try_get(\"bucket_start\").ok()` (and the same pattern at lines 353, 358, 363, 368, 373, 378) silently swallows column decode errors and substitutes `None`.\n> \n> When `has_time_bucket` (or any of the other dimension flags) is true the column is unconditionally present in the SELECT, so any `try_get` failure here is a real type/schema mismatch, not an absent column — masking it as `None` returns wrong data with no diagnostic.\n> \n> Fix: propagate the error with `.map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row decode error (bucket_start): {e}\")))?` (matching the pattern already used in the `query_raw` mapper).","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:06:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266103659","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266103659"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266103659"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266103659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":348,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":348,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266105419","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266105419,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrNBL","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **HIGH**\n> \n> This detached `tokio::spawn` runs the health-check loop forever with no `CancellationToken` and no handle stored anywhere, which violates MODKIT-LIFE-001 — background tasks must respect the module's cancellation token so the platform can shut them down deterministically.\n> \n> Relying on `pool.is_closed()` couples task lifetime to whoever happens to drop the pool, and on a normal module shutdown the task continues ticking against a still-open pool until the runtime is killed.\n> \n> Fix: take the `CancellationToken` from `ModuleCtx` (or the lifecycle hook), pass it into `run_health_check_loop`, and replace the bare `interval.tick().await` loop with `tokio::select!` on `tick()` and `token.cancelled()`.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:06:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266105419","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266105419"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266105419"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266105419/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":160,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":160,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266107355","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266107355,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrNfb","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **HIGH**\n> \n> `.map_err(|_|` discards the underlying `sqlx::Error` from pool creation.\n> \n> Operators investigating a startup failure see only the generic string `connection pool initialization failed` with no signal whether the cause was TLS handshake rejection, DNS resolution, authentication failure, or pool acquisition timeout — exactly the diagnostic data the `database_url`-redacting design relies on us preserving (the error itself does not contain credentials).\n> \n> Fix: log the source error before mapping (`error!(error = %e, \"...\")`) and wrap with context, e.g. `.map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed: {e}\"))`.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:06:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266107355","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266107355"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266107355"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266107355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":70,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":70,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266109384","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266109384,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrN_I","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+//! Retention policy setup for the `TimescaleDB` storage plugin.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::StoragePluginError;\n+\n+/// Applies the `TimescaleDB` retention policy to `usage_records` and removes\n+/// expired rows from `usage_idempotency_keys`.\n+///\n+/// # Errors\n+///\n+/// Returns [`StoragePluginError`] if any statement fails.\n+pub async fn setup_retention_policy(\n+    pool: &PgPool,\n+    retention: Duration,\n+) -> Result<(), StoragePluginError> {\n+    let interval = format!(\"{} seconds\", retention.as_secs());\n+\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"SELECT add_retention_policy('usage_records', $1::interval, if_not_exists => true)\",\n+    )\n+    .bind(&interval)\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        StoragePluginError::RetentionPolicySetupFailed(format!(\n+            \"failed to add retention policy for usage_records: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+\n+    sqlx::query(\"DELETE FROM usage_idempotency_keys WHERE created_at < NOW() - $1::interval\")","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/retention.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **HIGH**\n> \n> This `DELETE FROM usage_idempotency_keys` runs exactly once at plugin startup, so on a long-lived service the table grows unbounded between restarts.\n> \n> `usage_idempotency_keys` is the cross-partition dedup table touched on every counter ingest — once it is large enough that its index no longer fits in cache, every counter `create_usage_record` slows down, directly threatening the ≥10k records/sec throughput requirement (`cpt-cf-usage-collector-nfr-throughput`).\n> \n> Fix: turn this into a periodic background task (run alongside the health-check loop, gated by the module's `CancellationToken`) so old keys are pruned on the same cadence as the hypertable retention policy.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:07:14Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266109384","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266109384"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266109384"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266109384/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":33,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266111547","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266111547,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrOg7","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,7 +3,9 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n #[cfg_attr(feature = \"with-utoipa\", derive(utoipa::ToSchema))]\n #[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n pub struct PageInfo {\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]","path":"libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **MEDIUM**\n> \n> Adding `skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\"` to `PageInfo::next_cursor` (and `prev_cursor` below) silently changes the wire format for every `modkit-odata` consumer, not just usage-collector — the field disappears from JSON entirely instead of being serialized as `null`.\n> \n> Clients that destructure `next_cursor` from the JSON without defaulting (TypeScript narrow types, Go `omitempty`-aware decoders, schema validators) will break, and downstream OpenAPI schemas will start advertising the field as optional. This is a contract change in a shared library wedged into a feature PR.\n> \n> Fix: either keep the field always-present (revert) or scope this change to its own PR with a CHANGELOG entry and OpenAPI/contract review across all `modkit-odata` consumers.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:07:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266111547","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266111547"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266111547"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266111547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266113833","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266113833,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrPEp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n+    let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n+    let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n+    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n+    loop {\n+        interval.tick().await;\n+        if pool.is_closed() {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+        health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Executes a liveness probe against the pool and emits the `storage_health_status` gauge.\n+///\n+/// Emits `1.0` when the probe succeeds, `0.0` when it fails.\n+async fn health_check(pool: &PgPool, gauge: &opentelemetry::metrics::Gauge<f64>) {\n+    let healthy = sqlx::query(\"SELECT 1\").execute(pool).await.is_ok();\n+    let status = if healthy { 1.0_f64 } else { 0.0_f64 };\n+    gauge.record(status, &[]);\n+\n+    if healthy {\n+        debug!(\"TimescaleDB health check passed\");\n+    } else {\n+        error!(\"TimescaleDB health check failed: pool unreachable\");","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **MEDIUM**\n> \n> The failure branch logs only the static string `\"TimescaleDB health check failed: pool unreachable\"` and drops the `sqlx::Error` returned by the probe.\n> \n> Operators triaging a flapping `storage_health_status = 0` cannot tell whether the cause is pool exhaustion, TLS renegotiation, an idle-connection reset, or a real TimescaleDB outage — every failure looks identical in the logs.\n> \n> Fix: capture the error in `health_check`, e.g. `if let Err(e) = sqlx::query(\"SELECT 1\").execute(pool).await { error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB health check failed\"); }` and emit the gauge value separately.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266113833","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266113833"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266113833"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266113833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":190,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":190,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266116099","pull_request_review_id":4318669423,"id":3266116099,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrPoD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+\n+        let mut args = PgArguments::default();\n+        let mut param_idx: usize = 0;\n+\n+        for sv in &scope_params {\n+            param_idx += 1;\n+            match sv {\n+                SqlValue::Uuid(u) => add_arg(&mut args, *u)?,\n+                SqlValue::UuidArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::Text(s) => add_arg(&mut args, s.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::TextArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let time_start_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.0)?;\n+        let time_end_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.1)?;\n+\n+        let has_time_bucket = group_by\n+            .iter()\n+            .any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)));\n+        let has_usage_type = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::UsageType);\n+        let has_subject = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        let has_resource = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource);\n+        let has_source = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Source);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+        let sql = if use_raw_path {\n+            let time_col = \"timestamp\";\n+            let agg_expr = raw_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(resource_id) = query.resource_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(subject_id) = query.subject_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_records WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+        } else {\n+            let time_col = \"bucket\";\n+            let agg_expr = cagg_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 commented:\n\n> **LOW**\n> \n> This `if has_subject` (and `if has_resource` immediately below) branch is dead code on the cagg path: the routing decision at line 99–102 forces `use_raw_path = true` whenever `group_by` contains `Subject` or `Resource`, so `has_subject` / `has_resource` are guaranteed `false` here.\n> \n> The cagg branch can never run a `GROUP BY subject_type` or `GROUP BY resource_type` request through this code, which is misleading to a reader who assumes both branches are reachable.\n> \n> Fix: drop the two unreachable blocks, or — if the intent was to allow `Subject`/`Resource` group-by on the cagg path (using the low-cardinality `subject_type`/`resource_type` columns the view actually carries) — fix the routing decision to only force the raw path when `subject_id`/`resource_id` is the *filter*, not the GROUP BY dimension.","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:08:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266116099","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266116099"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266116099"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266116099/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":260,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":260,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266171834","pull_request_review_id":4318767529,"id":3266171834,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrdO6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+\n+        let mut args = PgArguments::default();\n+        let mut param_idx: usize = 0;\n+\n+        for sv in &scope_params {\n+            param_idx += 1;\n+            match sv {\n+                SqlValue::Uuid(u) => add_arg(&mut args, *u)?,\n+                SqlValue::UuidArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::Text(s) => add_arg(&mut args, s.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::TextArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let time_start_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.0)?;\n+        let time_end_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.1)?;\n+\n+        let has_time_bucket = group_by\n+            .iter()\n+            .any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)));\n+        let has_usage_type = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::UsageType);\n+        let has_subject = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        let has_resource = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource);\n+        let has_source = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Source);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+        let sql = if use_raw_path {\n+            let time_col = \"timestamp\";\n+            let agg_expr = raw_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(resource_id) = query.resource_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(subject_id) = query.subject_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_records WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+        } else {\n+            let time_col = \"bucket\";\n+            let agg_expr = cagg_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved by the refactor — but via \"drop the unreachable blocks\" rather than relaxing the routing.\r\n\r\nIn `3d19981` the cagg and raw branches were two parallel code blocks, and the cagg block at lines 260–268 had its own `if has_subject` / `if has_resource` that the upstream routing made unreachable.\r\n\r\nIn the current code (`pg_query_port.rs:301-455`) both branches share a single `build_aggregation_sql` driven by an `AggSqlVariant` (`has_id_columns: true` for raw, `false` for cagg). The `if has_subject` / `if has_resource` blocks at `pg_query_port.rs:346-361` now live in that shared assembler — they are reachable on the raw variant (which is the only variant that ever sets `has_subject`/`has_resource = true`, since the routing decision at `pg_query_port.rs:500-506` still forces `use_raw_path` whenever `group_by` contains `Subject`/`Resource`). The cagg-specific dead block is gone, so the \"misleading to a reader\" concern is resolved.\r\n\r\nI kept the routing strict (group-by `Subject`/`Resource` still forces raw) rather than serving low-cardinality `subject_type` / `resource_type` group-by from the cagg. The inner `if has_id_columns` guard at `pg_query_port.rs:347-350` / `355-358` is structured so that loosening the routing later would be a one-line change without touching the SQL builder.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:18:01Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:18:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266171834","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266171834"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266171834"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266171834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":260,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266116099,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":260,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266182942","pull_request_review_id":4318781558,"id":3266182942,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Crf8e","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n+    let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n+    let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n+    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n+    loop {\n+        interval.tick().await;\n+        if pool.is_closed() {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+        health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Executes a liveness probe against the pool and emits the `storage_health_status` gauge.\n+///\n+/// Emits `1.0` when the probe succeeds, `0.0` when it fails.\n+async fn health_check(pool: &PgPool, gauge: &opentelemetry::metrics::Gauge<f64>) {\n+    let healthy = sqlx::query(\"SELECT 1\").execute(pool).await.is_ok();\n+    let status = if healthy { 1.0_f64 } else { 0.0_f64 };\n+    gauge.record(status, &[]);\n+\n+    if healthy {\n+        debug!(\"TimescaleDB health check passed\");\n+    } else {\n+        error!(\"TimescaleDB health check failed: pool unreachable\");","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved. The `sqlx::Error` is now captured and emitted on the log line, and the gauge is emitted independently of logging.\r\n\r\nIn [`module.rs:375-396`](modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/module.rs#L375-L396), `health_check` matches on the probe result and, on `Err(e)`, walks the full `std::error::Error::source()` chain via `render_error_chain` so the SQLSTATE carried by `sqlx::Error::Database` and any further-nested cause survive into the log — without the chain walk the operator would only see the top-level `Display` (`\"pool timed out\"`, `\"encode error\"`, …) and could not distinguish pool exhaustion from TLS renegotiation from a real outage. The function returns `(value, reason, Option<String>)`; the caller emits the gauge value via `gauge.record(...)` regardless of log decision, and `log_health_transition` ([`module.rs:295-315`](modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/module.rs#L295-L315)) logs the detail:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nHealthLog::InitialFailure => {\r\n    error!(error_chain = %detail, \"TimescaleDB health check failed\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTwo extras beyond the suggested fix:\r\n\r\n- The gauge carries a `reason` label (`healthy` / `probe_failed` / `pool_closed`), so dashboards can separate a transient probe failure from a pool shutdown without parsing logs.\r\n- `error!` fires only on the healthy→failed transition; sustained outages drop to `debug!` to avoid ~120 identical lines/hour drowning out unrelated signal. The gauge still records every tick, so outage detection relies on staleness, not log volume.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:19:59Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:20:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266182942","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266182942"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266182942"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266182942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":190,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266113833,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":190,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266191939","pull_request_review_id":4318791997,"id":3266191939,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CriJD","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,7 +3,9 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n #[cfg_attr(feature = \"with-utoipa\", derive(utoipa::ToSchema))]\n #[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n pub struct PageInfo {\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]","path":"libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved — the `skip_serializing_if` change to `modkit-odata` has been dropped entirely in the refactor.\r\n\r\n**Current state of `libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs`:**\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n#[cfg_attr(feature = \"with-utoipa\", derive(utoipa::ToSchema))]\r\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\r\npub struct PageInfo {\r\n    pub next_cursor: Option<String>,\r\n    pub prev_cursor: Option<String>,\r\n    pub limit: u64,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nNo `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = ...)]` attributes on either cursor field.\r\n\r\n**Verification:**\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ git diff 1a481e22 HEAD -- libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs\r\n(no output)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`PageInfo` on the current branch is byte-identical to the version on `main` (last touched by `1a481e22`). The new TimescaleDB commit (`9eba77ad`) does not modify `page.rs` at all — the contract change was confined to the original `3d19981` and has been removed.\r\n\r\n**Wire format is preserved:** `next_cursor` / `prev_cursor` continue to serialize as JSON `null` when `None`, so no `modkit-odata` consumer (TypeScript clients, Go decoders, OpenAPI schemas) is affected.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:21:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:21:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266191939","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266191939"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266191939"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266191939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266111547,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266200887","pull_request_review_id":4318802544,"id":3266200887,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrkU3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+//! Retention policy setup for the `TimescaleDB` storage plugin.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::StoragePluginError;\n+\n+/// Applies the `TimescaleDB` retention policy to `usage_records` and removes\n+/// expired rows from `usage_idempotency_keys`.\n+///\n+/// # Errors\n+///\n+/// Returns [`StoragePluginError`] if any statement fails.\n+pub async fn setup_retention_policy(\n+    pool: &PgPool,\n+    retention: Duration,\n+) -> Result<(), StoragePluginError> {\n+    let interval = format!(\"{} seconds\", retention.as_secs());\n+\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"SELECT add_retention_policy('usage_records', $1::interval, if_not_exists => true)\",\n+    )\n+    .bind(&interval)\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        StoragePluginError::RetentionPolicySetupFailed(format!(\n+            \"failed to add retention policy for usage_records: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+\n+    sqlx::query(\"DELETE FROM usage_idempotency_keys WHERE created_at < NOW() - $1::interval\")","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/retention.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved. The unbounded-growth risk is gone: `usage_idempotency_keys` is now pruned on a recurring schedule alongside the health-check loop, exactly as suggested.\r\n\r\n**What changed**\r\n\r\n- `infra/retention.rs` factors the `DELETE` into a standalone `cleanup_idempotency_keys(pool, retention)` function. `setup_retention_policy` still calls it once at startup, but it's no longer the only caller.\r\n- `module.rs` spawns `run_idempotency_cleanup_loop` next to `run_health_check_loop` via the same `supervise_background_task` wrapper, both gated on `ctx.cancellation_token()`:\r\n  ```rust\r\n  supervise_background_task(\r\n      \"idempotency_cleanup\",\r\n      run_idempotency_cleanup_loop(pool, cfg.idempotency_retention, ctx.cancellation_token().clone()),\r\n  );\r\n  ```\r\n- The loop ticks on `IDEMPOTENCY_CLEANUP_INTERVAL` (1h), uses `MissedTickBehavior::Delay` to avoid catch-up bursts after runtime pauses, skips the immediate first tick (startup already ran the same `DELETE`), and exits cleanly on cancellation or `pool.is_closed()`. Cleanup errors are logged but don't kill the loop.\r\n\r\nNet effect: on a long-lived service the table now stays bounded to roughly `ingest_rate × idempotency_retention` instead of growing until the next restart, so the dedup index keeps fitting in cache and the ≥10k rec/s throughput target (`cpt-cf-usage-collector-nfr-throughput`) is no longer at risk from this path.\r\n\r\nSee `modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/module.rs:189-196` and `:317-361`, plus `src/infra/retention.rs:119-135`.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:23:07Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:23:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266200887","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266200887"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266200887"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266200887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266109384,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":33,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266208628","pull_request_review_id":4318811138,"id":3266208628,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrmN0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved. `module.rs:98` now reads:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n.map_err(|e| anyhow::Error::from(e).context(\"connection pool initialization failed\"))?;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe underlying `sqlx::Error` is preserved as the source of an `anyhow::Error` and the human-readable context is layered on top via `.context(..)`. Operators investigating a startup failure will see the full chain — TLS handshake rejection, DNS resolution failure, authentication failure, or pool acquire timeout — when the error is rendered with `{:#}` / `{:?}` at the module loader's single log point.\r\n\r\nThis is functionally equivalent to the suggested `anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed: {e}\")` but strictly better: it keeps the `sqlx::Error` as a structured `source()` link instead of flattening it into a string, so downstream code (and tests) can still match on the original error if needed. The `database_url`-redacting guarantee still holds because `sqlx::Error::Display` does not contain credentials.\r\n\r\nNo separate `error!(..)` is emitted at this site on purpose — the module loader logs each failure once, and double-logging at the call site inflates startup log volume (see the comment block at `module.rs:74-77`).\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:24:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:24:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266208628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266208628"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266208628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266208628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":70,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266107355,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":70,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266217850","pull_request_review_id":4318823206,"id":3266217850,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Crod6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved — the health-check loop now respects the module's `CancellationToken`.\r\n\r\n### What changed\r\n\r\n- `run_health_check_loop` now takes a `CancellationToken` parameter (`module.rs:236`) and is driven by `tokio::select!` on `cancel.cancelled()` and `interval.tick()` (`module.rs:252-255`), so it exits deterministically the moment the platform cancels the module.\r\n- The token is sourced from `ModuleCtx` via `ctx.cancellation_token().clone()` at spawn time (`module.rs:187`), satisfying MODKIT-LIFE-001.\r\n- `pool.is_closed()` is no longer the primary stop condition — it's retained only as a defensive secondary exit that emits a `reason=pool_closed` gauge reading before breaking (`module.rs:256-261`).\r\n- The same treatment is applied to the sibling `run_idempotency_cleanup_loop` (`module.rs:329-344`) for consistency.\r\n- The spawn itself is now wrapped by `supervise_background_task` (`module.rs:209-228`), which retains the `JoinHandle` long enough to surface panics / cancellations via `tracing` — addressing the related \"no handle stored anywhere\" concern from the same finding (RUST-OBS-001 / RUST-ASYNC-001).\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:25:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:25:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266217850","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266217850"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266217850"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266217850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":160,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266105419,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":160,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266232282","pull_request_review_id":4318842199,"id":3266232282,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Crr_a","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+\n+        let mut args = PgArguments::default();\n+        let mut param_idx: usize = 0;\n+\n+        for sv in &scope_params {\n+            param_idx += 1;\n+            match sv {\n+                SqlValue::Uuid(u) => add_arg(&mut args, *u)?,\n+                SqlValue::UuidArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::Text(s) => add_arg(&mut args, s.clone())?,\n+                SqlValue::TextArray(v) => add_arg(&mut args, v.clone())?,\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let time_start_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.0)?;\n+        let time_end_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+        param_idx += 1;\n+        add_arg(&mut args, query.time_range.1)?;\n+\n+        let has_time_bucket = group_by\n+            .iter()\n+            .any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)));\n+        let has_usage_type = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::UsageType);\n+        let has_subject = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        let has_resource = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource);\n+        let has_source = group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Source);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+        let sql = if use_raw_path {\n+            let time_col = \"timestamp\";\n+            let agg_expr = raw_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_id\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(resource_id) = query.resource_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(subject_id) = query.subject_id {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_id = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_id)?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_records WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+        } else {\n+            let time_col = \"bucket\";\n+            let agg_expr = cagg_agg_expr(query.function);\n+\n+            let mut select_cols: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            let mut group_by_exprs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+\n+            if has_time_bucket\n+                && let Some(GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(bs)) = group_by\n+                    .iter()\n+                    .find(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(_)))\n+            {\n+                let interval = bucket_size_to_pg_interval(*bs);\n+                select_cols.push(format!(\n+                    \"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col}) AS bucket_start\"\n+                ));\n+                group_by_exprs.push(format!(\"time_bucket('{interval}', {time_col})\"));\n+            }\n+            if has_usage_type {\n+                select_cols.push(\"metric AS usage_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"metric\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_subject {\n+                select_cols.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"subject_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_resource {\n+                select_cols.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"resource_type\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            if has_source {\n+                select_cols.push(\"module AS source\".to_owned());\n+                group_by_exprs.push(\"module\".to_owned());\n+            }\n+            select_cols.push(agg_expr.to_owned());\n+\n+            let select_clause = select_cols.join(\", \");\n+\n+            let mut where_clauses: Vec<String> = Vec::new();\n+            where_clauses.push(scope_sql.clone());\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} >= ${time_start_idx}\"));\n+            where_clauses.push(format!(\"{time_col} <= ${time_end_idx}\"));\n+\n+            if let Some(ref metric) = query.usage_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"metric = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, metric.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref resource_type) = query.resource_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"resource_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, resource_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref subject_type) = query.subject_type {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"subject_type = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, subject_type.clone())?;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(ref source) = query.source {\n+                param_idx += 1;\n+                where_clauses.push(format!(\"module = ${param_idx}\"));\n+                add_arg(&mut args, source.clone())?;\n+            }\n+\n+            let where_clause = where_clauses.join(\" AND \");\n+\n+            let limit_idx = param_idx + 1;\n+            let max_rows_limit = i64::try_from(query.max_rows)\n+                .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row limit overflow: {e}\")))?\n+                .saturating_add(1);\n+            add_arg(&mut args, max_rows_limit)?;\n+\n+            let order_clause = if has_time_bucket {\n+                \" ORDER BY bucket_start ASC\"\n+            } else {\n+                \"\"\n+            };\n+            let group_clause = if group_by_exprs.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\" GROUP BY {}\", group_by_exprs.join(\", \"))\n+            };\n+\n+            format!(\n+                \"SELECT {select_clause} FROM usage_agg_1h WHERE {where_clause}{group_clause}{order_clause} LIMIT ${limit_idx}\"\n+            )\n+        };\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-4\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-5\n+        let rows = sqlx::query_with(&sql, args)\n+            .fetch_all(&self.pool)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if is_transient_error(&e) {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::unavailable(format!(\"transient error: {e}\"))\n+                } else {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"storage error: {e}\"))\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-5\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-6\n+        let results: Vec<AggregationResult> = rows\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(|row| -> Result<AggregationResult, UsageCollectorError> {\n+                let value = row.try_get::<f64, _>(\"agg_value\").map_err(|e| {\n+                    UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"row decode error (agg_value): {e}\"))\n+                })?;\n+                let bucket_start = if has_time_bucket {\n+                    row.try_get(\"bucket_start\").ok()","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved in the refactor. The `try_get(...).ok()` sites in the `query_aggregated` row mapper have all been replaced with calls to a shared `decode()` helper (`pg_query_port.rs:125-136`) that maps `sqlx::Error` to `StoragePluginError::Serialization` / `UsageCollectorError::Internal` carrying the column name, then `?`-propagates it — same propagation discipline as the `query_raw` mapper.\r\n\r\nCurrent mapper at `pg_query_port.rs:609-665`:\r\n\r\n- `bucket_start`, `usage_type`, `resource_id`, `resource_type`, `source` are decoded as `T` via `Some(decode(row, \"<col>\")?)`, so any decode error is surfaced as a real schema/type mismatch rather than silently becoming `None`.\r\n- `subject_id` and `subject_type` are decoded as `decode::<Option<T>>(...)?` because those columns are genuinely NULLable in the underlying table; the `Option` is part of the SQL type, not an error-swallowing fallback.\r\n- `agg_value` uses the same `decode::<f64>` path.\r\n\r\nA short comment at lines 613-616 records the invariant (which selected columns are NOT NULL vs NULLable) so the distinction between `Some(decode(...)?)` and `decode::<Option<_>>(...)?` is intentional and reviewable.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:27:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:27:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266232282","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266232282"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266232282"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266232282/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":348,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266103659,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":348,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266244716","pull_request_review_id":4318858610,"id":3266244716,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CrvBs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved in the current revision of `pg_query_port.rs`. Routing now inspects both `query.bucket_size` and any `TimeBucket(BucketSize)` in `group_by`:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n// pg_query_port.rs:485-488\r\nlet cagg_too_coarse = matches!(query.bucket_size, Some(BucketSize::Minute))\r\n    || group_by\r\n        .iter()\r\n        .any(|d| matches!(d, GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(BucketSize::Minute)));\r\n```\r\n\r\n`cagg_too_coarse` then feeds the routing decision:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n// pg_query_port.rs:500-506\r\nlet use_raw_path = filter_resource\r\n    || filter_subject\r\n    || group_resource\r\n    || group_subject\r\n    || cagg_too_coarse\r\n    || scope_constrains_ids\r\n    || unsafe_time_range;\r\n```\r\n\r\n`BucketSize::Minute` is the only sub-hour variant in the SDK enum (`Minute | Hour | Day | Week | Month`), so checking it exhaustively covers the sub-hour case. A `BucketSize::Minute` request — whether expressed via `query.bucket_size` or `GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(BucketSize::Minute)` — now forces the raw `usage_records` path even without a `resource_id` / `subject_id` filter, so the CAGG can no longer be rebucketed at minute granularity.\r\n\r\nMismatch between the two fields is also rejected at the plugin boundary by `validate_bucket_size_consistency` (line 479), eliminating the silent two-sources-of-truth case.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:29:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:29:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266244716","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266244716"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266244716"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266244716/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":102,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266101536,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":102,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266257674","pull_request_review_id":4318877066,"id":3266257674,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CryMK","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n+    let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n+    let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n+    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n+    loop {\n+        interval.tick().await;\n+        if pool.is_closed() {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+        health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n+    }","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved. The health loop now records `storage_health_status = 0.0` (with a `reason=\"pool_closed\"` label) **before** breaking out, so the gauge no longer stays stuck at the previous healthy value.\r\n\r\n`modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/module.rs:256-261`:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nif pool.is_closed() {\r\n    // Distinct from a probe failure: the pool has been shut down and no further\r\n    // queries will succeed. Tagged so dashboards can separate shutdown from outage.\r\n    gauge.record(0.0_f64, &[KeyValue::new(\"reason\", \"pool_closed\")]);\r\n    break;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nA few extra bits worth noting:\r\n\r\n- The `pool_closed` label is distinct from `probe_failed`, so dashboards can tell operator-initiated shutdown apart from a live outage.\r\n- The test-only wrapper `health_check_for_tests` (`module.rs:417-426`) emits the same `(0.0, \"pool_closed\")` reading, and the integration test `health_check_metric` (`tests/integration.rs:309-335`) asserts it — closing the pool and verifying the tuple is `(0.0, \"pool_closed\")`.\r\n- A comment at `module.rs:230-235` documents the residual caveat: OTel gauges retain their last value indefinitely on the reader side, so once the loop exits the metric keeps that final `0.0` reading; alerts that need to distinguish \"process exited\" from \"process still reporting\" should monitor staleness, not the value alone.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:31:37Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:31:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266257674","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266257674"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266257674"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266257674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":176,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266098480,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":176,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266258411","pull_request_review_id":4318878006,"id":3266258411,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CryXr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,192 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` usage-collector storage plugin module.\n+//!\n+//! Registers a GTS plugin instance in the types registry and exposes\n+//! [`usage_collector_sdk::UsageCollectorPluginClientV1`] backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::Module;\n+use modkit::client_hub::ClientScope;\n+use modkit::context::ModuleCtx;\n+use modkit::gts::BaseModkitPluginV1;\n+use opentelemetry::global;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgPoolOptions;\n+use tracing::{debug, error, info};\n+use types_registry_sdk::{RegisterResult, TypesRegistryClient};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{UsageCollectorPluginClientV1, UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1};\n+\n+use crate::config::TimescaleDbConfig;\n+use crate::domain::client::TimescaleDbPluginClient;\n+use crate::infra::continuous_aggregate::setup_continuous_aggregate;\n+use crate::infra::migrations::run_migrations;\n+use crate::infra::otel_metrics::OtelPluginMetrics;\n+use crate::infra::pg_insert_port::PgInsertPort;\n+use crate::infra::pg_query_port::PgQueryPort;\n+use crate::infra::retention::setup_retention_policy;\n+\n+/// `TimescaleDB` production storage plugin for the usage-collector gateway.\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\",\n+    deps = [\"types-registry\", \"usage-collector\"]\n+)]\n+#[derive(Default)]\n+struct TimescaleDbStoragePlugin;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl Module for TimescaleDbStoragePlugin {\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1\n+    // @cpt-dod:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+        // Entry point: platform operator has invoked plugin startup (CLI or gateway startup flag).\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+        let cfg: TimescaleDbConfig = ctx.config().inspect_err(|_e| {\n+            error!(\"TimescaleDB plugin configuration load failed\");\n+        })?;\n+        cfg.validate().map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB plugin configuration validation failed\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"configuration validation failed: {e}\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-validate-config\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+        // TLS is enforced: database_url validated above to contain sslmode=require.\n+        // The URL is captured here and never written to logs or error messages.\n+        let database_url = cfg.database_url.clone();\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-build-secure-conn\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+        let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()\n+            .min_connections(cfg.pool_size_min)\n+            .max_connections(cfg.pool_size_max)\n+            .acquire_timeout(cfg.connection_timeout)\n+            .connect(&database_url)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|_| {\n+                error!(\"Failed to create TimescaleDB connection pool\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"connection pool initialization failed\")\n+            })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-build-pool\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        run_migrations(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB schema migration failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-4\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"schema migration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-run-migrations\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB schema migration completed; all schema objects are present\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        setup_continuous_aggregate(&pool).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup failed\");\n+            // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3c\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"continuous aggregate setup failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-setup-continuous-aggregate\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3a\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+        info!(\"TimescaleDB continuous aggregate setup complete; returning success to operator\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-operator-schema-migration:p1:inst-flow-smig-3b\n+\n+        setup_retention_policy(&pool, cfg.retention_default)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                error!(error = %e, \"TimescaleDB retention policy setup failed\");\n+                anyhow::anyhow!(\"retention policy setup failed\")\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let instance_id = UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1::gts_make_instance_id(\n+            \"cf.core._.timescaledb_usage_collector_storage_plugin.v1\",\n+        );\n+\n+        let registry = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n+        let instance = BaseModkitPluginV1::<UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1> {\n+            id: instance_id.clone(),\n+            vendor: \"virtuozzo\".to_owned(),\n+            priority: 10,\n+            properties: UsageCollectorStoragePluginSpecV1,\n+        };\n+        let instance_json = serde_json::to_value(&instance)?;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+        let results = registry.register(vec![instance_json]).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration call failed for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            anyhow::anyhow!(\"GTS registration failed\")\n+        })?;\n+        RegisterResult::ensure_all_ok(&results).map_err(|e| {\n+            error!(error = %e, \"GTS registration rejected for TimescaleDB plugin\");\n+            e\n+        })?;\n+        info!(%instance_id, \"GTS registration successful for TimescaleDB storage plugin\");\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-encryption-and-gts:p1:inst-register-gts\n+\n+        let insert_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgInsertPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let query_port: Arc<dyn crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort> =\n+            Arc::new(PgQueryPort::new(pool.clone()));\n+        let metrics: Arc<dyn crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics> =\n+            Arc::new(OtelPluginMetrics::new());\n+        let client = TimescaleDbPluginClient::new(insert_port, query_port, metrics);\n+        let api: Arc<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1> = Arc::new(client);\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+        ctx.client_hub()\n+            .register_scoped::<dyn UsageCollectorPluginClientV1>(\n+                ClientScope::gts_id(&instance_id),\n+                api,\n+            );\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-dod-production-storage-plugin-plugin-crate:p1:inst-register-client\n+\n+        info!(\n+            %instance_id,\n+            \"TimescaleDB usage-collector storage plugin started successfully\"\n+        );\n+\n+        tokio::spawn(run_health_check_loop(pool));\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async fn run_health_check_loop(pool: PgPool) {\n+    let meter = global::meter(\"timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin\");\n+    let gauge = meter.f64_gauge(\"storage_health_status\").build();\n+    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(std::time::Duration::from_secs(30));\n+    loop {\n+        interval.tick().await;\n+        if pool.is_closed() {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+        health_check(&pool, &gauge).await;\n+    }","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/module.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The author of this PR is on the CodeRabbit Free Plan. In order to use the Chat feature, please upgrade the PR author to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:31:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:31:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266258411","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266258411"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266258411"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266258411/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":176,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266098480,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":176,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266270565","pull_request_review_id":4318894543,"id":3266270565,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Cr1Vl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Resolved.** The CAGG-vs-raw routing now refuses to use `usage_agg_1h` unless the request is fully within the materialized horizon AND the requested granularity is hourly-or-coarser. See `modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs`.\r\n\r\n### 1. Time range must be inside the materialized window\r\n\r\nNew predicate `cagg_safe_range(start, end, now)` (lines 216–222) returns `true` only when:\r\n\r\n- both endpoints are hour-aligned (otherwise the boundary buckets cover records outside the requested range), AND\r\n- `end <= now - 1 hour` — matching the `end_offset => INTERVAL '1 hour'` on the refresh policy (`continuous_aggregate.rs:61`).\r\n\r\nIt is invoked at line 493–494 (`unsafe_time_range = !cagg_safe_range(...)`) and folded into `use_raw_path` at line 500–506. So a 2-hour window starting 30 minutes ago now routes to `usage_records`, not the cagg.\r\n\r\n`now` is injected as a parameter (not read inline) so the horizon edge is unit-testable without `Utc::now()` races.\r\n\r\n### 2. Bucket size is consulted before routing\r\n\r\nNew predicate `cagg_too_coarse` (lines 485–488) forces the raw path whenever the request asks for minute granularity — either via `query.bucket_size == Some(BucketSize::Minute)` or via `GroupByDimension::TimeBucket(BucketSize::Minute)` in `group_by`. Re-bucketing the 1-hour cagg at minute resolution would yield sparse hour-aligned rows with empty minutes in between; this guard prevents that.\r\n\r\nIn addition, `validate_bucket_size_consistency` (line 235) rejects with `InvalidArgument` if a caller sets `bucket_size` and `GroupBy::TimeBucket(_)` to different sizes — so the routing decision and the emitted SQL cannot disagree silently.\r\n\r\n### Bonus: closed-interval contract preserved\r\n\r\nEven on the cagg path, the SQL UNION ALLs the bucket aggregate with a raw-record projection at `timestamp = end` (see `build_cagg_boundary_corrected_from`, line 278), so records on the inclusive upper bound are not lost when switching from raw `<=` to bucket `<`.\r\n\r\n### Observability\r\n\r\nEach routing predicate (`cagg_too_coarse`, `unsafe_time_range`, `scope_constrains_ids`, `filter_resource`, `filter_subject`, `group_resource`, `group_subject`) is emitted as a separate field on the `query_aggregated routing decision` debug span (line 512–522), so an operator can tell *why* a query fell back to raw.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:33:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:33:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266270565","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266270565"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266270565"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266270565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":103,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266096489,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":103,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266271350","pull_request_review_id":4318895413,"id":3266271350,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Cr1h2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,663 @@\n+//! `PostgreSQL` implementation of the query port.\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};\n+use modkit_odata::SortDir;\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::Row as _;\n+use sqlx::postgres::PgArguments;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationFn, AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, BucketSize, GroupByDimension, RawQuery,\n+    UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{CursorV1, Page, PageInfo, UsageCollectorError};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+use crate::domain::scope::{SqlValue, scope_to_sql};\n+\n+pub struct PgQueryPort {\n+    pool: PgPool,\n+}\n+\n+impl PgQueryPort {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(pool: PgPool) -> Self {\n+        Self { pool }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn is_transient_error(e: &sqlx::Error) -> bool {\n+    match e {\n+        sqlx::Error::PoolTimedOut | sqlx::Error::PoolClosed | sqlx::Error::Io(_) => true,\n+        sqlx::Error::Database(db_err) => matches!(\n+            db_err.code().as_deref(),\n+            Some(\"40001\" | \"40P01\" | \"57P03\" | \"53300\" | \"08006\" | \"08001\")\n+        ),\n+        _ => false,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn add_arg<T>(args: &mut PgArguments, value: T) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError>\n+where\n+    T: for<'q> sqlx::Encode<'q, sqlx::Postgres> + sqlx::Type<sqlx::Postgres>,\n+{\n+    use sqlx::Arguments as _;\n+    args.add(value)\n+        .map_err(|e| UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"SQL argument binding failed: {e}\")))\n+}\n+\n+fn raw_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"COUNT(*)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"AVG(value)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn cagg_agg_expr(func: AggregationFn) -> &'static str {\n+    match func {\n+        AggregationFn::Sum => \"SUM(sum_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Count => \"SUM(cnt_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Min => \"MIN(min_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Max => \"MAX(max_val)::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+        AggregationFn::Avg => \"(SUM(sum_val) / NULLIF(SUM(cnt_val), 0))::float8 AS agg_value\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn bucket_size_to_pg_interval(size: BucketSize) -> &'static str {\n+    match size {\n+        BucketSize::Minute => \"1 minute\",\n+        BucketSize::Hour => \"1 hour\",\n+        BucketSize::Day => \"1 day\",\n+        BucketSize::Week => \"1 week\",\n+        BucketSize::Month => \"1 month\",\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl QueryPort for PgQueryPort {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    #[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+        let (scope_sql, scope_params) = scope_to_sql(&query.scope).map_err(|_| {\n+            UsageCollectorError::authorization_failed(\n+                \"scope translation failed \\u{2014} access denied\",\n+            )\n+        })?;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-1\n+\n+        let group_by = &query.group_by;\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1:inst-qagg-2\n+        let use_raw_path = query.resource_id.is_some()\n+            || query.subject_id.is_some()\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Resource)\n+            || group_by.contains(&GroupByDimension::Subject);\n+        tracing::debug!(use_raw_path, \"query_aggregated routing decision\");","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/pg_query_port.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The author of this PR is on the CodeRabbit Free Plan. In order to use the Chat feature, please upgrade the PR author to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:33:41Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:33:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266271350","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266271350"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266271350"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266271350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":103,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266096489,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":103,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266314648","pull_request_review_id":4318947969,"id":3266314648,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CsAGY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@\n+//! Schema migration runner for the `TimescaleDB` storage plugin.\n+\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::MigrationError;\n+\n+// @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1\n+/// # Errors\n+///\n+/// Returns [`MigrationError`] if any DDL statement fails against the database.\n+pub async fn run_migrations(pool: &PgPool) -> Result<(), MigrationError> {\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-1\n+    sqlx::query(\"CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS timescaledb CASCADE\")\n+        .execute(pool)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(|e| {\n+            MigrationError::Migration(format!(\"failed to create timescaledb extension: {e}\"))\n+        })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-1\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-2\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS usage_records (\n+            id              UUID        NOT NULL DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n+            tenant_id       UUID        NOT NULL,\n+            module          TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            kind            TEXT        NOT NULL CHECK (kind IN ('counter', 'gauge')),\n+            metric          TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            value           NUMERIC     NOT NULL,\n+            timestamp       TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,\n+            idempotency_key TEXT,\n+            resource_id     UUID        NOT NULL,\n+            resource_type   TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            subject_id      UUID,\n+            subject_type    TEXT,\n+            ingested_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n+            metadata        JSONB,\n+            PRIMARY KEY (id, timestamp)\n+        )\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| MigrationError::Migration(format!(\"failed to create usage_records table: {e}\")))?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-2\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-3\n+    sqlx::query(\"SELECT create_hypertable('usage_records', 'timestamp', if_not_exists => true)\")\n+        .execute(pool)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(|e| {\n+            MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+                \"failed to convert usage_records to hypertable: {e}\"\n+            ))\n+        })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-3\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-4\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-4\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-5\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_metric_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, metric, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_metric_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-5\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-6\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_subject_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, subject_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_subject_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-6\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-7\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_resource_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, resource_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_resource_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/migrations.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Feedback status: partially valid, addressed by routing — schema indexes unchanged\r\n\r\nThe current state (`migrations.rs:120-164`) keeps the same four secondary indexes — `(tenant_id, timestamp)`, `(tenant_id, metric, timestamp)`, `(tenant_id, subject_id, timestamp)`, `(tenant_id, resource_id, timestamp)` — and no new indexes were added for `resource_type`, `subject_type`, or `module`. The feedback is nevertheless resolved by how those dimensions are exposed and routed, not by widening the index list:\r\n\r\n1. **`module` / `source` is not a raw-query dimension.** `RawQuery` (`usage-collector-sdk/src/models.rs:370-390`) has no `source`/`module` field, and `query_raw` (`pg_query_port.rs:763-792`) never emits a `module = $n` predicate. The reviewer was conflating the raw and aggregated surfaces; the raw path cannot degrade on `module` because it cannot filter on `module`.\r\n\r\n2. **Aggregations on `module` / `resource_type` / `subject_type` don't hit the hypertable.** `query_aggregated` routes those through the `usage_agg_1h` continuous aggregate (`continuous_aggregate.rs:39-55`), which is `GROUP BY (bucket, tenant_id, metric, module, resource_type, subject_type)`. The raw path is taken only when `resource_id`/`subject_id` is filtered or grouped, the CAGG is too coarse (sub-hour), the time range is unmaterialized, or scope constrains record ids (`pg_query_port.rs:500-506`) — and the first two of those are already covered by `(tenant_id, resource_id, timestamp)` / `(tenant_id, subject_id, timestamp)`.\r\n\r\n3. **Raw queries on `resource_type` / `subject_type` still scan the hypertable**, but those columns are very low cardinality (a small fixed enum per tenant), so a dedicated btree on either would rarely beat the existing `(tenant_id, timestamp DESC)` range scan with the type as a residual predicate — Postgres' planner will normally pick the time-range index and ingest would pay for an index it doesn't get to use. In production these filters are also virtually always combined with `resource_id` / `subject_id` / `metric`, all of which are indexed and supply the actual selectivity.\r\n\r\nNet: the \"wide tenant/time scan\" failure mode the reviewer worried about cannot occur for `module`/`source` (not a filter on the raw API), is avoided for aggregations via the CAGG, and is the cheapest available plan for low-cardinality `*_type` filters on the raw surface — so no extra btree is warranted.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:39:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:39:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266314648","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266314648"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266314648"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266314648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266093524,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":110,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266315294","pull_request_review_id":4318948786,"id":3266315294,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CsAQe","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@\n+//! Schema migration runner for the `TimescaleDB` storage plugin.\n+\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::MigrationError;\n+\n+// @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1\n+/// # Errors\n+///\n+/// Returns [`MigrationError`] if any DDL statement fails against the database.\n+pub async fn run_migrations(pool: &PgPool) -> Result<(), MigrationError> {\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-1\n+    sqlx::query(\"CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS timescaledb CASCADE\")\n+        .execute(pool)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(|e| {\n+            MigrationError::Migration(format!(\"failed to create timescaledb extension: {e}\"))\n+        })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-1\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-2\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS usage_records (\n+            id              UUID        NOT NULL DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n+            tenant_id       UUID        NOT NULL,\n+            module          TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            kind            TEXT        NOT NULL CHECK (kind IN ('counter', 'gauge')),\n+            metric          TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            value           NUMERIC     NOT NULL,\n+            timestamp       TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,\n+            idempotency_key TEXT,\n+            resource_id     UUID        NOT NULL,\n+            resource_type   TEXT        NOT NULL,\n+            subject_id      UUID,\n+            subject_type    TEXT,\n+            ingested_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n+            metadata        JSONB,\n+            PRIMARY KEY (id, timestamp)\n+        )\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| MigrationError::Migration(format!(\"failed to create usage_records table: {e}\")))?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-2\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-3\n+    sqlx::query(\"SELECT create_hypertable('usage_records', 'timestamp', if_not_exists => true)\")\n+        .execute(pool)\n+        .await\n+        .map_err(|e| {\n+            MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+                \"failed to convert usage_records to hypertable: {e}\"\n+            ))\n+        })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-3\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-4\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-4\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-5\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_metric_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, metric, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_metric_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-5\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-6\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_subject_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, subject_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_subject_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;\n+    // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-6\n+\n+    // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-schema-migrations:p1:inst-mig-7\n+    sqlx::query(\n+        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_usage_records_tenant_resource_time \\\n+         ON usage_records (tenant_id, resource_id, timestamp DESC)\",\n+    )\n+    .execute(pool)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(|e| {\n+        MigrationError::Migration(format!(\n+            \"failed to create idx_usage_records_tenant_resource_time: {e}\"\n+        ))\n+    })?;","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-storage-plugin/src/infra/migrations.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The author of this PR is on the CodeRabbit Free Plan. In order to use the Chat feature, please upgrade the PR author to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:39:59Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:39:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266315294","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266315294"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266315294"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266315294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266093524,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":110,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266359671","pull_request_review_id":4319006217,"id":3266359671,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CsLF3","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,7 +3,9 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n #[cfg_attr(feature = \"with-utoipa\", derive(utoipa::ToSchema))]\n #[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n pub struct PageInfo {\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub next_cursor: Option<String>,\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub prev_cursor: Option<String>,\n     pub limit: u64,","path":"libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved in the refactor. Two changes address the original feedback:\r\n\r\n**1. `skip_serializing_if` reverted on the shared `modkit-odata` `PageInfo`** — `libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs` no longer carries `skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\"` on `next_cursor` / `prev_cursor`. Cursors serialize as `null` again, so external consumers of the shared library see no breaking change.\r\n\r\n**2. Usage-collector API now owns its own DTO** — `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector/src/api/rest/dto.rs` defines `PageInfoDto` (mirroring `modkit-odata::PageInfo`) and applies `skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\"` only there. The omit-on-final-page semantics live in this new endpoint's contract, not in the shared library. Since `/usage-collector/v1/raw` is a brand-new endpoint, there are no pre-existing JSON consumers to break.\r\n\r\n**Documentation updated** — the inaccurate \"Null next_cursor in page_info signals the final page\" wording in `api/rest/routes.rs` is gone. The DTO and PRD/DESIGN/feature docs now consistently say \"absent `next_cursor` signals the final page\" (e.g. `dto.rs:132`, `docs/PRD.md:365`, `docs/DESIGN.md:272`, `docs/features/0003-…query-api.md:185,208,558`). Tests at `tests/query_raw_tests.rs:77-79,153-155` and `handlers_tests.rs:1466,1617` assert the absent/omit semantics.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:45:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:45:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266359671","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266359671"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266359671"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266359671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":8,"original_line":10,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266085159,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266360520","pull_request_review_id":4319007402,"id":3266360520,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CsLTI","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,7 +3,9 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n #[cfg_attr(feature = \"with-utoipa\", derive(utoipa::ToSchema))]\n #[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n pub struct PageInfo {\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub next_cursor: Option<String>,\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub prev_cursor: Option<String>,\n     pub limit: u64,","path":"libs/modkit-odata/src/page.rs","commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The author of this PR is on the CodeRabbit Free Plan. In order to use the Chat feature, please upgrade the PR author to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-19T12:45:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:45:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266360520","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266360520"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3266360520"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3266360520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":8,"original_line":10,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266085159,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267097735","pull_request_review_id":4319922931,"id":3267097735,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Cu_SH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` storage plugin client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::Instant;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, RawQuery, UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{Page, UsageCollectorError, UsageCollectorPluginClientV1};\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::StoragePluginError;\n+use crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort;\n+use crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics;\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+\n+/// Storage plugin client backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+#[domain_model]\n+pub struct TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    insert_port: Arc<dyn InsertPort>,\n+    query_port: Arc<dyn QueryPort>,\n+    metrics: Arc<dyn PluginMetrics>,\n+}\n+\n+impl TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    /// Creates a new client wrapping the given insert port, query port, and metrics port.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        insert_port: Arc<dyn InsertPort>,\n+        query_port: Arc<dyn QueryPort>,\n+        metrics: Arc<dyn PluginMetrics>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            insert_port,\n+            query_port,\n+            metrics,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl UsageCollectorPluginClientV1 for TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1\n+    async fn create_usage_record(&self, record: UsageRecord) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-1\n+        // Plugin entry point; called by the gateway when delegating record storage.\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-1\n+        if record.kind == UsageKind::Counter && record.value < 0.0 {\n+            self.metrics.record_schema_validation_error();\n+            return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                \"invalid record: counter value must be >= 0\",\n+            ));\n+        }\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-2\n+        if record.kind == UsageKind::Counter && record.idempotency_key.is_empty() {\n+            self.metrics.record_schema_validation_error();\n+            return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                \"invalid record: idempotency_key required for counter records\",\n+            ));\n+        }\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-2\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-3\n+        let result = self.insert_port.insert_usage_record(&record).await;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-3\n+\n+        let rows_affected = match result {\n+            Ok(n) => n,\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-4\n+                if let StoragePluginError::InvalidRecord(ref msg) = e {\n+                    tracing::warn!(error = %msg, \"unexpected unique constraint violation in usage_records\");\n+                    self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                    self.metrics\n+                        .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                    return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                        \"unexpected unique constraint violation\",\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-4\n+\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-4\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-5\n+                if let StoragePluginError::Transient(ref msg) = e {\n+                    self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                    self.metrics\n+                        .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                    return Err(UsageCollectorError::unavailable(format!(\n+                        \"transient error: {msg}\"\n+                    )));\n+                }\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-5\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-4\n+\n+                self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                self.metrics\n+                    .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"storage error: {e}\")));\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        let elapsed_ms = start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0;\n+        self.metrics.record_ingestion_latency_ms(elapsed_ms);\n+        if rows_affected == 0 {\n+            self.metrics.record_dedup();\n+        } else {\n+            self.metrics.record_ingestion_success();\n+        }\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-5\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-7\n+        Ok(())\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-7\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-5\n+    }\n+\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+        let result = self.query_port.query_aggregated(query).await;\n+        self.metrics\n+            .record_query_latency_ms(\"aggregated\", start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+        result\n+    }\n+\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-raw:p1\n+    async fn query_raw(&self, query: RawQuery) -> Result<Page<UsageRecord>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+        let result = self.query_port.query_raw(query).await;\n+        self.metrics\n+            .record_query_latency_ms(\"raw\", start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+        result\n+    }","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/domain/client.rs","commit_id":"9ffbebd3f88d3afe331838b4cdc61a859ed18b41","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved. Both query paths now emit success/error counters alongside latency.\r\n\r\nIn `modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/domain/client.rs`:\r\n\r\n- `query_aggregated` (lines 117–131): on `Ok` calls `metrics.record_query_success(\"aggregated\")`, on `Err` calls `metrics.record_query_error(\"aggregated\")`.\r\n- `query_raw` (lines 134–145): on `Ok` calls `metrics.record_query_success(\"raw\")`, on `Err` calls `metrics.record_query_error(\"raw\")`.\r\n\r\nBacked by the `PluginMetrics` trait (`src/domain/metrics.rs:15-16`) with the OTel implementation in `src/infra/otel_metrics.rs:76-96`, which increments a `query_total` counter labeled with `query_type` (`aggregated`|`raw`) and `status` (`success`|`error`), plus a dedicated `query_errors_total` counter on the error branch.\r\n\r\nThis distinguishes \"no traffic\" (counter flat) from \"all queries failing\" (error counter rising, success flat) and satisfies the PR's query-counter observability requirement.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-19T14:30:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T14:30:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3267097735","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267097735"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1927#discussion_r3267097735"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1927"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267097735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":145,"original_line":145,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3266091090,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":145,"position":145,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267098810","pull_request_review_id":4319924124,"id":3267098810,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7Cu_i6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+//! `TimescaleDB` storage plugin client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::Instant;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+use usage_collector_sdk::models::{\n+    AggregationQuery, AggregationResult, RawQuery, UsageKind, UsageRecord,\n+};\n+use usage_collector_sdk::{Page, UsageCollectorError, UsageCollectorPluginClientV1};\n+\n+use crate::domain::error::StoragePluginError;\n+use crate::domain::insert_port::InsertPort;\n+use crate::domain::metrics::PluginMetrics;\n+use crate::domain::query_port::QueryPort;\n+\n+/// Storage plugin client backed by a `TimescaleDB` connection pool.\n+#[domain_model]\n+pub struct TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    insert_port: Arc<dyn InsertPort>,\n+    query_port: Arc<dyn QueryPort>,\n+    metrics: Arc<dyn PluginMetrics>,\n+}\n+\n+impl TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    /// Creates a new client wrapping the given insert port, query port, and metrics port.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        insert_port: Arc<dyn InsertPort>,\n+        query_port: Arc<dyn QueryPort>,\n+        metrics: Arc<dyn PluginMetrics>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            insert_port,\n+            query_port,\n+            metrics,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl UsageCollectorPluginClientV1 for TimescaleDbPluginClient {\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1\n+    // @cpt-flow:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1\n+    async fn create_usage_record(&self, record: UsageRecord) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-1\n+        // Plugin entry point; called by the gateway when delegating record storage.\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-2\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-1\n+        if record.kind == UsageKind::Counter && record.value < 0.0 {\n+            self.metrics.record_schema_validation_error();\n+            return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                \"invalid record: counter value must be >= 0\",\n+            ));\n+        }\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-1\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-2\n+        if record.kind == UsageKind::Counter && record.idempotency_key.is_empty() {\n+            self.metrics.record_schema_validation_error();\n+            return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                \"invalid record: idempotency_key required for counter records\",\n+            ));\n+        }\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-2\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-2\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-3\n+        let result = self.insert_port.insert_usage_record(&record).await;\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-3\n+\n+        let rows_affected = match result {\n+            Ok(n) => n,\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-4\n+                if let StoragePluginError::InvalidRecord(ref msg) = e {\n+                    tracing::warn!(error = %msg, \"unexpected unique constraint violation in usage_records\");\n+                    self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                    self.metrics\n+                        .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                    return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(\n+                        \"unexpected unique constraint violation\",\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-4\n+\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-4\n+                // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-5\n+                if let StoragePluginError::Transient(ref msg) = e {\n+                    self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                    self.metrics\n+                        .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                    return Err(UsageCollectorError::unavailable(format!(\n+                        \"transient error: {msg}\"\n+                    )));\n+                }\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-5\n+                // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-4\n+\n+                self.metrics.record_ingestion_error();\n+                self.metrics\n+                    .record_ingestion_latency_ms(start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+                return Err(UsageCollectorError::internal(format!(\"storage error: {e}\")));\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        let elapsed_ms = start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0;\n+        self.metrics.record_ingestion_latency_ms(elapsed_ms);\n+        if rows_affected == 0 {\n+            self.metrics.record_dedup();\n+        } else {\n+            self.metrics.record_ingestion_success();\n+        }\n+\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-5\n+        // @cpt-begin:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-7\n+        Ok(())\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-create-usage-record:p1:inst-cur-7\n+        // @cpt-end:cpt-cf-usage-collector-flow-production-storage-plugin-storage-backend-ingest:p1:inst-flow-ing-5\n+    }\n+\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-aggregated:p1\n+    async fn query_aggregated(\n+        &self,\n+        query: AggregationQuery,\n+    ) -> Result<Vec<AggregationResult>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+        let result = self.query_port.query_aggregated(query).await;\n+        self.metrics\n+            .record_query_latency_ms(\"aggregated\", start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+        result\n+    }\n+\n+    // @cpt-algo:cpt-cf-usage-collector-algo-production-storage-plugin-query-raw:p1\n+    async fn query_raw(&self, query: RawQuery) -> Result<Page<UsageRecord>, UsageCollectorError> {\n+        let start = Instant::now();\n+        let result = self.query_port.query_raw(query).await;\n+        self.metrics\n+            .record_query_latency_ms(\"raw\", start.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.0);\n+        result\n+    }","path":"modules/system/usage-collector/plugins/timescaledb-usage-collector-plugin/src/domain/client.rs","commit_id":"9ffbebd3f88d3afe331838b4cdc61a859ed18b41","original_commit_id":"3d1998170dab6e34be5396cf535d19a6317d4517","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbi