I Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4468478011","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1925#issuecomment-4468478011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1925","id":4468478011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABCleQOw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-16T23:03:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T21:52:43Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `023a4fc5-cc1f-4c97-9e71-944c8397ee34`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between f30bf51eca84451e72c4c58aefb9237c77a3037c and fd8a040750d2d3250c0d0aa6cee3037999c39b91.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `Makefile`\n* `tools/scripts/md-fabric.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (1)</summary>\n\n* Makefile\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a Python rectangle-packing library with MaxRects variants and layout optimization, a new md-fabric TOML config mapping docs into categories and views, placeholder README, and a Makefile target `md-fabric` that runs the md-fabric script to generate HTML output.\n\n## Changes\n\n**MD-Fabric Documentation Pipeline**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Rectangle packing primitives and core algorithm** <br> `tools/scripts/lib/rectpack_local.py`|Introduces `Rectangle` geometry helpers and `PackingAlgorithm` base; implements MaxRects with free-rectangle splitting, placement selection, and pruning.|\n|**Packing heuristics and candidate generation** <br> `tools/scripts/lib/rectpack_local.py`|Adds MaxRects heuristic variants (MaxRectsBl, MaxRectsBssf, MaxRectsBaf, MaxRectsBlsf), sort orders, dataclasses for layout candidates/metrics, and offline generation of layout candidates with density/aspect scoring and dominance pruning.|\n|**Optimization and factory** <br> `tools/scripts/lib/rectpack_local.py`|Computes stacked-layout metrics, multi-heuristic repacking search, iterative category-width optimization, and exposes `newPacker(...)`/`_OfflinePacker` wrapper for packing execution and introspection.|\n|**md-fabric configuration and views** <br> `tools/scripts/md-fabric.toml`|Adds `skip_dirs`, category bucket mappings for repository/CyPilot/ModKit/modules markdown, and multiple view definitions (Claude, Codex, Windsurf, Cursor, Copilot, Antigravity) with start paths and default depths.|\n|**Build integration and placeholder docs** <br> `Makefile`, `docs/md-fabric/README.md`|Adds `md-fabric` phony target and recipe to run `python3 ./tools/scripts/md-fabric.py --out docs/md-fabric/md-fabric.html`. README clarifies `md-fabric` folder holds autogenerated artifacts.|\n\n## Estimated Code Review Effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through bins and padded frames,  \n> I nudged each rectangle into lanes,  \n> From TOML maps to HTML bright,  \n> The layout hums into the light,  \n> Docs tucked in rows — a rabbit's delight.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4468478011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1924,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924","source_state":"closed","source_author":"MikeFalcon77","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1924] feat(modkit): Windows CNG rustls CryptoProvider for Windows FIPS","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feature/fips_windows","pr_head_sha":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"MikeFalcon77","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924","id":3695663204,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7cR1hk","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1924","number":1924,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(modkit): Windows CNG rustls CryptoProvider for Windows FIPS","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes the cross-OS FIPS 140-3 gap left open by ADR 0001 (Windows was explicitly deferred). Routes --features fips on Windows through `rustls-cng-crypto`, a rustls::crypto::CryptoProvider backed by Windows CNG (bcrypt.dll). CNG itself is FIPS 140-3 validated by Microsoft per OS release; `fips_provider()` opts into CNG's Approved-algorithm subset (AES-GCM TLS 1.3 + ECDHE-AES-GCM TLS 1.2; ECDSA/RSA-PSS/RSA-PKCS#1 v1.5 verify; P-256/P-384 ECDHE; SHA-256/384; no ChaCha20, no x25519, no PQ).\r\n\r\nWired through the existing 4-way cfg-dispatch in modkit::bootstrap:: init_crypto_provider and modkit_http::tls::get_crypto_provider:\r\n- macOS+fips    → Apple corecrypto    (ADR 0001, existing)\r\n- Windows+fips  → Windows CNG          (ADR 0003, new)\r\n- Linux+fips    → AWS-LC FIPS          (existing)\r\n- no-fips       → aws-lc-rs default    (existing)\r\n\r\nFail-closed when Windows is not in system-wide FIPS mode. The upstream crate's `fips::enabled()` helper is pub(crate), so we detect the same condition via the documented empty-provider shape: when FipsAlgorithmPolicy != 1, `fips_provider()` returns a CryptoProvider with empty cipher_suites / kx_groups. We refuse to install in that case with `CryptoProviderError::SystemFipsModeNotEnabled` rather than degrade the FIPS claim with a non-handshakeable provider.\r\n\r\n`cyberware-rustls-fips-shim` extended to exclude Windows from rustls/fips (was: not(macos); now: not(any(macos, windows))). Side effect: aws-lc-fips dylib is no longer linked into Windows+fips binaries — `bcrypt.dll` is the only crypto-relevant import, mirroring the Apple-frameworks-only linkage on macOS+fips.\r\n\r\nCross-compile verification gate: `make check-windows-fips` via `cargo xwin` (cargo-xwin downloads the MSVC sysroot, ninja drives cmake-based transitive C deps like libz-ng-sys). Verified locally on macOS that the full cyberware-example-server --features fips cross-checks green against x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Windows FIPS 140-3 support via a CNG crypto provider with fail-closed behavior when system FIPS mode is disabled.\n  * Added Windows+FIPS build/verification tooling for cross-checking FIPS builds.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Expanded FIPS 140-3 docs with per-OS provider details, algorithm/TLS scope, verification steps, and Windows prerequisites.\n  * Updated example probe docs and startup messaging to cover Windows FIPS behavior and verification.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Setup now installs NASM on Windows if missing.\n  * License allow-list updated to include OpenSSL.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-16T21:45:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T22:36:21Z","closed_at":"2026-05-16T22:36:21Z","merged_at":"2026-05-16T22:36:21Z","merge_commit_sha":"a49c65ce7b9ca7b2f51f8a8c4ec6dd5f41865bdc","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1924/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","head":{"label":"MikeFalcon77:feature/fips_windows","ref":"feature/fips_windows","sha":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237645146,"node_id":"R_kgDOScT3Wg","name":"cyberware-rust","full_name":"MikeFalcon77/cyberware-rust","private":true,"owner":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77/cyberware-rust","description":"All-in-one open-source framework & middleware for enter