d_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4464268343","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1918#issuecomment-4464268343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1918","id":4464268343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABChdUNw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T22:34:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T23:52:32Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `cad3ac3d-3d5f-4ce8-8621-5df74aabf8a4`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 191dbeff184cf2f8fb366a956b113099296a6d5f and 79d1dd684fe178883c19c3f35e43cee385088840.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (9)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/oagw/docs/DESIGN.md`\n* `modules/system/oagw/docs/features/0002-cpt-cf-oagw-feature-management-api.md`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/alias.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/bind.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/mod.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/e2e_smoke_test.rs`\n* `modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/management_api_test.rs`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/oagw/test_management_lifecycle.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (2)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/oagw/docs/features/0002-cpt-cf-oagw-feature-management-api.md\n* modules/system/oagw/docs/DESIGN.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (4)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/tests/e2e_smoke_test.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/alias.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/bind.rs\n* modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/mod.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nMigrates SSRF from a boolean to SsrfPolicy/SsrfGuard, wires a shared guard into module and proxy, implements control-plane domain services (alias, merge/resolution, bind, budget, validation), refactors the data-plane proxy pipeline, and updates configs, docs, and tests.\n\n## Changes\n\n**SSRF Protection Policy Restructuring**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **SSRF Policy Definition and Guard** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/ssrf.rs` | `SsrfPolicy` struct with `enabled` flag, allow/deny CIDR and hostname lists; `Cidr` helper parsing/containment; `SsrfGuard` enforces allow-first evaluation and provides block reasons; built-in hostname deny-list limited to `localhost` and `localhost.localdomain`; expanded unit tests. |\n| **Config and Module Integration** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/config.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/module.rs` | Replaces `OagwConfig.ssrf_protection` boolean with `ssrf_policy: SsrfPolicy`; module init builds shared `SsrfGuard` from policy and wires it into control-plane and data-plane components. |\n| **Pingora Proxy and Test Builders** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/pingora_proxy.rs`, `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/test_support.rs` | `PingoraProxy`, `DnsDiscovery`, and `PingoraEndpointSelector` now accept and store `Arc<SsrfGuard>` instead of a boolean; DNS resolution and fallback paths use `SsrfGuard` to filter IPs/hostnames with reasoning; tests and test builders use `SsrfGuard::disabled()` for disabled behavior. |\n\n**Control Plane Domain Service Layer**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Alias Lifecycle** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/alias.rs` | Alias validation (non-empty, ≤253 chars, allowed ASCII set, no `.`/`..`, requires alphanumeric), normalization (lowercase, strip trailing dot), derivation from endpoint lists (hostname-based derivation with common registrable suffix and optional `:port`), and create/update enforcement functions that implement alias immutability and derivation rules. |\n| **Bind Validation** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/bind.rs` | Defines bind action constants and `BindOverrides`; `validate_bind_constraints` enforces base bind permission and per-field override permissions based on sharing mode; `validate_secret_ref_accessible` checks `cred://` secret reachability; `validate_ancestor_bind` finds nearest matching ancestor and delegates validation. |\n| **Budget Validation** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/budget.rs` | `validate_budget_config` enforces budget invariants; `ControlPlaneServiceImpl::validate_budget_allocation` ensures child allocations fit within closest allocated ancestor budget; `validate_descendants_within_budget` ensures proposed tightened budgets still accommodate existing descendants. |\n| **Configuration Merging** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/merge.rs` | `is_visible_to_descendant` and `compute_effective_config` merge ordered ancestor upstreams into an effective `Upstream` applying per-field sharing semantics: auth (`Enforce` sticky), rate limit (stricter wins with pool ownership handling), plugins (concat + dedup/override), CORS (Inherit/Enforce handling and validation), and add-only tags; includes rate normalization helpers. |\n| **Domain Validation Rules** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/validation.rs` | `validate_match_rules` (exactly one of http/grpc), `validate_endpoints` (non-empty, no IPv6 literals, all-IP vs all-hostname consistency, RFC1123 hostname rules), `validate_endpoints_ssrf` (consult `SsrfGuard` when enabled), `check_route_overlap` (detect enabled HTTP route conflicts). |\n| **Service Core Implementation** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/mod.rs` | `ControlPlaneServiceImpl` with repo/tenant-resolver/policy/credstore/ssrf dependencies and `new(...)` constructor; implements CRUD flows: `create_upstream`, `get/list_upstreams`, `update_upstream` (full replace, alias immutability enforcement when endpoints unchanged), `delete_upstream` (cascade delete routes), route CRUD, and `resolve_proxy_target` using merge/resolution helpers. |\n| **Alias and Route Resolution** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/resolution.rs` | `build_tenant_chain` builds ordered tenant ancestry; `resolve_alias` selects closest visible enabled upstream, constructs merge chain, optionally resolves a `Route` with ancestor fallback, and returns effective merged `Upstream` (+ optional `Route`); `find_route_in_chain` searches tenant scopes for a matching route. |\n\n**Data Plane Request/Response Pipeline Refactoring**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Request Parsing** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs` | Introduces `ParsedRequest` and `parse_proxy_request` to extract alias, normalize path suffix, parse/URL-decode query, validate headers, and choose buffered vs streaming body handling with `max_body_size` enforcement; `proxy_request` now consumes the parsed form. |\n| **Response Pipeline Helpers** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs` | Adds `apply_response_pipeline` to run transforms, inject CORS, apply header rules, and insert rate-limit headers for both HTTP and WebSocket 101 flows; `finalize_response` delegates to it after guard processing. |\n| **Plugin and Auth Execution** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs` | Extracts `execute_auth_plugin`, `execute_guard_requests` (fail-hard), `execute_transform_requests` (log-and-continue), and `check_rate_limits` (upstream then route, tightest outcome); builds `ResponsePipelineCtx` for response processing. |\n| **WebSocket and Bridge Handling** <br> `modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/infra/proxy/service.rs` | Introduces `handle_websocket_upgrade` to perform 101 upgrade earlier, run guard+transform pipeline, sanitize upgrade headers, and stash duplex bridge IO into response extensions; streaming path enforces `max_body_size` via background tasks; buffered path avoids explicit write-half shutdown. |\n\n**Configuration and Documentation**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **YAML Config and ADR** <br> `config/*`, `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/config/base.yaml`, `modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-resource-identification.md` | Replaces `ssrf_protection: false` with `ssrf_policy.enabled: false` in multiple configs for e2e/dev; ADR updated with \"Alias Immutability on Update\" section describing alias as routing/trust key and a rejection matrix for endpoint transitions that would change a derived alias. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~75 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 From booleans bare to policies deep,  \n> The gateway now guards what must keep,  \n> Aliases fixed, merges that blend,  \n> Proxy and control-plane stitched end-to-end,  \n> A rabbit refactors with a careful leap!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4464268343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267378128","pull_request_review_id":4320255051,"id":3267378128,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CwDvQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,245 @@\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::model::Endpoint;\n+\n+/// Maximum length for an upstream alias.\n+const MAX_ALIAS_LENGTH: usize = 253;\n+\n+/// Validate an alias: non-empty, max length, safe charset (alphanumeric + `.:-_`),\n+/// must contain at least one alphanumeric character, and must not be a dot-segment.\n+pub(in crate::domain::services) fn validate_alias(alias: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n+    if alias.is_empty() {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(\"alias must not be empty\"));\n+    }\n+    if alias.len() > MAX_ALIAS_LENGTH {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(format!(","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/alias.rs","commit_id":"79d1dd684fe178883c19c3f35e43cee385088840","original_commit_id":"890eda3ceae693e05b8baa183f0d29b64270ee82","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Still DomainError? I thought we agreed that we block all new development with the DomainError pattern.","created_at":"2026-05-19T15:08:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T15:08:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1918#discussion_r3267378128","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1918","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267378128"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1918#discussion_r3267378128"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1918"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267378128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":14,"original_line":14,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":14,"position":14,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/3267425836","pull_request_review_id":4320317100,"id":3267425836,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs7CwPYs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,245 @@\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+use crate::domain::model::Endpoint;\n+\n+/// Maximum length for an upstream alias.\n+const MAX_ALIAS_LENGTH: usize = 253;\n+\n+/// Validate an alias: non-empty, max length, safe charset (alphanumeric + `.:-_`),\n+/// must contain at least one alphanumeric character, and must not be a dot-segment.\n+pub(in crate::domain::services) fn validate_alias(alias: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n+    if alias.is_empty() {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(\"alias must not be empty\"));\n+    }\n+    if alias.len() > MAX_ALIAS_LENGTH {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(format!(\n+            \"alias must not exceed {MAX_ALIAS_LENGTH} characters\"\n+        )));\n+    }\n+    if !alias\n+        .chars()\n+        .all(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || matches!(c, '.' | ':' | '-' | '_'))\n+    {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(\n+            \"alias contains invalid characters; only alphanumeric, '.', ':', '-', '_' are allowed\",\n+        ));\n+    }\n+    // Reject dot-segments and punctuation-only aliases to prevent path traversal\n+    // and ambiguous URL segments in /proxy/{alias}/{path}.\n+    if alias == \".\" || alias == \"..\" {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(\n+            \"alias must not be a dot-segment ('.' or '..')\",\n+        ));\n+    }\n+    if !alias.chars().any(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric()) {\n+        return Err(DomainError::validation(\n+            \"alias must contain at least one alphanumeric character\",\n+        ));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Normalize an alias to lowercase. Hostname trailing dots are already\n+/// handled by `Endpoint::normalized_host()` during derivation; this covers\n+/// user-provided explicit aliases. All trailing dots are stripped.\n+pub(in crate::domain::services) fn normalize_alias(alias: &str) -> String {\n+    alias.to_ascii_lowercase().trim_end_matches('.').to_string()\n+}\n+\n+/// Check whether the given endpoints are all IP addresses.\n+fn endpoints_are_ip(endpoints: &[Endpoint]) -> bool {\n+    !endpoints.is_empty() && endpoints.iter().all(Endpoint::is_ip)\n+}\n+\n+/// Attempt to derive an alias from the endpoint list.\n+///\n+/// Returns `Some(alias)` when derivation succeeds (hostname-based), or\n+/// `None` when an explicit alias is required (IP-based or no common suffix).\n+///\n+/// Derivation rules:\n+/// - Single host, standard port → hostname\n+/// - Single host, non-standard port → hostname:port\n+/// - Multiple hosts, all identical → treated as single-host\n+/// - Multiple hosts, common domain suffix (≥2 labels) → common suffix;\n+///   non-standard port is appended (e.g., `vendor.com:8443`) to avoid\n+///   collisions between pools on different ports\n+/// - Multiple hosts, no common suffix → `None`\n+/// - IP addresses → `None`\n+pub(in crate::domain::services) fn compute_derived_alias(endpoints: &[Endpoint]) -> Option<String> {\n+    if endpoints.is_empty() || endpoints_are_ip(endpoints) {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Collect unique normalized host contributions.\n+    let contributions: Vec<String> = endpoints.iter().map(|e| e.alias_contribution()).collect();\n+\n+    // De-duplicate: if all identical, treat as single-endpoint.\n+    let unique: Vec<&str> = {\n+        let mut v: Vec<&str> = contributions.iter().map(String::as_str).collect();\n+        v.sort_unstable();\n+        v.dedup();\n+        v\n+    };\n+\n+    if unique.len() == 1 {\n+        return Some(unique[0].to_string());\n+    }\n+\n+    // Multi-host: extract pure hostnames for common suffix computation.\n+    let hosts: Vec<String> = endpoints.iter().map(|e| e.normalized_host()).collect();\n+    let suffix = common_domain_suffix(&hosts)?;\n+\n+    // Append :port when the pool uses a non-standard port so that\n+    // pools with the same domain suffix but different ports get\n+    // distinct aliases (e.g., `vendor.com` vs `vendor.com:8443`).\n+    // validate_endpoints guarantees all endpoints share the same port.\n+    if endpoints[0].is_standard_port() {\n+        Some(suffix)\n+    } else {\n+        Some(format!(\"{suffix}:{}\", endpoints[0].port))\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract the longest common domain suffix from a set of hostnames.\n+///\n+/// Returns `Some(suffix)` if the common suffix has ≥2 labels, `None` otherwise.\n+/// Example: `[\"us.vendor.com\", \"eu.vendor.com\"]` → `Some(\"vendor.com\")`.\n+pub(super) fn common_domain_suffix(hosts: &[String]) -> Option<String> {\n+    if hosts.is_empty() {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Split each host into labels, reversed (rightmost first).\n+    let reversed: Vec<Vec<&str>> = hosts\n+        .iter()\n+        .map(|h| h.split('.').rev().collect::<Vec<_>>())\n+        .collect();\n+\n+    // Find the longest common prefix of the reversed labels.\n+    let min_len = reversed.iter().map(|r| r.len()).min().unwrap_or(0);\n+    let mut common_count = 0;\n+    for i in 0..min_len {\n+        let label = reversed[0][i];\n+        if reversed.iter().all(|r| r[i] == label) {\n+            common_count += 1;\n+        } else {\n+            break;\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Minimum 2 common labels (e.g. `vendor.com`, not just `com`).\n+    if common_count < 2 {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Reconstruct the suffix in correct order.\n+    let suffix: Vec<&str> = reversed[0][..common_count].iter().rev().copied().collect();\n+    let candidate = suffix.join(\".\");\n+\n+    // Reject public suffixes (e.g. \"co.uk\", \"com.au\") that are not registrable\n+    // domains. A registrable domain has at least one label beyond the public\n+    // suffix (e.g. \"vendor.co.uk\" is registrable, \"co.uk\" is not).\n+    if psl::domain(candidate.as_bytes()).is_none() {\n+        tracing::debug!(suffix = %candidate, \"common suffix is a public suffix (not a registrable domain), alias must be explicit\");\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    Some(candidate)\n+}\n+\n+/// Enforce alias rules on upstream **creation**.\n+///\n+/// - Hostname-derivable endpoints: alias is auto-derived; user-provided alias\n+///   is rejected with `400 Validation`.\n+/// - IP or non-derivable endpoints: explicit alias is required.\n+pub(in crate::domain::services) fn enforce_alias_create(\n+    user_alias: Option<&str>,","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw/src/domain/services/management/alias.rs","commit_id":"890eda3ceae693e05b8baa183f0d29b64270ee82","original_commit_id":"890eda3ceae693e05b8baa183f0d29b64270ee82","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebr