r`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0205_operation_builder/ui/missing_tag.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0205_operation_builder/ui/missing_tag.stderr`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0205_operation_builder/ui/valid_operation.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0503_plugin_client_suffix/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0504_client_versioning/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0504_client_versioning/tests/system_module_exemption.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/ui/bad_direct_sqlx.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/ui/bad_direct_sqlx.stderr`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0707_drop_zeroize/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0707_drop_zeroize/ui/good_no_zeroing.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0802_use_odata_ext/ui/valid_odata.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/ui/permission_strings.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/gts_struct_schema_for.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/gts_struct_schema_for.stderr`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/ui/naming_correct_case_tests.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/ui/naming_path_correct_tests.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/ui/tests.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1301_no_print_macros/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/ui/bad_tryfrom_assoc_error.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/ui/bad_tryfrom_assoc_error.stderr`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/ui/good_from_preserve.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1303_no_primitive_type_alias/src/lib.rs`\n* `tools/dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes (2)</summary>\n\n* tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/gts_struct_schema_for.rs\n* tools/dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0110_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/gts_struct_schema_for.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR modernizes the Rust codebase by refactoring multiple dylint lint implementations to use idiomatic patterns (matches!, if-let chains, is_some_and), extends build tooling to validate the tools/dylint_lints crate with additional fmt and clippy checks, and updates test fixtures and UI stderr outputs to reflect refactored code spans.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Build system and cross-cutting lint refactorings**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Build tooling: Makefile fmt and clippy targets** <br> `Makefile` | Extended `fmt` target to check formatting for both root and tools/dylint_lints workspace; added `dev-clippy` target to run clippy for tools/dylint_lints alongside root checks. |\n| **Lint utilities refactoring** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs` | Refactored helper functions to use compact conditional patterns: is_temp_path uses multi-line checks, is_in_sdk_crate uses early returns, get_path_str_from_session uses Option::map, test_comment_annotations_match_stderr simplifies stderr parsing with rfind. |\n| **Contract layer lints (de0103, de0104, de0110) refactoring** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0103_no_http_types_in_contract/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0104_no_api_dto_in_contract/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0110_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0110_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/*` | Three contract-layer lints refactored: de0103 single-lines if condition, de0104 replaces match with matches!, de0110 reorganizes schema_for! detection and adds early return after first GTS match. Test fixtures and stderr updated to reflect span changes. |\n| **API layer: OperationBuilder validation (de0205) comprehensive refactoring** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0205_operation_builder/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0205_operation_builder/ui/*` | de0205 control-flow refactored with chained if-let patterns; contains_operation_builder_constructor simplified with pattern matching; check_builder_chain uses if-let instead of match; extract_tag_value streamlined. Comprehensive test fixture updates with const INVALID_TAG, multi-line formatting, and refined error spans. |\n| **Domain layer lints (de0301, de0308) refactoring** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs` | Domain-layer lints refactored: de0301 check_type_in_domain rewritten with explicit multi-line pattern for generic-argument recursion; de0308 HTTP_PATTERNS condensed to single-line constant and generic-argument traversal reformatted. |\n| **Client layer lints (de0503, de0504) and integration tests** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0503_plugin_client_suffix/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0504_client_versioning/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0504_client_versioning/tests/system_module_exemption.rs` | de0503 is_plugin_api refactored into multi-line boolean expression; de0504 emit_lint reformatted into multi-line function signature. System module exemption integration test refactored with multi-line cargo check args and narrowed DE0504 detection logic with updated assertion messages. |\n| **Security lints (de0706, de0707) refactoring and test updates** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/ui/*`, `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0707_drop_zeroize/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de07_security/de0707_drop_zeroize/ui/good_no_zeroing.rs` | de0706 refactored with compact if-let patterns for generic-argument recursion; de0707 LazyLock initializations condensed, is_zero_literal uses if-let + && pattern, ZeroingVisitor detection arms refactored to chained conditionals with is_some_and. Test fixture secure_erase signature changed from Vec<u8> to &mut [u8]. UI test spans updated. |\n| **REST API conventions: OData extension test (de0802)** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0802_use_odata_ext/ui/valid_odata.rs` | OData extension helper methods with_odata_filter and with_odata_orderby now reference generic type parameter T via std::any::type_name::<T>() to avoid dead-code warnings. |\n| **GTS layer lints (de0901, de0902) refactoring and test updates** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/ui/permission_strings.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/ui/*` | de0901 introduces const { ... } for IN_TEST_DEPTH, simplifies cfg(test) detection via is_some_and, adjusts argument extraction to args.first(); de0902 simplifies generic-type-argument matching with combined conditional and adds early return. Test fixtures updated: permission_strings uses MockResolver directly and derives Default for MockPermissionBuilder. |\n| **Testing conventions lint (de1101) refactoring and new test files** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de11_testing/de1101_tests_in_separate_files/ui/*` | de1101 implementation refactored with explicit multiline formatting for path validation, cfg(test, ...) recursion, and test assertions without changing detection semantics. Three new empty ui test files added. |\n| **Common patterns lints (de1301, de1302, de1303) refactoring and test updates** <br> `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1301_no_print_macros/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1303_no_primitive_type_alias/src/lib.rs`, `tools/dylint_lints/de13_common_patterns/de1302_error_from_to_string/ui/*` | de1301 imports reformatted to multi-line, is_proc_macro_crate and is_bin_crate simplified via contains(), is_test_item rewritten to check last path segment; de1302 is_hidden_expansion uses matches!; de1303 PRIMITIVE_BACKING_TYPES condensed. Test fixtures updated with multi-line struct initializers and comment formatting; stderr files adjusted for diagnostic spans. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~12 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *Whiskers twitching with Rust delight,*  \n> *Pattern matching shines so bright,*  \n> *If-let chains and matches! bloom,*  \n> *Idiomatic code clears the room,*  \n> *Refactored lints hop into the night!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4462702088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1916,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1916","source_state":"closed","source_author":"fluiderson","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1916] fix(dylint): fix lint annotation line reporting","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"dylintfx","pr_head_sha":"8d070a6884357bd61ab21598d99090fc4142d59c","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"fluiderson","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1916","id":3691635568,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7cCeNw","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1916","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1916.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1916.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1916","number":1916,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(dylint): fix lint annotation line reporting","user":{"login":"fluiderson","id":90795031,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzk1MDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90795031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson","html_url":"https://github.com/fluiderson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fluiderson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For example,\r\n\r\n```rs\r\n// simulated_dir=/cyberfabric/modules/some_module/contract/\r\nuse serde::Deserialize;\r\n\r\n// Should trigger DE0101 - Serde in contract\r\n#[allow(dead_code)]\r\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize)]\r\npub struct Order {\r\n    pub id: String,\r\n    pub total: f64,\r\n}\r\n\r\n#[allow(dead_code)]\r\n// Should trigger DE0101 - Serde in contract\r\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize)]\r\npub enum UserRole {\r\n    Admin,\r\n    User,\r\n    Guest,\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn main() {}\r\n```\r\n\r\nreports\r\n\r\n```\r\nIn \"deserialize.rs\": Line 5 has '// Should trigger DE0101 - Serde in contract' comment but no corresponding error in .stderr file\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhen the expected error is\r\n\r\n```\r\nIn \"deserialize.rs\": Line 4 has '// Should trigger DE0101 - Serde in contract' comment but no corresponding error in .stderr file\r\n```\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbi