- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `6c7ad3d1-2a74-432e-9c6a-2e3c48cf7274`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between dc5a98e305e863de913555f175c910b5e9604220 and 80d8d9b5c1c2fb60d41c0c3dc142c00279975f7d.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (35)</summary>\n\n* `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n* `Makefile`\n* `README.md`\n* `config/quickstart.yaml`\n* `docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md`\n* `docs/api/api.json`\n* `docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0004-single-root-tenant-model-topology.md`\n* `docs/arch/authorization/INTEGRATION_TEST_PLAN.md`\n* `docs/arch/authorization/TENANT_MODEL.md`\n* `docs/modkit_unified_system/02_module_layout_and_sdk_pattern.md`\n* `docs/modkit_unified_system/13_e2e_testing.md`\n* `libs/modkit/src/api/openapi_registry.rs`\n* `modules/credstore/QUICKSTART.md`\n* `modules/file-parser/QUICKSTART.md`\n* `modules/mini-chat/README.md`\n* `modules/mini-chat/deploy/helm/mini-chat/templates/configmap.yaml`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs.orig`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs.orig`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/license_middleware.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/license_middleware.rs.orig`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/middleware_order.rs`\n* `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/middleware_order.rs.orig`\n* `modules/system/nodes-registry/QUICKSTART.md`\n* `modules/system/nodes-registry/README.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/docs/features/0001-sdk-module-foundation.md`\n* `modules/system/tenant-resolver/QUICKSTART.md`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/hello_world/test_hello_world.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/config/base.yaml`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/conftest.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/test_live_smoke.py`\n* `testing/e2e/requirements.txt`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces a comprehensive API gateway system with configurable server prefix support, renaming the default prefix from `/cf` to `/cw`. The core work includes OpenAPI servers field support, a complete ApiGateway module implementation with middleware orchestration, extensive test infrastructure for authentication and licensing, and systematic documentation updates across all modules and guides.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Core API Gateway and OpenAPI Infrastructure**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n|**OpenAPI servers configuration support** <br> `libs/modkit/src/api/openapi_registry.rs` | `OpenApiInfo` adds `servers: Vec<String>` field, `build_openapi` conditionally populates OpenAPI `.servers(...)`, and request-body content building is refactored into a reusable `build_request_body_content` helper. |\n|**Core ApiGateway module and HTTP server lifecycle** <br> `modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs.orig` | Implements complete `ApiGateway` struct with configuration, router caching, middleware orchestration, HTTP server startup, and OpenAPI registration. Includes `Module`, `ApiGatewayCapability`, and `OpenApiRegistry` trait implementations with comprehensive unit and integration tests. |\n|**Configuration, prefix normalization, and middleware** <br> `config/quickstart.yaml`, `modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs`, `modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs`, `modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` | Configures example prefix as `/cw`, documents and normalizes `prefix_path` with segment-boundary safety, and populates OpenAPI servers field from normalized prefix. |\n|**Authentication middleware test suite** <br> `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs.orig`, `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs` | Comprehensive auth-disabled/enabled test modes covering token validation, bearer security metadata, path parameters with prefix, resolver error handling, and CORS preflight bypass. |\n|**License middleware test suite** <br> `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/license_middleware.rs.orig`, `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/license_middleware.rs` | Feature-based access control tests validating license denial, problem+json responses, and behavior with configured prefix paths. |\n|**Middleware ordering test suite** <br> `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/middleware_order.rs.orig`, `modules/system/api-gateway/tests/middleware_order.rs` | Validates MIME, CORS, rate-limit, and request-id middleware execution order with correct token consumption timing. |\n\n**Documentation and Configuration Migration to /cw Prefix**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n|**Example server configuration and quickstart** <br> `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `Makefile`, `README.md`, `docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md` | Updates example server binary name, OpenAPI URL default, user-facing URLs, and quickstart documentation to reference `/cw/` routes and health endpoints. |\n|**OpenAPI document server configuration** <br> `docs/api/api.json` | Adds top-level `servers` section with `/cw` URL for generated clients. |\n|**Module QUICKSTART and README updates** <br> `modules/credstore/QUICKSTART.md`, `modules/file-parser/QUICKSTART.md`, `modules/mini-chat/README.md`, `modules/mini-chat/deploy/helm/mini-chat/templates/configmap.yaml`, `modules/system/nodes-registry/QUICKSTART.md`, `modules/system/nodes-registry/README.md`, `modules/system/tenant-resolver/QUICKSTART.md` | All module documentation updated to reflect gateway-prefixed URLs using `/cw` and configurable prefix explanation. |\n|**Architecture and SDK documentation** <br> `docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0004-single-root-tenant-model-topology.md`, `docs/arch/authorization/TENANT_MODEL.md`, `docs/arch/authorization/INTEGRATION_TEST_PLAN.md`, `docs/modkit_unified_system/02_module_layout_and_sdk_pattern.md`, `docs/modkit_unified_system/13_e2e_testing.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/docs/features/0001-sdk-module-foundation.md` | Architecture docs reword deployment terminology, integration test plan updates endpoint paths, SDK guides and E2E testing documentation updated to use `/cw` prefix in examples. |\n|**E2E test configuration and fixtures** <br> `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/config/base.yaml`, `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/conftest.py`, `testing/e2e/modules/mini_chat/test_live_smoke.py`, `testing/e2e/requirements.txt` | Mini-chat E2E tests updated to use `/cw` prefix in API base URLs and health checks; pytest minimum version updated to 9.0.3. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A gateway rises tall, with `/cw` paths so fine,*  \n> *Servers now configurable, middleware in line,*  \n> *From auth to licensing, each test shines bright,*  \n> *The fabric transforms—hop forward into the light!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- announcements_start -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> <details>\n> <summary>💬 Introducing Slack Agent: The best way for teams to turn conversations into code.</summary>\n> \n> [Slack Agent](https://www.coderabbit.ai/agent) is built on CodeRabbit's deep understanding of your code, so your team can collaborate across the entire SDLC without losing context.\n> \n> - Generate code and open pull requests\n> - Plan features and break down work\n> - Investigate incidents and troubleshoot customer tickets together\n> - Automate recurring tasks and respond to alerts with triggers\n> - Summarize progress and report instantly\n> \n> Built for teams:\n> \n> - **Shared memory** across your entire org—no repeating context\n> - **Per-thread sandboxes** to safely plan and execute work\n> - **Governance built-in**—scoped access, auditability, and budget controls\n> \n> One agent for your entire SDLC. Right inside Slack.\n> \n> 👉 [Get started](https://agent.coderabbit.ai/)\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- announcements_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4459897674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":1909,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1909","source_state":"closed","source_author":"jalankulkija","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #1909] feat(minichat): Add support of Anthropic API","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"issue-1251","pr_head_sha":"145432d4874370acc0712627a65be5010a84fcc2","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"jalankulkija","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1909","id":3689566322,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7b6lBy","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1909","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1909.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1909.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1909","number":1909,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(minichat): Add support of Anthropic API","user":{"login":"jalankulkija","id":260627792,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4jdUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260627792?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija","html_url":"https://github.com/jalankulkija","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds first-class support for Anthropic's Messages API to mini-chat. Chats can now route to Claude models while continuing to use Azure / OpenAI for primary file storage; a pluggable knowledge-search (RAG) tool ships in the same change.\r\n\r\n### Anthropic Messages API\r\n\r\n- New `AnthropicMessagesProvider` adapter (`/v1/messages`) implementing `LlmProvider`: streaming SSE state machine, non-streaming `complete()`, structured error parsing (rate-limit → `RateLimited`, others → `ProviderError` with HTTP/status context), wire-level diagnostic logging.\r\n- `ProviderKind::AnthropicMessages` registered in `create_provider` and the OAGW provisioning layer; `upstream_headers_for_kind` injects `anthropic-version` and allowlists `anthropic-beta` / `accept` per request.\r\n- `ProviderEntry.rag_provider` config field decouples LLM provider from storage provider — Anthropic chats can keep Azure as the RAG backend via `resolve_rag_provider`. `MiniChatConfig::validate_provider_refs` catches typo'd references at boot.\r\n\r\n### Anthropic Files API (parallel uploads)\r\n\r\n- New `AnthropicFilesClient` (upload / delete via OAGW, multipart body, `files-api-2025-04-14` beta opt-in, 404-as-success on delete).\r\n- `attachments` table gains `anthropic_file_id` + `anthropic_status` (`not_attempted` → `pending` → `uploaded` | `failed`); new migration `m20260417_000004_add_anthropic_fields`.\r\n- `AttachmentService::upload_file` performs a best-effort secondary upload to Anthropic Files API for Anthropic-backed chats, sharing the buffered image `Bytes` with the thumbnail generator. DB-conn failures are scoped inside the best-effort block so the primary upload always reaches `ready`.\r\n- `AnthropicMessagesProvider` substitutes the primary `provider_file_id` with the Anthropic file id when building outbound `image` / `document` blocks; dropped blocks are logged. The lookup map is built per-request via `build_anthropic_file_id_map`.\r\n- Cleanup is wired end-to-end: both `AttachmentCleanupHandler` and `ChatCleanupHandler` carry the Anthropic alias + file id in their outbox payloads and issue a secondary `DELETE /v1/files/{id}` after the primary delete. Failures log but never block primary cleanup.\r\n\r\n### Knowledge-search (RAG) tool\r\n\r\n- New `KnowledgeRetriever` domain port + `AzureKnowledgeRetriever` infra impl backed by Azure vector-store search.\r\n- `KnowledgeSearchConfig` (toggle, vector store id, provider id, top-k, max chunk chars, system-prompt guard).\r\n- Agentic loop in `provider_task::spawn_provider_task`: provider-emitted `TerminalOutcome::ToolUse` for `search_knowledge` triggers retrieval, post-processing (dedup + score-sort + chunk-index URI assignment + UTF-8-safe truncation), and replay via `raw_input_items`. Output is formatted as Anthropic `search_result` blocks or as `[SOURCE_N]` text depending on the adapter. Per-message call limit is enforced with a soft notice; a hard `max_calls + 2` iteration cap terminates the turn as `agentic_iterations_exceeded` if the model keeps requesting.\r\n- `file_search_completed_count` plumbed end-to-end: new `chat_turns` column (migration `m20260512_000005`), `ToolCallType::FileSearch`, per-call persistence from the agentic loop, orphan-watchdog recovery (with negative-value clamp), and propagation to the `UsageEvent`.\r\n- New metrics: `knowledge_search` (counter, `ok` / `error`), `knowledge_search_latency_ms`, `knowledge_search_chunks`.\r\n\r\n### Typed model-policy params\r\n\r\n- New `LlmRequest.api_params: ModelApiParams` channel replaces the per-adapter `additional_params` hand-rolling for temperature / top_p / penalties / stop / reasoning effort / extra_body. OpenAI Responses, vLLM Responses, and Anthropic adapters consume it directly; Anthropic correctly drops `temperature` when `top_p < 1.0` for the reasoning-model constraint. (Chat Completions adapter still TODO.)\r\n- `LlmProviderError::RateLimited` now surfaces `retry-after` to the SSE error message.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Knowledge-search (RAG) tool for semantic document retrieval during conversations.\n  * Anthropic provider support, including optional Anthropic file uploads and provider-aware request handling.\n  * Optional secondary file upload flow for attachments with best-effort cleanup of secondary provider files.\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * New usage metrics for knowledge search (results, latency, chunks) and tracking for secondary-cleanup skips.\n  * Configuration validation for RAG/provider settings and safer cleanup/delete flows.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1909?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-15T12:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T07:31:19Z","closed_at":"2026-05-19T07:31:19Z","merged_at":"2026-05-19T07:31:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"14247cbec3fc806836515248687dcfb0bfa9155f","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1909/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/1909/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1909/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/145432d4874370acc0712627a65be5010a84fcc2","head":{"label":"jalankulkija:issue-1251","ref":"issue-1251","sha":"145432d4874370acc0712627a65be5010a84fcc2","user":{"login":"jalankulkija","id":260627792,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4jdUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260627792?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija","html_url":"https://github.com/jalankulkija","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jalankulkija/followers","following_url":"h