dentifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4459180610","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1907#issuecomment-4459180610","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1907","id":4459180610,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABCcmyQg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T10:58:48Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T10:59:56Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `ec2bdd5d-245e-4eaf-ab37-7ee0a2a3e9e5`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between dc5a98e305e863de913555f175c910b5e9604220 and 87ae287b8c2f0894dfe9431ed37496b647462fc5.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (20)</summary>\n\n* `.cypilot/config/artifacts.toml`\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/ADR/0001-cpt-cf-usage-collector-adr-scoped-emit-source.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/ADR/0002-cpt-cf-usage-collector-adr-two-phase-emit-authz.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/DECOMPOSITION.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/DESIGN.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/PRD.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/features/0001-cpt-cf-usage-collector-feature-sdk-and-ingest-core.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/Cargo.toml`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/README.md`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/api.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/error.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/error_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/gts.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/lib.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/models.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/models_tests.rs`\n* `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces the `usage-collector-sdk` crate, a transport-agnostic contracts library for the usage collector system. It includes updated ADRs clarifying the `runtime.factory()` pattern and two-phase authorization flow, complete system decomposition and PRD updates, comprehensive data models with strict serde validation, public client/plugin API traits, and authorization/error infrastructure with GTS schema registration.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Usage Collector SDK Implementation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Workspace & Foundation Setup** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `.cypilot/config/artifacts.toml`|Add the new SDK crate to workspace members/dependencies and exclude it from Cypilot traceability during incremental PR rollout.|\n|**Architecture Decision Records & Design Foundation** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/ADR/0001-*.md`, `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/ADR/0002-*.md`|ADR-0001 documents the shift from `for_module()`-scoped clients to `runtime.factory()` module-scoped factories bound at init. ADR-0002 specifies two-phase PDP authorization (factory `.authorize()` before transaction; emitter `.enqueue()` with in-memory validation) with three-state subject intent contract and freshness enforcement.|\n|**Comprehensive Design & Specification Documents** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/DECOMPOSITION.md`, `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/PRD.md`, `modules/system/usage-collector/docs/features/0001-*.md`|DECOMPOSITION defines 8 features (SDK/emitter, REST client, query API, production storage, type system, rate limiting, retention, operator ops). PRD expands ingestion to SDK and REST paths with OAuth2/PDP authorization per path. Feature spec details two-phase authorize/enqueue, outbox pipeline, gateway handlers, and comprehensive DoD/acceptance criteria.|\n|**SDK Crate Manifest & Cargo Configuration** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/Cargo.toml`|New library crate with dependencies for ModKit, AuthZ, async, chrono/uuid, serde, and GTS.|\n|**Data Models with Full Serde & Validation Tests** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/models.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/models_tests.rs`|`UsageKind` (gauge/counter), `AllowedMetric`, `ModuleConfig`, `Subject`, and `UsageRecord` with serde strictness (deny unknown fields, conditional metadata serialization, snake_case enums). Tests cover JSON round-trips, field validation, non-finite values, forward compatibility, and negative cases.|\n|**Client & Plugin API Contracts with Documentation** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/api.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/README.md`|`UsageCollectorClientV1` and `UsageCollectorPluginClientV1` async traits define gateway and storage plugin interfaces. README documents SDK purpose, security invariants, usage patterns for config queries and record construction, and plugin integration.|\n|**Authorization Constants & Error Domain Definitions** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/authz_tests.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/error.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/error_tests.rs`, `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/gts.rs`|Authorization defines PDP properties/actions and registers `USAGE_RECORD` resource type with supported properties. Error module defines `UsageCollectorError`, resource-scoped error types, and GTS schema; tests validate wire identifiers and property invariants.|\n|**Crate Root & Public Surface Definition** <br> `modules/system/usage-collector/usage-collector-sdk/src/lib.rs`|Declares all public submodules and re-exports primary traits, error types, schemas, and models to form the crate's public API surface.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A new SDK stands tall and bright,*  \n> *With models, traits, and contracts tight,*  \n> *Serde tests hop through JSON streams,*  \n> *Authorization guards our dreams,*  \n> *UsageCollector's foundation gleams!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4459180610/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4459204486","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/1907#issuecomment-4459204486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/1907","id":4459204486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs8AAAABCcoPhg","user":{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T11:02:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T11:17:24Z","body":"Previous review from @Artifizer:\r\n\r\n> ## SDK interface review\r\n> \r\n> Overall the structure is solid — clean trait split, good security doc on `UsageCollectorClientV1`, and the error constructors are ergonomic. The issues below are things that will matter once the follow-on crates build on top of this contract; easier to fix now than when `usage-emitter` and the REST client are already shipped.\r\n> \r\n> ---\r\n> \r\n> ### 🔴 Required changes\r\n> \r\n> #### 1. `subject_id` / `subject_type` are a co-varying pair — group them\r\n> \r\n> `UsageRecord` has two separate `Option<_>` fields that must always be set together:\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> pub subject_id: Option<Uuid>,\r\n> pub subject_type: Option<String>,\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> The type system doesn't enforce that invariant. Any caller can set one and leave the other `None`, and the gateway would silently accept a malformed record.\r\n> \r\n> **Fix:** introduce a `SubjectRef` struct and replace both fields with `Option<SubjectRef>`:\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> pub struct SubjectRef {\r\n>     pub id: Uuid,\r\n>     pub kind: String,\r\n> }\r\n> \r\n> // in UsageRecord:\r\n> pub subject: Option<SubjectRef>,\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> This also simplifies the serde test — one field to check instead of two — and eliminates the `skip_serializing_if` duplication.\r\n\r\nThis is now fixed.\r\n\r\n> #### 2. `is_retryable()` is missing from `UsageCollectorError`\r\n> \r\n> The emitter's outbox will need to decide whether to retry a failed delivery. Without this helper it has to pattern-match the enum directly, coupling it to internal error variants. `mini-chat-sdk` already establishes this pattern with `is_transient()` / `is_permanent()`.\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> /// Returns `true` for transient errors that are safe to retry.\r\n> #[must_use]\r\n> pub fn is_retryable(&self) -> bool {\r\n>     matches!(self, Self::Unavailable { .. } | Self::PluginTimeout | Self::CircuitOpen)\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> `AuthorizationFailed`, `Internal`, and `ModuleNotFound` are permanent — retrying won't change the outcome.\r\n> \r\n\r\nI've changed the SDK to use canonical errors from modkit.\r\n\r\n> #### 3. `idempotency_key: String` should be `Uuid`\r\n> \r\n> The test constructs it as `Uuid::new_v4().to_string()`, which is a hint the field really is a UUID. Using `String` loses the type contract and forces every call site to produce a string representation. With `Uuid` the field roundtrips through serde cleanly, avoids a heap allocation, and prevents malformed keys from slipping through.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure we force idempotency key type to be stricter than opaque string. Industry-convention idempotency keys (Stripe, IETF idempotency-key draft) are opaque client strings, often deterministic (tenant:event:ts) for natural deduplication. Typing the field as Uuid precludes that pattern entirely and forces every external caller — including REST clients and future forwarders — into one format.\r\n\r\n> ### 🟡 Improvements\r\n> \r\n> #### 4. `UsageCollectorPluginClientV1` has no batch method\r\n> \r\n> Storage plugins are the hot path for ingestion. TimescaleDB (Feature 4) supports bulk `INSERT` — but the trait today only exposes a single-record API. Adding a `create_usage_records_batch` with a sequential default impl costs nothing and lets backends override for efficiency without a breaking change later:\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> async fn create_usage_records_batch(\r\n>     &self,\r\n>     records: Vec<UsageRecord>,\r\n> ) -> Result<(), UsageCollectorError> {\r\n>     for record in records {\r\n>         self.create_usage_record(record).await?;\r\n>     }\r\n>     Ok(())\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nI suggest this to be moved to a separate PR in the chain, as this will require substantial changes to existing PRs.\r\n\r\n> #### 5. `AllowedMetric`, `ModuleConfig` are missing `utoipa::ToSchema` and `PartialEq`\r\n> \r\n> `UsageKind` has `#[derive(utoipa::ToSchema)]` but the structs that contain it don't. If `get_module_config` ever appears in an OpenAPI spec (likely, given the REST client in PR 3), these will need it. Add `PartialEq` at the same time — it makes test assertions on `ModuleConfig` responses possible without field-by-field comparison.\r\n\r\nFixed.\r\n\r\n> #### 6. `UsageKind` is missing `Hash`\r\n> \r\n> It derives `Eq` but not `Hash`. Any caller wanting a `HashMap<UsageKind, _>` or `HashSet<UsageKind>` is blocked for no reason.\r\n> \r\n\r\nFixed.\r\n\r\n> \r\n> ### ✅ What's good\r\n> \r\n> - Security invariant on `UsageCollectorClientV1` (never register in `ClientHub`) is clearly documented — this is the right place for it.\r\n> - `#[must_use]` on all error constructors.\r\n> - Inline doc on `metadata` explaining the 8 KiB limit and the `null`-vs-absent serde behaviour.\r\n> - The GTS schema registration follows the established `BaseModkitPluginV1` pattern.\r\n> - Test file co-location via `#[path = \"...\"]` matches project conventions.\r\n> \r\n> ---\r\n> \r\n> All of the above are implemented and verified (19 tests pass) on branch `claude/review-sdk-interface-GC95y` — feel free to cherry-pick or use as a reference.\r\n> \r\n> ---\r\n> _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4459204486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]}]}
